{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3","id":715607,"title":"Irked Reads Ex3","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-22T14:47:26-07:00","id":715607,"title":"Irked Reads Ex3","content":"Along with probably half the other people on this forum, but!<br /> <br /> LET\u2019S READ EXALTED 3<br /> <br /> The book stands at 659 pages; there are no bookmarks, etc. yet, which is as expected.<br /> <br /> The cover is, as was foretold, a placeholder. It\u2019s definitely not the finished cover in general \u2013 it has a big, flat \u201cEX3\u201d to one side and no other text. Hopefully this applies to the art as well, because, ugh \u2013 giant closed-eyed generic wuxia lady is, uh, not really setting the tone or giving me any idea what to expect. There\u2019s also an ugly seam running down her arm where it overlaps the \u201cEX3 thing,\u201d so, yeah, hoping this is very temporary - it's an ugly piece.<br /> <br /> First inside page is exactly one sentence. Well, all right.<br /> <br /> We launch into an old-school WW fiction intro. True confessions: I never liked those. They were almost always long-winded and borderline incomprehensible if you didn\u2019t already know the universe \u2013 or were to me, anyway; I know a lot of people have great affection for them. This one is a bit of Borgstromantic fiction, from what\u2019s been said. There\u2019s some weird kerning and seemingly missing spaces right out of the gate \u2013 like, literally first paragraph \u2013 which is a bit odd. Things seem to smooth out after that, and it\u2019s a pretty serviceable fic\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026 leading right into the two page spread of Wu Jian. Which is, all misgivings about two page spreads aside, absolutely gorgeous. Well done.<br /> <br /> The rest of the fic is a mixed bag: it does this grand, sweeping legendary-sounding text, and then switches to almost Whedonesque banter. I don\u2019t picture Exalted characters saying, \u201c\u2026 OK?\u201d and yet here we are. But it <i>does</i> convey the grandeur and possibility of the Solar Exalted, without making the Dragon-Blooded look lesser for it, and that\u2019s an accomplishment. It\u2019s also absolutely chock full of supernatural things happening as commonplace, probably-in-the-house-next-door events, and that\u2019s an interesting tonal shift, as well.<br /> <br /> Next page has some anime-ish page featuring a mix of signature characters old and new. Hello, old friends. I've missed you.<br /> <br /> Table of contents! Chapter 6 entry is, uh, <i>bad</i>: it\u2019s missing a bunch of Abilities (Archery, say) and including a bunch of things that aren\u2019t Abilities (unless \u201cSex\u201d has been added to the sheet this edition). Several page numbers are also obviously wrong. Ch. 7 is missing a space in \u201cSnake Style\u201d and has an extra 4 in \u201cSorcerous Workings.\u201d Most of the rest seems workable.<br /> <br /> Next up: Introduction!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T16:12:51-07:00","id":716032,"title":"","content":"Opening quotes are from Tanith Lee, on demon-queens, and Abraham Lincoln, on power. Good quotes, interesting choices.<br /> <br /> Another fic! Which is cool, but I\u2019m 18 pages in now, and it would be nice to get to the actual text. This is one of those short chapter-opener fics: Novia Claro, Solar (and presumably Night) stealths her way onto a Realm ship, steals their plans, and vanishes. It\u2019s perfectly serviceable, if not really a stand-out.<br /> <br /> Page 20: \u201cIntroduction: The First and Final Days.\u201d All right, text!<br /> <br /> \u201cIt has been said that Creation is doomed,\u201d says the book, \u201cBut it was not always that way.\u201d And the text isn\u2019t confirming that what\u2019s said is true, either \u2013 it\u2019ll be interesting to see how much of 1e\u2019s \u201ccanonical ending\u201d is going to appear.<br /> <br /> Good summary of the Exalted history \u2013 no mention of the Primordials by name, which feels like a deliberate choice. The First Age is explicitly called out as five thousand years long \u2013 interesting. The Usurpation is blamed on \u201cthe other Exalted,\u201d which raises interesting questions.<br /> <br /> That previewed Aztek-looking art piece makes a reappearance, and it\u2019s <i>much</i> better this time: better color, the Solar is obviously fighting some titanic abomination and not just a big dude, and the armies at the bottom are still on their feet. Really good changes all around.<br /> <br /> The history seems relatively unchanged \u2013 rebellion, First Age, Usurpation, shogunate, Contagion, Fari Folk invasion - which I\u2019m cool with. P. 22 gives us another typo \u2013 the armies of Creation \u201ccrumbed.\u201d Some of the verbiage seems to be getting away from the author; on failing to conquer the Lunar dominions, \u201cthe Empress threaded the boundaries of her empire with legions and set about draining conquered lands of their resources so that her Realm could grow mighty and wroth for a return.\u201d Er, how did looting the lands make her nation \u201cwroth?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Empress\u2019s disappearance is left <i>very</i> ambiguous, to the delight of all, I imagine. Warstriders are mentioned by name, which may reassure some folks who were afraid magitech was just <i>gone</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, it\u2019s probably worth mentioning at this point: page numbers are in the middle of the page, as they were in the preview. Why would you do this? Why would <i>anyone</i> do this? Page numbers go in the corners so that you can flip through the darned book to the page you\u2019re looking for; putting them smack in the middle makes that impossible.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t mentioned the background yet, basically because it isn\u2019t registering on me. It\u2019s\u2026 a background, I guess? This chapter is a full sun on a grey-blue sky, with cranes silhouetted across it. It\u2019s not by any means bad, and it generally avoids being distracting, but I\u2019d have been fine with a mostly white background, too.<br /> <br /> P. 23 abruptly switches tense from past to present tense \u2013 \u201cThe Empress\u2019s disappearance <i>presages</i>\u201d \u2013 and then immediately returns to past tense.<br /> <br /> The end of the intro states that it\u2019s now impossible to save Creation \u2013 but then, it was impossible for Solars to kill \u201cthe enemies of the gods,\u201d too, and look how that turned out. The clear implication is that it <i>could</i> \u2013 maybe \u2013 turn out different.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re in the mandatory \u201cWhat is an RPG?\u201d section. The Storyteller is explicitly defined as a player, which I imagine will matter to combat transparency in a bit.<br /> <br /> Glosssary time! Apparently all living beings have an anima; the Exalted are unusual in that theirs is visible. Huh. Daiklave gets a pronunciation guide, which, heh, is probably wise. (Demesne and Sidereal do, too, thankfully.) The Deathlords are mentioned as \u201c[maybe] the most powerful beings to walk the world in this age,\u201d but are <i>not</i> called out as Solar ghosts. The Exigents and Liminals get name-checked; the Alchemicals and Infernals do <i>not</i>. (Neither, for that mention, do Primordials, though Yozis do. Malfeas is mentioned as a place, but not an entity.)<br /> <br /> Fiction resources! Tanith Lee and Lord Dunsany, of course; Howard, Moorcock, and GRRM are present as well. (R. Scott Bakker is not, alas.) FF7, Claymore, and the Book of Judges also make the cut, among others. It\u2019s a good list!<br /> <br /> Here endeth the Introduction.<br /> <br /> <i>The Good:</i> Really great art; solid introduction to the setting as a whole.<br /> <i>The Bad:</i> There\u2019s a lot more typos so far than I would have expected, given the length of time in development.<br /> <i>The Ugly:</i> Those page numbers, dude. The heck.<br /> <br /> Up next: \u201cChapter One: The Exalted.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T17:12:35-07:00","id":716305,"title":"","content":"Chapter One: The Exalted<br /> <br /> Perfect Soul, our new sig Zenith, gets a fiction. And it\u2019s a pretty great intro; she Exalts while cursing the Unconquered Sun as a distant, uncaring god and smashing one of his shrines, which is cool all the way around. On the downside, the fic highlights two problems with the formatting: first, that there\u2019s no italics to indicate when we\u2019re reading someone\u2019s thoughts, and second, that it takes a second or so of squinty scrutiny to distinguish a comma from a period in this font.<br /> <br /> We get a great full-page picture of PS kneeling before the statue of the Sun. It\u2019s a cool, striking image; the Sun looks a little like Julius Caesar with four arms, which is a good look. (Er, how\u2019s she supposed to reach his head to smash it, though? And didn\u2019t the fic say the statue was painted?)<br /> <br /> Sidebar \u2013 the lifespans of the Exalted. Sounds about like it was in 2e: a few hundred for Dragon-Blooded, a few thousand for Celestials, longer for Sidereals, maybe forever for Abyssals. The rest get a who-knows-what\u2019s-up-with-them shrug.<br /> <br /> We get a discussion of Solar Exaltation that will be familiar to those who have read old editions: tend to be exceptional already, Exalt during moments of stress, overcome impossible odds, etc. Child Solars are explicitly called out as possible; the Zenith message-from-the-Sun is also mentioned as a unique feature of that caste.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded Exaltation is mentioned as a matter of blood; there\u2019s no reappearance of 2e\u2019s \u201cmust be heroes\u201d sidebar. Liminals and Exigents again get a big shrug.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s a new feature: <i>Essence fever</i>, a drive that compels new Solars to go forth and change the world. It\u2019s a nice bit of explanation for why your character is out adventuring. It also includes what feels like a bit of tut-tutting at people who say, \u201cI spend some Essence to...,\u201d but the section as a whole is good.<br /> <br /> Summary of the world continues, hitting what seem like good major points: caste marks, demesnes, and so on. The Dragon-Blooded book gets a plug. Then we come to THE EXALTED! It\u2019s a two page spread that\u2019s\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026 that\u2019s the same thing we saw back at the end of the opening fic, with all the signature characters. The heck? It\u2019s a lot bigger now, but these figures are pretty low-detail anime faces; I don\u2019t think they benefit from being enlarged.<br /> <br /> First up are THE SOLAR EXALTED. Who have a blurb that is\u2026 hard-to-read italic-cursive stuff. Eh, okay. We get caste summaries, and descriptions of the Solar schtick: <i>mastery</i>, of martial arts, of sorcery, of the world in general. We also get a \u201cPlay one of these Exalted if you want\u2026\u201d which is a nice touch, though \u201c\u2026 to actually be able to play the game in the next six months\u201d is not listed among them.<br /> <br /> Cool full-page picture of five Solars. They\u2019re a martial-looking bunch; I think these are <i>not</i> our sig five. Two of them are white-haired pretty boys, which is a bit odd, but it\u2019s a nice piece. The art in general is a lot more paints and soft lines so far than it was in 2e, which works well.<br /> <br /> THE ABYSSAL EXALTED are not called out explicitly as tainted Solars \u2013 interesting. They are described as servants of the Deathlords, and as romantic, chivalrous necromancers \u2013 which seems to mean they kill people to make a point, and not just \u2018cuz.<br /> <br /> Maybe it\u2019s just me, but the language here feels a little overwrought. \u201cPLAY ONE OF THE ABYSSAL EXALTED if you want to be a warrior-poet of macabre passions and dark romance\u201d forces me unavoidably to picture <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=56R3hU-fWZY\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, which may not be the desired outcome.<br /> <br /> Cool picture of\u2026 are all of these Abyssals wearing <i>clothes</i>? Like, actual clothes that conceal the flesh beneath? They look dangerous and imposing, anyway, which I imagine is the intended effect. Colors are nicely muted.<br /> <br /> THE DRAGON-BLOODED are the first Exalts whose picture seems to show them <i>doing something</i>: five brightly colored warriors (you do you, white-jade-dude-with-bull-horns) are standing over what looks like the corpse of a massive elemental dragon. Their description is, in contrast to the rest, very focused on externals: their <i>family</i>, their <i>stockpile of weapons</i>, their <i>inherited evocations</i>, and so on.<br /> <br /> THE LUNAR EXALTED get a dose of oWoD Werewolf RAAAAEG; apparently, they\u2019re compelled to break stuff (where \u201cstuff\u201d is \u201cmodern civilizations\u201d and \u201cancient technology\u201d). Their image is fine \u2013 tattoos, check; beastman form, check \u2013 but I don\u2019t really have a strong sense of how most of these images so far are <i>different</i> from the others.<br /> <br /> THE SIDEREAL EXALTED \u2013 masters of astrology, fate, and martial arts \u2013 have probably my favorite image so far: one of these subtle, super-secret ninja bureaucrats is about eight feet tall and carrying an axe as big as he is. Awesome.<br /> <br /> THE LIMINAL EXALTED \u2013 \u201cmade in madness and born from death\u201d \u2013 are described as basically Frankenstein\u2019s monsters: replacing old limbs with fresh ones, bound to their creators, and doomed to degenerate into savage horrors without some kind of tie to humanity. Cool.<br /> <br /> THE EXIGENTS ARE pretty vague \u2013 some of the description boils down to \u201cYou can be all sorts of things.\u201d Apparently the Exigent Exaltations can be stolen and corrupted, before bonding with a human, which is a neat idea. Their image is a mixed bag, but Strawmaiden Janest continues to look awesome.<br /> <br /> AND THE TALE OF THE EXALTED CONTINUES shows us Lissome Avid Engineer, what\u2019s probably an Infernal, and\u2026 some guy with a black cloud over his head. No idea what\u2019s up with him. The LAE art looks <i>familiar</i>, though \u2013 is this a trace of existing art, or is she just very distinctive?<br /> <br /> Oh, it\u2019s a two page spread! Yeah, no idea who the rest of you guys are. This two page spread is less awesome than the one of Wu Jian, which puts me back in kind of a, \u201cUgh, two page spreads,\u201d frame of mind, but it\u2019s otherwise very serviceable.<br /> <br /> <i>The Good:</i> This is a strong introduction to lots of different types of Exalts; it\u2019s a bit long, but it feels like I could have my players read it and have a strong sense of what they want to play. It\u2019s a good opener, and I love the opening picture with the UncSun statue.<br /> <i>The Bad:</i> The art here is nice \u2013 again, I like the line-free paintings \u2013 but nothing really stands out. The pieces mostly feel muted, which works for, say, the Abyssals, but doesn\u2019t really inspire me to play a Solar. There are only a couple of characters \u2013 Axe Sidereal, primarily \u2013 who make me say, \u201cHeck yeah, I want to be <i>that</i> guy.\u201d<br /> <i>The Ugly:</i> Nope, I got nothing this time. Chapter was pretty good.<br /> <br /> <br /> Up next: &quot;Chapter Two: The Age of Sorrows.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T18:34:36-07:00","id":716694,"title":"","content":"Chapter Two: \u201cThe Age of Sorrows.\u201d<br /> <br /> Opening fic \u2013 hey, it\u2019s a previous signature character! Hi, Seven Devils Clever! This is a bit of fiction of\u2026 mixed quality, and <i>darn</i> those commas are starting to drive me crazy. Last paragraph has two speakers, with no break between. Art piece shows us our two characters and a couple of gorilla henchmen \u2013 which, yay gorilla henchmen, but I\u2019m a little disappointed not to see a bit of Faxai after how much the fic built it up.<br /> <br /> We get a brief description of the world \u2013 short, evocative, to the point. Nice. There\u2019s also a cool picture of Not-Zeus towering over some mortal worshipper. The book breaks down some of the major spirit types: gods (who rule portfolios of concepts and are some mix of distant and corrupt), including the Incarnae in specific; elementals (born of the interplay of Creation\u2019s natural elements), with a picture of a surprisingly cute three-story-tall otter-thing; and demons (the \u201cslaves and children\u201d of the enslaved Yozis). The write-ups here suggest broadly what you\u2019d <i>do</i> with these things, which is helpful.<br /> <br /> Huh, Yu-Shan is now an island in a quicksilver ocean. Okay. We get a nice little picture of the result, with zeppelins and sky-boats and some kind of flying thing; it has a very technological feel to it, which contrasts nicely with most of what we\u2019ve seen of Creation.<br /> <br /> And a map! A tiny, tiny map. Like, I\u2019m at 129% magnification, and I can\u2019t read most of this text. This\u2026 is not usable.<br /> <br /> Our section on the Realm is written in present tense, and includes a description of the ruthless power of the Wyld Hunt. This is a little odd; back in the Intro, we were told that the Hunt had \u201clapsed.\u201d Which is it?<br /> <br /> Ooh, Rakan Thulio sidebar. Thulio is a rebel against heaven, a rogue Sidereal whose love went for someone else. Well, that\u2019s\u2026 a little petty, dude; losing in love hurts, but we don\u2019t all try to burn down Creation over it. <a href=\"http://www.harkavagrant.com/index.php?id=373\" target=\"_blank\">Not in Scamander\u2019s river.</a> Thulio and his minions, a group of rogue Sidereals (yikes, that has to hurt) and the fate-defying <i>Getimian</i> Exalted, are apparently at war with Heaven now. There\u2019s a picture of shadowy, hooded figures; it also includes Thulio, who is\u2026 very purple, and not especially like his comic appearance, I don\u2019t think?<br /> <br /> We get a letter to a Sidereal (probably?) discussing the Empress, her history, and some theories on her disappearance. It\u2019s a nice set of Storyteller options.<br /> <br /> Hey, it\u2019s that infamous Empress-flashing-some-thigh picture. And\u2026 ah ha ha, they drew a robe over that leg. Fabulous. That\u2026 really looks kind of bad, actually; the modesty-robe is fuzzy in ways that don\u2019t match the rest of the art.<br /> <br /> Oh, Regent Fokuf. You\u2019re back. Hooray.<br /> <br /> Ooh, we get both a summary of the Great Houses and a house mons for each of them. That\u2019s immediately useful flavor \u2013 nice.<br /> <br /> Speaking of neat story hooks, apparently a Realm legion has gone rogue somewhere in the Threshold. That\u2019s got <i>lots</i> of potential; I sort of hope it never gets any more detail than that.<br /> <br /> Mnemon, are you still permanently 15? That was not the best feature of 2e. The Realm parade image you\u2019re part of is still excellent, though, even if I do have to scroll across two pages to see it.<br /> <br /> The names of the Immaculate Dragons are just hilarious. \u201cSextes Jyllis, He Who Hath Thrown Much Grass\u201d probably has the worst of it.<br /> <br /> All of this stuff is <i>useful</i>, though \u2013 it\u2019s good stuff that you\u2019d want to know if you were involving the Realm in a game.<br /> <br /> Days are back to 24 hours, which is\u2026 probably for the best.<br /> <br /> Exigents are <i>not</i> generally Wyld Hunt targets, which is interesting; why, if they\u2019re <i>especially</i> good, the Immaculate Faith teaches they might even reincarnate as Dragon-Blooded!<br /> <br /> We get treatments of the Guild and currency, which are welcome \u2013 I have tried and failed to break new players of saying \u201cI pull out some gold pieces.\u201d Weird kerning again, on p. 77- looks like \u201cSi lver.\u201d<br /> <br /> I swear this is word-for-word the sidebar on jade currency from 2e. Am I wrong?<br /> <br /> Man, the north looks <i>sweet</i>. Ravening wolfmen, a mammoth, some kind of crazy elk-horned fair folk thing \u2013 I immediately want to fight these guys. The east gets a nice overgrown ziggurat thing, which fits well with the feel of most games I\u2019ve played in that direction. The south is the first directional art that doesn\u2019t grab me \u2013 it just feels kind of generically \u201cYep, this is the desert.\u201d The <i>next</i> page, though, has a dude jousting at a tyrant lizard, and <i>hecks to the yeah</i>. The south is kind of\u2026 pirate-y, which is okay; hey, Moray Darktide, how ya doing?<br /> <br /> Each direction gets several cool new locations: the inmates-running-the-asylum prison-city of Fortitude, say, or the Realm city of Gloam, which is haunted by something vampirish. (That\u2019s\u2026 a little too cute for my tastes, honestly, but whatevs.) Palanquin gets an image: it\u2019s a city in a basin, literally held maybe a half-mile above the ground by four statues. It\u2019s worth noting that virtually every place described seems to be dramatically supernatural in some way; again, that\u2019s an interesting feel \u2013 pure-human settlements seem to be the exception rather than the rule, with most places having sorcerer-kings or god-blooded champions or ancient pre-human races or <i>something</i>.<br /> <br /> The Lover and Bagrash Kol get name-dropped, though without explanation.<br /> <br /> \u2026 That is a picture of an Aztec man with a raiton head, and for him I will forgive a multitude of sins.<br /> <br /> The Lunar dominions get described briefly, and\u2026 man, they are not sympathetic. The Lunar plan is, broadly:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Find a tribe.</li> <li>Promise them the world.</li> <li>Throw them at the Realm to die bravely on legionnaire swords. Wave goodbye.</li> <li>Go to step 1.</li> </ol><br /> This is all good stuff, but man, this chapter is <i>long</i> \u2013 I\u2019m starting to get weary of the detail reading through it.<br /> <br /> Apparently the Dragon-Blooded seek to use the five shrines of the Caul to open the path to \u201cFeng-Yi\u201d to revive their fading blood, whatever <i>that</i> means.<br /> <br /> We finally get a description of the Wyld and the Underworld, which rounds them out in general terms \u2013 enough to fake it for a while. And, hey, there\u2019s Masky! You, uh, you been working out, there, dude? You look a lot scarier than the last time I saw you. The deathlords in general are discussed, but left <i>very</i> vague; even how many there are is left as a question, and there\u2019s still no mention of \u201cBTW crazy Solar ghosts,\u201d which may suggest that that\u2019s not necessarily true anymore.<br /> <br /> Phew! And that\u2019s the chapter.<br /> <br /> <i>The Good: </i>Useful descriptions of almost every part of Creation; you could run a game out of this detail, and the direction sections are crawling with story hooks. Very solid work throughout, with some really lovely art (T-rex jouster! Raiton Aztec man!).<br /> <i>The Bad:</i> That tiny, useless map. The empress\u2019s knees. This chapter being loooooooooong \u2013 like, I\u2019m on page 117 or so now, and most of that is this chapter.<br /> <i>The Ugly: </i>\u201cShe thought he might want to bang her like a fine drum, but she didn\u2019t want to raise her tail to such a gruesome old buck.\u201d What even, guys. No.<br /> <br /> <br /> Up next: Chapter 3, &quot;Character Creation.&quot; But, uh, probably not tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T05:57:48-07:00","id":718718,"title":"","content":"Chapter 3: Character Creation<br /> <br /> Ooh, Liminalfic! We meet Echoing Breath, who is hunting down a long-dead Solar po-soul and the five Dragon-Blooded he killed. This is probably the first thing to give me any real interest in Liminals; Echoing Breath can catch glimpses of the world as it was, which is a neat idea to build a character around.<br /> <br /> Chargen does a pretty typical \u201cFind out what your game is about/write a blurb\u201d dance, which is absolutely standard and is not how I have created any character ever. (\u201cRead the entire Charm chapter and look for a place where you go OH MAN OH MAN\u201d might have been time consuming advice, though.)<br /> <br /> Not to beat a dead horse, but <i>man</i> these fonts are bad. It really stands out in the sub-heading \u201cAttributes\u201d \u2013 the first letter could plausibly be mistaken for a lowercase \u201cd.\u201d It\u2019s a small thing, but the difficulty in just reading the book is a persistent disruption.<br /> <br /> We have a standard WW-style 8/6/4 distribution, with all of the usual problems that come with that (distributing four dots as 5/1/1 gets you about twice as much bang for your buck as 3/3/1, for instance). Each caste now gets five <i>out of eight possibilities</i> as their Cate abilities, which I think is a <i>great</i> change, though \u2013 that\u2019s a lot more flexibility in caste creation, and it\u2019s also a nice solution to the Dawn problem.<br /> <br /> We get a big angry Solar dude with a golden halo around his head \u2013 possibly Exalting in the ruins of his home? He\u2019s cool looking, but again, the picture is very washed out \u2013 lots of browns and bronzes, and it just doesn\u2019t <i>pop</i> like some of the colorful 2e art.<br /> <br /> The choice of Caste Abilities is especially important because you\u2019re going to pick one of them as your <i>Supernal Ability</i> \u2013 an Ability where you can buy Charms all the way up to Essence 5, right out of the gate. That\u2019s very cool \u2013 it gives a better sense of, \u201cYes, we\u2019re both Twilights, but <i>this</i> is the thing that defines <i>my</i> legend.\u201d Seems like it stops mattering the closer you get to E5, though \u2013 and do note that, if you want to be any sort of supernal violence-person, you need to be a Dawn. (Supernal is <i>only</i> from caste, not favored.)<br /> <br /> Brawl is in the Ability list, and Martial Arts is\u2026 vague. Let\u2019s come back to that.<br /> <br /> 28 Ability dots later, we\u2019re adding Specialties! That\u2019s a nice distinguishing feature out of the gate. Specialties are also capped at +1 bonus die per roll now, which is <i>good</i> \u2013 no more \u201cgotta be +3 or you\u2019re a chump.\u201d We do get a little tip on buying Abilities efficiently, but, like\u2026 just make it all the same cost, guys. Don\u2019t make this a puzzle to be solved.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds are fused into Merits now \u2013 I think that was spoiled? You start with fifteen Charms \u2013 hoo boy \u2013 aaaaaand that\u2019s a picture of a lady tearing a bear in half. It\u2019s a big, mean looking bear, but, heh, one of the other bears watching this happen looks kind of traumatized. Nice.<br /> <br /> Paraphrasing, the next section says, \u201cPick some Intimacies, in ways we are not going to explain now!\u201d All righty. Finally, pick a Limit Trigger \u2013 not a break, just a trigger \u2013 and spend some bonus points.<br /> <br /> Hi, bonus points. No, didn\u2019t miss you. *starts houserule list*<br /> <br /> We get final calculations: motes, Willpower, health, etc. An earlier section clarified that \u201cdots\u201d are permanent ratings, while \u201cpoints\u201d are expended over time\u2026 but that verbiage doesn\u2019t seem to show up in the rest of the chapter. We don\u2019t see Willpower points mentioned, and I can\u2019t image motes are now called \u201cmote points.\u201d<br /> <br /> Speaking of motes, the Essence pool calculations are\u2026 kind of arbitrary looking. Like, (Essence x 7) + 26 \u2013 where does that number come from? (Well, from 2e, but at least there it was sort of justified \u2013 why that exact calculation?<br /> <br /> We get alternate chargen for mortals and experienced Solars, which, cool. You are <i>not</i> able to buy Essence up with bonus points this time around \u2013 that\u2019s a big change. One more piece of art, and\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026 is there a lot more European-looking art this time? Like, the Abyssals have a guy in full plate armor; this picture has two dudes who look very much like standard knights defending a castle. It just feels a little more\u2026 traditional fantasy trappings, I guess, and less of Exalted\u2019s usual flavorings.<br /> <br /> Also, there are a <i>lot</i> of pictures where the Exalted are just kind of standing around. Bear-shredding lady is one of the first big counterexamples to that.<br /> <br /> We get an example of chargen, which is nice, and which takes three pages to get through. This, uh, this is not going to be any quicker than it was in past editions, is it? Might want to plan 3-4 hours for when you go to run chargen.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the chapter! Notably absent, relative to last edition: <i>Motivations</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>The Good:</i> Cool Liminal fiction. Clear, straightforward character creation, backed by examples, even if most of the things we\u2019re messing with aren\u2019t really explained yet. Bear-shredding lady.<br /> <i>The Bad:</i> Some of the art and font choices continue to not impress \u2013 too much brown, too many ambiguous characters. Give me some color, guys!<br /> <i>The Ugly</i>: The chargen minigame looks <i>better</i> \u2013 that is, absent some of its most egregious offenders \u2013 but I\u2019d bet you can still rack up 50-100 XP of discrepancy without even trying. Hard to say for sure yet, though \u2013 there\u2019s no sign of an XP table to help guide you through that decision.<br /> <br /> Next up: &quot;Chapter 4: Traits!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-23-2015, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:52:30-07:00","id":720254,"title":"","content":"CHAPTER 4: TRAITS<br /> <br /> Prince Diamond is up! And negotiating with a river god, via some pretty straightforward, \u201cWell, have fun dealing with the Immaculates!\u201d trickery. Which feels like the kind of thing a player might do in game, but also\u2026 I dunno. I\u2019m not super-impressed with Diamond\u2019s uber-negotiation skills, but that's pretty petty - it's a very serviceable fiction.<br /> <br /> Although, do Exalts deal with normal mortals at all? The first fiction had a Solar interact with two Dragon-Blooded, a Sidereal, and a god. Novio Claro doesn\u2019t really interact with anyone, but she clarifies that the guy she slips past is a Dragon-Blooded, I think. Seven Devil Clever talks to a Lunar named Mangler, accompanied by some ape-men. Echoing Breath fought with ghosts, and the ghosts <i>of Exalts</i> at that. Now we have Prince Diamond, whose companions are a wolf-man and a god.<br /> <br /> If I\u2019m reading Exalted for the first time, this is the point where I start to think, \u201cOh, okay, so <i>mortals don\u2019t matter</i>. Gotcha.\u201d And I\u2019m pretty sure that\u2019s not what the authors have said they were going for.<br /> <br /> Anyway, actual chapter. We open with a summary of what the chapter will be\u2026 and two more typos.<br /> <br /> The rules on the Great Curse summarize that you gain Limit for acting against Intimacies. Great, guys, but I still don\u2019t know what a \u201cMajor Intimacy\u201d is \u2013 maybe that should come first? The rules also reference \u201cgaining one point of Limit for each success,\u201d but we don\u2019t have any idea how die rolls work yet. The Curse explicitly only erupts during dramatically appropriate moments, at ST\u2019s discretion. Actually, for that matter, the form the Break takes is <i>also</i> ST\u2019s discretion. This feels a little bit like the game is saying, \u201cDo the thing that messes your player up in a baaaaad way,\u201d which seems kind of\u2026 group-tension-inducing? At least when the Break is predetermined, you get the poison for which you signed up. On the other hand, this should produce more narratively-appropriate breaks\u2026 it\u2019s a mixed bag. Edit: And a few pages later, we get a sidebar that says, roughly \u201cOkay, but Storytellers, don\u2019t be a jerk about this; don\u2019t try to invalidate the character.\u201d Which is good\u2026 but we\u2019re also told to choose moments and breaks that are, basically, maximally disruptive. This feels like a hard line to walk.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a lot more unexplained verbiage here \u2013 Defining Intimacies, points of Willpower, unacceptable influence, Resolve. This section really feels like it needs to come later.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m at about seven typos so far this chapter, and we\u2019re about three pages in; about five of those are words broken across lines without hyphens. This is the winner so far.<br /> <br /> Limit breaks can end prematurely if something story-critical happens (i.e., your allies get attacked while you\u2019re sulking in your tent). That\u2019s a good thing to note explicitly.<br /> <br /> Full-page spread: Volfer! And his\u2026 shadowy cloud-sword-thing. Volfer looks kind of\u2026 squnched. Like, he\u2019s bent over, crouching, reaching back for his sword \u2013 I dunno, doesn\u2019t do anything for me. He\u2019s <i>still not doing anything</i>, which is beginning to become a theme in the art.<br /> <br /> The Dawns led the Exalted against \u201cthe might of the Undersea,\u201d among other things. Hm. There\u2019s a section here on \u201cAnima effects\u201d\u2026 which is just a pointer to p. 175. I'd vote for just cutting the section if it isn\u2019t going to say anything.<br /> <br /> Perfect Soul (and the Zeniths, natch): better picture, but, like, why is she a Zenith? What about this image conveys that to me?<br /> <br /> Shen! Shen? We haven\u2019t seen much of him yet \u2013 the Sig Twilight is\u2026 well, okay, he\u2019s Doctor Strange. He\u2019s got the beard, he\u2019s got the face, the robes, the popped collar, and an extra glowing eye hovering in front of him. He\u2019s <i>very clearly a Twilight</i>, which is great, but the homage is a little too spot-on.<br /> <br /> Novia! Also has black smoke behind her. Which makes better sense for a Night, but when she and Volfer <i>both</i> have that, it sort of gives a weird association. Novia\u2019s pretty ripped, here.<br /> <br /> Prince Diamond! Again, could be any caste; the associations are just not strongly conveyed for any of the sigs except Shen and maybe Volfer. The actual text descriptions are good, but I think those may also be lifted from 2e in places \u2013 not sure.<br /> <br /> New section \u2013\u201cdttributes.\u201d No, hang on, \u201cAttributes\u201d \u2013 the font continues to vex. Manipulation is \u201clying + trying to coax out a specific response different from your own feelings,\u201d which seems like a broad enough distinction; it also handles staying composed, via whatever \u201cGuile\u201d is.<br /> <br /> Picture of a lady punching a chariot! The chariot itself looks good \u2013 it\u2019s exploded into bits and flinders \u2013 but the lady doesn\u2019t have any real sense of action \u2013 she just looks sort of posed in front of it. She\u2019s also glowing purple \u2013 which, maybe it\u2019s good to have some more diversity in anima banners, but it\u2019d be nice to see more people actually glowing <i>gold</i>.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, you can take a 5,\u201d says the sidebar. Well, thanks? I plan to take <i>as many of them as I can</i>, because that\u2019s the XP-efficient thing to do in the system you\u2019ve provided, but this is better than some WoD-style tsk-tsking.<br /> <br /> Most soldiers have two dots of a relevant fighty Ability. Well.<br /> <br /> Ability descriptions call out which ones are important in combat \u2013 good! \u2013 but <i>don\u2019t have example Specialties</i>. What the heck? We\u2019ve gotten one sidebar on the subject; given that everyone\u2019s supposed to start with <i>four</i>, some examples would be nice.<br /> <br /> Crafting! Crafting is now\u2026 infinite subskills.<br /> <br /> Why.<br /> <br /> So, like, apparently \u201cWeapon forging\u201d and \u201cArmoring\u201d are sufficiently distinct that you need to buy <i>two completely independent Abilities</i> to cover them. Because, man, if there was one thing I loved in 2e, it was needing to buy a bunch of different elemental subskills, and now I can buy <i>fifty</i> of them. But hey, for <i>totally mundane</i> stuff, I might be able to hack a cross-skill applicability at +1 difficulty. Well.<br /> <br /> P. 153 and ahahahahaha, I take it all back, all the art up until now has been fine. <i>This</i> is bad art \u2013 Chompy hiding under the cake table. Or, well, a mannequin of Chompy hiding under the cake table.<br /> <br /> Lore has sub-fields of expertise, which I guess makes sense, but stops short of Craft\u2019s\u2026 thing.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts! Okay, finally some details. MA is an Ability, but you have to have a Merit before you can take it. Each MA has its own Ability, raised independently. That\u2019s\u2026 going to be a lot of XP.<br /> <br /> Socialize is an influence-generating Ability now, which is kind of different; it still has its \u201cRead the room\u201d features from 2e, though.<br /> <br /> Up next: Merits!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-23-2015, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:17:04-07:00","id":720725,"title":"","content":"So merits are a mix of Backgrounds and\u2026 well, merits, now. In contrast to some of my \u201cSolars who don\u2019t do anything\u201d critiques, the next page has a lady god-king who is pretty clearly lording it up \u2013 possibly Perfected Soul? Good on you, lady \u2013 rock your giant dragon-lion throne thing.<br /> <br /> Merits are divided into chargen-only, purchasable post-chargen, and only earned through story progression. That makes sense \u2013 Gills probably shouldn\u2019t be a spontaneous 6 XP purchase.<br /> <br /> Merit dots have a scaling cost, which is a little funny; if you buy a merit that\u2019s two dots <i>only</i>, it\u2019s 6 XP, but to buy a merit that has 1- and 2-dot ratings is 9 (3 for the first dot, 6 for the second). This causes some odd outcomes; Mighty Thew is a 1, 2, and 3-dot merit, while Pain Tolerance is a 4-dot-only merit. To get Mighty Thews to 3 costs 3 BP or 18 XP; to get Pain Tolerance costs 4 BP or 12 XP. I\u2019m curious on the logic in not just making it a flat 3XP/dot.<br /> <br /> This is a big group of merits! Which is cool, though I wish it was a little easier to pick the important ones \u2013 Artifact, Resources, etc. \u2013 out from, like, \u201cChameleon.\u201d That was one advantage of putting Merits in a separate category, I guess.<br /> <br /> Daiklaves and the like are automatically three dots or more; higher level artifacts get Evocations. Gotta say, Evocations are one of the coolest ideas to come out of this edition so far, and this seems like a natural way to structure their access.<br /> <br /> Command allows you to adjust slider bars on your troops\u2019 numbers vs. skill, but nothing on their magicalness \u2013 which makes complete sense, but I have a player who really wants a unit of ghost soldiers, and I\u2019m not sure how to ballpark that.<br /> <br /> Cult gives free Willpower instead of free motes now, which is cool. Willpower is supposed to be a lot scarcer this edition, so that\u2019s probably a much bigger bonus than it would have been in 2e.<br /> <br /> Demesnes are simplified \u2013 there are only two settings, rather than a gradation of five. You have a big demesne or a little one, basically; big ones are better for use as a \u201csorcerous means.\u201d Edit: Actually having a hearthstone is a separate merit, though apparently some demesnes can generate hearthstones. Edit Edit: Or you can take the Manse background, which gives you the benefit of <i>both</i>. Bweh?<br /> <br /> Familiar caps out at 3, and Familiar 3 gets you a t-rex. Half the fanbase immediately declares \u201cTHERE\u2019S MY NEXT CHARACTER.\u201d<br /> <br /> A <i>lot</i> of these merits feel like additional specialties \u2013 \u201c+1 die in [narrow circumstances].\u201d That feels kind of\u2026 bloat-y, to me, though I don\u2019t know as it actually hurts anything.<br /> <br /> Language is a merit! That\u2019s a <i>really</i> good change. And ha, Mnemon has developed a super-poetic lyrical language that\u2019s <i>also</i> a 1984 NuSpeak-style \u201cThere is no way to say THE DRAGON BLOODED ARE JERKS in this language.\u201d That\u2019s a fabulous touch.<br /> <br /> Just being able to buy a martial art costs a 4-dot merit. Then you have to buy the ability. That\u2019s a heck of a barrier to entry \u2013 to what end, I wonder?<br /> <br /> I do not understand the conversion rates under Resources. The conversion rate seems to be 1 talent = 8000 koku, <i>except</i> in four dots, where 4-6 talents is 16k-50k koku.<br /> <br /> We get a range of flaws, which do not generate bonus points (good!) but can be used to earn \u201csolar experience,\u201d which is currently undefined, if they cause you problems. That sounds like a reasonable way to go.<br /> <br /> You can spend Willpower points to raise your Defense by 1! That was a point of confusion in 2e \u2013 it\u2019s nice to have it spelled out. Sleep gets you a flat point of Willpower \u2013 no more Conviction min-maxing, hooray!<br /> <br /> Okay, finally some explanation of Intimacies. Intimacies are either <i>Ties</i>, links to people or places or ideas, or <i>Principles</i>, which are more like statements of belief. \u201cMy wife (affection)\u201d is a Tie; \u201cNobody calls me chicken\u201d is a principle. Intimacies also have a strength: Minor, Major, or Defining. Some Charms apparently power up with a supporting Intimacy. These are cool ideas, and look like the foundation of a good system.<br /> <br /> \u2026 The next page has a sidebar tut-tutting at people who try to game the Intimacy system, which rankles me a bit. \u201cYour Intimacies are too powerful,\u201d just seems like an ugly position to argue over.<br /> <br /> Bottom of the page has an example health track. Not sure whether I like it \u2013 it\u2019s flexible, but with all the health levels on the same line, I\u2019ll have to completely rewrite the thing whenever I gain a new -0. The example is welcome, anyway.<br /> <br /> Characters recover motes at 5/round in combat, or 5/hour out of combat. That creates some odd incentives. The anima banner goes up one level per five motes of Peripheral spent \u201cin an instant,\u201d which is waaaaaaaaaaaaaay simpler than 2e.<br /> <br /> Good use of bold in this section \u2013 in all sincerity; it calls attention to some of the more critical points well.<br /> <br /> New anima powers! Dawns can scare zombies, heh, recover more \u201cInitiative,\u201d and can reset what\u2019s described as something like D&amp;D4\u2019s encounter powers. That\u2019s cool. Zeniths feel the emotions of the deceased, burn creatures of darkness (which are currently undefined), and command spirits. Twilights gain \u201cfive Hardness,\u201d play Pokemon with spirits, and gain a \u201cpeace out\u201d power. Nights can auto-dampen Essence expenditures so they don\u2019t add to the anima \u2013 nice \u2013 make good Stealth rolls, and can conceal their identities perfectly. The Eclipse\u2026 huh. The Eclipse Oath causes a \u201cterrible curse,\u201d of undefined effect; Eclipse charmshare is restricted to \u201cspirits, Fair Folk, and similar supernatural beings.\u201d<br /> <br /> Experience points are, um, <i>really terribly formatted</i> right now \u2013 the column breaks are completely wrong. \u201cSolar experience,\u201d which is capitalized more-or-less at random, is awarded for developing an Intimacy or acting in a caste-appropriate way; you spend it on anything that\u2019s <i>not</i> Solar Charms. I\u2019m hardly the first to observe this, but that\u2019s kind of a backwards naming convention, there. I\u2019m pretty sure this is another houserule, for me: I\u2019d rather all my players keep the same XP totals, so I\u2019ll track a group bonus, rather than a player-by-player one.<br /> <br /> Essence 4+ is noted as extremely rare among centuries-old Celestials, which is a little offputting; I understand the idea that \u201cIchigo\u2019s growth curve is not normal for a Soul Reaper,\u201d but I\u2019d rather not have my hero triumph over the Dragon-Blooded by virtue of his mountains of superior XP. It\u2019s nice to have an explicit statement, even if I disagree with the one made, though.<br /> <br /> Essence raises go Legends of the Wulin style \u2013 that is, you can\u2019t spend XP to get them, but they come automatically as you spend XP \u2013 which is <i>great</i>. That\u2019s a really excellent improvement.<br /> <br /> <i>The Good:</i> All components of chargen covered; several new, cool ideas. Some more dynamic art as the chapter went on, which was nice.<br /> <i>The Bad:</i> Definitely the worst-edited of the chapters so far \u2013 many, many words broken across lines; a fair number of typos or extra spaces; and at least one table that\u2019s badly misformatted.<br /> <i>The Ugly:</i> Chompy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oof. Finished. Quick question: is this at all useful to anyone?<br /> <br /> Up next(?): \u201cChapter 5: Systems and Conflict.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:29:39-07:00","id":720780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720725#post720725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oof. Finished. Quick question: is this at all useful to anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite the fact that I own the book, I find it very useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:32:55-07:00","id":720785,"title":"","content":"Yeah! It's fun to read and cool to see different story perspectives on the whole book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:45:41-07:00","id":720809,"title":"","content":"I'm curious what people think of the overall contents of the new Resources merit, since I (arguably over)wrote it this time. The currency numbers per dot are, I believe, the same as they ever were, but I spent a lot of time working out what they (were always apparently meant to) mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:49:42-07:00","id":720817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720809#post720809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what people think of the overall contents of the new Resources merit, since I (arguably over)wrote it this time. The currency numbers per dot are, I believe, the same as they ever were, but I spent a lot of time working out what they (were always apparently meant to) mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, my favorite part about Resources now is actually that you don't NEED it for your character to start with whatever mundane equipment he needs for his concept. XD<br /> <br /> EDIT: In all seriousness though, they seem good to me. About the only thing that kind of threw me at first when it comes to economy is getting used to the idea that a dirham was MORE than a dinar, not less (as it was both historically and in 2e).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","user":"CycloneJoker","date":". 10-23-2015, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:51:54-07:00","id":720829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720817#post720817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, my favorite part about Resources now is actually that you don't NEED it for your character to start with whatever mundane equipment he needs for his concept. XD</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean that even if you don't have dots left over to put into Resources, you aren't automatically destitute, homeless, and dressed in rags?<br /> Excellent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:52:01-07:00","id":720832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720809#post720809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what people think of the overall contents of the new Resources merit, since I (arguably over)wrote it this time. The currency numbers per dot are, I believe, the same as they ever were, but I spent a lot of time working out what they (were always apparently meant to) mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! Can you clarify what the ratio of talents to koku is supposed to be? Resources 3 and 5 both seem okay, assuming it's 1:8000, but 4 seems... off.<br /> <br /> It does kind of feel like a little more detail than most games are going to need, honestly - like, I don't think I've ever gone into more specific detail than &quot;You throw down a handful of jade&quot; - but I don't think it's bad to have a clearly developed currency system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:55:34-07:00","id":720860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720829#post720829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean that even if you don't have dots left over to put into Resources, you aren't automatically destitute, homeless, and dressed in rags?<br /> Excellent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Within reason, you can have appropriate gear to your concept. Your former soldier probably doesn't have a wagon full of looted swag and fine horses, but he can still have his weapon, his armor, a few personal effects, and a horse if he was--for example--a Medoan rider or something.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Though it should be noted that you're still flat friggin' broke if you have Resources 0, it's just that you're not completely bereft of any worldy possessions anymore. Unless that's what you want, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","user":"CycloneJoker","date":". 10-23-2015, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T16:00:49-07:00","id":720870,"title":"","content":"Resources 0 isn't necessarily flat broke (although it does encompass that), it just means that you don't have spare money lying around the place. Having a resources rating at all means you're unusually wealthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":3559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","user":"Lanaya","date":". 10-23-2015, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T16:04:27-07:00","id":720877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720870#post720870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resources 0 isn't actually flat broke (although it does encompass that), just that you don't have spare money lying around the place. Having a resources rating at all means you're unusually wealthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. It can represent having JUST enough money that it all goes into your day-to-day survival and lifestyle with bupkus left over. Basically, you no longer have to factor in your concept when picking a Resources level; it's all about how much excess disposable income you want your character to have. It's a fucking genius design decision and I applaud the developers for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T16:15:44-07:00","id":720898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720725#post720725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oof. Finished. Quick question: is this at all useful to anyone?<br /> <br /> Up next(?): \u201cChapter 5: Systems and Conflict.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, actually, really useful for me, because your commentary keeps me reading through some of the dryer parts of the text where I have a tendency to skim and shouldn't! So thanks for using humor to keep me on task through this undertaking. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T17:08:57-07:00","id":721160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720809#post720809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what people think of the overall contents of the new Resources merit, since I (arguably over)wrote it this time. The currency numbers per dot are, I believe, the same as they ever were, but I spent a lot of time working out what they (were always apparently meant to) mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my favorite little changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T17:15:47-07:00","id":721170,"title":"","content":"(Thanks for the feedback, all - I'll keep going when I can, then. Feel free to jump in if you want to argue and/or want me to go back to something. In full disclosure, I've seen most of this text before, but I'm doing my best to approach it fresh.)<br /> <br /> Chapter 5 has probably my favorite first-paragraph-of-a-fic yet: \u201cHer mother always said that rain was the tears of Danaa\u2019d \u2013 one droplet for each transgression against the Immaculate Philosophy. It had been raining more, lately.\u201d I don\u2019t know why that grabs me in a way most of the others don\u2019t, but it does.<br /> <br /> The rest of the fic is fairly solid. It\u2019s a Dragon-Blooded fighting a Solar, from the DB\u2019s point of view, which is a nice touch. (It even has some mortals in it. They promptly die.) My only beef with it is that the Solar seems\u2026 well, kind of like a poncy idiot; he throws a bunch of mortals at an Exalt without a second thought while he poses in the rain. And then, at the end, I think he\u2019s meant to come across as kind of sympathetic or appealing\u2026 but it\u2019s a little too late. For me, anyway; that critique aside, I think this is the best one so far. Art on the next page is a fight in the rain, heck yeah, but does not help me see the Solar as a serious figure with whom I would consider teaming up \u2013 he\u2019s got kind of a Young Michael Jackson thing going on.<br /> <br /> We get three rules:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Golden Rule: If you don\u2019t like it, change it.</li> <li>Orichalcum Rule: If the rules output nonsense, ignore them.</li> <li>Storyteller\u2019s Rule (er, what?): If the player pulls shenanigans, stop him.</li> </ol>I think my fondness for these rules is going to be inversely proportionate to how often the system is likely to need them. We\u2019ll see!<br /> <br /> The rules advise you to ease into some of the complexity, which is sounding like a good idea. There\u2019s a really quite nice glossary of combat terms, and \u2013<br /> <br /> - wait a sec \u2013<br /> <br /> - yes, they have <i>quite successfully</i> disambiguated the terms \u201cround\u201d (everybody goes once!), \u201cturn\u201d (you go once!), and \u201caction\u201d (you do one thing on your turn!). For those struck down in the 2e What Does Action Mean Anyway War of \u201907, we pray; for everyone else, huzzah!<br /> <br /> \u201cTraits\u201d get explained again, which is forgivable redundancy for a new audience. Exalted use a different difficulty scale than normal people, which suggests that a Diff 1 roll for an Exalt or other hero would be, Diff ~3 for anyone else. (How does that fit with most professionals having Ability 2? Is that only true for Heroic Professionals?) <i>Removing an appendix</i> is apparently Diff 1, which seems\u2026 low? I\u2019m not really sold on this difficulty curve in general; seems like almost every task is going to end up in the Diff 1-2 range, which seems awfully trivial. Maybe that\u2019s the intent? But then why bother to have high stats in anything you aren\u2019t rolling against another hero? We\u2019ll see, I guess.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s another one of the preview art pieces \u2013 Solar dude walks into a bar looking smug. His sword\u2019s handle still looks awfully short to me, but Sword Expert Guy I am <i>decidedly not</i>.<br /> <br /> The rolling mechanics is basically the same as Ex2, thus far. Botches are still around; it would have been nice to have a call-out as to how they interact with Willpower. (The answer appears to be \u201cYou can spend WP and still botch.\u201d)<br /> <br /> Stunt time! (Obligatory: <i>still hate the heading font.</i>) Overlong descriptions are not stunts. <a href=\"https://&quot;http://www.megatokyo.com/index.php?strip_id=750\u201d\" target=\"_blank\">Thank heavens.</a> Stunts are still one, two, or three \u201cpoint\u201d \u2013 which seems like a poor choice of words, since \u201cpoint\u201d is a system term with an unrelated meaning. (Someone suggested Minor, Major, or Defining, which seems like a good fit.) Stunt die bonuses are doubled \u2013 two dice for a one point, or a +1 bonus a static value like defense. That\u2019s nice \u2013 it\u2019s statistical parity on both sides. Higher level stunts mix dice and successes \u2013 to repeat a question I saw elsewhere, why do this? Why not just give 1/2/3 successes on both offense and defense? That\u2019d be cleaner and fit better with the \u201cone point\u201d notation, in addition to resolving faster.<br /> <br /> Anyway, one point stunts are the new \u201cYou can get this every turn,\u201d but they give nothing (other than dice). You should get one two-point stunt every couple of scenes, netting 1wp each time, and one guy might get <i>one</i> three-point stunt in a night, for 2wp. That is a <i>much</i> more restricted rate of WP gain than 2e, given that 2e\u2019s rate was close to \u201cAm I taking an action? Then I\u2019m recovering Willpower.\u201d<br /> <br /> I hate this font. Have I mentioned that? Here\u2019s a new reason: I\u2019m pretty sure this page has a mix of headings and sub-headings, and I cannot, visually, tell which is which. I <i>assume</i> \u201cBonuses and Penalties\u201d is a sub-heading of \u201cAction Complications,\u201d because otherwise the latter isn\u2019t really a section at all.<br /> <br /> Hm. Penalties are presented as a way of working around fixed difficulties \u2013 i.e., shooting an apple in a windstorm gets a higher difficulty, but shooting an Abyssal during a windstorm gets a penalty. That seems like a bit of a kludge. My experience is that no one in 2e ever used non-wound penalties for anything; it\u2019ll be interested to see if that holds true in 3e.<br /> <br /> Extended rolls! If you make an extend roll at difficulty 3, and roll four successes, you get two net towards your extended roll. That seems\u2026 kinda confusing, doesn\u2019t it? Like, wouldn\u2019t it be clearer to be able to just subtract the difficulty?<br /> <br /> In an opposed roll, in case of a tie, \u201cThe Storyteller awards victory to the player with the best stunt.\u201d So\u2026 that\u2019s either judging between the player and himself, or two players, right? Neither of those is a place where I want to say, \u201cOh, yeah, Bob\u2019s stunt was definitely worse than the other guy\u2019s\u201d \u2013 I think I might rely on the Legends of the Wulin rule (\u201cin case of a tie, the passive actor loses \u2013 the sneaky guy goes unnoticed, etc.\u201d).<br /> <br /> (I haven\u2019t mentioned backgrounds much, but this one is a little distracting \u2013 it\u2019s a brush-stroke-y thing, but it\u2019s got what looks like some bad compression artifacts in places.)<br /> <br /> Combat time! Okay, micro-survey: you have an Initiative rating, which is basically \u201cHow well did you roll at the start of the battle?\u201d That\u2019s pretty standard \u2013 but you have two kinds of attack, and one of them (the <i>Withering</i> attack) only deals damage to your Initiative. It steals it, more accurately; if you take X damage, you lose X Initiative, and the other guy gains X+1. Sooner or later, he throws out a <i>Decisive</i> attack, spending all his current Initiative in an attempt to damage your actual health. I\u2019m curious how well characters will be able to recover fatal levels of Initiative if the initial exchange fails to do the job \u2013 if everyone rolls well, that\u2019s a lot of Init in the collective pool to start, but a bunch of it will disappear the first time someone connects with a big Decisive.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you can push someone into negative Init, and they recover from that back to 3 after a couple of turns; maybe that compensates for it somewhat.<br /> <br /> This is a bunch of unique stuff, but I think it\u2019s explained relatively clearly, to the game\u2019s credit \u2013 all this takes maybe a page to summarize, though there\u2019s no detailed step-by-step progression yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-10-2015, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T17:35:04-07:00","id":721227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=721170#post721170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m curious how well characters will be able to recover fatal levels of Initiative if the initial exchange fails to do the job \u2013 if everyone rolls well, that\u2019s a lot of Init in the collective pool to start, but a bunch of it will disappear the first time someone connects with a big Decisive.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you can push someone into negative Init, and they recover from that back to 3 after a couple of turns; maybe that compensates for it somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the fact that a successful Withering gets you the initiative you stole <i>plus one</i> is an important (pre-Charms) factor here in increasing available initiative; two opponents who trade equal successful withering attacks both wind up at +1 initiative compared to where they started the round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T17:45:53-07:00","id":721262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=721227#post721227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect the fact that a successful Withering gets you the initiative you stole <i>plus one</i> is an important (pre-Charms) factor here in increasing available initiative; two opponents who trade equal successful withering attacks both wind up at +1 initiative compared to where they started the round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, but that's going to take a while to add up - statistically, you need ~18i to deal 7 HLs, and building that back up at +1 per successful hit is likely to take a while. It definitely <i>helps</i>; I'm curious whether it's enough.<br /> <br /> Smacking people into negatives is the other big factor here; my suspicion is it may be the larger contributor on average, but that's just a suspicion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:14:56-07:00","id":721329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=721170#post721170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stunt time! (Obligatory: <i>still hate the heading font.</i>) Overlong descriptions are not stunts. <a href=\"https://\u201d &#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.megatokyo.com/index.php?strip_id=750\u201d]Thank</a> heavens.[/url] Stunts are still one, two, or three \u201cpoint\u201d \u2013 which seems like a poor choice of words, since \u201cpoint\u201d is a system term with an unrelated meaning. (Someone suggested Minor, Major, or Defining, which seems like a good fit.) Stunt die bonuses are doubled \u2013 two dice for a one point, or a +1 bonus a static value like defense. That\u2019s nice \u2013 it\u2019s statistical parity on both sides. Higher level stunts mix dice and successes \u2013 to repeat a question I saw elsewhere, why do this? Why not just give 1/2/3 successes on both offense and defense? That\u2019d be cleaner and fit better with the \u201cone point\u201d notation, in addition to resolving faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would also make botching impossible, and allow you to automatically bypass all difficulty 1 actions even if you only had one die to work with, effectively removing difficulty 1 and difficulty 0 are usable concepts. Neither of those are desirable things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:18:55-07:00","id":721338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=721227#post721227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect the fact that a successful Withering gets you the initiative you stole <i>plus one</i> is an important (pre-Charms) factor here in increasing available initiative; two opponents who trade equal successful withering attacks both wind up at +1 initiative compared to where they started the round.</div> </div> </div> </div>We did a LOT of tweaking during the playtesting to assuage my fears about Initiative draining out of the combat economy too fast, leaving people with mostly empty pools flailing at eachother in near-crash states and taking forever to get enough resources to actually throw a useful <b>decisive</b> attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:19:47-07:00","id":721343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=721262#post721262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely, but that's going to take a while to add up - statistically, you need ~18i to deal 7 HLs, and building that back up at +1 per successful hit is likely to take a while. It definitely <i>helps</i>; I'm curious whether it's enough.<br /> <br /> Smacking people into negatives is the other big factor here; my suspicion is it may be the larger contributor on average, but that's just a suspicion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Initiative Break bonus you're about to run into also helps pump fresh Init into the economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:41:55-07:00","id":721391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=721329#post721329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would also make botching impossible, and allow you to automatically bypass all difficulty 1 actions even if you only had one die to work with, effectively removing difficulty 1 and difficulty 0 are usable concepts. Neither of those are desirable things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. As written, it's ambiguous to me whether bonus successes prevent botches - the book says &quot;if <i>the roll</i> generates no successes,&quot; which can be legitimately parsed a couple different ways. My default parsing was that this excluded bonus successes; that's wrong? (Same question applies to spending Willpower, obvs.)<br /> <br /> I see your point on the rest, but I guess I'm not really bothered by a stunting Exalt auto-succeeding at diff 1 rolls; again, a point of Willpower would do that for you, too, right? As written, a one-point stunt still gives you almost a 90% chance of passing, and a two-point stunt (if you can manage it - granting that they're much less frequent) will still give you a guarantee.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Initiative Break bonus you're about to run into also helps pump fresh Init into the economy </div> </div> </div>That's a really good point - thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-23-2015, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:55:52-07:00","id":721405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=721391#post721391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. As written, it's ambiguous to me whether bonus successes prevent botches - the book says &quot;if <i>the roll</i> generates no successes,&quot; which can be legitimately parsed a couple different ways. My default parsing was that this excluded bonus successes; that's wrong? (Same question applies to spending Willpower, obvs.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Spending Willpower would guarantee you got at least one success, thus negating the possibility of a botch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see your point on the rest, but I guess I'm not really bothered by a stunting Exalt auto-succeeding at diff 1 rolls; again, a point of Willpower would do that for you, too, right? </div> </div> </div>Yes. A point of Willpower is a significant expenditure of resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As written, a one-point stunt still gives you almost a 90% chance of passing, and a two-point stunt (if you can manage it - granting that they're much less frequent) will still give you a guarantee. </div> </div> </div>Two point stunts are a non-trivial effort. I find the difference between &quot;probably going to to make it&quot; and &quot;don't even bother picking up the dice&quot; to be enormous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:57:53-07:00","id":721409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=721405#post721405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spending Willpower would guarantee you got at least one success, thus negating the possibility of a botch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. For whatever it's worth, I find &quot;the roll generates&quot; to be a source of ambiguity there; I wouldn't have said that the success from Willpower was generated by the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-23-2015, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T19:05:21-07:00","id":721415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=721170#post721170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Art on the next page is a fight in the rain, heck yeah, but does not help me see the Solar as a serious figure with whom I would consider teaming up \u2013 he\u2019s got kind of a Young Michael Jackson thing going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's Michael Jackson vs. <a href=\"http://metalgear.wikia.com/wiki/The_Boss\" target=\"_blank\">The Boss</a>. I can dig it.<br /> <br /> And, unsurprisingly, I'm enjoying reading your commentary. Plus, since I'm unlikely to have a chance to play anytime soon, I'm having a hard time working up the motivation to just read it through, so you're saving me some of the trouble of finding the things that have changed since 2nd ed. So, thanks for that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T19:16:28-07:00","id":721434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720809#post720809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what people think of the overall contents of the new Resources merit, since I (arguably over)wrote it this time. The currency numbers per dot are, I believe, the same as they ever were, but I spent a lot of time working out what they (were always apparently meant to) mean.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My group and I were just talking about this. Comparing to the resources writeup in 2E, the 2E version felt like it was much more specific in telling you what you have, where the 3E version tells you what sort of people have this rating. We unanimously found the 3E version superior - knowing whether I have a second horse or how often, precisely, my family eats meat is far less important than knowing who my peers are and how my resource rating helps define how I fit into the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T19:35:04-07:00","id":721449,"title":"","content":"Ah, there\u2019s that step-by-step combat! So, interesting notes: Withering attacks benefit from your weapon; Decisive ones don\u2019t. (Withering Accuracy is going to be higher, presumably.) Defense is, as Holden has noted, a Difficulty rather than a penalty \u2013 in other words, offense breaks ties. Soak is useless against actual damaging attacks, which is\u2026 odd; Hardness applies <i>only</i> to Decisive attacks, but if successful it outright negates the attack. That\u2019s an oddly binary result in a system that otherwise is all about grades of damage \u2013 \u201cHow high does Hardness go?\u201d is going to be a question to watch.<br /> <br /> Ticks are still around\u2026 sort of; \u201cone tick\u201d is basically \u201cone Initiative number, when people with that Initiative act.\u201d There are some good call-outs on obvious glitch situations \u2013 someone\u2019s Initiative falling to such a point that they come up twice in a single round, for instance, does <i>not</i> mean they get to act twice.<br /> <br /> We get what looks like two art pieces showing the same scene, with Novia and the others standing over some kind of golem with a bunch of swords sticking out of him. Side note: I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve seen two pictures yet portray Volfer the same way, arm-shield-thing notwithstanding.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve critiqued some verbiage, so let me note that I like this: when you kick someone down to Init 0, you <i>Crash</i> them, and you get a bonus for doing so. On the other side, the bonus is called an \u201cInitiative Break bonus,\u201d which seems like an unnecessary extra term \u2013 why not just call it a \u201cCrash bonus?\u201d<br /> <br /> Crashing the guy who Crashed you gets a suite of bonuses, including an extra turn, but also a bit of rules complexity \u2013 I\u2019m curious whether people have seen this happen enough to make it worth the mental overhead.<br /> <br /> Parry looks poised to outperform Evasion in defense values \u2013 Parry can gain bonuses from gear, while Dodge only takes penalties. Onslaught penalties are back, but are now \u201c-1 for every attack made against you until your next turn,\u201d rather than being tracked separately for different characters. That\u2019s a nice simplification \u2013 and given the way Initiative values can swing around, you could potentially be sitting on a 2*(# attackers) Onslaught penalty. It\u2019s unclear from this description exactly when you begin suffering from the Onslaught penalty \u2013 it\u2019s presumably <i>not</i> applied to the attack generating the penalty, but the rules are unclear.<br /> <br /> Flurries are back! But in a very limited way: you can make two actions, with a penalty, but they can\u2019t both be attacks or both moves or etc. Attacking from range now requires an (unflurryable) Aim action, which is a pretty handy solution to the endless-kiting-archer problem.<br /> <br /> I keep seeing references to \u201cthreshold successes\u201d \u2013 has that been defined anywhere post-glossary? There, it\u2019s \u201cextra successes,\u201d which makes sense \u2013 but it\u2019s weird that that\u2019s not also the rule for extended actions. Anyway.<br /> <br /> We come to movement, and the idea of <i>range bands</i> \u2013 which are sort of narrative regions, it appears, sort of like LotW\u2019s zones. You measure distance in terms of how many bands someone is away from you. So much better than 2e\u2019s yards-based measurements? <i>So much better.</i><br /> <br /> Movement does this neat thing where you can move from one band to another reflexively, <i>unless</i> there are enemies in the band with you, and then it\u2019s a contested roll called a Disengage. If you get away, you get a free move the next time one of them gets back into your band. On the other hand, if you\u2019re charging somebody, you can choose to both Move and Rush, covering an extra band if you succeed on the contested roll (and again, moving an extra time the next time they try to move away). At a glance, combat movement seems to heavily favor closing in; an enemy approaching can both Move and Rush, while the guy moving away can only Disengage. (Disengaging also costs Initiative; Rushing doesn\u2019t.) I like that Dodge gets this other field of utility now \u2013 you <i>might actually roll that Ability</i> in this edition.<br /> <br /> Can I continue to make Disengage attempts while in the negatives? Presumably yes, but I don\u2019t see that the rules say one way or the other.<br /> <br /> We also bump into cover, which suggests an issue that\u2019s heretofore unmentioned: we need to track not only ranges, but also the relative direction to various combatants. My feel is that \u201cband\u201d isn\u2019t really the right word for what we\u2019re describing here \u2013 what we\u2019ve really got is some kind of narratively-defined space, of the \u201cbubbles connected by arrows on the map\u201d sort. If people are moving around relative to each other, it seems like anything else is going to be a bit nightmarish for tracking relative distances.<br /> <br /> We come at last to gambits. I <i>love</i> gambits; these are opportunities for you to cash in your Initiative to do any kind of weird, one-off thing you can think of. Disarms? God of War-style shenanigans? Shoving your enemy off a cliff? Heck yeah. Grapples?<br /> <br /> \u2026 Not that sure about grapples, honestly. If a brawler lands a Grapple on you \u2013 that\u2019s a Decisive hit, producing at least 2 Initiative successes \u2013 he starts a grapple. You roll (Strength + Brawl) to contest it, but heck, man, you\u2019re not a grappler \u2013 you fight with the sword. If you lose, and you will, he\u2019s going to get (1 + threshold successes) rounds of beating on you at Defense 0. It\u2019s not quite so bad as it was in 2e \u2013 you can still attack (at a penalty, against his normal Defense), and each attack or hit you make on him cuts the duration of the grapple \u2013 but in a one-on-one fight, it seems like you\u2019re still probably pretty dead. That\u2019s not bad, for an attack that can be reasonably fired off at 5i.<br /> <br /> You can also Distract the enemy, which basically means \u201cyou give some Initiative to an ally.\u201d Several people have tried to explain the benefits of Distract to me, and without Charms, it still seems pretty awfully limited.<br /> <br /> We get a Dresden-style \u201cInstead of dying, you can choose to absorb some damage by getting a hand chopped off,\u201d which is a great panic button for characters just a couple health levels over the line.<br /> <br /> \u201cAMMUNITION: There are two ways to track ammunition.\u201d I tend to favor \u201cDon\u2019t,\u201d but presumably this is for people who feel a need to do <i>something</i>.<br /> <br /> Clash attacks! So, this is cool. If you and someone else with the same Initiative swing at each other, you do the samurai thing where you both run past and then one of you falls over dead. Or, well: you both roll attacks, and the guy who rolls low gets hit. Pity the man who rolled a Decisive against your Withering strike, I guess; the loser also takes extra damage and loses a chunk of his Defense.<br /> <br /> Mounts look like a big deal: better movement, bonuses on the attack roll, bonus defense. Nice \u2013 horses were more liability than asset in 2e.<br /> <br /> We get <i>very detailed</i> rules for surprise. You\u2019re a lot worse off if you get completely bushwhacked than if you know there\u2019s a bad guy out there <i>somewhere</i>, and are just working on the \u201cBut where?\u201d part. (\u201cKeep walking\u201d seems like the optimal defense, in the latter situation \u2013 moving while stealthed is rough.) We get a big section \u2013 like, most of a page - on how to mechanically do the thing where you\u2019re interrogating the guy with a knife to his neck, which feels like overkill, but eh.<br /> <br /> Finally, we come to <i>uncountable damage:</i> for those occasions when Mount Metagalapa decides to sit on you. HGD, old buddy, are you still out there somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-23-2015, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T06:12:31-07:00","id":722756,"title":"","content":"<i>Battle groups</i> are the new mass combat system. We roll a bunch of fighters up into a glom; they only do Withering damage, but it rolls over into health track damage if you Crash (yikes!). Meanwhile, any Withering damage they take goes straight to their health track, but, (1) it\u2019s a big track, and (2) I hope they run out before you do. Battle groups can also effectively grapple you \u2013 at which point they\u2019re making Withering attacks at Defense 0 that roll over into your death. That\u2019s\u2026 ouch.<br /> <br /> (Here\u2019s a guy running through a burning hunting lodge, or something, carrying a kid. It\u2019s not bad, but why is it <i>here</i>?)<br /> <br /> Battle groups get nastier when they\u2019re being commanded by a leader \u2013 the leader\u2019s extra successes on a command roll translate into extra dice for the unit. (If I kill a legion\u2019s commander, can it immediately pop out another dude as the new commander? Does \u201cdefending yourself\u201d count as an action for which the unit gets extra dice \u2013 i.e., does its Defense go up?) It <i>appears</i> that splitting one battle group into several chunks will produce something that can murder the original \u2013 more attacks, more net health levels \u2013 and so, naturally, we get a sidebar sternly scolding us <i>not</i> to do that. Er, then shouldn\u2019t combining two groups produce a net gain of capability, rather than a net loss?<br /> <br /> We also get a section on generals trying to out-general each other, which basically comes down to, \u201cMake opposed Int+War rolls, high roller chooses one of these bonuses.\u201d<br /> <br /> Okay, social influence time. This also means we start getting definitions for some of those earlier terms \u2013 your <i>Resolve</i> is resistance to persuasion, and your <i>Guile</i> is your Ability to keep your feelings to yourself. Your Intimacies can boost your Resolve \u2013 the stronger the Intimacy, the more it boosts (or penalizes) your Resolve. The numbers for boosting and penalizing aren\u2019t equal, though, which is a little unfortunate.<br /> <br /> So, what can you do socially?<ul><li>You can <i>instill</i> Intimacies, adding or removing them from someone else \u2013 but if you want to buff an existing Intimacy, you have to have another Intimacy to support the effort. I <i>like</i> that \u2013 it encourages you to build supporting networks of belief.</li> <li>You can <i>persuade</i> them to take an action \u2013 but only if you\u2019ve built or discovered appropriate Intimacies first! A Minor Intimacy will get someone to inconvenience themselves; they\u2019ll give up their job for a Major; they\u2019ll face almost certain death for a Defining. Again, this is a really nice context-sensitive system.</li> <li>You can <i>bargain</i> or <i>threaten</i> them into taking some action, offering valuables or the threat of harm in lieu of an Intimacy.</li> <li>You can <i>inspire</i> them to be filled with an emotion, though you can\u2019t control what they do with that emotion.</li> <li>You can <i>read intentions</i> to suss out someone\u2019s motivations or Intimacies.</li> </ul>I really like that, in general \u2013 it feels like a broadly useful spectrum of actions that learns a lot from 2e\u2019s missteps. It\u2019s also complex enough that it\u2019s probably hiding some missteps of its own, but it <i>looks</i> good.<br /> <br /> Appearance still grants bonuses to social rolls, though it\u2019s scaled <i>way</i> back \u2013 you only gain it on offense, and based off the target\u2019s Resolve rather than their Appearance. That\u2019s nice, but you can also use Appearance as the base of a social roll, now \u2013 is there a concern here of double-dipping, or is it just expected that most rolls won\u2019t be able to use Appearance?<br /> <br /> You can still spend Willpower to shake off most social influence, which is good. Attempts to persuade you have a totally separate system \u2013 and honestly, this is the part I like least; it feels like a lot of complexity in a very small interaction. To shake off persuasion, you need a <i>second</i> Intimacy \u2013 not the one you used to defend, and not the one they used to attack. There\u2019s some weird interactions here; you might want to keep one of your best Intimacies back for use in \u201cshaking off,\u201d because the one you use for that has to be as strong as the one they\u2019re attacking with.<br /> <br /> We also get rules for re-persuading someone \u2013 broadly, it\u2019s harder to convince them after they\u2019ve been convinced once. This was a big hole in 2e, but I\u2019m not sure it\u2019s better now; as others have noted, there\u2019s some incentive here to persuade everyone in the party to do the-thing-they-were-going-to-do-anyway, because that makes them much more resistant to later persuasion. Which is a bit silly, but it works!<br /> <br /> Is that a Firefly shout-out? It looks like a Firefly shout-out. *approves*<br /> <br /> There follow the Million Specific Systems, which I\u2019m not going to try to summarize in detail here. We get some nice rules for Investigation, which clarify what the Storyteller should be telling a successful investigator \u2013 this is useful advice. We also get a pretty terrible picture of Volfer at a bar. What\u2019s happening here, anyway? Fata-Kun is clearly sitting; where are Volfer\u2019s legs? What\u2019s going on with the way the wall bends behind them? Who thought it was a good idea to draw a head with the topknot as the only visible feature? \u2026 Is that Peleps Deled with a moustache? Why is Fata-Kun drawn with fat black lines when Volfer and the rest aren\u2019t? <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pZEmFT6VxSw?t=50s\" target=\"_blank\">What's wrong with your faaaaace?</a><br /> <br /> Leadership! All right! Leadership rules from the guys who gave us the CRM system, who finally solved the \u201cBureaucracy doesn\u2019t do anything\u201d problem. Let\u2019s play god-kings, with some actual rules for the \u201cking\u201d part of that. Let\u2019s do this. The leadership rules are\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026 uh\u2026<br /> <br /> Okay, the Leadership system in its entirety is: Does the player have the stuff he needs to do a task? Then he can do it! But maybe something bad will happen, like a war or some assassins or something. And\u2026 that\u2019s it. That\u2019s how we\u2019re supporting playing god-kings: \u201cMake something up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Did I mention these rules take four pages?<br /> <br /> <i>Anyway.</i> There\u2019s a sidebar on social penalties, which feels about ten pages out of place, and some middling art, and then we switch topics. Feats of Strength now have prerequisite Strength as well as minimum successes \u2013 wonder what\u2019s the motivation there? We get environmental penalties ranging from \u201cit\u2019s too hot\u201d (1B/hour) to \u201cAdorjan hates you\u201d (4A/round). Falling damage is\u2026 pretty darn fatal; if you fall two range bands, you\u2019re looking at 7+ levels of damage. The rules advise you to let characters stunt to avoid falls \u2013 well, yeah, given that they\u2019re otherwise going to explode, I bet so. (How far is a Medium range fall, anyway?)<br /> <br /> Poison! So this should be interesting; 2e poisons were stupidly broken, tending to make every blow a potentially fatal strike. Here\u2026 interesting. Most combat-time poisons only do Initiative damage until you Crash, at which point they begin killing you. So what happens if someone poisons my drink with Arrow Frog Venom \u2013 that is, if I start suffering from it outside of combat? Poisons still inflict penalties on all die pools, though, which feels pretty crippling \u2013 but if you have to land a Decisive to inflict them, maybe that\u2019s not such a big deal. At a glance, Curare looks like the way to go \u2013 it\u2019s going to stick them with a -2 penalty that\u2019s likely to last the rest of the fight.<br /> <br /> (But really, why can I shrug off rattlesnake venom but take lethal from arsenic? Some of the choices here don\u2019t make immediate sense to me.)<br /> <br /> (The matching of relevant tables to their rules is not really ideal here; most things are ending up at least a page after the rules discussing them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T06:48:10-07:00","id":722797,"title":"","content":"This is quite useful Irked, you've pointed out several things I missed.<br /> <br /> Couple of things:\u200b<br /> 1) You said you were wandering how often people crash the person who crashed them. It seems to me so far that people get crashed then get back up by crashing someone else quite often, but it's rarely the person who crashed them (as he probably now has high initiative). But it did happen once (I think the Changing Moon was crashed, then the Full Moon knocked the enemy's initiative down to a low number, he missed his attack, then the Changing Moon crashed him).<br /> <br /> 2)You made a mistake in your description of Rush. You said if you win you get to move again, then once more if they move back. Actually, you don't immediately move an extra move (presumably you did the Rush after taking your reflexive move though), you just get to move for free if they move. I'm not sure if you get to do this an infinite amount of times (if they're able to move several times) or just once. Disengage specifies it only works once, Rush doesn't.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-24-2015, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T10:27:36-07:00","id":723537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=722797#post722797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is quite useful Irked, you've pointed out several things I missed.<br /> <br /> Couple of things:\u200b<br /> 1) You said you were wandering how often people crash the person who crashed them. It seems to me so far that people get crashed then get back up by crashing someone else quite often, but it's rarely the person who crashed them (as he probably now has high initiative). But it did happen once (I think the Changing Moon was crashed, then the Full Moon knocked the enemy's initiative down to a low number, he missed his attack, then the Changing Moon crashed him).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, okay. Did you find it natural to keep up with the rules for counter-crashing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2)You made a mistake in your description of Rush. You said if you win you get to move again, then once more if they move back. Actually, you don't immediately move an extra move (presumably you did the Rush after taking your reflexive move though), you just get to move for free if they move. I'm not sure if you get to do this an infinite amount of times (if they're able to move several times) or just once. Disengage specifies it only works once, Rush doesn't. </div> </div> </div>Well son of a gun, you're right. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T11:44:07-07:00","id":723799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720809#post720809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what people think of the overall contents of the new Resources merit, since I (arguably over)wrote it this time. The currency numbers per dot are, I believe, the same as they ever were, but I spent a lot of time working out what they (were always apparently meant to) mean.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the new merit it works nicely but I was sad to see that in the book there is not a list like found in <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Manacle and </span></span><span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Coin</b></span></span> of things and cost to complement it. Would it be too much to ask if someone could pull the info from the old book and mock it up into Ex3 format and release it as a free download?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T12:01:11-07:00","id":723858,"title":"","content":"This next section is pretty sick \u2013 er, I mean, it\u2019s the list of diseases. We get a pretty good list of basic human illnesses to release as sweeping plagues. (Aside: I ran a 2e plague game, which was ultimately just infuriating for my players - \u201cYou are helpless when faced with these ravages\u201d is a strong thematic statement, but didn\u2019t fit with anything else the game was pitching to them. We\u2019ll see what it looks like this time.) We <i>also</i> get a cool supernatural illness, the puppeteer plague, which brings your skeleton to unlife inside you and has it claw its way out. That\u2019s terrifying!<br /> <br /> The resultant undead is called, um, a bonesider. Really? That\u2019s what you\u2019re going with?<br /> <br /> Leprosy is described as minimally contagious. It\u2019s difficulty 1 to resist contracting, i.e., \u201con par with removing someone\u2019s appendix safely.\u201d Again, these difficulty scales seem kind of whack.<br /> <br /> \u201cTreating wounds\u201d follows the rules listed back on p. 174, except that it omits the (+1 for treating yourself) described there.<br /> <br /> Treating poison requires an hour, apparently. Hope you were poisoned with hemlock or arsenic, because the others are going to be done by that. Wait, except, \u201con the battlefield,\u201d you can treat poison in one action(?) for +2 difficulty. Okay, but again \u2013 what happens if I drink rattlesnake venom?<br /> <br /> So here\u2019s an interesting thing; Lore now allows you to simply declare facts about the world, as long as you have a relevant specialty and the ST doesn\u2019t reject them \u2013 \u201cOh, this side of the mountain will get all the rain\u201d or \u201cI know an herb we can burn to turn the flame blue,\u201d say. We get basically no guidelines for setting difficulties for the roll to do this, though, other than a statement that the ST should make them up \u2013 well, yes. Or more explicitly: the rules say to base the difficulty on \u201cHow thrilling is it\u201d if a character knows the thing. What does <i>that</i> mean? Are thrilling things easier to know, or harder? I would have assumed that, y\u2019know, <i>obscurity </i>was the more relevant feature there\u2026<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if I object to this system in general, but it feels like this weird, touchy-feely narrative thing has been bolted onto what is, in general, a very gamist-simulationist system. Almost everything you do has its difficulties set based on what the world is; we don\u2019t make the cliff harder to climb because it would be thrilling if someone fell off. The design logic here may be perfectly sound on its own, but it feels orthogonal to the rest of the game\u2019s direction.<br /> <br /> Ah, here\u2019s a <i>partial</i> resolution to the complaint: we break Lore into diff 1-4, 5-7, or 8-10 based on\u2026 okay, no, I\u2019m still not actually sure where to peg anything, from this description.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s change the subject. The next section is\u2026 Crafting.<br /> <br /> Oh dear.<br /> <br /> So, Crafting has been a controversial topic on the internet for months now. SLS affectionately called it a \u201ccookie clicker\u201d game; I\u2019d apply the same term, but probably with a less positive attitude. In broad terms, crafting comes in four levels of project: <i>Basic</i> (fletch one arrow), <i>Major</i> (make a mundane sword or boat), <i>Superior</i> (build the Titanic, or an artifact), and <i>Legendary</i> (build the Five Metal Shrike.) Each level generates colored <i>experience points</i> \u2013 silver for Basic, gold for Major, white for Superior \u2013 which have to be cashed in to perform the next level up of project. Also, you only get color-xp if the project does something: earns you money, makes a new friend, furthers an Intimacy, etc. Some levels of crafting also require <i>slots</i>, which determine the number of projects of that level you can work on at the same time. (It appears to be the case that, if I have thirty Major slots, I can finish thirty Major projects in the time it takes someone else to do one, which seems\u2026 a little weird? And yes, a mortal with sufficient color-xp can do that.) Superior and Legendary projects only allow a fixed number of rolls to complete; hope you brought an Excellency, dude, because even Artifact 2 requires you to be able to average 9 successes per roll (in addition to stockpiling ~60 gxp). Artifact 5 requires you to average, uh, 21 successes a roll. Also, you\u2019re going to need Craft (Artifacts) for sure, Craft (Some relevant mundane thing), or Craft (Geomancy) if you want a manse. (For those of you keeping score at home, it\u2019s 19 XP to raise one Craft Ability to 5, assuming you favor Craft.) For fancy old-timey projects, you\u2019ll also want Craft (First Age) and sorcery, to use its entirely separate make-stuff system that isn\u2019t detailed here.<br /> <br /> (There\u2019s a picture here of a guy gesturing and doing\u2026 something?... with lightning and a couple of giant blue men. I can\u2019t make heads or tails of this picture \u2013 relative distance, scale, and even foreground-background ordering don\u2019t make any sense to me. The top half looks like the two men are standing right in front of Gesturing Guy, except one of their hands is <i>behind</i> the house in the background. But then there\u2019s a tiny little man at their feet, so I guess they\u2019re really far off, actually? I don\u2019t know.)<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I <i>strongly dislike</i> basically all of this, but two things in particular: (1) I hate that Major crafts still require prerequisites, i.e., a swordsmith can\u2019t make swords unless he works in <i>more basic </i>projects periodically to fuel up. (Because\u2026?), and (2) it irritates me that all of this complexity is in service to something that isn\u2019t a game. Like, the actual process of crafting affords no chance to be clever, or to make interesting decisions; you can try to optimize your color-xp rewards (\u201cIntimacy: I love making stuff\u201d and a good relationship with a shopkeeper cover two of the three), but the actual making-process is just a sequence of grinding rolls with no choices. You don\u2019t get to weigh choices, or consider alternatives, or ponder the tradeoffs of different materials \u2013 you just keep rolling them bones as long as you can afford to pay up.<br /> <br /> Make it simple, or make it something I can strategize about. Combat does the latter; Investigation, say, does the former. Craft does neither.<br /> <br /> &lt;/rant&gt;<br /> <br /> There follows a kind of weird interlude on boats. Boats actually give you separate die bonuses for different parts of a ship \u2013 like, you might get +1 to sailing from the rowers, +2 from the sails, +1 from the design, etc., if you\u2019re trying to get somewhere in a hurry. Two ships in a fight both roll to collect Momentum (not Initiative? Why the new term?) which is spent to perform various maneuvers against the enemy vessel, like boarding or ramming them. This is not a bad system, but it\u2019s strange that it\u2019s so divorced from the land-based maneuvering system \u2013 it seems like these should be two cases of the same system, not two entirely different rules sets.<br /> <br /> Also peculiar: one possible strategem rolls +Speed, while the others roll +Maneuver. But every single listed ship has a higher Speed than a Maneuver \u2013 given that this is a contested roll, is it intended that the guy jockeying for position is always disadvantaged vs. the guy just going for all-out speed? It would be nice to have that explicit, if so.<br /> <br /> And with that \u2013 and an entirely blank page \u2013 we\u2019re done.<br /> <br /> <i>The Good:</i> Combat and social influence both look <i>much</i> improved from their 2e versions; you can tell that the folks who wrote this had played 2e and had felt some of the failure-states of that system. Most of the miscellaneous rules \u2013 environments, disease, etc. \u2013 look pretty solid, as well. Battle groups look <i>much</i> easier to handle than War Pants ever were.<br /> <i>The Bad:</i> The utter lack of a large-scale management system. The odd multiplication of systems in a couple of places \u2013 naval vs. land warfare being the obvious one, but there are a lot of edge-case systems multiplying here (\u201chow to hold a knife to someone\u2019s neck,\u201d for instance). Individually, these may be fine, but this chapter is ~60 <i>very dense</i> pages.<br /> <i>The Ugly:</i> Craft looks like a frustrating mess. Having played with it now, it also <i>plays</i> like a frustrating mess.<br /> <br /> Up next: \u201cChapter 6: Charms.\u201d Heeeeeeere we go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-24-2015, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T14:03:58-07:00","id":724115,"title":"","content":"Volferfic. Actually <i>really hilarious</i> Volfer fic, in which he uses a strategically-labeled loincloth (\u201cContents personally inspected by the Scarlet Empress\u201d) to bait a bar full of Realm soldiers into a fight. It\u2019s a pretty great picture, as well. Alas, same mortal-interaction problems as the previous bits: one mortal gets a half-sentence out, and then he dies. The only other speaking parts are Volfer and a Dragon-Blooded lady.<br /> <br /> We get a little side call-out that <i>no one</i> would <i>ever</i> try to label Charms as if they were discrete powers. Sure, because who ever heard of <i>that</i> happening in wuxia? It\u2019d just be ridiculous!<br /> <br /> \u201cMagic, techniques, powers \u2013 Solar Charms are all of these, and none of them.\u201d Well, I believe the first half of that. This entire section \u2013 which goes on for most of a page, insisting repeatedly that, no, this isn\u2019t magic, we\u2019re just <i>saying</i> that it is \u2013 is a little bit ridiculous; if it\u2019s simplest for us-the-readers to think of this as doing magic, why isn\u2019t it simplest for the folks in the world to think of it that way, as well? (And if there\u2019s some easier way for them to think about it, why don\u2019t we talk about it that way, too?)<br /> <br /> None of this seems to <i>matter</i>, except that it\u2019s going to throw fuel on a thousand internet fights, but it seriously stretches on for more than a page.<br /> <br /> Next heading: \u201cCharm Style\u201d and OH MY GOSH IT\u2019S STILL GOING. \u201cThe Charms allow the <i>player </i>to describe and depict a Solar with greater and greater levels of power and skill, but it is not the Charms which allow the <i>Solar </i>to have such power and skill.\u201d Just\u2026 just <i>stop</i>, introduction. I want to read about my awesome Solar magic, not be berated for thinking about it as awesome Solar magic.<br /> <br /> (Oh, but Martial Arts Charms <i>are</i> distinct techniques, and everyone thinks of them that way. Naturally.)<br /> <br /> Hm. All Charms have to be activated pre-roll \u2013 including soak Charms, per Holden. Er, but in what order do we declare? Simultaneously? Attack-first? Do we counter-bid, where each of us declares until we both pass?<br /> <br /> Sorcery counts against the dice cap now \u2013 interesting.<br /> <br /> Hm. Okay, we have nothing like a steps-of-resolution process here, nor do we have the old Charm-conflict-resolution table. So how\u2019s that going to be handled? There\u2019s a general, \u201cWell, this happens, unless the Charm says otherwise\u201d \u2013 guess we\u2019ll see what goes down.<br /> <br /> Hm, so you can\u2019t spend Initiative below 0 to pay for Charms. That\u2019s a good rule \u2013 but is it a general one? Does it apply to, say, Disengage?<br /> <br /> Per this description, Supplemental Charms enhance a rolled action, but only one of the matching Ability. Reflexive Charms create actions or enhance unrolled actions. Cool, that\u2019s a clean break between types.<br /> <br /> <i>Bridge</i> Charms have alternate prereqs. Are they an Integrity-only thing? This description keeps mentioning Integrity as a weird exception to the normal rules. The idea of alternate prereqs makes sense, though \u2013 hearkens back to some of the Dawn Solution stuff. <i>Mute</i> Charms don\u2019t add to anima \u2013 that\u2019s a nice touch. <i>Psyche</i> looks like the new UMI keyword. <i>Combo-OK </i>is <u>gone</u>, and we here say thankya.<br /> <br /> Excellencies have kind of a weird break point \u2013 they\u2019re both Supplemental (when used to enhance die rolls) and Reflexive (when used to enhance static values). That\u2019s awkward, though it does reflect the division above. (Is the Reflexive/Supplemental break still meaningful? It used to matter to combos, but that\u2019s all gone. What\u2019s lost by making everything Reflexive, specifying that Charms can only enhance their own Ability? We already have a category of \u201cSupplemental, but breaking the normal restriction.\u201d) On the plus side, free Excellencies in anything Caste, Favored, or with at least one Charm!<br /> <br /> Okay, so here\u2019s how I\u2019m going to do this: I\u2019ll break Abilities down one-at-a-time, but heck if I\u2019m going to try to mention every single Charm. I\u2019ll call out stuff that stands out as I go, though.<br /> <br /> <u>Archery</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 32<br /> By Ability requirement: 0/1/3/4/24<br /> By Essence requirement: 7/7/9/4/3/2<br /> <br /> Right off the bat, a concern: Sight Without Eyes is Reflexive, 1m, removes penalties. It also says \u201cShe may make an Archery attack\u201d \u2013 if it wasn\u2019t wildly out of line with the cost, I\u2019d parse that as this creating an attack, since that\u2019s one of the two major jobs of a Reflexive. Surely \u201cIf she makes an attack\u2026\u201d or similar would be better. (At E5, the Solar can see through cover, which does\u2026 what?)<br /> <br /> Several of these powers (i.e., There Is No Wind) are Reflexive and yet enhance rolled actions (i.e., shooting people). Doesn\u2019t that break the fundamental definition from a few pages back?<br /> <br /> Yeesh, Accuracy Without Distance is still a perfect attack. Ouch.<br /> <br /> Heh, Immaculate Golden Bow can grow Evocations now. Nice.<br /> <br /> Rain of Feathered Death doesn\u2019t appear to work as in its example; each attack does \u201cCurrent Initiative \u2013 last successes\u201d damage. So, I have 10i; I roll 10i for 2 successes on the first hit. On the second hit, I only roll 8i, for two more successes. But there\u2019s no indication that my \u201ccurrent Initiative\u201d drops \u2013 so on the third, I roll 8i again. Except, no, that\u2019s not what the example shows at all. Surely this should be \u201ccurrent Initiative \u2013 sum of successes on previous hits\u201d or similar.<br /> <br /> Searing Sunfire Interdiction says you can act first on the next round. And if two Charms both declare this\u2026?<br /> <br /> Good gosh, at E6, Searing Sunfire Interdiction allows you to just indefinitely cancel the turns of anyone you can hit \u2013 <i>everyone</i> you can hit.<br /> <br /> Hm. Heavens Crash Down says it can be used to Clash \u2013 that is, it grants an extra Clash attack? Again, there\u2019s ambiguity as to what is <i>enhancing</i> an attack, and what is <i>providing</i> an attack \u2013 this and Sight Without Eyes are both Reflexive, so that\u2019s no help. The repurchase says it \u201cremoves the Perilous keyword, allowing the Solar to spend herself into negatives\u201d \u2013 but that\u2019s not a feature of the Perilous Keyword; that\u2019s a default property of <i>all</i> Charms. Seems like Perilous serves no function here.<br /> <br /> Kudos to Holden for reorganizing the Charms by Essence rating \u2013 it\u2019s a much better intro. The themes of Archery seem to be making a <i>lot</i> of big, Decisive attacks, ignoring the need to Aim, and punishing anyone who gets close/tries to stop you from leaving/has the temerity to crash near you. There\u2019s also incentive for you to stay close to take advantage of several of those. I like it!<br /> <br /> There are a <i>lot</i> of multiattack Charms here \u2013 upwards of five, depending how you want to count \u2013 though most of them require you to make a Decisive.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Revolving Bow Discipline \u2013 keep shooting the guy until either you miss or he crashes. (Then zap him for Crashing, with the right other Charms.)<br /> <i>No</i>: Probably Sight Without Eyes, which lets you shoot in the dark \u2013 again, I almost never see STs use situational penalties, which means this almost never does anything.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Relative to previous editions? Probably Heart-Eating Incineration, which costs <i>levels of anima</i> to fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T15:21:05-07:00","id":724259,"title":"","content":"<u>Athletics</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 30<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/2/7/4/16<br /> By Essence requirement: 11/7/7/3/2<br /> <br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: reroll 5s and 6s until they disappear, 1i for every 10 rolled, reroll all non-successes, Excellency cost permanently reduced.<br /> <br /> Monkey Leap is a little less useful than it used to be \u2013 it lets you cover the same ground as before, but with a jump rather than a normal move. Er\u2026 actually, how far can you jump, normally? How hard is it to do this feat without a Charm?<br /> <br /> Soaring Crane Leap lets you survive a fall without dying. Which- hm. Which is actually really useful, because falls are <i>lethal</i>, except that the rules on falls said to give players every opportunity to not fall. One wonders whether falls are just <i>too</i> lethal \u2013 whether no one will realistically use them, and so Charms to mitigate them are unneeded. Why force this Charm to be repeatedly reactivated? Is it overpowered for it to let you survive falls in one usage?<br /> <br /> We get a sidebar on Aiming, which feels about five pages late. It\u2019s also a <i>lot</i> of caveats for which Charms don\u2019t need to have an Aim action \u2013 this feels like prime territory for a keyword.<br /> <br /> Foe-Vaulting Method is a once-a-scene Charm requiring a successful roll; if it works, it gives your enemy -2 Defense vs. one attack. That\u2019s not nothing, but it\u2019s pricey. But\u2026 okay, hang on. This is a Reflexive Charm, so it creates an action. So I pop it, succeed, and make a Decisive attack, resetting to base Initiative. (1) Do I still get a normal attack this turn, or was that it? (2) If I can find some way to reset to a \u201cbase\u201d of 6+ Initiative, can I immediately pop it again in the same round? (The Dawn Anima will do that at E6, but that seems like a high cost.)<br /> <br /> Lightning Speed is the first in what I suspect will be a long list of Charms that do nothing but fiddle with dice; this one adds basically +.1275 successes/die.<br /> <br /> Increasing Strength Exercise gives +(Essence) damage to all Decisive attacks, which gets mean fast with, say, Archery\u2019s mega-Decisives flurries. At E3, that\u2019s plausibly +18i at no added cost every turn.<br /> <br /> Ten-Ox Meditation does not feel like a great Charm. Okay, the process is this: you make a (Strength + Athletics) roll that you normally couldn\u2019t succeed at. For each three successes you get <i>beyond what you actually need</i>, you can momentarily boost your Strength by one; if you boost it far enough, you succeed. That feels pretty edge-case-y; if you\u2019re low strength, you\u2019re already going to have an awful hard time to rolling three over what you need. The justifying example already feels pretty implausible \u2013 that\u2019s eighteen successes on twenty dice; even with a reroll, that\u2019s not likely, and since you\u2019re activating the Charm <i>before </i>you find out whether you\u2019re going to roll well...<br /> <br /> Thunderbolt Attack Prana doubles all rolled damage on an attack, which sounds like the start of a pretty nasty fight-opening combo. It\u2019s also nice for swatting guys out of the sky \u2013 fun.<br /> <br /> Spider-Foot Style has a duration measured in multiple turns, which is a little sad \u2013 I\u2019d hoped we were done with that.<br /> <br /> Unbound Eagle Approach adds \u201cglide more\u201d to Soaring Crane Leap. Just not feeling this one, guys \u2013 16 XP to float sideways-ish?<br /> <br /> Leaping Tiger Attack is great for closing the distance with a kiting archer \u2013 it\u2019s basically an extra band of movement. If you\u2019re not already high Init enough to use it, though, you\u2019re stuck \u2013 if you can\u2019t catch the archer, you can\u2019t build up, either.<br /> <br /> Bleh. Athletics-only motes \u2013 thanks, game, but I\u2019m quite content with the resources I already have to track.<br /> <br /> Thunder\u2019s Might presumably has to be activated in advance, like any other Charm, but I can see being confused by that \u2013 it\u2019s a reroll effect, and that\u2019s not the natural inclination.<br /> <br /> So, Nine Aeon\u2019s Thew lets you meet <i>any</i> Strength prerequisite, which makes Ten-Ox Meditation completely redundant. Better yet, it\u2019s not even an upgrade \u2013 it\u2019s in a totally different branch of the Athletics tree.<br /> <br /> Themes of Athletics seem to \u201cgo anywhere\u201d (treetops, water, the walls, the sky), \u201clift anything,\u201d and \u201cclose with anyone.\u201d A lot of very solid-looking Charms, and then a handful that just look like padding. The Rush game is <i>strong</i> here, though \u2013 closing from four range bands or more is entirely possible.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Thunderclap Rush Attack. Cool, powerful, multiple uses.<br /> <i>No:</i> Ten-Ox Meditation. Redundant, unreliable, underpowered.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> The speed with which Athletics effects want to turn themselves back off again. I\u2019d guess it\u2019s to prevent sniping from mid-river and/or the ceiling, but it\u2019s well below the rate of mote replacement if you really are untouchable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T18:05:54-07:00","id":724638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=723537#post723537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, okay. Did you find it natural to keep up with the rules for counter-crashing?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was more we went &quot;oh, wasn't there some rule about this? How did it work?&quot; and went and looked it up.<br /> But then, the players have so far fought some mortal martial artists, one DB with no combat charms who died in 2 rounds, a battlegroup of Bisclavets (I don't know if I spelled that right), and a mortal sorcerer and his 30 raiders. So, it's not like we've done tons and tons of complicated combats and have completely got the hang of it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T19:16:39-07:00","id":724749,"title":"","content":"<u>Awareness</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 22<br /> By Ability requirement: 0/1/7/5/9<br /> By Essence requirement: 11/5/4/2/0<br /> <br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Reroll 6s until they disappear; 1m for each 9 and 2m for each 10; revert (Essence) of the enemy\u2019s double-successes to single successes; free full Excellency; reroll 10s until they disappear; 10s add to a pool of bonus successes for future use; reroll Essence nonsuccesses, and reroll another die for each success that turns up; enemy\u2019s 1s become your 10s and 2s become your 9s; reroll 1s until they disappear.<br /> <br /> This is the first Ability with no Essence 5 Charms, which seems odd given how front-and-center Supernal is. Given fully <i>half</i> the Charms are E1, actually, this (at first glance) seems like one of the worst choices for a Supernal. The number of Ability 5 Charms is still persistently high, though \u2013 it really seems like you\u2019re going to want to go \u201call in\u201d or \u201cnot at all\u201d in an Ability.<br /> <br /> Surprise Anticipation Method can <i>retroactively make Charms cheaper</i>, which\u2026 no, please and thank you. Its second effect is to allow the subconscious use of Charms, which feels a bit like an air-breathing mermaid \u2013 has anything previously said you <i>can\u2019t</i> activate Charms while asleep?<br /> <br /> The Keen X and Y Charms are kind of odd. You can really feel the attempt to make the non-sight senses pay off \u2013 \u201cyou can smell things you have Intimacies for\u201d and \u201cyou can taste the feelings that went into a meal\u201d aren\u2019t bad, but they\u2019re a little bit niche; \u201cI can smell how many people are in the room\u201d is getting a little silly, though.<br /> <br /> Studied Ear Espial is 1m for +3 dice on an attempt to spot stealthy characters while moving. So, er, 8XP for a 2m discount on your Excellency in a very specific circumstance?<br /> <br /> Sidebar: \u201cSpace-Saving Concession, Developer 5, Essence 3\u201d \u2013 there\u2019s an implication there somewhere, I feel like \u2013 paraphrasing, \u201cEvery Awareness Charm with X and Y, except these two, can be extended to a duration of one turn.\u201d This\u2026 really feels like it should be a keyword.<br /> <br /> Awakening Eye generates a bunch of extra successes that go into a pool for later use. I have really liked the first two trees; I am really hating Awareness so far. Every other Charm seems to introduce some new resource that needs to be tracked: a library of smells, a pool of extra successes, a batch of Awareness-only motes, a sidebar with effects not mentioned in the actual Charms\u2026<br /> <br /> I mean, look at just the unique mechanical complexity! That\u2019s <i>just how the die rolls get twisted</i>, before we get into the new extra resources.<br /> <br /> Living Pulse Perception is one success when someone is hiding in an enclosed room with you \u2013 again, two motes off on your Excellency in an <i>extremely</i> narrow circumstance. This is just kind of thin soup \u2013 there\u2019s almost nothing in here where you\u2019d go \u201cWOW,\u201d despite this being the smallest tree so far.<br /> <br /> Is it just me, or does Unsurpassed Sight Discipline have no actual rules text until you get to the Special Activation Rules?<br /> <br /> Blink again does not specify whether it needs to be activated in advance of the roll.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Exalt can visualize an object she is taking, in sections no larger than a horse\u2019s head.\u201d You need a <i>Charm</i> for that? In a splat that can reflexively generate light for 1m?<br /> <br /> In contrast with the above, Dedicated Unerring Ear is really cool: you can hear your Intimacy-people speak your name and talk to you, no matter where they are. That\u2019s very cool \u2013 give me more Awareness stuff like that! And Eye of the Unconquered Sun is still crazy-good \u2013 instant disintegration of almost every concealing effect, at the cost of being a giant glowy \u201cIIIII SEEEEEE YOOOOOOOU\u201d figure.<br /> <br /> Themes of Awareness are\u2026 man, I don\u2019t even know. Noticing stuff good, I guess, and then a weird hodge-podge of knowing things about people and not ever getting snuck up on. Dip Sensory Acuity Prana and Keen Sight Technique and get out.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Dedicated Unerring Ear is a broad new capability that would otherwise be entirely impossible. Awesome.<br /> <i>No</i>: Any Charm that gives a handful of still-counts-as-a-Charm bonus dice, but at a verrrrrry slight discount, in This One Exact Circumstance That May Never Come Up.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Any Charm dealing with taste and smell; maybe taste and smell just shouldn\u2019t be dedicated trees, I dunno. The absence of any Essence 5 effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T21:46:12-07:00","id":725157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=722756#post722756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We also get rules for re-persuading someone \u2013 broadly, it\u2019s harder to convince them after they\u2019ve been convinced once. This was a big hole in 2e, but I\u2019m not sure it\u2019s better now; as others have noted, there\u2019s some incentive here to persuade everyone in the party to do the-thing-they-were-going-to-do-anyway, because that makes them much more resistant to later persuasion. Which is a bit silly, but it works!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like rules for pep talks or those scenes when the general goes out in front of his army for a grand &quot;We will win this battle!&quot; speech!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T23:05:05-07:00","id":725251,"title":"","content":"You raised a good point about jumping: I couldn't see anywhere in the book that explained the basic rules of jumping. Anyone know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T05:31:29-07:00","id":725624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=724115#post724115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We get a little side call-out that <i>no one</i> would <i>ever</i> try to label Charms as if they were discrete powers. Sure, because who ever heard of <i>that</i> happening in wuxia? It\u2019d just be ridiculous!</div> </div> </div> </div>This just drives me nuts. I can understand a sidebar saying &quot;<i>Not all</i> Exlated consider their charms discrete powers.&quot; Basically an &quot;It's perfectly okay if you want to play Hercules&quot; sidebar. But to say that we're <i>not allowed </i>to play Kenshin or Ichigo? Plus it doesn't even make sense. How does Solar Swordsman <i>not</i> consider shooting a Giant Beam of Deadly Golden Light at people a discrete power from, say, just swinging his sword normally? Note to the devs: you may prefer your games without the technique shouting and over-the-top naming stuff that happens in a lot of shonen anime and wuxia. And that's fine. But that's the source material that got many of us into these games. Some of us <i>like</i> that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T06:20:11-07:00","id":725762,"title":"","content":"No characters in wuxia ever shout out technique's names from the top of their lungs, only anime do that, and I'm fine with Exalted not being anime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T06:31:26-07:00","id":725773,"title":"","content":"Here's some totally not wuxia where people yell out different techniques - <a href=\"https://youtu.be/mphrZoYDAkc\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/mphrZoYDAkc</a> (although to be fair, they are technique names and not &quot;moves&quot;, but that's how it is in most anime anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T07:19:54-07:00","id":725863,"title":"","content":"The technique's names calling absolutely ruin all of the nice cheography, seeing that amount cheesiness just reinforced my belief in &quot;No Charm Name Shouting in Exalted&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:20:52-07:00","id":726276,"title":"","content":"Irked: on leprosy, it actually is minimally contagious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:50:13-07:00","id":726326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=722797#post722797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) You said you were wandering how often people crash the person who crashed them. It seems to me so far that people get crashed then get back up by crashing someone else quite often, but it's rarely the person who crashed them (as he probably now has high initiative). But it did happen once (I think the Changing Moon was crashed, then the Full Moon knocked the enemy's initiative down to a low number, he missed his attack, then the Changing Moon crashed him).</div> </div> </div> </div>The most common circumstance for an Initiative Shift is, in my experience: A crashes B; A Decisively attacks B and resets to base Initiative; B survives the attack and makes a Withering attack against A; B Crashes A, gets the Initiative Shift. &quot;B survives the attack&quot; is what makes certain Resistance, Dodge and Melee Charms so important--in some cases it's better to weather a hit than to make your opponent miss and keep most of their Initiative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=724749#post724749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cThe Exalt can visualize an object she is taking, in sections no larger than a horse\u2019s head.\u201d You need a <i>Charm</i> for that? In a splat that can reflexively generate light for 1m?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely certain that the Ex3 rules allow for reflexive light generation for 1m. I suppose it depends on how you read &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\">The Solar may cause her Caste Mark to appear and display itself for as long as she desires.</span></span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 10-25-2015, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:03:32-07:00","id":726523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=725863#post725863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The technique's names calling absolutely ruin all of the nice cheography, seeing that amount cheesiness just reinforced my belief in &quot;No Charm Name Shouting in Exalted&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, yeah, I can see that. Though I find it isn't it refreshing compared to all the &quot;Aha! I can see in your eyes you know the secret technique, and I know that you know that, and you know that I know that you know that... from our oh so knowing glances... of course we're both far too refined to actually talk about such techniques while we're fighting&quot;? (Or, God, the ones where they're pretending to be drinking a cup of tea together or something while secretly fighting and we the audience are all like half silently &quot;C'mon guys. Please. End. This. Farce.&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:14:55-07:00","id":726553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=725762#post725762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No characters in wuxia ever shout out technique's names from the top of their lungs, only anime do that, and I'm fine with Exalted not being anime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the techniques still have names. And Exalted is as much anime as it is wuxia, which is to say, inspired by both in addition to a lot of other things. There is nothing mechanically lost in people naming techniques and/or yelling them out, so why ban it? Why not just say &quot;Some of the things that inspired Exalted have characters that do these things. These things are okay to leave in if you like. But it's also inspired by western myths, like Hercules, that don't do that, so it's okay not to do them, too. Do whatever your table thinks is fun.&quot; But it's also that it just doesn't make sense. There are plenty of charms that are quite clearly distinct techniques, and it would take a lot of hand-waving and head scratching to justify your character not thinking of them as distinct techniques, and I just don't see what you gain by trying to force that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:18:57-07:00","id":726561,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts Charms are explicitly named technique-widgets in-setting. Sidereal native Charms probably are as well. Solar native Charms are not, they are purely an abstraction of intangible skill, even the ones that don't necessarily fit that mould like Phantom Steed and GSS. <br /> <br /> This has been discussed a number of times before since the &quot;Solar Charms aren't discrete Things in-setting&quot; was announced by the writers, and the simple answer as to why is, &quot;because the writers wanted to do it that way.&quot; That's pretty much it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T19:28:06-07:00","id":727888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=726276#post726276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irked: on leprosy, it actually is minimally contagious</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, I know. Sorry, let me rephrase that complaint: resisting leprosy is difficulty 1, which sounds fairly easy. But difficulty 1 is, by the book, on par with removing someone's appendix safely.<br /> <br /> So my beef isn't with the leprosy claim - it's that the difficulty scale is weeeeeird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=726326#post726326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely certain that the Ex3 rules allow for reflexive light generation for 1m. I suppose it depends on how you read &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\">The Solar may cause her Caste Mark to appear and display itself for as long as she desires.</span></span>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>... Huhhhhh. I didn't catch that at all. Interesting.<br /> <br /> But, like, surely a Solar should be able to glow, right? Given that they can do that accidentally, it just feels weird to say they can't do it deliberately. And... even if not, I'm not sure &quot;visualize this thing you're touching&quot; is something I'd bill the character for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-25-2015, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T12:05:03-07:00","id":729570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=727888#post727888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, like, surely a Solar should be able to glow, right? Given that they can do that accidentally, it just feels weird to say they can't do it deliberately. And... even if not, I'm not sure &quot;visualize this thing you're touching&quot; is something I'd bill the character for.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would probably make some sense to be able to generate light whenever, but I have to admit that losing that ability makes the darkvision Charms more useful.<br /> <br /> But yeah, making that power free once you have the Charm seems reasonable. I might be inclined to charge a mote for, say, reading the density or internal composition of an object based on touch. E.G. &quot;The wall is only an inch thick here,&quot; or &quot;This 'man' doesn't have any internal organs.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T18:59:14-07:00","id":730699,"title":"","content":"<u>Brawl</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 49<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/0/7/9/32<br /> By Essence requirement: 11/11/19/5/3<br /> <br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Reroll 10s, reroll 5s and 6s until they disappear, free full Excellency, reroll 1s and 10s until they disappear.<br /> <br /> Structure-wise, this is an odd one \u2013 less than a quarter of the Charms are accessible at E1. If my back-of-the-envelope numbers are right, Brawl has more Ability 5, Essence 3+ Charms than Awareness has altogether. It feels like an obvious Supernal candidate, again in contrast with Awareness.<br /> <br /> Fists of Iron states that it lets you parry Lethal barehanded. Can you not, normally? I mean, you couldn\u2019t in 2e, but I don\u2019t remember that in the combat section.<br /> <br /> This is a pretty offense-heavy Ability, but it\u2019s not purely ATTACK ATTACK ATTACK \u2013 we get, for instance, a turnlong Onslaught negator, which is a pretty a big deal. Onslaught\u2019s a pretty big thing for Brawl, actually: if your opponent has been piled on, you get more damage, more defense\u2026 Edit: And here\u2019s an effect to make your Onslaught penalty stick around, and one to cripple them as long as the penalty sticks around,<br /> <br /> Good grief. Heaven Thunder Hammer is an no-risk effect \u2013 that is, you pay to activate it after you hit with it. If you connect with a Decisive, you send the opponent flying. At 4 HLs of damage, you get to also drop the opponent from a medium height. Hey, remember those falling rules? The ones that make people, uh, explode? HTH is an Essence 1 source of falling damage on tap; if you ever let a Solar Brawler connect with you, be prepared for the ~4L you actually take to be supplemented with another ~7L of unavoidable damage that doesn\u2019t have to be paid until afterwards. (The Charm says that E3, you double the successes for the purpose of determining how far someone is hurled. Does that modify their falling damage as well? It seems like it would have to \u2013 the two are linked \u2013 but that means a base-initiative, no-Charms-enhancing love-tap could stick on another 7L as a surprise after-effect. It\u2019s also unclear whether the 7+ success effect is only applicable at E3+.)<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s a grappler preserving his turns of control, even if he gets attacked. I am getting the vibe that, once a Solar Brawler lands a Decisive hit with any amount of Initiative, you\u2019re dead.<br /> <br /> Thunderclap Rush Attack looks like a great dip \u2013 free extra movement, applicable for use with other Abilities than Brawl, which is cool. Aaaand then we get more of that \u201cbreak ties in favor of the better stunt\u201d thing.<br /> <br /> Okay, this has <b>got to be a goof</b>. Solar Cross-Counter costs 1i (+ other stuff) and has the Perilous keyword. There\u2019s a note that the Solar can spend 1wp to remove the Perilous keyword, i.e., to let it be used in Crash. But it <i>still costs 1i</i>, and Charms can\u2019t pay Init costs below 0 unless they say they can, even without the Perilous keyword. Literally, this lets you pay 1wp to accomplish nothing.<br /> <br /> Burning Fist Burial enhances an existing punch. I thought Reflexives didn\u2019t do that? Also, it doesn\u2019t specify whether it can be used with non-Brawl Abilities.<br /> <br /> Ooh, Blade Rebuking Wrath is a disarming Charm!<br /> <br /> I do like the \u201cAll the Essence 1 stuff first\u201d ordering, but the resulting set does feel a little disjointed. Just came across an E2 grappling Charm, and was like, \u201cOh, yeah, that was a subtree, wasn\u2019t it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Wow, speaking of good dips \u2013 Dancing With Strife Technique is a free WP for avoiding an attack with 5+ successes, with a not-impossible reset condition. That\u2019s really handy. But why is this Reflexive-no-cost instead of Permanent \u2013 because of the reset? Why do we have both Reflexive-no-cost and Permanent as types?<br /> <br /> Adamantine Fists of Battle \u2013 rerolls 10s, but doesn\u2019t reroll the rerolls?<br /> <br /> So, funny story: I remember one of the first fights I got into with Hatewheel \u2013 back when he was still relatively new and we all thought Exalted might be dead-ish except for Ink Monkeys \u2013 was over the Charm name \u201cCancel the Apocalypse.\u201d I argued that \u201cpunch a dude real hard\u201d was not the most straightforward effect to associate a name like that. Five years later, we\u2019re all a little older and wiser, a little calmer, maybe, and yep, I am totally sticking by that assessment; it\u2019s a ridiculous name.<br /> <br /> I like that several of these effects reward having high Strength \u2013 Exalted needs more reason to have other Attributes than Dex.<br /> <br /> Fire-Eating Fist lets you repeatedly juice up by blocking your opponent\u2019s Elemental Bolts or similar. Er, who\u2019s going to continue throwing elemental bolts after you eat the first one?<br /> <br /> River-Binding Wrath is 2m for +.125 suxx/dice \u2013 i.e., about a quarter more successes than normal \u2013 on a grappling roll. Yep, grapplers will kill you.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why Wicked Dissolve Dust has the name it has. Didn\u2019t this used to smash up buildings or something? It\u2019s a \u201cput your captive between you and an incoming attack\u201d Charm now.<br /> <br /> Eh heh heh, Shockwave Technique lets you go bowling for enemies with a guy you have grappled. That\u2019s fun. Fatal, probably, but fun.<br /> <br /> The Ferocious Jab + Fivefold Fury Onslaught combo is somewhat reduced. Honestly, a little more concerned about HTH right now, but I mean, these are great tastes that taste great together \u2013 punch a guy six times, and if you ever hit, tack on an extra 7L for funsies. (By \u201cgreat tastes\u201d I mean \u201cthis ends most fights from base Initiative with the other guy exploding.\u201d)<br /> <br /> Striving Aftershock Method is the second half of that \u201creset to 6i\u201d combo I pondered on the other day. (Rereading, I see this does not grant free attacks, the definition of the Reflexive keyword notwithstanding.) Here\u2019s the pattern:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Pop Foe-Vaulting Method; make a surprise attack. Pay 3i; hit with a Decisive with whatever you have left. Land the hit.</li> <li>Be a Dawn, with anima flaring. Reset to 4i.</li> <li>Pop Striving Aftershock Method for 2m. Reset to 6i instead. Reset Foe-Vaulting Method.</li> <li>Repeat as many times as desired; total cost to reduce your opponent\u2019s Defense by 2 each turn is 2m. You won\u2019t do much base damage with any particular hit, but you\u2019re a brawler; you have options.</li> </ol>Obviously not an infinitely sustainable combo, since you have to hit in step 1. On the other hand, gambits are decisive attacks -<br /> <br /> - aren\u2019t they? P.199 says yes, they\u2019re \u201ca special sort\u201d of decisive. P.183 just says they\u2019re <i>similar to</i> decisives. Which is it? If it\u2019s the former, you could spam grapples every turn; 1m for Vicious Lunge makes you almost certain to succeed at the attempt. Given that you <i>will</i> kill the enemy if you land the hit, and he\u2019s at -2 Defense for surprise, that\u2019s a pretty terrifying combination. Stack River-Binding Wrath if you want a virtually assured grapple success for 3m.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s\u2026 man. That\u2019s terrifying. That\u2019s 2e-style \u201cif this hit lands, say goodbye to the fight (p.s. this hit will land).\u201d<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an undodgeable, unblockable attack \u2013 first of those we\u2019ve seen. Withering-only, though.<br /> <br /> Orichalcum Fists of Battle requires having a turn to burn, but <i>dang</i>. Stack this with FFO \u2013 every attack gets +Essence dice and rerolls 1s and 10s until they disappear. (This Charm specifies it retains successes from rerolled 10s. Adamantine Fists of Battle didn\u2019t. Is this significant, or just an oversight?)<br /> <br /> Heaven Fury Smite gives you a free Decisive after crashing the enemy. Which\u2026 a grappler can do in one turn, trivially. I just\u2026 there is so very much lethal stuff here, I\u2019m a bit overwhelmed.<br /> <br /> \u2026 which brings us to Ascendant Battle Visage. \u201cHer hair may lengthen and change colors\u201d \u2013 yeah, I\u2019ve seen enough anime to know etc.<br /> <br /> Themes: Clashing. Grappling. Doing all of the damage, no matter how little Initiative you initially hit with.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes: </i>There\u2019s a lot of really powerful synergy here \u2013 you can feel how a lot of the Charms work together to give you this utterly unstoppable juggernaut damage-engine. Which sounds like great fun to play, but\u2026<br /> <i>No: \u2026</i>I do not see any way to avoid being basically murdered by a grappler, at present. The on-contact damage potential is just <i>so very high</i>.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Sledgehammer Fist Punch: \u201cThis attack is neither withering nor decisive.\u201d Er, what? (It breaks stuff, not people, but still.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-26-2015, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T19:12:14-07:00","id":730711,"title":"","content":"&quot;Cancel the Apocalypse&quot; always sounded more like a Sidereal Bureaucracy Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8802-codexgigas","name":"Codexgigas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T08:54:34-07:00","id":732359,"title":"","content":"<u>Bureaucracy</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 26<br /> By Ability requirement: 2/1/3/2/18<br /> By Essence requirement: 11/5/7/2/1<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks:<br /> <br /> Hope you like Ability 5, kids! This is another one that feels like a pretty weak choice for Supernal \u2013 3 Charms at Essence 4+?<br /> <br /> Okay, hot off the crazy murderdeath that is Brawl, let\u2019s switch gears: Bureaucracy. I\u2019m particularly interested to see what Bureaucracy Charms do in light of the\u2026 underwhelming?... leadership system earlier; what does it mean to be a Supernal Bureaucrat, in this setting?<br /> <br /> So, here\u2019s the Charms at a glance:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Detect quality of a good.</li> <li>Know how much you can sell a thing for.</li> <li>Know someone\u2019s budget and whether he plans to cheat you.</li> <li>People can feel how great a merchant you are.</li> <li>Know what Bureaucracy specialties the people around you have.</li> <li>Scenelong - add Bureaucracy to a Read Intentions roll, sometimes.</li> <li>Unfailingly sense people\u2019s Intimacies towards an organization.</li> <li>Sense when someone tries to turn a member of an organization against it.</li> <li>Accelerate granting bureaucratic requests.</li> <li>Scenelong - add Bureaucracy to Socialize and Investigate in a bureau; all members of the bureau trust you.</li> <li>Scenelong \u2013 add half Bureaucracy to social influence or bureaucratic ends.</li> <li>Bargain with double-7s.</li> <li>Sense deals being made around you via Bureaucracy or Larceny.</li> <li>Remove corruption, with unclear results.</li> <li>Induce corruption, slowing bureaucratic process.</li> <li>Add half Bureaucracy to social influence to follow The Rewlz.</li> <li>Sell anything to anyone.</li> <li>Recover willpower for doing Bureaucracy.</li> <li>Sense magic targeting your organization; stop it, if necessary.</li> <li>Profile the person using magic on your organization.</li> <li>Kill a project.</li> <li>Free bureaucracy Excellency, once per season.</li> <li>Finish a project, without actually undertaking it.</li> <li>Your bureaucracy may no longer _____.</li> <li>Compel a person to act in his official capacity.</li> <li>Enhance an organization\u2019s die pools; make it a bulwark against the Wyld.</li> </ol><br /> #8 \u2013 Enigmatic Bureau Organization \u2013 implies, but does not actually state, that it only works if the Solar is\u2026 what, leading the organization? A member in authority over the affected character? As written, it applies to all organizations, which, uh, seems like the Solar\u2019s going to be getting a lot of mental sticky notes. Why is this free Reflexive and not Permanent?<br /> <br /> #9, Speed the Wheels, accelerate the bureaucratic delay. Soooo\u2026 how long are those, normally? Is \u201cThe Fair Folk won\u2019t turn over records for three centuries\u201d a common thing?<br /> <br /> #17, Soul-Snaring Pitch, is legitimately a terrifying and useful power \u2013 automatically successful against most mortals by Essence 3, and enormously expensive to resist regardless. If it succeeds, and it\u2019s likely to do so, you make the target willing to pay very nearly anything for your chosen object.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do love the sole Essence 5 entry here \u2013 the last one in the list. \u201cMy organization supports reality itself\u201d is just very cool.<br /> <br /> A <i>lot</i> of these, though, are\u2026 kind of thin. There are a bunch of pseudo-Infinite Masteries here, granting limited scenelong Excellency use \u2013 that\u2019s #6, 10, 11, and 16; #18 and 22 are similar slow-time resource regenerators (saving you Willpower and motes, respectively). Some of the others are just underwhelming; #1 and #2, Frugal Merchant Method and Insightful Buyer Method, are <i>together</i> about equal to 2e\u2019s Frugal Merchant Method \u2013 and the 2e version also granted bonus dice! Did anyone feel like the 2e version was just too potent a package? So many of the others have the problem that small-scale haggling in Exalted is basically meaningless; if you don\u2019t change a price by a full order of magnitude \u2013 that is, by a resource dot or more \u2013 there\u2019s no actual in-game consequence to the shift. This isn\u2019t D&amp;D, where a 10% reduction in gear price would be an actual big deal \u2013 whatever this does for you, it\u2019s doing in the land of flavor text. That\u2019s a tough environment to write Charms for, I\u2019m sure \u2013 and the powers here that feel legitimately powerful break out of that \u201cslight edge in bargaining\u201d slot to make broad edits of organizations or human desires. Of my four players, none have taken Bureaucracy Charms, and it\u2019s not hard to see why \u2013 when the name of the Ability is <i>bureaucracy</i>, you need a hook to grab people right out of the gate, and Antiques Roadshow: The Charm ain\u2019t it.<br /> <br /> Themes of bureaucracy include knowing what people want, and giving it to them; gaining persistent competency (expressed through scenelong die-adders) in bureaucratic situations; and convincing members of a bureaucracy to do what they\u2019re supposed to do (or not, depending).<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Soul-Snaring Pitch offers a lot of power in a small package. I can think of many approaches enabled by having this Charm.<br /> <i>No:</i> Almost all of the Essence 1 effects.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird: </i>#20, Omen-Spawning Beast, is one of what\u2019s a rare breed so far: what <i>appear to be</i> Solar reality-hacking Charms. Activating it, you find notes detailing who has used magic against you \u2013 notes that are, apparently, called into existence by the Charm itself. #23 \u2013 Infinitely Efficient Register \u2013 is similar. Who has completed the project? What resources went into its development? Apparently, the Charm retroactively does that for you. (Is this magic? It\u2019s described like magic \u2013 is it supposed to be Stuff That Just Happened Normally, expressed in Charm form?)<br /> <br /> (Is the numbered list useful at all?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T09:19:03-07:00","id":732385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=732359#post732359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Is the numbered list useful at all?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I found it easier to cross-reference with your list of short descriptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T10:37:38-07:00","id":732579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=730699#post730699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Brawl</u><br /> Good grief. Heaven Thunder Hammer is an no-risk effect \u2013 that is, you pay to activate it after you hit with it. If you connect with a Decisive, you send the opponent flying. At 4 HLs of damage, you get to also drop the opponent from a medium height. Hey, remember those falling rules? The ones that make people, uh, explode? HTH is an Essence 1 source of falling damage on tap; if you ever let a Solar Brawler connect with you, be prepared for the ~4L you actually take to be supplemented with another ~7L of unavoidable damage that doesn\u2019t have to be paid until afterwards. (The Charm says that E3, you double the successes for the purpose of determining how far someone is hurled. Does that modify their falling damage as well? It seems like it would have to \u2013 the two are linked \u2013 but that means a base-initiative, no-Charms-enhancing love-tap could stick on another 7L as a surprise after-effect. It\u2019s also unclear whether the 7+ success effect is only applicable at E3+.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not no-risk. You have to actually roll at minimum 3 damage to get any effect (2 at E3). My reading is that you have to pay for the charm after the attack is rolled but before damage is rolled. Which does raise the question of why we don't have the combat steps anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T10:44:55-07:00","id":732624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=732385#post732385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> #9, Speed the Wheels, accelerate the bureaucratic delay. Soooo\u2026 how long are those, normally? Is \u201cThe Fair Folk won\u2019t turn over records for three centuries\u201d a common thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone's got a mountain to climb. Twilights want to craft artifact N/A, Dawns want to punch out the Juggernaut, and Eclipses want to start swaying the bureaucracies of Yu-Shan. Considering godly lifespans and heavenly corruption, Speed the Wheels feels like the starting point for tackling that bureaucratic climb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T11:55:27-07:00","id":732768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=732579#post732579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not no-risk. You have to actually roll at minimum 3 damage to get any effect (2 at E3). My reading is that you have to pay for the charm after the attack is rolled but before damage is rolled. Which does raise the question of why we don't have the combat steps anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a question I am asking myself a lot as I read through. <i>Exactly when</i>, for instance, do you accumulate a new point of Onslaught penalty?<br /> <br /> It's a fair point on HTH - still, being able to retroactively tag any Decisive with it after the attack hits (and the defender's missed most of his window) is a huge deal. Especially once that doubling effect goes in play, you can assume that even a minimum-Initiative hit is likely to be fatal to a 7HL character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeptic Tank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=732624#post732624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone's got a mountain to climb. Twilights want to craft artifact N/A, Dawns want to punch out the Juggernaut, and Eclipses want to start swaying the bureaucracies of Yu-Shan. Considering godly lifespans and heavenly corruption, Speed the Wheels feels like the starting point for tackling that bureaucratic climb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can believe this, but I just have no idea how long any particular thing should take. Anywhere we say, &quot;Yep, centuries to get a result,&quot; we're also effectively saying &quot;Any party without a Bureaucrat need not even consider talking to this organization,&quot; so that's kind of a sticky question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-27-2015, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T12:08:50-07:00","id":732789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=732768#post732768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anywhere we say, &quot;Yep, centuries to get a result,&quot; we're also effectively saying &quot;Any party without a Bureaucrat need not even consider talking to this organization,&quot; so that's kind of a sticky question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a fine statement, as long as going 'the official route' isn't the only path to the goal. If my circle doesn't have a bureaucrat, but wants to meet Ahlat, they'd better have either a social character who can talk their way into a party, or a dawn of enough note to warrant a look. The bureaucratic route will have some upsides (meet in a safe environment on a predictable timescale) and downsides (takes time, unlikely to be kept a secret), but requires a high entry bar to make it a practical alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T12:10:46-07:00","id":732797,"title":"","content":"That's fair! I do think Speed the Wheels is on the better end of the Bureaucracy Charms - it at least has a clear &quot;bypass problems I couldn't normally resolve&quot; usage, even if I do feel a bit like I'm pulling numbers directly out of my rear (&quot;Getting a permit will be, um, 1d10 * 10^(1d10) days.&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T12:40:34-07:00","id":732831,"title":"","content":"For the &quot;what's good to pick for a supernal.&quot; I think Holden has stated that some fun tricks are at essence 4-5, but the real power is in essence 3. As a general trend anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T13:59:25-07:00","id":733064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=732831#post732831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the &quot;what's good to pick for a supernal.&quot; I think Holden has stated that some fun tricks are at essence 4-5, but the real power is in essence 3. As a general trend anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>And while that's nice and all, it's a statement that feels very starting-character-centric. Supernal doesn't just let you pick charms at chargen of up to Essence 5, it lets you continue to buy charms up to Essence 5 as your character gains more XP. So some time into the game, once everyone has hit Essence 3, the people who picked a Supernal with a lot of Essence 4 and 5 stuff still can get new toys not available to other people, while the ones who picked things like Supernal Awareness feel like chumps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T14:02:13-07:00","id":733070,"title":"","content":"Hang on, folks, this is the long one.<br /> <br /> <u>Craft</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 60(!)<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/2/9/5/43<br /> By Essence requirement: 18/15/17/5/5<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Gain sxp or gxp for each 10 rolled, \u201croll a free full Excellency,\u201d reroll 10s and 6s until they disappear, bonus non-Charm dice and successes, buy an extended die cap for your Excellency, roll an extra die for every 3 successes recursively, gain an extra 3 dice if the last entry turns up 3+ successes, make your Excellency cheap for a day.<br /> <br /> Well. Here we go. Craft is structures a bit peculiarly; first off, it\u2019s by far the largest tree so far, easily twice as large as several of the others. Second, even in the context to this point, it\u2019s strikingly top-heavy; almost 3/4 of them require a Craft Ability at 5, and nearly half require at least Essence 3. Craft is also unique in that it doesn\u2019t follow the \u201cAll the Essence 1s, then the E2s, E3s, etc.\u201d pattern that every other Ability has so far. Instead, it\u2019s grouped in a series of (intersecting) sub-trees, with each sub-tree arranged in the normal order. This makes some logical sense, given the sheer size of the overall tree.<br /> <br /> In any event. The Craft Charms, in the order they appear:<br /> <br /> Charms that help with Efficiency, i.e., \u201csaving on crafting points\u201d:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>(2*Essence) free Major slots.</li> <li>Reduce cost of making a Major slot.</li> <li>Convert dots from one Craft Ability to a related one.</li> <li>Spend gxp to raise a new Craft Ability.</li> <li>Convert 4sxp &lt;-&gt; 2gxp &lt;-&gt; 1wxp</li> <li>Gain (Major Slots) gp at the end of every story.</li> <li>Gain one Superior slot.</li> <li>Reduce cost of making a Superior slot.</li> <li>Earn sxp while making a Superior project.</li> <li>Finish a Superior project at lower cost.</li> <li>Build Superior projects in Major slots.</li> <li>Once a season, whip out a free 2-dot Artifact.</li> <li>Chain the gxp from one Superior project into the next, making it easier and more rewarding.</li> <li>Gain two Legendary slots.</li> <li>Convert all wxp into real experience points.</li> <li>Spend wxp 5:1 in place of real experience points for Lore Charms and similar effects.</li> <li>On finishing a Legendary project, gain bonus successes to your next Superior/Legendary.</li> <li>While building 10 Artifacts of the same level simultaneously, immediately finish one of them at no cost.</li> <li>On death, reveal that the you that died was really a magic-robot-clone, and the real you has been elsewhere the whole time.</li> </ol>Notation switches here from \u201c[color] experience points, which is the notation used in Ch. 5, to simply \u201c[color] points.\u201d I like this better.<br /> <br /> Exegesis of the Distilled Form (Efficiency, #15) has a pile of costs to reduce its efficacy, and caps at 20 XP in any event\u2026 but it still fundamentally bugs me. Spend-xp-to-get-xp is not a great thing to have, whatever the caveats; either Craft is overpriced and this balances it out, in which case make Craft cheaper so this isn\u2019t the must-have for parity, or Craft is priced appropriately and this makes it undercosted, in which case this should go away. Neither option strikes me as particularly good.<br /> <br /> I am strongly tempted to simply remove project slots as a concept, which immediately pares off about ten Charms.<br /> <br /> Dual-Magnus Prana (Efficiency, #19, i.e. \u201cthe Doombot Charm\u201d) is just as vexing as it ever was. I\u2019ve heard this described as the \u201cLupin in the turkey\u201d problem: it doesn\u2019t matter how good your Solar Investigator was, or how thoroughly he searched the scene, if Lupin can retroactively declare himself to have been hiding in the turkey the whole time. In the same way, doesn\u2019t much matter how thorough your ambush plans, or how intense your magical scrutiny, if it turns out the Solar was a robot, retroactively. Surprise! This is before we come to setting-integrity questions about the ability to have fully-functional Solar duplicate clones running around. (Why just one? Why not have you and your doombot active simultaneously?)<br /> <br /> Momentum (i.e., \u201cget more points):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>When you roll for a project with no Excellency, gain sxp for each 10.</li> <li>+1sp per objective on a Basic project</li> <li>+1gp when meeting all objectives on a project</li> <li>Finish a Basic or Major project in moments, with your bare hands.</li> <li>Roll dice every story, gain sxp or gxp for roll.</li> <li>Gain sxp and gxp for each Craft Ability at 5, once a day.</li> <li>Accelerate Superior or Legendary projects to weeks/months.</li> <li>Gain 3 wxp/story.</li> <li>Invent artifact tools out of the air for a temporary purpose.</li> </ol>Heck yeah, Craftsman Needs No Tools (#4). Stay awesome.<br /> <br /> Peerless Paragon of Craft (#5) \u2013 why \u201croll a free full Excellency?\u201d Why not just roll the pool? It\u2019s the same number of dice.<br /> <br /> One of the more interesting suggestions I\u2019ve heard \u2013 thanks, Aquillion! \u2013 was to use Words-As-Workshop Method (#9) as a way of playing a Girl Genius-style character \u2013 always able to pull some useful gadget out of nowhere. That sounds fun! It seems <i>implicit</i>, but is not actually <i>stated</i>, that the wonders you create in this way shouldn\u2019t be, say, an occult lens that boosts your energy attacks \u2013 that could stand to be explicit, either way.<br /> <br /> Repairing and Reforging (i.e., repairing and reforging):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Break stuff.</li> <li>Make a mundane object permanently durable.</li> <li>Repair a nearly destroyed thing.</li> <li>Create a major slot for repairs only.</li> <li>Extra craft points for repairs.</li> <li>Make an object temporarily nigh-invulnerable.</li> <li>An object \u2013 and anyone nearby \u2013 can resist the Wyld for extended periods.</li> <li>You and allies gain (Essence) dice to rolls using smarty-pants Abilities.</li> <li>Add Evocations to a weapon.</li> <li>Make an object that lasts forever \u2013 an ever-burning candle, say.</li> <li>Bonus successes to repair an object.</li> <li>Switch up which Evocations in a weapon are live.</li> <li>Add Evocations to a weapon again.</li> <li>Free Evocations.</li> </ol>I really like Durability-Enhancing Technique (#2); while it goes against my usual \u201cclear task you couldn\u2019t otherwise perform\u201d standard for good Charms, it gives good reason for a Solar to make mundane things in a way mortals can\u2019t, which is cool. Chaos-Resistance Preparation (#7) is similarly interesting, giving the crafter a handy way to march his army into the teeth of madness. So is The Art of Permanence (#10), which lets you make pseudo-minor-artifacts by imbuing mundane things with permanence. This is definitely my favorite Craft sub-tree so far.<br /> <br /> Crack-Mending Technique (#3) is very cool \u2013 I can see a Solar investigator sifting through the ashes, piecing a burned letter together again. It\u2019d be nice if the actual crafting side of it had more than some vague \u201cThis may reduce difficulties, I dunno,\u201d language.<br /> <br /> Design Beyond Limit (#9) and Hero-Forging God Weapon (#13) are hard to evaluate, given that they talk about Evocations in a way that no longer applies (I\u2019m told \u2013 haven\u2019t gotten there yet). Soul-Forge Tempering (#14) is a little vexing, in that \u201cpay XP for a Charm, so you can spend more XP on a weapon, so you can save XP on Evocations\u201d way. Do other Solar XP sinks \u2013 sorcery, martial arts, etc. \u2013 get this kind of discounting from a properly-invested character? I could see Sidereals having something similar for teaching.<br /> <br /> Power (i.e., POWAH, UNLIMITED POWAH):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Reroll 10s until they disappear (and 6s, with repurchase).</li> <li>Free full Craft Excellency once a week.</li> <li>Basic and Major projects get double 9s, 8s, or 7s, with repurchases.</li> <li>Act as if you had three more Craft Charms than you did; you can switch up which ones.</li> <li>Bonus non-Charm successes/dice on non-Basic projects. (Why both?)</li> <li>Spend craft points for bonus non-Charm successes.</li> <li>Convert non-successes to 10s, for every <i>three of a kind</i> success you roll.</li> <li>Infinite Craft Mastery. Like, literally, exactly that, except daylong.</li> <li>Spend sxp to raise the limit of your Excellency.</li> <li>Roll once for a Superior or Legendary project; this doesn\u2019t count against the maximum allowed rolls.</li> <li>Roll an extra die for every three successes on a Craft roll.</li> <li>Get an extra roll before the end of Superior/Legendary projects.</li> <li>If #11 produces 3+ more successes, add 3 more dice.</li> </ol>Flawless Handiwork Method (#1) again fails to specify \u201ckeeping successes\u201d as you reroll 10s.<br /> <br /> Bright-Forging Prana (#4), whatever <i>that</i> means, is just irritating \u2013 buy one Charm now so you can get any three free Charms you want, swapping \u2018em out once a story.<br /> <br /> Unbroken Image Focus (#6) requires mentally separating \u201c# successes\u201d and \u201c# dice that came up a success,\u201d which sounds like trivial, but obnoxious, mental overhead.<br /> <br /> The bean-counting game is <i>strong</i> in this tree. First Movement of the Demiurge (#7) is probably the worst offender here, though Divine Inspiration Technique (#11) and Horizon-Unveiling Insight (#12) are about as bad. I can\u2019t even really picture what it would look like to roll this tree with all the bells and whistles running \u2013 and even then, in all likelihood it\u2019s going to be one of six or more rolls that you need to make, not the one that actually ends the project. I can\u2019t help but feel like you\u2019d get the same result as a lot of this just by saying, I don\u2019t know, \u201cYou get +1 success for every 4 successes you rolled; you may repurchase this Charm (Essence) times.\u201d<br /> <br /> I made a list of all the Charms that revolve around slots or silver points, and there are about 18-19 of them. I suspect if you cut those, and brought the tree down to a more manageable 41 \u2013 <i>still</i> 41 Charms! \u2013 the result would feel less absurdly bloated. (You would probably want to eliminate sxp entirely in this case, but I'm not viewing that as a negative.) Note that you start with 15 Charms, and by Essence 5 you could have bought up to 37 more; if you spent <i>all</i> of that on Craft, you still wouldn't have the full tree presented here.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Most of the repair and reforging tree. Craftsman Needs No Tools, i.e. \u201cCraftsman Actually Gets to Do Things On Camera.\u201d<br /> <i>No:</i> The 10+ Charms that do nothing but grant slots, or make slots cheaper, or allow you to use different slots, or slots slots slots slots slots. My how-many-in-this-tree numbers don\u2019t even consider that most of those can be repurchased multiple times.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> So does the game want you to make basic projects, or not? Are these an important part of preserving the narrative of a crafter, or are they busywork to bypass once you\u2019re a Solar? The actual crafting system says the former; the plethora of \u201cALL THE SXP, FOREVER\u201d Charms say very much the latter, once they\u2019ve mugged you for a few of your Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-27-2015, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T14:13:34-07:00","id":733086,"title":"","content":"The way I have come to see for the craft rules...it is mostly going to be a problem for non solar. Solar get so many ways to stack silver xp which then they can convert into gold xp and with charms that convert gold xp to white xp for legendary projects...and charms making automatic success on some projects, essentially the only time a twilight with supernal craft will have issues is at the beginning of the game, since he needs some time to get on the crafting and get of course his silver/gold xp every season or is it story? I forget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T14:44:51-07:00","id":733118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dual-Magnus Prana (Efficiency, #19, i.e. \u201cthe Doombot Charm\u201d) is just as vexing as it ever was. I\u2019ve heard this described as the \u201cLupin in the turkey\u201d problem: it doesn\u2019t matter how good your Solar Investigator was, or how thoroughly he searched the scene, if Lupin can retroactively declare himself to have been hiding in the turkey the whole time. In the same way, doesn\u2019t much matter how thorough your ambush plans, or how intense your magical scrutiny, if it turns out the Solar was a robot, retroactively. Surprise! This is before we come to setting-integrity questions about the ability to have fully-functional Solar duplicate clones running around. (Why just one? Why not have you and your doombot active simultaneously?) </div> </div> </div>I love the Craft abilities and the whole thing... But I honestly would fluff that charm differently. Rather than &quot;Surprise Doombot&quot;, I would rule that the Solar has invested so much brilliance in their Sorcery and building ability, that they've made a perfect duplicate of themselves in cold storage. When they die, their soul immediately jumps to the copy. You can't have more than one you active at a time because your soul is required to animate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T14:49:10-07:00","id":733123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=733118#post733118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love the Craft abilities and the whole thing... But I honestly would fluff that charm differently. Rather than &quot;Surprise Doombot&quot;, I would rule that the Solar has invested so much brilliance in their Sorcery and building ability, that they've made a perfect duplicate of themselves in cold storage. When they die, their soul immediately jumps to the copy. You can't have more than one you active at a time because your soul is required to animate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fluff-wise, at least, I'd find that a lot less irritating. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T14:51:15-07:00","id":733126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=733118#post733118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love the Craft abilities and the whole thing... But I honestly would fluff that charm differently. Rather than &quot;Surprise Doombot&quot;, I would rule that the Solar has invested so much brilliance in their Sorcery and building ability, that they've made a perfect duplicate of themselves in cold storage. When they die, their soul immediately jumps to the copy. You can't have more than one you active at a time because your soul is required to animate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's not rules-as-written, I'd run the simulacrum as a telefactor rather than an android. This neatly avoids the two-PCs-at-once problem, and defines the simulacrum's Charm use as channeling the PC's Essence rather than possessing any innate capability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T15:03:07-07:00","id":733157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WhirlwindMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=733064#post733064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And while that's nice and all, it's a statement that feels very starting-character-centric. Supernal doesn't just let you pick charms at chargen of up to Essence 5, it lets you continue to buy charms up to Essence 5 as your character gains more XP. So some time into the game, once everyone has hit Essence 3, the people who picked a Supernal with a lot of Essence 4 and 5 stuff still can get new toys not available to other people, while the ones who picked things like Supernal Awareness feel like chumps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's the thing; E4 and E5 charms are so few in number that you've probably already got all of them by the time you hit E3, and not so potent that it matters for the people who aren't getting them. If I took supernal awareness and my buddy took supernal melee, I'm not going to feel all that terribly left out because at E4 said buddy has access to two more charms than I do, one of which is very expensive and situational and the other is a nice but not tremendously impressive boost to a charm that got all its real power at E2. And there are still going to be so many E1-3 charms for me to buy in other abilities that are probably more powerful than either Circle of Bright Reaving or Protection of Celestial Bliss, so I'm not running out of cool charms to buy or getting weaker charms. What's the issue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T15:13:30-07:00","id":733173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=733086#post733086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I have come to see for the craft rules...it is mostly going to be a problem for non solar. Solar get so many ways to stack silver xp which then they can convert into gold xp and with charms that convert gold xp to white xp for legendary projects...and charms making automatic success on some projects, essentially the only time a twilight with supernal craft will have issues is at the beginning of the game, since he needs some time to get on the crafting and get of course his silver/gold xp every season or is it story? I forget.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it seems to me that the point is, &quot;it takes even a mortal wordsmith a lot of time to make a sword,&quot; where the Solar artisan can quickly get to the point where she cranks them out from raw ore at a clip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T16:58:27-07:00","id":733426,"title":"","content":"For people who watched Kara no Kyoukai Dual-Magnus Prana is what Touko Aozaki used in Paradox Spiral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T18:07:47-07:00","id":733563,"title":"","content":"<u>Dodge</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 26<br /> By Ability requirement: 0/1/4/5/16<br /> By Essence requirement: 8/10/7/0/1<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: +1 Evasion for every 1 or 2 your enemy rolls, enemy loses 1i per 1 rolled, enemy loses one success per 1 rolled, gain 1i per 1 or 2 enemy rolls.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s exactly one Charm over Essence 3, for those of you keeping score at home, and something like 2/3 of them at Ability 5.<br /> <br /> The Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Spend Initiative to raise Dodge, breaking the cap.</li> <li>Disengage with double-9s.</li> <li>Keep the Initiative for Disengaging (or even earn it back, if you close again).</li> <li>Have Evasion 2+ when ambushed.</li> <li>After dodging an effect, move one range band.</li> <li>When you dodge, the enemy loses 1i.</li> <li>Your Evasion wins ties, rather than losing them.</li> <li>Remove any penalties to Evasion.</li> <li>Disengage while at short range, rather than close.</li> <li>On a successful dodge, redirect the attack to anyone at close range.</li> <li>Gain the 1i lost by the opponent from #6.</li> <li>Perfectly dodge any attack.</li> <li>Opponent loses 1i for each 1 rolled on the attack.</li> <li>+1 non-Charm bonus to Evasion for rest of scene.</li> <li>Ignore all Evasion penalties against enemies with lower Initiative. Cut cost of #1 in half. Gain 1i each round you are at close range and not struck.</li> <li>Convert enemy 1s into -1 successes.</li> <li>#7 and #16 don\u2019t count as Charms for the purpose of #21.</li> <li>Cancel damage at 4m/die. Or maybe 4m/success. Who knows?</li> <li>Retreat twice after disengaging instead of once.</li> <li>On a successful dodge, gain 1i per 1 or 2 enemy rolls.</li> <li>On a successful dodge without Charms, crash the enemy and steal his Initiative.</li> <li>Learn an enemy Charm and become immune to its effects.</li> <li>Create extra -0 health levels; if hit by an attack that only damages these levels, you count as dodging it.</li> <li>Gain 1i for every -0 health level you lose.</li> <li>Stand still for a round, and heal health levels.</li> <li>After using SSE, gain 1i/round until you are struck or move too far away.</li> </ol><br /> Reed in the Wind (#1) seems very unclearly worded. The text says \u201cReed in the Wind raises the cap on how much the Solar can enhance her Evasion by her Essence.\u201d So: is this saying that\u2019s a permanent improvement in the Solar\u2019s cap, just for knowing the Charm? Is it saying that as long as I invest at least 2i in a bonus through Reed in the Wind, I can buy extra bonuses from my Excellency? Is it saying that I can buy an extra (Essence) points of Evasion, but only via Reed in the Wind? What?<br /> <br /> Leaping Dodge Method (#5) is not explicitly a Disengage \u2013 does it benefit from Shadow Dancer Method (#3)?<br /> <br /> Can I use Shadow Over Water (#8) to negate, say, a Solar Brawler\u2019s ability to add my current Onslaught penalty to his Defense? If SOW \u201cremoves any penalties to the Exalt\u2019s Evasion,\u201d does that mean I can be not suffering from Onslaught while he uses Wind and Stones Defense? (Actually, is Wind and Stones defense just useless, unless your enemy has been stuck with persistent Onslaught penalties? Normally, those go away on your turn, right?)<br /> <br /> Is 0i a suitable number to spend to count as \u201cusing\u201d Reed in the Wind, for the purposes of resetting Seven Shadow Evasion (#12)? (P.S.: Hi, SSE!) Presumably not, but the rules don\u2019t indicate as much, and in general, \u201cno cost\u201d is a suitable cost to pay for a Charm \u2013 look at all those 0-cost Reflexives.<br /> <br /> Vaporous Division (#18) contradicts itself \u2013 its cost says it\u2019s 4m/die, while its text says it\u2019s 4m/success.<br /> <br /> Hundred Shadow Ways (#22) has a sidebar explicitly clarifying its usage. Which is good, I guess, because the sidebar says things that the Charm text doesn\u2019t even vaguely imply \u2013 such as that an attack enhanced with only the Charm you\u2019re \u201cstudying\u201d automatically fails. From the Charm text, you\u2019d think such an attack only resolved as it normally would without the enhancing Charm.<br /> <br /> Themes of Dodge: Charging up from not getting hit, daring your enemies to take swings, disengaging, and time travel(?).<br /> <br /> <i>Yes: </i>Most of these effects are pretty solid, honestly \u2013 I like almost all of them. Seven Shadow Evasion \u2013 our first perfect defense! \u2013 probably takes the cake, though.<br /> <i>No:</i> Dice triiiiiiiicks.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird: </i>Reflex Sidestep Technique (#4) is just\u2026 well, plain weird. It explicitly <i>undoes</i> damage, in its fluff \u2013 which doesn\u2019t match its mechanical effect at all (\u201cbetter dodging when ambushed\u201d). It also has a weird side effect \u2013 it gives you 2 Evasion, +1 for every 1 or 2 the enemy rolls; you can only use Dodge Charms if this gets you back to full base Evasion. That means the worse you are at dodging, and so the lower your Evasion is, the more likely you are to be able to use Seven Shadows Evasion (say). Harm Dismissing Meditation (#25) is even weirder \u2013 it actually <i>does</i> undo damage, which is described as \u201cstepping outside the moment\u201d you were hurt at some point after the fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T18:19:45-07:00","id":733588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=733126#post733126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's not rules-as-written, I'd run the simulacrum as a telefactor rather than an android. This neatly avoids the two-PCs-at-once problem, and defines the simulacrum's Charm use as channeling the PC's Essence rather than possessing any innate capability.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was very amused to see Dual Magnus Prana, since I play a character who discovered that he was not a Solar at all, but only the clone of a Solar Twilight who made him to trick the other party members into not realising he'd escaped. So now there's a charm to explain how said Twilight made the copy.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:02:29-07:00","id":734360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=733157#post733157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's the thing; E4 and E5 charms are so few in number that you've probably already got all of them by the time you hit E3, and not so potent that it matters for the people who aren't getting them. If I took supernal awareness and my buddy took supernal melee, I'm not going to feel all that terribly left out because at E4 said buddy has access to two more charms than I do, one of which is very expensive and situational and the other is a nice but not tremendously impressive boost to a charm that got all its real power at E2. And there are still going to be so many E1-3 charms for me to buy in other abilities that are probably more powerful than either Circle of Bright Reaving or Protection of Celestial Bliss, so I'm not running out of cool charms to buy or getting weaker charms. What's the issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess that's a decent point. Having thought about it more, I think the core thing in my mind isn't so much the &quot;jealousy&quot; that I described above as the fact that, as far as I can tell, once you hit Essence 5, Supernal stops meaning anything. And I think that's a little unfortunate, because I love the idea of Supernal. And I think it's especially unfortunate that, for some abilities, Supernal stops meaning much of anything at Essence 3 or 4. Maybe people won't end up caring much in play? I don't know. But I feel like it'd be nice if there were something, even something small, that sets a Supernal Melee character apart from non-Supernal Melee characters, even at Essence 5. Look at Sorcery, for example. It doesn't matter how good everyone gets, you are still going to be better at your Control Spell than anyone else, and I wish Supernal was that way, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T08:54:50-07:00","id":734910,"title":"","content":"<u>Integrity</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 31<br /> By Ability requirement: 2/1/5/3/20<br /> By Essence requirement: 6/13/10/2<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Gain 1m for every 1 or 2 rolled on social influence or curses, (Essence) of your enemy\u2019s 1s are treated as -1 success or (Essence) successes are rerolled.<br /> <br /> Roughly 2/3 of the Charms are at Ability 5; again, there are only 2 in the E4-E5 range. (Weirdly, the E1 range is also pretty thin \u2013 this set lives heavily in the E2-E3 range. Integrity is also the only tree (so far) to use the <i>Bridge</i> keyword, which allows a number of these Charms to be taken without actually buying into Integrity. Glancing through, the theory seems to be that martial artists, in particular, should be able to meditate without entering Integrity. Not sure I follow the motivation, there, but all right.<br /> <br /> The Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Ignore penalties from injuries and other harm to your Resolve and Guile.</li> <li>Gain +2 Resolve against issues you\u2019ve resisted in the past.</li> <li>Resist the natural twisting power of the Charm.</li> <li>Magic can alter you, but it cannot immediately render you unable to be who you are. (\u201cTurn into a duck\u201d becomes \u201cBecome duck-ish, but continue to daiklave things just fine; also, you can break this curse.\u201d)</li> <li>Become immune to any curse you\u2019ve broken via #4.</li> <li>Spend 5m for 1wp when resisting social influence or magic.</li> <li>Gain 1m for every 1 or 2 rolled on social influence or curses.</li> <li>+1 Resolve when defending with Ties/Principles. Effect stacks with multiple Solars.</li> <li>Meditate for an hour; gain +2 successes on a concentration-based roll.</li> <li>Treat a use of #9 as a full night\u2019s sleep, also restoring 20m and resetting 1/day Charms.</li> <li>Reject influence even after being persuaded.</li> <li>Make one of your Principles (nearly) inviolable.</li> <li>Sense when someone nearby is considering acting against a Principle you like.</li> <li>Pray with your followers for an hour; for the duration, they can resist the Wyld, disease, and hardship.</li> <li>Use your Willpower to resist an attack with no clear means of defense.</li> <li>Your followers gain Intimacies and bonus dice when they see you succeed socially.</li> <li>Your sermons feed your followers.</li> <li>Outside combat, turn motes into Willpower.</li> <li>1/day, raise your Resolve at 1m/point instead of 2m/point.</li> <li>After being forced to act against an Intimacy, shatter the effect controlling you.</li> <li>When your Intimacies are challenged, ignore the cost of three Charms to resist harm or influence.</li> <li>While using #9, you cannot be influenced, but you also can\u2019t react to others.</li> <li>Steal successes from your enemy\u2019s social influence.</li> <li>Use a Defining Principle to shake off major contradictory magical effects.</li> <li>Everyone around you realizes you have a particular Defining Principle.</li> <li>Learn a bunch of <i>non-Eclipse-tagged</i> Spirit Charms, as long as they fit your Principles and Charms.</li> <li>When using #9, heal and avoid the need for food.</li> <li>While using #9, become immune to harm.</li> </ol><br /> Stubborn Boar Defense (#2) makes a reference to \u201cthe Solar\u2019s Lunar mate.\u201d But the earlier Lunar section spoke of the destruction of the Lunar-Solar bond \u2013 one wonders how these will interact in future publications.<br /> <br /> Integrity Protecting Prana (#3) is permanent, but with a cost. You have to activate it. What? Also, what? Like\u2026 what possible reason is there for this not to be Reflexive, at this point? It\u2019s also scaled waaaaay back, functioning only against twisting environmental effects and not directed action.<br /> <br /> I kind of like Destiny Manifesting Method (#4), but it\u2019s there to fight off effects for which we have no examples. I want to see the use before evaluating its benefit.<br /> <br /> I was very excited by Undying Solar Resolve (#7) until I noticed it\u2019s another \u201cpool of motes that can only be used on one thing.\u201d I do not need five of these.<br /> <br /> Mind-Cleansing Prana (#9) is\u2026 odd. The die bonus isn\u2019t great, and neither is the hourlong duration \u2013 though it can reward you with a WP at the end. (The cost seems almost meaningless, honestly \u2013 if you have an hour to kill, you could recover 5m, right?) On the other hand, this becomes the basis for a <i>lot</i> of the upper parts of the Integrity tree; they really, really want you to play Integrity Guy as this sort of\u2026 meditative, invulnerable messiah figure. There\u2019s a pretty clear archetype in here, actually, which is kind of cool.<br /> <br /> Energy Restoration Prana (#10) resets your 1/day Charms when you use it. It, uh\u2026 it\u2019s a 1/day Charm, with no cost. I think the intent is clear, buuuuuuut\u2026<br /> <br /> Righteous Lion Defense (#12) really shows the change in mindset from 2e \u2013 rather than a perfectly inviolable defense, it\u2019s a Principle against which the enemy must succeed <i>twice</i> if they want to convince you to act against it.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a little uncomfortable with Phoenix Renewal Defense (#15)\u2019s implication that there are attacks with no clear defensive vector.<br /> <br /> Spirit-Tempering Practice (#18) blows my mind a little \u2013 it\u2019s a flat 4m-&gt;1wp conversion engine, with no restrictions other than \u201cnot in combat\u201d and \u201conce a scene.\u201d This is the biggest remover of the \u201cNo, willpower is really important you guys\u201d philosophy that \u2013 I had thought \u2013 Ex3 was holding to pretty tightly; several of the, \u201cUnder these exact circumstances, you may regain a Willpower once\u201d effects look pretty pale if you can just flat convert motes to Willpower multiple times a session.<br /> <br /> Righteous Soul Judgment (#21) says it can be used \u201cto complete a feat of strength\u201d \u2013 does that mean you auto-succeed, or what? Do you still need to meet the Strength prereq?<br /> <br /> Eminent Paragon Approach is an E3 Charm to let everyone know you have a Principle. Other methods of achieving this end: announce \u201cI feel really strongly about X! Also, I have 8 XP available!\u201d<br /> <br /> Themes: caring for your followers, being a wise meditative figure, being completely unflappable. Fits very well with what is seems like Integrity <i>should</i> do.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Most of the twist-resisting Charms. Most of the messianic effects.<br /> <i>No</i>: Divine Mantle (#26) completely bypasses the <i>otherwise very firm</i> limits on Spirit Charmshare. There are, uh, some pretty mean spirit powers out there.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Spirit-Tempering Practice. \u201cWillpower\u2019s really hard to get, unless you\u2019re this guy, and then eh.\u201d<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T10:14:45-07:00","id":735128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eminent Paragon Approach is an E3 Charm to let everyone know you have a Principle. Other methods of achieving this end: announce \u201cI feel really strongly about X! Also, I have 8 XP available!\u201d </div> </div> </div>I think you're underestimating this quite a bit. Sure, you can claim that you have a defining Principle of 'I fight for Justice' or 'I must defend Creation/the weak' when meeting a Wyld Hunt, but they'll just shout &quot;Lying Anathema, die!&quot;. If you use this charm, then they become aware without doubt that you DO have that Principle. Sure, you could try saying what the charm shows, but the thing is that Eminent Paragon Approach lets you prove it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T10:30:54-07:00","id":735148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735128#post735128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're underestimating this quite a bit. Sure, you can claim that you have a defining Principle of 'I fight for Justice' or 'I must defend Creation/the weak' when meeting a Wyld Hunt, but they'll just shout &quot;Lying Anathema, die!&quot;. If you use this charm, then they become aware without doubt that you DO have that Principle. Sure, you could try saying what the charm shows, but the thing is that Eminent Paragon Approach lets you prove it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see this charm creating or strengthening intimacies in others, even though that's not an explicit part of the text. While there are social influence actions to do that already, there's also the option to change intimacies based on what makes sense, without needing to roll. So this is the charm that makes the scared farmers peeking around the corner see the Solar kicking the corrupt tax collectors around and exclaim, &quot;He's really gonna clean up this town!&quot; And this makes it easier to organize them into a secret cadre of freedom fighters, etc. Even if the Solar doesn't have a real investment in building intimacies through words, he can let his deeds speak and form the basis of future interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T10:51:48-07:00","id":735243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735128#post735128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're underestimating this quite a bit. Sure, you can claim that you have a defining Principle of 'I fight for Justice' or 'I must defend Creation/the weak' when meeting a Wyld Hunt, but they'll just shout &quot;Lying Anathema, die!&quot;. If you use this charm, then they become aware without doubt that you DO have that Principle. Sure, you could try saying what the charm shows, but the thing is that Eminent Paragon Approach lets you prove it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're a Wyld Hunt member. You see an Anathema do what seems like a sincere, from-the-heart righteous gesture, and as far as you can tell he seems totally legit.<br /> <br /> Do you:<br /> a) Accept the truth of this occurrence (&quot;Wow, he is a decent guy!&quot;)?<br /> b) Assume this is some sort of dirty deceptive Anathema trick, equivalent to <i>failing</i> your Read Intentions check (&quot;Die, lying Anathema!&quot;)?<br /> <br /> It seems like the Charm lives in this weird space where it only interacts with characters who are actively trying not to judge whether or not you're at all sincere, who are not persuaded by your actual works of sincerity, and yet, on having a gut feeling that you seem sincere, are going to go with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T11:28:26-07:00","id":735369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735243#post735243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you:<br /> a) Accept the truth of this occurrence (&quot;Wow, he is a decent guy!&quot;)?<br /> b) Assume this is some sort of dirty deceptive Anathema trick, equivalent to <i>failing</i> your Read Intentions check (&quot;Die, lying Anathema!&quot;)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me ask a question, too. You have a fairly low Read Intentions Pool and are still doing a Read Intentions action on someone with fairly high Guile, do you:<br /> a) Accept whatever it tells you as true and act/RP accordingly?<br /> b) Assume that you failed and whatever Intention you just got told is the opposite of what's true and act accordingly?<br /> <br /> If your character Reads Intentions (whether he fails or not doesn't even matter) then the result IS what he believes. That's the entire point of the charm. Normally, when an Anathema does some seemingly sincere gesture, the Wyld Hunt member can distrust him etc. But this charm automatically makes everyone aware that YES, he IS sincere. You don't get to weasel out of that by saying 'sure, I believe he is sincere, but since I believe that he's obviously using evil Anathema magic and is insincere.'<br /> <br /> Granted, he could spend wp to ignore any attempts of using Eminent Paragon Approach as evidence to instilling an Intimacy towards you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T11:31:40-07:00","id":735376,"title":"","content":"You understand he holds this sincere belief<br /> And don't believe him to be lying. Then there's drama of whether or not you let your religious beliefs overwrite something you know to be true and kill him anyway. <br /> <br /> The DB is not aware of the read intentions check because that is a system abstraction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T11:34:14-07:00","id":735382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735369#post735369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me ask a question, too. You have a fairly low Read Intentions Pool and are still doing a Read Intentions action on someone with fairly high Guile, do you:<br /> a) Accept whatever it tells you as true and act/RP accordingly?<br /> b) Assume that you failed and whatever Intention you just got told is the opposite of what's true and act accordingly?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should be doing A because B is metagaming, interpreting a system result into the narrative inappropriately. B unfortunately happens a lot in the &quot;do I see something&quot; or &quot;don't believe someone&quot; contexts but it's something we should be aware of and not fall into even if playing it straight buts us at a detriment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T12:30:07-07:00","id":735513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735369#post735369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me ask a question, too. You have a fairly low Read Intentions Pool and are still doing a Read Intentions action on someone with fairly high Guile, do you:<br /> a) Accept whatever it tells you as true and act/RP accordingly?<br /> b) Assume that you failed and whatever Intention you just got told is the opposite of what's true and act accordingly?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that he <i>seems</i> sincere, as far as I can tell. This probably produces a guarded reaction, because (if I know that this is a cleverpants subtle guy), he'd probably seem sincere to me no matter the truth. Semidecidability is how &quot;Can I tell if he's lying?&quot; checks generally work, isn't it?<br /> <br /> (The same answer applies if someone used the Charm.)<br /> <br /> Do you think the book is assuming a different reaction? It doesn't specify at all what happens if I fail a Read Intentions roll...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your character Reads Intentions (whether he fails or not doesn't even matter) then the result IS what he believes. </div> </div> </div>I guess that's a yes, for you. I'm not sure this is so - does a Read Intentions roll say &quot;This is what I think,&quot; or &quot;This is what appears to be true; my character may or may not trust appearances?&quot; Does a failed Read Intentions roll say <i>anything</i>, or does it just shrug? Does making a Read Intentions roll ever disadvantage you, absent magic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-28-2015, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T13:05:48-07:00","id":735607,"title":"","content":"I play Read Intentions as an attempt to find out how someone feels, not as Stare Intently, which helps me make sure there's risk in any action I ask someone to roll for. Also, I don't set things up so the players can just shotgun rolls all the time, such as for lore checks. Awareness to avoid an ambush is one of the few exceptions. Other than that I tell the players what I think their characters would know, and if someone has a good reason to know more that I forgot about, I just tell them more.<br /> <br /> Coming back to Read Intentions, I almost always play this as the character engaging with someone to find out how he feels. Typically that means having a conversation, though I'm open to other ways of provoking someone to reveal feelings (e.g. making a pass to see how the NPC reacts) or spying on someone to catch him in an unguarded moment. All of those carry at least some risk - in conversation you reveal that you're interested in a topic, for example, and following someone around or whatever has more obvious risks. Some Socialize charms get away from this, but that's OK since they have a cost. YMMV and all - I really dislike rolling without a meaningful downside, but not everyone prioritizes that of course.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T13:09:42-07:00","id":735615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735243#post735243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you:<br /> a) Accept the truth of this occurrence (&quot;Wow, he is a decent guy!&quot;)?<br /> b) Assume this is some sort of dirty deceptive Anathema trick, equivalent to <i>failing</i> your Read Intentions check (&quot;Die, lying Anathema!&quot;)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this should be modeled in some way via principles (Major Principle: the Anathema are supernaturally competent deceivers). This would let the system organically allow you to &quot;metagame&quot; where that actually makes sense in character while also providing a mechanism for reflecting when even your doubts have been overcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T13:25:56-07:00","id":735637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735615#post735615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this should be modeled in some way via principles (Major Principle: the Anathema are supernaturally competent deceivers). This would let the system organically allow you to &quot;metagame&quot; where that actually makes sense in character while also providing a mechanism for reflecting when even your doubts have been overcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intimacies are much less ambiguously &quot;stuff my character believes,&quot; yeah, and they have the advantage of being a quantifiable mechanical hook. I think a Minor Principle of &quot;That Anathema really <i>does</i> believe such-and-such&quot; would give more to work with, here. (And would probably be overpowered for a 1m can't-fail effect, I suppose, but that's a separate problem.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T13:30:30-07:00","id":735676,"title":"","content":"The charm feels almost like a magical version of &quot;It's not what it looks like!&quot; The situation I imagine is something like, powerful noble hears noises and comes running into his daughter's room in the middle of the night, to see her, huddling terrified in a corner wearing only her nightclothes, with a strange man standing over her, weapon drawn. Rather than risk him misunderstanding and calling for guards, you activate this charm, keying off your principle &quot;I will not permit the dead to torment the living,&quot; at which point he automatically notices that you're not so much standing <i>over</i> her, as <i>in front</i> of her, and she's not staring terrified at <i>you</i>, but at the opposite corner of the room, and when he follows her gaze, sees two red eyes staring out of the darkness and ghostly claws form out of nothing. It can force people to notice things they might otherwise not have noticed in the heat of the moment by automatically making them pass a check they might not have bothered making at all. But in the situation being described in previous posts, there is no mechanical benefit to the situation. Yeah, you appear trustworthy, but of course you do, you're a deceptive evil demon. The DB doesn't know that he passed a check, he doesn't know that he made the check at all, he just knows that Anathema are evil, and have evil, deceptive magics, so what does it matter if everything appears to be kosher? Maybe if he prided himself on being able to see through any deception, it might give him pause, but without that reason to trust his eyes, why would he?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T13:39:02-07:00","id":735684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735637#post735637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intimacies are much less ambiguously &quot;stuff my character believes,&quot; yeah, and they have the advantage of being a quantifiable mechanical hook. I think a Minor Principle of &quot;That Anathema really <i>does</i> believe such-and-such&quot; would give more to work with, here. (And would probably be overpowered for a 1m can't-fail effect, I suppose, but that's a separate problem.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What I actually meant was that our DB raised in the Immaculate faith would have acquired this principle of &quot;The Anathema are supernaturally competent deceivers&quot; either explicitly on the sheet or reflected just as part of whatever strength principle the DB holds towards the faith, and would be able to use that principle to &quot;defend&quot; against a read intentions action (successful or not) that returned a result of &quot;yes that anathema believes in goodness and justice&quot;. The DB would be able to choose to use that principle to disbelieve the result. (Maybe the principle gets added to the target's Guile?) Then the potency of this Integrity charm might lay in being able to force its way past those principles.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, there is a bit of a weirdness here in that a Solar that wants to <i>persuade</i> a DB that she is pro-bunnies and rainbows currently has to overcome some heavy intimacies, but if the DB simply does a read intentions none of those intimacies matter - the DB is in-character convinced. Moreover, in this sort of situation it may actually be beneficial to have a <i>low</i> guile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","user":"AtG","date":". 10-28-2015, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T13:47:10-07:00","id":735695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735684#post735684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, there is a bit of a weirdness here in that a Solar that wants to <i>persuade</i> a DB that she is pro-bunnies and rainbows currently has to overcome some heavy intimacies, but if the DB simply does a read intentions none of those intimacies matter - the DB is in-character convinced. Moreover, in this sort of situation it may actually be beneficial to have a <i>low</i> guile.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly why it doesn't make any sense to have a Read Intentions attempt <i>force</i> a character to believe whatever they think appears to be true. Read Intentions, to make any sense, must be &quot;This is what appears to be true to your character, but RP whether or not he believes those appearances.&quot; Unfortunately, that interpretation makes this charm of extremely niche usefulness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T14:05:24-07:00","id":735755,"title":"","content":"I'd probably go with WhirlwindMonk's interpretation up there.<br /> This is the &quot;It's not what it looks like&quot;/&quot;I don't need to explain what I'm doing, people see what I'm doing&quot;-charm.<br /> <br /> A Zenith hunting down a crowd of young men, beating them down one by one, without this charm, in broad daylight:<br /> A guy on a rampage. We should stop him.<br /> <br /> A Zenith hunting down a crowd of young men, beating them down one by one, but with this charm, in broad daylight:<br /> A guy who really hates slavers. Respect.<br /> <br /> ...at least, it would be really nice if that <i>was</i> how it worked.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T14:17:29-07:00","id":735776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735755#post735755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably go with WhirlwindMonk's interpretation up there.<br /> This is the &quot;It's not what it looks like&quot;/&quot;I don't need to explain what I'm doing, people see what I'm doing&quot;-charm.<br /> <br /> A Zenith hunting down a crowd of young men, beating them down one by one, without this charm, in broad daylight:<br /> A guy on a rampage. We should stop him.<br /> <br /> A Zenith hunting down a crowd of young men, beating them down one by one, but with this charm, in broad daylight:<br /> A guy who really hates slavers. Respect.<br /> <br /> ...at least, it would be really nice if that <i>was</i> how it worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I don't see anything in the rules that says it <i>doesn't</i> work that way. It's just the fact that it's limited to Defining intimacies and can only be used once a story makes it feel like it ought to be either less niche, or more potent within its niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T14:19:46-07:00","id":735809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WhirlwindMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735695#post735695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly why it doesn't make any sense to have a Read Intentions attempt <i>force</i> a character to believe whatever they think appears to be true. Read Intentions, to make any sense, must be &quot;This is what appears to be true to your character, but RP whether or not he believes those appearances.&quot; Unfortunately, that interpretation makes this charm of extremely niche usefulness.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really good point - I wasn't considering the weird interplay &quot;compulsory Read Intentions&quot; would have otherwise.<br /> <br /> (Another side issue with RI as &quot;this is what you are sure of&quot; - since the Charm doesn't actually create Intimacies, it <i>still</i> wouldn't allow you to, say, try to convince the Dragon-Blooded to not kill you. You'd have to build up Major-ish Intimacies to that effect to actually perform social influence, even though the DB is convinced you're on the up and up!)<br /> <br /> (You could, of course, say that &quot;The DB is convinced you're telling the truth&quot; sidesteps the social system, but that's not really a mark in its favor, for me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-28-2015, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:08:34-07:00","id":735944,"title":"","content":"<u>Investigation</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 17<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/1/1/2/12<br /> By Essence requirement: 6/3/5/2/1<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Free full Excellency<br /> Themes: Detect crime automatically; compel the truth of who a criminal is from objects, recreations of the crime, or his own lips.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m looking forward to this tree \u2013 \u201cSolar Sherlock Holmes\u201d has always sounded cool, and the trees have never quite measured up. Let\u2019s see what we\u2019ve got!<br /> <br /> (Well, first, we\u2019ve got a Divine Mantle sidebar that\u2019s about a page too late.)<br /> <br /> The Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Auto-detect \u201cThere\u2019s something fishy here; roll to try to notice it.\u201d Nice!</li> <li>Auto-detect \u201cLarceny is being used nearby.\u201d</li> <li>Case a scene in seconds, with bonuses.</li> <li>1/scene, free full Excellency.</li> <li>Profile criminal based on crime scene; auto-detect characters matching profile.</li> <li>Tell whether one statement is true or false.</li> <li>1/scene, roll Investigation with double-8s.</li> <li>Get an alert (and an explanation) when a character acts against your profile of him.</li> <li>Compel a character to honestly answer questions.</li> <li>Infinite Investigation Mastery, roughly.</li> <li>Momentarily restore destroyed evidence.</li> <li>Auto-succeed on a case scene action. Make Holmes-style logical connections between objects and events.</li> <li>Reenact the events of the crime from the perspective of one of the participants.</li> <li>Sense the emotions of the person who left behind a piece of evidence.</li> <li>Reset any Investigation Charms with limited use frequency (#4, 7, 9, and 17).</li> <li>Understand the perpetrator\u2019s motivations, as per read intentions.</li> <li>Enter your \u201cMind Manse\u201d and solve some piece of the mystery.</li> </ol>This is our shortest tree so far, isn\u2019t it? And over two-thirds at Ability 5. Hooray.<br /> <br /> I really like Watchman\u2019s Infallible Eye (#1), which codifies a basic \u201cI\u2019m a great investigator\u201d competence.<br /> <br /> Judge\u2019s Ear Technique (#6) is nerfed hard \u2013 one statement, not a scene of truths. It also points out one of the things 3e seems to be outright missing: a generalized Charm-conflict resolution system. This Charm calls out how it, specifically, deals with conflict, but there\u2019s no general-case solution. I didn\u2019t expect to miss the UFvIO table, but I think I do!<br /> <br /> Evidence-Restoring Prana (#11) is great \u2013 I love the idea of a Solar investigator plucking evidence from the air.<br /> <br /> Ten Magistrate Eyes (#12) really feels like it ought to upgrade Evidene-Discerning Method, i.e., the other \u201ccase-the-scene-in-seconds\u201d power. Well, or else ditch the \u201cin seconds\u201d part from this one, or something \u2013 it just feels redundant as-is.<br /> <br /> Er, why does the Solar investigator in this drawing have <i>wings</i>? I kind of like the picture, in general \u2013 the fish-eye view works for it.<br /> <br /> Unknown Wisdom Epiphany (#13) suggests someone has been watching Hannibal; this might as well be called This Is My Design Prana. Which is in no way a negative.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes</i>: I think my favorite Charm in the set is also the first \u2013 \u201cHang on, my crime senses are tingling.\u201d Unknown Wisdom Epiphany is also pretty great, though.<br /> <i>No:</i> Mind Manse Meditation (#17) is waaaaay too much flavor piled on top of a simple idea: the Storyteller tells you how to solve a piece of your mystery, or at least how to make progress on it. I don\u2019t think that\u2019s a bad space for a Charm \u2013 it\u2019s a good anti-frustration feature, at a minimum \u2013 but it\u2019s hard to suss out of the text. \u201cMind Manse\u201d is also a little too cute for me, Holmes allusions aside.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird: </i>Empathic Recall Discipline (#16) is kind of odd \u2013 what is this doing that Unknown Wisdom Epiphany isn\u2019t? They\u2019re both very heavily fluff-texted Charms, and I\u2019m just not parsing the distinction between their effects. (Of the two, UWE is the cooler description by a fair mile \u2013 is it <i>just</i> supposed to grant actions, without motivations?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:13:10-07:00","id":735958,"title":"","content":"A few months ago, someone asked me: &quot;If you had to choose between a politician you respected and trusted, and one that you thought could get the job done, which would you choose?&quot; My response was that if I'm trusting politician X, then X is probably just very good at manipulating me, and I'm better off with Y.<br /> <br /> Then they stated which two politicians this exercise had been based on, and I realized that I did in fact trust X more than Y, and did in fact want X to get the nomination more than Y. The belief that I couldn't fully trust any politician was not sufficient to overwhelm my belief that X was being genuine. Now, it's possible that somebody more cynical would have stronger protective Intimacies to preserve their distrust, but the fact of the matter is that I was convinced of X's sincerity, and since I was convinced, the general rule stating that I shouldn't trust politicians seemed less applicable.<br /> <br /> All that to say: people are able to hold contradictory beliefs, at least for a time. Eventually, one may win out, but that doesn't necessarily happen immediately. &quot;All Anathema lie&quot; can and will coexist with &quot;this Anathema's all right,&quot; because that's how people's minds work. Then you can spend WP to ignore one of the things you believe, but which one you choose to ignore depends a lot on circumstance and the social atmosphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:28:37-07:00","id":735994,"title":"","content":"Side note/Callback:<br /> About the &quot;Seeing in darkness&quot;-charms discussed on page 4 (of this topic, <i>not</i> the core book!) - they're useful if you want things to <i>stay</i> dark. I mean, it's all fine and dandy if you don't mind announcing your presence to everyone with a line of sight to you, but light sources tend to be very easy to spot. If you want to hide, better learn to stay in the dark.<br /> And even if hiding isn't the issue any more, if it comes to a battle, you're still the Solar heavily invested in Awareness. Chances are you're better at coping with darkness than your opponent is - don't blow it by turning into a Christmas tree.<br /> Last but not least, there are things like heavy fog/smoke that can impair vision, and no amount of glow can help you there. Also, who knows, magical darkness may be a thing, too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:46:02-07:00","id":736039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735994#post735994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side note/Callback:<br /> About the &quot;Seeing in darkness&quot;-charms discussed on page 4 (of this topic, <i>not</i> the core book!) - they're useful if you want things to <i>stay</i> dark. I mean, it's all fine and dandy if you don't mind announcing your presence to everyone with a line of sight to you, but light sources tend to be very easy to spot. If you want to hide, better learn to stay in the dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Darkness is my ally!&quot; <br /> -Zatoichi","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T16:11:49-07:00","id":736114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=734910#post734910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stubborn Boar Defense (#2) makes a reference to \u201cthe Solar\u2019s Lunar mate.\u201d But the earlier Lunar section spoke of the destruction of the Lunar-Solar bond \u2013 one wonders how these will interact in future publications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, the Bond was broken by <i>murdering all the Solars.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=734910#post734910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of like Destiny Manifesting Method (#4), but it\u2019s there to fight off effects for which we have no examples. I want to see the use before evaluating its benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want examples, skip ahead to the Fair Folk antagonists. Some of the demons have them too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T16:32:16-07:00","id":736156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=736114#post736114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, the Bond was broken by <i>murdering all the Solars.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* That seemed like a plausible interpretation of the original passage - but it wasn't the only reading, and it isn't what I would have assumed absent the call out in this Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want examples, skip ahead to the Fair Folk antagonists. Some of the demons have them too. </div> </div> </div>Cool, thanks. I'll look forward to getting there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T16:50:07-07:00","id":736233,"title":"","content":"@Irked -- I'm really glad someone else caught that Unknown Wisdom Epiphany could be called &quot;This Is My Design Prana&quot;.<br /> <br /> As far as the Solar/Lunar Bond, my guess is that Lunars will have the option of taking a Merit to have their Bond still active/functional... either that or the Stubborn Boar Defense thing is just a throwback to a different idea that they had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:09:57-07:00","id":736419,"title":"","content":"<u>Larceny</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 29<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/3/5/8/12<br /> By Essence requirement: 9/9/7/2/2<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Bank successes for later use, spend Initiative from your next Join Battle roll, add opponent\u2019s 10s to your roll, treat two numbers 2-5 as 10s<br /> <br /> Themes: Be a criminal, steal anything, be anyone, go anywhere, avoid all suspicion.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>You can attract criminals, avoid the attention of magistrates, or appear to be involved in any crimes in the area.</li> <li>Appear to belong, wherever you are; boost your Guile to resist detection.</li> <li>Treat another\u2019s uncertainty as a Minor Intimacy.</li> <li>Claim ownership of a thing.</li> <li>Read Intentions better against someone while gambling.</li> <li>Cheat at a board game or poison a drink.</li> <li>Infallibly steal a thing.</li> <li>Automatically pick a lock.</li> <li>Create a perfect disguise.</li> <li>1/scene, mute five motes.</li> <li>Convince a target you\u2019ve always owned something you steal from him.</li> <li>Bank successes for future Larceny actions.</li> <li>Add successes to a Larceny roll, at the cost of future Initiative.</li> <li>Build points to spend on retroactive(?) larceny actions.</li> <li>Perfectly palm an object.</li> <li>Steal someone\u2019s pants. Or, well, something else in plain sight, but probably pants.</li> <li>Steal from several yards away, even with obstacles in the way.</li> <li>Pretend to be another person, including special effects.</li> <li>Treat some number from 2-5 as a 10.</li> <li>Plant evidence on a target.</li> <li>Steal from someone trying to pickpocket you.</li> <li>Steal your enemy\u2019s weapon mid fight.</li> <li>Teleport through a door. But, like, skillfully, not with magic.</li> <li>Adopt a disguise instantly.</li> <li>Wear two disguises at once.</li> <li>Prevent criminals and creatures of darkness from attacking you, briefly; enable a number of weird theft possibilities (dreams, Initiative, etc.).</li> <li>Make your disguises \u201cretroactively harder to pierce.\u201d</li> <li>1/scene, free full Larceny Excellency.</li> </ol><br /> Seasoned Criminal Method (#1) is a really great plot-hook generator \u2013 it guarantees your ability to Do Crimes anywhere you go. Swift Gambler\u2019s Eye (#5) is just the opposite \u2013 an<i> extremely</i> narrow effect, that\u2019s still only a little better than just using your Excellency.<br /> <br /> Flawless Pickpocketing Technique (#7) says that, when opposed by magic, it \u201cadds the Solar\u2019s Essence in successes.\u201d To the pickpocket technique, I guess, but again, some kind of general rule would be nice here. (An Excellency counts as magic, right?)<br /> <br /> Actually, wait, what\u2019s going on here? It gives +Essence successes, okay. It can\u2019t be detected at all. Then we\u2019re told it can\u2019t be detected with Awareness. Then we\u2019re told magic gets -4 dice, in addition to the bonus successes this gets. Then we\u2019re told Larceny-detecting magic can\u2019t detect this, unless the user of said Larceny-detecting magic also knows <i>FPT specifically</i>. What? Are Abyssals and the like just automatically out of the running, then?<br /> <br /> Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise (#9) is proof against human senses, and inhuman senses, but not supernatural senses. I guess I get that one, but it took a couple readings to click.<br /> <br /> Doubt-Sealing Hiest (#11), i.e., \u201cWhat, this thing I just stole? No, I\u2019ve always had it,\u201d is just a great image.<br /> <br /> Unshakeable Rogue\u2019s Spirit (#13) requires you to keep track of how much Initiative you <i>will have paid</i> from your <i>next</i> Join Battle roll, which just makes me shudder a little.<br /> <br /> Master Plan Meditation (#14) doesn\u2019t actually specify <i>when</i> you can start spending the points it collects. The implication seems to be that you can destroy evidence after the fact \u2013 but how far after the fact? After it\u2019s been found? After it\u2019s been put in the police locker? I don\u2019t find either of those implausible, per se, but they would make it clear that this is another of those reality-hack Charms (and not just flavor of \u201cwooOOOOOooo, I am sooooo skillful\u201d). Ahh, okay, there\u2019s a sidebar, which clarifies that it\u2019s <i>not</i> retroactive \u2013 it\u2019s just declared when someone would reveal a piece of evidence. How does that work, though? The cops show up to arrest you, start proudly declaring evidence, and halfway through everything turns out to have never existed?<br /> <br /> Proof-Eating Palm (#15) seems weirdly dedicated to <i>not</i> storing items in Elsewhere. Why?<br /> <br /> Fate-Shifting Solar Arete (#19) is a favored target for questionable balance so far. With the upgrade, it\u2019s an 80% increase in your expected number of successes \u2013 which has dramatic effects for, say, Crafting, sorcerous workings, or anything else that would assume a sane and fixed pool distribution. Alternatively, given its 1/day usage, it comes darned close to guaranteeing a Decisive attack lands. This would be a devastatingly powerful Charm in any one Ability \u2013 by far better than almost any dice-adder that\u2019s out there, except in usability. (And a number of the existing dice-adders are unlikely to pop more than once a day, if that.) Cross-Ability, it\u2019s kind of ridonkulous.<br /> <br /> Skillful Reappropriation (#20) is pretty fun \u2013 I know of characters who would get a lot of use out of that Charm. Reversal of Fortune (#21), by contrast, is ridiculously situational \u2013 how often do characters expect to get pickpocketed, that counter-theft becomes superior to just walking around using your normal super-pickpocketing?<br /> <br /> Null Anima Gloves (#26) seems to have no resistance mechanism. I\u2019m just not following this one: my hands start glowing (which seems odd to be \u201cnull anima\u201d), and the Mask of Winters can\u2019t attack me for thirty seconds\u2026 because\u2026? (Or at least, I assume the Mask qualifies, since Creature of Darkness <i>isn\u2019t defined</i>.) Shouldn\u2019t this have the Psyche keyword, given that it irresistibly compels behavior?<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Again, I think some of the simplest Charms are the best \u2013 \u201cI\u2019ma be a criminal now!\u201d is pretty great. Most of the stuff that\u2019s more-or-less lifted from 2e is solid.<br /> <i>No:</i> Fate-Shifting Solar Arete just feels completely out of place, and particularly out of proportion.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird</i>: Null Anima Gloves is this massive grab-bag of effects \u2013 there are half-a-dozen or more sub-powers you can choose with it. (And what\u2019s null anima about the gloves, anyway?) Also, why does this edition have beef with \u201cElsewhere?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:18:03-07:00","id":736424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=735958#post735958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few months ago, someone asked me: &quot;If you had to choose between a politician you respected and trusted, and one that you thought could get the job done, which would you choose?&quot; My response was that if I'm trusting politician X, then X is probably just very good at manipulating me, and I'm better off with Y.<br /> <br /> Then they stated which two politicians this exercise had been based on, and I realized that I did in fact trust X more than Y, and did in fact want X to get the nomination more than Y. The belief that I couldn't fully trust any politician was not sufficient to overwhelm my belief that X was being genuine. Now, it's possible that somebody more cynical would have stronger protective Intimacies to preserve their distrust, but the fact of the matter is that I was convinced of X's sincerity, and since I was convinced, the general rule stating that I shouldn't trust politicians seemed less applicable.<br /> <br /> All that to say: people are able to hold contradictory beliefs, at least for a time. Eventually, one may win out, but that doesn't necessarily happen immediately. &quot;All Anathema lie&quot; can and will coexist with &quot;this Anathema's all right,&quot; because that's how people's minds work. Then you can spend WP to ignore one of the things you believe, but which one you choose to ignore depends a lot on circumstance and the social atmosphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that would be great, if that charm actually said it did that. It doesn't. It doesn't automatically convince people to trust you against their better(?) judgement. All it says is that they succeed on a Read Intentions action, which does precisely nothing to mechanically affect the actions of that character. Any other effects you give it, such as forcing the DB to acknowledge that maybe <i>this </i>Anathema really isn't all that bad of a guy, is your own choice and is not an explicit mechanical effect of the charm.<br /> <br /> And as much as this game probably suffers from some sub-system bloat, I really like that they gave some good attention to some normally anemic areas, like sailing, investigation, hold-ups, etc. I appreciate the effort, even if the sheer number of subsystems could make Storytelling a game especially difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:45:45-07:00","id":736476,"title":"","content":"Seasoned Criminal Method is sneakily even better for crime-fighters than criminals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:52:42-07:00","id":736488,"title":"","content":"That's a good point.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> Good sweet heavens, I have more than another hundred pages to go of this - even before we get to martial arts/sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T08:48:29-07:00","id":738436,"title":"","content":"<u>Linguistics</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 33<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/0/5/4/23<br /> By Essence requirement: 10/7/11/3/2<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: None that I caught on first pass!<br /> <br /> Themes: Conceal messages, speak and be understood, understand when others are speaking, compel seemingly-nonsense behavior from your targets, write quickly.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Copy a book in seconds.</li> <li>Forge handwriting; render a perfect copy.</li> <li>Hide a message to a specific individual in another written message.</li> <li>As #3, but spoken instead of written.</li> <li>Double-9s (or 8s, or 7s, with repurchases) on written works.</li> <li>Interpret one statement in a foreign language, or parse \u201cabstruse language.\u201d</li> <li>Communicate via body language.</li> <li>Fuse two languages into a new language that speakers of either tongue can understand.</li> <li>Automatically sense the Intimacies behind a written work.</li> <li>After using #9, raise Resolve by Linguistics/2.</li> <li>Write in the style of another person.</li> <li>Write an anonymous letter, which readers will assume was written by a specific person.</li> <li>Compel the reader to announce the contents of the message.</li> <li>Prevent the reader from repeating the contents of the letter.</li> <li>Speak a language that everyone can understand.</li> <li>The character\u2019s Guile cannot be pierced while she\u2019s reading.</li> <li>Read faded scripts.</li> <li>Copy any magic embedded in a document.</li> <li>Edit a document without trace.</li> <li>Target forgets all known languages.</li> <li>Kill someone who has no sensible Intimacies.</li> <li>Convince someone of the truth of an assertion \u2013 but then have them do the opposite of that.</li> <li>Learn a new language.</li> <li>Maintain a perfect memory of a written work.</li> <li>Read a book at superhuman speed.</li> <li>Write a book in your miiiiiiiiiiind.</li> <li>Reduce time required to compose a work, though not the time to write it.</li> <li>Combine Simple Charms on a single work.</li> <li>Hold people spellbound as long as you speak (or as long as they read what you have written).</li> </ol><br /> Why are Letter-Within-A-Letter Technique and Subtle Speech Method (#3 and 4) two different Charms? Is there a meaningful difference here that wouldn\u2019t be covered by \u201cWhen used on a letter, ____; when used in a speech, _____\u201d?<br /> <br /> Sagacious Reading of Intent (#9) is narrow, but powerful \u2013 automatic knowledge of Intimacies offers some interesting possibilities. \u2026 And then we chain into Word-Shield Invocation (#10), which (1) only works after using SRoI, and (2) is a cheaper Excellency. Pass.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat Burning Question:\u201d says the sidebar, \u201cWhat happens if you combine Essence-Laden Missive and Voice Caging Calligraphy? A: You tell me.\u201d Guys, if the rest of your systems were clear and unambiguous in their interaction, this might be funny. As is, the humor\u2019s a little too dark for me.<br /> <br /> Essence-Laden Missive (#13) states that it compels the character to announce the message aloud, <i>as an Inspire action</i>. But inspire actions are emotional triggers, aren\u2019t they? Shouldn\u2019t this be a persuade action, since it\u2019s compelling a specific behavior?<br /> <br /> Single-Voice Kata (#15) includes callouts about how spirits and fair folk get mad at you for using it, which is an interesting flavor note \u2013 I\u2019m not sure whether that makes the Charm more or less useful, but it\u2019s definitely more interesting.<br /> <br /> Power-Snaring Image (#18) solves an old problem, where the Solar can make an amazing magical document and perfectly copy it, and yet the copy isn\u2019t magic. (Surely this implies that the Solar\u2019s writings really are magic, in any event, and not just very skillful \u2013 a copy would catch that.)<br /> <br /> Twisted Words Technique (#22) is\u2026 either crazy-powerful or not, I\u2019m not sure. The Charm itself suggests that it acts as an Inspire action, creating behavior \u2013 like the monk going to live with the prostitutes. But the <i>sidebar</i> seems to be explicit that it\u2019s only modifying Intimacies, kicking them up or down a level (in the direction opposite what it appears to do). If it works in the former way, it seems trivial to convince an Immaculate to abandon the Wyld Hunt (by getting him to agree that Solars must be hunted). In the latter case, you might weaken his Intimacy, but he\u2019s still probably going to try to kill you. The verbiage in the Charm talks about \u201cpersuasion caused by this Charm\u201d \u2013 but <i>persuade</i> is a system term, meaning \u201cinduce behavior.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rereading the opening parts of the Charm, it <i>does</i> seem like this is behavior-creation \u2013 \u201cthe target will feel overwhelmingly compelled <i>to act</i>\u2026\u201d So that is persuasion, and the Charm is correct. Does it <i>also</i> function as an Instill action, or is this an either/or? Does this trivially dispatch Immaculates, given that you\u2019re appealing to a very strong Intimacy and they can\u2019t spend Willpower to resist?<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t help but see Unbreakable Fascination Method (#29) as the old Metal Gear Solid \u201cleave out a magazine, totally distract the guards\u201d thing.<br /> <br /> This is just not an immediately inspiring tree. Lots of utility, but not a lot that fired my imagination \u2013 though that part may be me, rather than the Charms themselves.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Sagacious Reading of Intent.<br /> <i>No:</i> Mind-Scribing Method (#26), i.e., \u201cWrite a book in your head and copy it down later.\u201d That\u2019s a stunt, not two sessions\u2019 worth of XP.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Cup Boils Over (#21) just feels\u2026 well, honestly, it feels like it\u2019s there so that if someone ever says, \u201cIt seems like Intimacies are more liability than help,\u201d that the internet can reply, \u201cNo, because Cup Boils Over will kill you if you don\u2019t have Intimacies.\u201d If that\u2019s accurate, that\u2019s a pretty obnoxious treat-the-symptoms thing; if it\u2019s not, and it may not be, I\u2019m not sure how else to use this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:11:17-07:00","id":738751,"title":"","content":"Cup Boils Over is the coup de grace after you've spent several scenes convincing someone that everything they believe in is bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:44:27-07:00","id":738902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=738751#post738751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cup Boils Over is the coup de grace after you've spent several scenes convincing someone that everything they believe in is bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not just several scenes - that's &quot;I systematically hunted down and destroyed every Intimacy they had, which requires first building up other Intimacies from which to launch those attacks, and then <i>tearing back down</i> those Intimacies I just created, in a system where my target can generate new Intimacies spontaneously whenever it would seem to fit with his characterization.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, maybe that <i>is</i> the intended effect, but that's a pretty crazy barrier to entry - it would be far, far easier to convince someone to go play in traffic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:47:19-07:00","id":738910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=738751#post738751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cup Boils Over is the coup de grace after you've spent several scenes convincing someone that everything they believe in is bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the person at that point is basically a sad little marshmallow it just seems like a lot of effort when you could just as easily kill them in their sleep with Stealth and a pillow, or from a rooftop with Archery. <br /> <br /> It keeps getting touted as being super amazing but at the point it's applicable your opponent isn't remotely anything special to go up against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T11:26:51-07:00","id":739035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WhirlwindMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=736424#post736424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that would be great, if that charm actually said it did that. It doesn't. It doesn't automatically convince people to trust you against their better(?) judgement. All it says is that they succeed on a Read Intentions action, which does precisely nothing to mechanically affect the actions of that character. Any other effects you give it, such as forcing the DB to acknowledge that maybe <i>this </i>Anathema really isn't all that bad of a guy, is your own choice and is not an explicit mechanical effect of the charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm suggesting that it's difficult for people to think, &quot;I think I successfully read this person's intentions, but I probably only <i>think</i> so,&quot; even if nothing mechanically enforces that. That kind of thinking requires careful consideration, overwhelming dedication, and/or a distrust of your own skills (which is difficult for Exalted to manage). Can it be done? Sure. But my point was that it's hard. People don't like to assume that they failed at something when they can believe that they succeeded instead. The mechanics can't perfectly replicate the experience of being a person.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T11:41:19-07:00","id":739104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=738436#post738436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Twisted Words Technique (#22) is\u2026 either crazy-powerful or not, I\u2019m not sure. The Charm itself suggests that it acts as an Inspire action, creating behavior \u2013 like the monk going to live with the prostitutes. But the <i>sidebar</i> seems to be explicit that it\u2019s only modifying Intimacies, kicking them up or down a level (in the direction opposite what it appears to do). If it works in the former way, it seems trivial to convince an Immaculate to abandon the Wyld Hunt (by getting him to agree that Solars must be hunted). In the latter case, you might weaken his Intimacy, but he\u2019s still probably going to try to kill you. The verbiage in the Charm talks about \u201cpersuasion caused by this Charm\u201d \u2013 but <i>persuade</i> is a system term, meaning \u201cinduce behavior.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rereading the opening parts of the Charm, it <i>does</i> seem like this is behavior-creation \u2013 \u201cthe target will feel overwhelmingly compelled <i>to act</i>\u2026\u201d So that is persuasion, and the Charm is correct. Does it <i>also</i> function as an Instill action, or is this an either/or? Does this trivially dispatch Immaculates, given that you\u2019re appealing to a very strong Intimacy and they can\u2019t spend Willpower to resist?</div> </div> </div> </div>This charm feels like it's incredibly powerful and allows you to be Bugs Bunny, just from my read?<br /> <br /> &quot;Man, them dog people are whack, right?&quot;<br /> &quot;You're telling me, buddy.&quot;<br /> &quot;I seriously can't think of anything that would be worse than living with dog people.&quot;<br /> &quot;Exactly! I am totally a cat person.&quot;<br /> &quot;I think you should live with some dog people.&quot;<br /> &quot;Man, I'm gonna go live with some dog people!&quot;<br /> <br /> Between the charm and the sidebar, it seems like this leaves the intimacy intact on their sheet (&quot;Man, I can't stand dog people.&quot;) while the actions contradict that, and that someone has to apparently manipulate the social influence system to convince them &quot;Hey, you don't like dog people. Why are you living with dog people?&quot; to get the effect to snap. This would be less effective in a blunter society, but in places where you just don't <i>admit</i> the emperor is naked, it could be ridiculously powerful.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Hello Solar UMI with extra mind-screw. @_@","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T11:42:13-07:00","id":739117,"title":"","content":"Quite limited niche, but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733623-behemoth-slaying-missives\"> I think Cup Boils Over might work as to kill those nearly indestructible behemoths</a>. The ones who can read, at least XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T11:46:41-07:00","id":739148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739035#post739035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm suggesting that it's difficult for people to think, &quot;I think I successfully read this person's intentions, but I probably only <i>think</i> so,&quot; even if nothing mechanically enforces that. That kind of thinking requires careful consideration, overwhelming dedication, and/or a distrust of your own skills (which is difficult for Exalted to manage). Can it be done? Sure. But my point was that it's hard. People don't like to assume that they failed at something when they can believe that they succeeded instead. The mechanics can't perfectly replicate the experience of being a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect them to perfectly replicate being a person, but in this case, the mechanics are fully capable of handling what you're suggesting. If the charm also made a reflexive Instill action that attempted to give a minor intimacy of &quot;Believes His Motives (That Anathema Over There)&quot;, that'd do exactly what you'd describe. The average person would accept it, no question, your average Realm dragonblooded could resist it using a minor or major intimacy of &quot;Anathema are not to be trusted&quot;, and a devout Immaculate monk could probably call it unacceptable influence due to their defining intimacy of &quot;All anathema are evil&quot;. Or you could model it as a Persuade attempt to convince the people around to believe in you. Heck, you could probably make it work with an Inspire action with a magical twist or two from the base mechanics. There are plenty of ways you could accomplish &quot;Not only does this look true, but you believe that's it's true,&quot; and the charm instead interacts with mechanics that have zero explicit mechanical means of accomplishing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T11:55:52-07:00","id":739207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739117#post739117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite limited niche, but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733623-behemoth-slaying-missives\"> I think Cup Boils Over might work as to kill those nearly indestructible behemoths</a>. The ones who can read, at least XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw that post, and it was fabulous.<br /> <br /> Am now picturing a Monty Python-style &quot;Funniest Joke in the World&quot; used against Juggernaut. &quot;<b>THAT'S NOT FUNNY</b> - pffffhahahaha...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T11:59:13-07:00","id":739225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=736419#post736419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unshakeable Rogue\u2019s Spirit (#13) requires you to keep track of how much Initiative you <i>will have paid</i> from your <i>next</i> Join Battle roll, which just makes me shudder a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is nice for Black Claw Stylists despairing over their high Awareness + Wits pool. You see, one of the first BC charms requires at least one enemy to beat you to initiative, and there's no way, as far as I can tell, to intentionally reduce the number of dice you roll on Join Battle - this charm can help you with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:41:56-07:00","id":739313,"title":"","content":"<u>Lore</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 48<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/2/3/3/39(!)<br /> By Essence requirement: 7/7/20/9/5<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Reroll 6s until they disappear, \u201crecurring 10s,\u201d<br /> <br /> Themes: Give and take supernatural resources, train people, know everything past and future, CRAFT NEW WORLDS BY DINT OF YOUR SUPERIOR WILL, drop nukes.<br /> <br /> This is our third-largest tree so far, coming in behind Brawl and Craft. Don\u2019t have Lore 5? Probably not the Charm tree for you. On the other hand, this is probably one of the strongest Supernal entries \u2013 over a quarter of its Charms are E4-E5. Cry your bitter tears, Awareness!<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Protect an object or character from Wyld-twisting.</li> <li>Characters within short range are protected from the Wyld.</li> <li>Get ALL the Lore Specialties, and get bonuses when they apply.</li> <li>Teach the unteachable. Row row, fight da powa.</li> <li>Spend your XP to train someone else. Roll XP as dice at end of story; recover successes.</li> <li>Transfer motes to an ally.</li> <li>Transfer Willpower to an ally.</li> <li>Hide one lesson inside another.</li> <li>Reroll nonsuccesses when using #5.</li> <li>Gain bonuses when introducing/challenging facts.</li> <li>Reroll 6s when introducing/challenging facts.</li> <li>Reveal the function of an object.</li> <li>Accept wounds from an ally.</li> <li>Make #6 and #7 Reflexive, with bonuses.</li> <li>Use #5 to train many people at once.</li> <li>Use #5 to teach spells or Charms.</li> <li>Receive a vision of how to use an artifact.</li> <li>Gain Evocations for free.</li> <li>Add non-Charm dice to thinky problems, permanently.</li> <li>Push wounds onto a target.</li> <li>Drain motes from the target.</li> <li>Convert the target\u2019s personal motes to peripheral or vice-versa.</li> <li>Steal damage from an attack through your mystic mumblings.</li> <li>Regain 1m when you roll a 10 on a Lore roll.</li> <li>Reset your anima to dim.</li> <li>Burn out your anima, restoring motes to allies.</li> <li>Allow #6 and #7 to be used at range.</li> <li>Destroy Wyld-twisting effects.</li> <li>TEAR NEW REALITY FROM THE LAUGHING TEETH OF MADNESS.</li> <li>When using #29, create specialist workers.</li> <li>When using #29, gain bonus successes.</li> <li>Make artifact weapons using #29.</li> <li>Skip a roll when using #29.</li> <li>Make a book you thought up using Mind-Scribing Method.</li> <li>Grant Charms you don\u2019t know to a character (maybe you!).</li> <li>Predict the future, granting bonuses to those who follow your predictions and penalties to those who don\u2019t.</li> <li>Steal Willpower and Initiative by posing a riddle.</li> <li>Recover extra motes.</li> <li>Boost the effect of #24 to 8s, 9s, and 10s for one roll.</li> <li>Reduce cost of one use of #29.</li> <li>Gain double-8s on one use of #29.</li> <li>Build a manse using #29.</li> <li>Regenerate motes while using #29.</li> <li>Drop a nuke on an enemy nation from your basement. Yes, really.</li> <li>Gain 3wp.</li> <li>Trade motes and Initiative for Willpower.</li> <li>Reduce cost of #29</li> </ol>The entry-level Charms here are solid stuff \u2013 broad Wyld protections, big expansions of your breadth of knowledge. Really good Charms for many different concepts to pick up.<br /> <br /> Flowing Mind Prana just sort of hurts. \u201cTrain NPCs, but you\u2019ll pay roughly half the cost of the traits they gain\u201d is just not a fun notion, especially after already paying the 8 XP for the Charm. You could, I suppose, have someone else in the party pick up the same Charm and train each other \u2013 on alternating stories, I guess \u2013 but that\u2019s not <i>less</i> weird, and it potentially leaves the two of you quite a bit ahead of the rest of the party after the first few arcs. This really seems to be designed to feed off the Craft Charm that turns color points into real XP, which is great if you\u2019re a crafter, I suppose, and kind of an annoying barrier otherwise. Tireless Learner Method (#9) offers you the chance to sink <i>another</i> 8 XP into training Charms to up your average return to 75% of the XP invested. (\u201cYou can go over the original amount!\u201d it promises, as it inexplicably bills you an extra 1XP per use. Yes, and you can roll &gt;11 successes on 10 dice, but how often does that happen?)<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still not wild about how the Lore rules are so different from the entire rest of the game\u2019s resolution engine, but I do respect that the Charms here integrate well with them. Some oddities, though; Bottomless Wellspring Approach says it doubles extra successes when introducing/challenging facts \u2013 okay, but that doesn\u2019t seem to <i>do</i> anything. Facts are a flat difficulty, with no reward for grades of success.<br /> <br /> Truth-Rendering Gaze (#12) specifies that it\u2019s a Read Intentions action to figure out what an object is for. Okay, but what difference does that make?<br /> <br /> Essence Font Technique (#14) makes it hard to read your splat descriptions, or tell where one subheading ends and another begins. (I kid! I kid!) More seriously, it introduces <i>recurring 10s</i> as a system term for \u201creroll 10s until they stop appearing,\u201d which seems like it would be nice to have in use <i>somewhere other than this one Charm</i>.<br /> <br /> Selfsame Master Instructor (#15) seems to have an effect unrelated to its name; more to the point, it allows you to train someone else in Charms or spells. Er, can\u2019t you normally just <i>learn</i> Charms or spells? Is there actually a barrier this is overcoming?<br /> <br /> Hey, how does one figure out how to use an artifact <i>normally</i>? Sacred Relic Understanding (#17) suggest the answer is \u201ca high-difficulty Lore roll, <i>with this Charm</i>\u201d \u2013 which would have been my guess for how one does so <i>without</i> a Charm.<br /> <br /> Hi, there, Wake the Sleeper (#18). I\u2019m Fate-Shifting Solar Arete. With me, a stunt, and a point of Willpower, you should be able to average &gt;21 successes on a Lore roll, which is enough to grab <i>eight Evocations</i> off an Artifact 5 in one pop, at no Experience cost. That\u2019s 80 XP worth of goods per story; for reference, if you favor Lore and Larceny, you could buy the 14 Charms needed for this combo for just 112 XP, and you\u2019d still have all those Lore and Larceny Charms at the end.<br /> <br /> Force-Draining Whisper (#23) is a great Charm \u2013 it\u2019s a solid combat Charm in a very non-combat Ability, which feels like it\u2019ll fit well for a number of characters. It\u2026 doesn\u2019t really seem like a Clash effect, though?<br /> <br /> Flowing Essence Conversion (#25) would have been great in 2e, but I feel <i>certain</i> there\u2019s some better way to reset an anima banner in 3e. Like, say, the very next Charm. (The Charm also doesn\u2019t seem to trust us to know what the Mute keyword does.)<br /> <br /> Power-Restoring Invocation (#26) loses the Perilous keyword at E5. Since it costs Initiative, though, this still does\u2026 precisely nothing. (This section in general is really inconsistent about saying \u201cIgnore this requirement if Lore is your Supernal\u201d \u2013 Force-Draining Whisper, for instance, lacks it. Has <i>any</i> other section bothered with that?) Er, couldn\u2019t half the text of this Charm be eliminated by adding \u201c3a\u201d to its cost?<br /> <br /> HECK YEAH WYLD-SHAPING TECHNIQUE (#29). This has been one of the most absurd Charms in past editions \u2013 either it threatened to kill you with every use, or it gave you anything you could ever want. 3e appears to <i>finally</i> chart a middle course that is crazy-useful but not <i>outright better</i> than most alternatives. I really like the push-your-luck mechanic of making and remaking the world until it fits the pattern you want. It does seem to contradict itself, though \u2013 it says at one moment that you need the deep Wyld for it to work, and in the next that you can shape gold \u201cat Creation\u2019s rim.\u201d Are we to understand that the middlemarches are the rim? Has that been explained anywhere?<br /> <br /> One note \u2013 WST says to \u201cremove 1 from the roll result.\u201d \u201cRemove\u201d here is clearly \u201csubtract,\u201d but \u201cremove 1\u201d is awfully close to terminology that does something rather different.<br /> <br /> You <i>are</i> going to get mobbed by raksha if you use this Charm. I don\u2019t understand the sentence relating number of demesnes to successes \u201cspent on upgrades to its area\u201d \u2013 the example given seems to contradict the text. Once you have Wyld-Called Weapon (#32), this is still pretty clearly the fast, efficient way to make weapons \u2013 again, if you can hold off the raksha.<br /> <br /> Prophet of Seventeen Cycles (#36) has inconsistent rules and examples. The rules say: if you follow the prediction, you get a bonus, and otherwise you get a penalty. Well and good. The example says: you predict Mnemon will muster forces this summer; if she does, she gets a bonus, if she doesn\u2019t, she gets a penalty. Okay. <i>Then</i> the rules say that if you <i>attack</i> Mnemon this summer, you take penalties. What? Where did that come from?<br /> <br /> Unstoppable Magnus Approach (#45) lets you convert motes and Initiative into Willpower. It also comes with a free sidebar, chiding you for slowing down the battle by converting Initiative into Willpower. Pick one! (The best fix I\u2019ve seen so far allows you to <i>substitute</i> paying m/I somewhere that you would <i>otherwise</i> pay 1wp. That seems like it avoids the issue, though either way it\u2019s awfully pricey compared to Integrity\u2019s 4m:1wp conversion rate.)<br /> <br /> My overall impression is that this is a very solid tree, albeit one with some Charms I wouldn't touch with a ten-foot pole. That said, it also feels as though it was written out of sequence with most of the rest of the book - it's missing some standard terminology (spending anima levels), adds some non-standard verbiage (explaining the Mute or Supernal keywords to us), and introduces some terms the rest of the book never picks up on (&quot;recurring 10s&quot;).<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> HECK YEAH WYLD-SHAPING TECHNIQUE.<br /> <i>No:</i> Tome-Rearing Gesture (#34). \u201cI can Wyld-Shape a book!\u201d Um\u2026 good for you?<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird</i>: God-King\u2019s Shrike (#44). \u201cNuke a region from your basement\u201d feels entirely out of proportion with the scale of the effects we\u2019ve seen so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-29-2015, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:46:07-07:00","id":739324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739313#post739313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flowing Mind Prana just sort of hurts. \u201cTrain NPCs, but you\u2019ll pay roughly half the cost of the traits they gain\u201d is just not a fun notion, especially after already paying the 8 XP for the Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you assume it's for teaching NPCs? You get a lore-using PC to amplify all the XP that your circle gains by teaching other PCs and then recouping a bunch of the XP they spent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:49:57-07:00","id":739333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739324#post739324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you assume it's for teaching NPCs? You get a lore-using PC to amplify all the XP that your circle gains by teaching other PCs and then recouping a bunch of the XP they spent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because &quot;Hey, Bob, you know how we all have the same amount of XP? How would you feel about giving us half of yours?&quot; is not a table dynamic I have ever seen someone volunteer for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:53:28-07:00","id":739342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739333#post739333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because &quot;Hey, Bob, you know how we all have the same amount of XP? How would you feel about giving us half of yours?&quot; is not a table dynamic I have ever seen someone volunteer for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got two groups for 3e, and both of them have a player who decided to take Flowing Mind Prana because they liked the idea of handing XP out to their fellow PCs. Just because a certain charm isn't fun for you doens't mean nobody will like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:54:24-07:00","id":739344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739333#post739333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because &quot;Hey, Bob, you know how we all have the same amount of XP? How would you feel about giving us half of yours?&quot; is not a table dynamic I have ever seen someone volunteer for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, in my Werewolf game, a player of mine has his concept built and working. Sure, he <i>could</i> get more powers or stats, but that breaks his character development a little too fast for his liking so he's just piling XP, uncertain of what to do with it. He asked if he could give this XP to others, but I said no (because the other players want it to min-max, not because I hate the player)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:56:40-07:00","id":739349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739313#post739313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prophet of Seventeen Cycles (#36) has inconsistent rules and examples. The rules say: if you follow the prediction, you get a bonus, and otherwise you get a penalty. Well and good. The example says: you predict Mnemon will muster forces this summer; if she does, she gets a bonus, if she doesn\u2019t, she gets a penalty. Okay. <i>Then</i> the rules say that if you <i>attack</i> Mnemon this summer, you take penalties. What? Where did that come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Her player may then make a pronouncement against an ongoing project based on knowledge her studies reveal, creating bonuses for those who act in accordance with her accurate predictions, and penalties for those who go against them.&quot; In the latter part of the example, the rebels are going against the prediction by depriving Mnemon of the breathing room to consolidate her forces while gathering resources until winter. Therefore, the rebels suffer the penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:57:15-07:00","id":739350,"title":"","content":"#19 is second only to FSSA in its system-breaking ability. It's a capbreaker that applies to Craft and Sorcerous Workings. fowaief;wje","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:02:37-07:00","id":739395,"title":"","content":"I keep wondering if GKS is actually making a disaster happen by virtue of conveniently predicting it (where he disaster otherwise wouldn't happen), or is it taking the concept of introducing a fact to its logical extreme. <br /> <br /> Also if it's meant to be the former, that is totally a Sid Charm, not Solar, and I will fight with knives anyone who disagrees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:06:43-07:00","id":739406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739342#post739342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got two groups for 3e, and both of them have a player who decided to take Flowing Mind Prana because they liked the idea of handing XP out to their fellow PCs. Just because a certain charm isn't fun for you doens't mean nobody will like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool. The reactions I have here are certainly not intended to stand in for &quot;the reactions anyone will ever have to this material&quot; - they're my reactions, and the reactions I would anticipate from the people I have gamed with over the past decade. If the Charm would be a hit in your group, that's great!<br /> <br /> Also, I do consider PC-on-PC use, a couple of lines down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:10:25-07:00","id":739417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739349#post739349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Her player may then make a pronouncement against an ongoing project based on knowledge her studies reveal, creating bonuses for those who act in accordance with her accurate predictions, and penalties for those who go against them.&quot; In the latter part of the example, the rebels are going against the prediction by depriving Mnemon of the breathing room to consolidate her forces while gathering resources until winter. Therefore, the rebels suffer the penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the actually-provided prophecy doesn't say anything about Mnemon having &quot;breathing room.&quot; It says:<br /> -Mnemon won't attack until fall at the earliest.<br /> -Over the summer, she'll consolidate her forces.<br /> -Over the summer, she'll conserve water and gather resources.<br /> <br /> That's it! There's no rider constraining the rebel activity at all - indeed, Mnemon spending the summer consolidating would seem to make summer an ideal time for them to attack.<br /> <br /> Edit: Rephrasing a little, I understand the prophecy to describe Mnemon's plans. If Mnemon's actions are in accord with her predicted plans, then sure, she gets a bonus. But &quot;Hey, we're going to come kill you now, Mnemon,&quot; has nothing to do with Mnemon's plans - she's doing a great job of consolidating forces, right up until she gets murdalized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-29-2015, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:12:41-07:00","id":739419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739395#post739395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep wondering if GKS is actually making a disaster happen by virtue of conveniently predicting it (where he disaster otherwise wouldn't happen), or is it taking the concept of introducing a fact to its logical extreme.<br /> <br /> Also if it's meant to be the former, that is totally a Sid Charm, not Solar, and I will fight with knives anyone who disagrees.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty clearly the former, I think. &quot;Her consciousness is recognized, in turn, by the universe. In this instance, what the Solar realizes she causes to happen.&quot; Plus, you know, canceling the prophecy is an act of <i>mercy</i>, which implies control over the outcome.<br /> <br /> I will, however, stand at your side in the knife-fight. Solar reality-hacking effects rub me very much the wrong way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:16:02-07:00","id":739428,"title":"","content":"Thirding the &quot;this is a quintessential Sidereal charm&quot; objection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:16:25-07:00","id":739431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739417#post739417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the actually-provided prophecy doesn't say anything about Mnemon having &quot;breathing room.&quot; It says:<br /> -Mnemon won't attack until fall at the earliest.<br /> -Over the summer, she'll consolidate her forces.<br /> -Over the summer, she'll conserve water and gather resources.<br /> <br /> That's it! There's no rider constraining the rebel activity at all - indeed, Mnemon spending the summer consolidating would seem to make summer an ideal time for them to attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>The prediction isn't &quot;Mnemon will choose to do this,&quot; it's &quot;This is what will happen.&quot; The rebel attack prevents Mnemon from consolidating and gathering resources. Whether she intended to do so or not is immaterial to the prediction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:18:14-07:00","id":739437,"title":"","content":"One explanation may be that, since the Solar did not predict a rebel attack, such a rebel attack would go against this prediction.<br /> <br /> A problem I see with this is that the most efficient prediction is simply a variant of &quot;We win&quot;. &quot;The rebels will defeat Mnemon's troops while said troops are consolidating their forces for winter&quot; - now, anything that goes against &quot;the rebels will win&quot; takes a dice penalty.<br /> <br /> I kind of feel like stuff like that should be excluded, but I don't see how.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:21:41-07:00","id":739444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739431#post739431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The prediction isn't &quot;Mnemon will choose to do this,&quot; it's &quot;This is what will happen.&quot; The rebel attack prevents Mnemon from consolidating and gathering resources. Whether she intended to do so or not is immaterial to the prediction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I find that a very non-obvious reading; I think I'd call shenanigans on any Storyteller who claimed that in response to the given prophecy. I <i>do</i> read it as &quot;Mnemon will do this.&quot;<br /> <br /> At a minimum, your reading suggests this is a very bad prophecy, and what should have been said was, &quot;Mnemon's going to <i>try to</i> consolidate her forces over the summer, but she'll fail when we kill her.&quot; That has effectively no downside - and if we can avoid the downside through that trivial of a text manipulation, I'd prefer a reading where the prophecy says, &quot;This is what they're going to try to do,&quot; and just leave it at that. You get bonuses if you <i>do</i> try to do [thing], and penalties if you don't try to do [thing], and what everyone else does is up to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-29-2015, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:22:00-07:00","id":739445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739333#post739333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because &quot;Hey, Bob, you know how we all have the same amount of XP? How would you feel about giving us half of yours?&quot; is not a table dynamic I have ever seen someone volunteer for.</div> </div> </div> </div>How else could it work? If it's a guaranteed gain or even a break-even for the loremaster, then every party should have one. As it is, over the long term the character typically won't lose much XP and will make the party much stronger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:24:10-07:00","id":739453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739419#post739419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty clearly the former, I think. &quot;Her consciousness is recognized, in turn, by the universe. In this instance, what the Solar realizes she causes to happen.&quot; Plus, you know, canceling the prophecy is an act of <i>mercy</i>, which implies control over the outcome.<br /> <br /> I will, however, stand at your side in the knife-fight. Solar reality-hacking effects rub me very much the wrong way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy fix:<br /> <br /> 1. This is just an introduction of a super fact<br /> 2. Screw the &quot;the universe bends to your will senpai!!!!!&quot; bit<br /> 3. The Solar's &quot;mercy&quot; if it's canceled is rewritten as the Solar saying their prediction was factually wrong, as in, &quot;whoops, I read this rainfall report wrong, you won't actually have a thousand year flood this winter! My bad!&quot; Or was made on the basis of bad facts like &quot;this was predicated on accurate crop yield reports but corrupt bureaucrats have been deliberately under reporting the crop yields to skim some of the tax for themselves, and under the REAL numbers there's no chance of famine!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:28:34-07:00","id":739463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739453#post739453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Easy fix:<br /> <br /> 1. This is just an introduction of a super fact<br /> 2. Screw the &quot;the universe bends to your will senpai!!!!!&quot; bit<br /> 3. The Solar's &quot;mercy&quot; if it's canceled is rewritten as the Solar saying their prediction was factually wrong, as in, &quot;whoops, I read this rainfall report wrong, you won't actually have a thousand year flood this winter! My bad!&quot; Or was made on the basis of bad facts like &quot;this was predicated on accurate crop yield reports but corrupt bureaucrats have been deliberately under reporting the crop yields to skim some of the tax for themselves, and under the REAL numbers there's no chance of famine!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, it's not hard to fix. (I'm likely to fix it with a magic marker.) But as written, pretty sure it's a reality-hack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739445#post739445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How else could it work? If it's a guaranteed gain or even a break-even for the loremaster, then every party should have one. As it is, over the long term the character typically won't lose much XP and will make the party much stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious answer is &quot;as per Tiger-Warrior Training,&quot; perhaps with a rider about other trained PCs incurring XP-debt. That makes it useful for training your scholar-king NPCs without any risk of XP-multiplication or -wasting, and you still <i>can</i> train other PCs if you want to - it becomes a &quot;bypass training times&quot; Charm rather than a &quot;generate XP imbalances&quot; Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-29-2015, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:31:11-07:00","id":739468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739444#post739444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I find that a very non-obvious reading; I think I'd call shenanigans on any Storyteller who claimed that in response to the given prophecy. I <i>do</i> read it as &quot;Mnemon will do this.&quot;<br /> <br /> At a minimum, your reading suggests this is a very bad prophecy, and what should have been said was, &quot;Mnemon's going to <i>try to</i> consolidate her forces over the summer, but she'll fail when we kill her.&quot; That has effectively no downside - and if we can avoid the downside through that trivial of a text manipulation, I'd prefer a reading where the prophecy says, &quot;This is what they're going to try to do,&quot; and just leave it at that. You get bonuses if you <i>do</i> try to do [thing], and penalties if you don't try to do [thing], and what everyone else does is up to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the flavor text of the Charm, it's clear that this isn't prophecy in the sense of, &quot;The stars and the whims of Fate compel the actions of those involved.&quot; It's more along the lines of, &quot;My study of geography and logistics tells me that the situation is favorable to Mnemon if she retrenches, and unfavorable if she attacks.&quot; It's not that some higher power is casting mystical fortune on Mnemon and ill-luck on the rebels. Rather, you've assessed that one should never get involved in a land war in Asia, and the rebels decided to get involved in a land war in Asia. And perhaps they can win the land war in Asia! But the odds are against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:37:49-07:00","id":739510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739468#post739468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the flavor text of the Charm, it's clear that this isn't prophecy in the sense of, &quot;The stars and the whims of Fate compel the actions of those involved.&quot; It's more along the lines of, &quot;My study of geography and logistics tells me that the situation is favorable to Mnemon if she retrenches, and unfavorable if she attacks.&quot; It's not that some higher power is casting mystical fortune on Mnemon and ill-luck on the rebels. Rather, you've assessed that one should never get involved in a land war in Asia, and the rebels decided to get involved in a land war in Asia. And perhaps they can win the land war in Asia! But the odds are against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see that this is at odds with my suggested prophecy - it just requires the addition of some easy fluff text. &quot;Mnemon thinks that the hot summer months are the time to rebuild her forces - but she doesn't know this land like we do, and she doesn't know that the valley ravines will stay wet all summer long. She'll waste time conserving water, right up until the day we fall on her and destroy her.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We're going to win!&quot; prophecies are trivial to justify, whatever the narrative roots. If you're constrained to, &quot;These are the plans so-and-so will follow,&quot; that's a much more limited - and much more interesting - Charm, because it takes, &quot;Eh, we win&quot; off the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-29-2015, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:51:13-07:00","id":739538,"title":"","content":"Insofar as you're insisting that the example given in the text of the Charm itself is wrong, and that in fact it means much the opposite of what it's intended to mean and that the Charm functions in a manner opposite to its presented intention, we have no basis for discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:57:39-07:00","id":739556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739538#post739538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insofar as you're insisting that the example given in the text of the Charm itself is wrong, and that in fact it means much the opposite of what it's intended to mean and that the Charm functions in a manner opposite to its presented intention, we have no basis for discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>My argument is basically twofold:<br /> 1) That the way the example is described <i>appears to be</i> at odds with the way the rest of the Charm is described.<br /> 2) That if it's actually the example that's correct, and the rules-description that's not coming across, then the Charm encourages lawyer-wording prophecies so as to give the same net effect as if the example was <i>not</i> correct - and that this is an undesirable state of affairs.<br /> <br /> Edit: I feel like you and I are sniping at each other, here, and I'm not sure why that's happened. I have a lot of respect for your work, and for some of the really great ideas in the book - but it's precisely because I want the game to be amazing that I'm tilting as hard as I can at the stuff that doesn't seem (to me!) as though it works. I thought we were exploring the plausibility of different readings and their consequences; your last post sounds as if you think I'm just being contrary for the sake of being contrary, and that's not at all what I want to convey. Perhaps my posts have sounded similarly harsh, though - tone, the internet, etc. Could we reset a little bit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-29-2015, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:07:52-07:00","id":739581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739556#post739556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument is basically twofold:<br /> 1) That the way the example is described <i>appears to be</i> at odds with the way the rest of the Charm is described.<br /> 2) That if it's actually the example that's correct, and the rules-description that's not coming across, then the Charm encourages lawyer-wording prophecies so as to give the same net effect as if the example was <i>not</i> correct.<br /> <br /> If that puts us an impassable distance apart, that's unfortunate - but this doesn't seem like an unreasonable line of argument.<br /> <br /> Edit: I feel like you and I are sniping at each other, here, and I'm not sure why that's happened. I have a lot of respect for your work, and for some of the really great ideas in the book - but it's precisely because I want the book to be amazing that I'm tilting as hard as I can at the stuff that doesn't seem (to me!) as though it works. I thought we were exploring the plausibility of different readings and their consequences; your last post sounds as if you think I'm just being contrary for the sake of being contrary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The example reads fine to me. It predicts two things will happen:<br /> <br /> 1) Mnemon will not attack the rebels before fall.<br /> 2) She will spend the summer months consolidating forces, gathering resources and conserving water.<br /> <br /> It then specifies that if Mnemon herself takes action to violate one of those (in this example, #1, by attacking early), she will take a penalty. If the rebels take action to violate one of those (in this example, #2, by interrupting the prediction that she would be consolidating forces etc. during the summer rather than fighting rebels), then they will get a penalty.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that I would have prefered a somewhat clearer example, as all of these lore prediction actions and charms are opening up questions of the in-game mechanism by which these things work. A prediction involving the choices of one actor ascribing penalties to another actor based on their own choice took a few readings to grok, but I think Minton's details clear up any further issues I had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:17:20-07:00","id":739603,"title":"","content":"My reading of that charm was the Loremaster saying &quot;The weather will be very bad for a Summer campaign (based on my study of meteorology) so the smartest thing for her to do is gather resources for a winter campaign instead&quot;. So of course the rebels take a penalty when they try attacking in the summer, because the Solar has predicted that the weather will be bad for fighting, which is why Mnemon is delaying in the first place.<br /> If you predict that a series of heavy storms will hit Lathe and so the smuggler business there will suffer a hit, that still causes storms to hit Lathe and mess up other stuff as well, like regular trade or maybe a naval campaign that was supported to be launched. If you predict a plague to hit a City and cause a famine, that may cause the plague to spread even if you didn't specifically include that in your prediction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:40:19-07:00","id":739666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739395#post739395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep wondering if GKS is actually making a disaster happen by virtue of conveniently predicting it (where he disaster otherwise wouldn't happen), or is it taking the concept of introducing a fact to its logical extreme.<br /> <br /> Also if it's meant to be the former, that is totally a Sid Charm, not Solar, and I will fight with knives anyone who disagrees.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'll pick up a butterknife and wave it halfheartedly in your general direction.<br /> <br /> I'd argue it isn't really a Sid charm on the grounds that Sids are more about influencing reality in more sideways and indirect fashions, usually by rewarding behavior they want and punishing behavior they don't want by inflicting curses and blessings on someone by manipulating the threads of Fate.<br /> <br /> GKS is more a brute force method, saying &quot;THIS WILL HAPPEN, DEAL WITH IT&quot; by looking so closely at the fabric of reality that they hit one of the hidden flaw points in Creation and cause a cascade of events that culminates in the utter ruin that they were attempting to investigate. There's an Occult charm to that effect, and an Integrity charm that lets you temporarily fuse with reality at a fundamental level, so I don't think it's too out of their themes to declare a fact as true.<br /> <br /> Plus, Astrology is probably going to be way more versatile, so Sids will still trump Solars in manipulating causality. As they should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 10-29-2015, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:44:24-07:00","id":739680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739603#post739603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading of that charm was the Loremaster saying &quot;The weather will be very bad for a Summer campaign (based on my study of meteorology) so the smartest thing for her to do is gather resources for a winter campaign instead&quot;. So of course the rebels take a penalty when they try attacking in the summer, because the Solar has predicted that the weather will be bad for fighting, which is why Mnemon is delaying in the first place.<br /> If you predict that a series of heavy storms will hit Lathe and so the smuggler business there will suffer a hit, that still causes storms to hit Lathe and mess up other stuff as well, like regular trade or maybe a naval campaign that was supported to be launched. If you predict a plague to hit a City and cause a famine, that may cause the plague to spread even if you didn't specifically include that in your prediction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The charm doesn't really say that, though. It says you do some research and then say &quot;Boy, there are some really nasty things that could go wrong if she tries to invade in the summer, so, being a smart tactician, I'm sure she'll decide to consolidate her forces and wait until fall to attack.&quot; Then, if she attacks, just like you predicted, all sorts of things can go wrong. It doesn't say that if she doesn't attack, all the elemental attacks and resource shortages happen <i>anyway</i>, just to other people. Maybe they do? But you're not making a prediction about the world in general, you are, to quote the charm text, making &quot;a pronouncement against an ongoing project.&quot; That's the key disconnect here, I think. Are you making a &quot;pronouncement against a project,&quot; which implies this charm targets the project itself, and doesn't affect outside things, or are you making predictions about the state of the world that leads to certain project choices being advantageous? Eric is saying it's the latter, which seems to be supported by the example, but I think the former is a perfectly reasonable reading of the mechanical part of the text. A bit of rewording of the charm text and the example would probably help avoid this confusion and would be pretty easy to do.<br /> <br /> Honestly, my bigger concern is how vague the whole thing is. What does &quot;vastly more successful and easier to complete than otherwise&quot; mean? Sure, for the NPC army in the example, the storyteller can just hand-wave it pretty easily, but what if I make a prediction about a Manse I'm building? What does that do for me? Can I suddenly complete it months ahead of schedule? Do the magical materials I need just show up on my doorstep? And how big of penalties do I get to my rolls if I then decide to violate my prediction? And why is it only the first War rolls that get penalized in the example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:47:32-07:00","id":739688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739444#post739444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I find that a very non-obvious reading; I think I'd call shenanigans on any Storyteller who claimed that in response to the given prophecy. I <i>do</i> read it as &quot;Mnemon will do this.&quot;<br /> <br /> At a minimum, your reading suggests this is a very bad prophecy, and what should have been said was, &quot;Mnemon's going to <i>try to</i> consolidate her forces over the summer, but she'll fail when we kill her.&quot; That has effectively no downside - and if we can avoid the downside through that trivial of a text manipulation, I'd prefer a reading where the prophecy says, &quot;This is what they're going to try to do,&quot; and just leave it at that. You get bonuses if you <i>do</i> try to do [thing], and penalties if you don't try to do [thing], and what everyone else does is up to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, Eric's explanation is also how I interpreted it on first read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:59:06-07:00","id":739748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739688#post739688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, Eric's explanation is also how I interpreted it on first read.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it is sounding like that's the more common reading, and that the one WWM and I have is the less common, at least per our teensy sample size.<br /> <br /> I can only say that I found it <i>very</i> confusing. Some of this may come from playing Legends of the Wulin, which has very similar prediction mechanics, but would not do something like the latter part of the Charm here? That's obviously not the Charm's fault, if that is the explanatory factor - I'm just trying to sort out what the common elements could be.<br /> <br /> In any event, I would prefer the Charm specifically bless some course of action, at the expense of cursing the others - that'd mean your enemies could, say, throw obstacles into the way of your one blessed route in order to force you out of it, without themselves being cursed for interfering with the <i>outcome</i> of the blessed route. As is, &quot;I foresee victory in all my endeavors, because reasons&quot; seems too easy of a prophecy to stack on once every few days.<br /> <br /> (I also think that it'd be nice to have some mechanical hooks to hang its effects on, but that probably ties back to the fact that there's not a project system per se.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T15:09:14-07:00","id":739773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739748#post739748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of this may come from playing Legends of the Wulin, which has very similar prediction mechanics, but would not do something like the latter part of the Charm here? That's obviously not the Charm's fault, if that is the explanatory factor - I'm just trying to sort out what the common elements could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking the same thing. I might have to stat up Blind Lotus as a Twilight with this charm just for kicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T15:19:45-07:00","id":739826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739463#post739463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious answer is &quot;as per Tiger-Warrior Training,&quot; perhaps with a rider about other trained PCs incurring XP-debt. That makes it useful for training your scholar-king NPCs without any risk of XP-multiplication or -wasting, and you still <i>can</i> train other PCs if you want to - it becomes a &quot;bypass training times&quot; Charm rather than a &quot;generate XP imbalances&quot; Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of the charm is to build up the rest of the circle, to be a legendary scholar or sifu. Look at all the other charms here to lend essence, WP, and health to allies. This is along the same lines, except that the character is permanently strengthening others.<br /> <br /> Making NPCs better can happen off screen and without dice to roll or stats to look at, unless they're actually fighting alongside you or doing something else in a tense scene, rather than in the background of the game.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what &quot;risk&quot; there is to multiplying or losing xp. It's not like that sentence accidentally wrote itself. The deliberate result of these charms is that the character may (probably will) come out a little behind in an effort to build up the rest of the party. If you mean that risks some harm to the game, well, it's not like we have tightly calibrated recommendations for encounter difficulty that this is throwing off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T15:51:32-07:00","id":739904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739826#post739826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of the charm is to build up the rest of the circle, to be a legendary scholar or sifu. Look at all the other charms here to lend essence, WP, and health to allies. This is along the same lines, except that the character is permanently strengthening others.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>A</i> point, sure. But there's an upgrade here that lets the Charm work on groups of people at once - &quot;train NPCs&quot; is pretty clearly one of its purposes, given that play groups don't normally run 15-25 people.<br /> <br /> Again, I addressed both &quot;train PCs&quot; and &quot;train NPCs&quot; in the original post. What are we arguing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-29-2015, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T16:05:41-07:00","id":739923,"title":"","content":"Supernal lore characters at lower essence still benefit from training up to Essence x 5 people. Since NPCs don't use xp or standard stats in this book it would be odd to train them this way.<br /> <br /> I don't see the point in any charm to train NPCs to be better at administering your organization or city or whatever - that's too much of a purely narrative benefit even for me, especially in light of the leadership system. Bureaucracy takes care of things more directly, not bothering with NPC statblocks.<br /> <br /> Training times also seem like a bad thing to write charms around, since a lot of groups ignore or change them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T16:17:35-07:00","id":739965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739923#post739923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal lore characters at lower essence still benefit from training up to Essence x 5 people. Since NPCs don't use xp or standard stats in this book it would be odd to train them this way.<br /> <br /> I don't see the point in any charm to train NPCs to be better at administering your organization or city or whatever - that's too much of a purely narrative benefit even for me, especially in light of the leadership system. Bureaucracy takes care of things more directly, not bothering with NPC statblocks.<br /> <br /> Training times also seem like a bad thing to write charms around, since a lot of groups ignore or change them.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs* I didn't write the Charm. For a non-Supernal character, it works on a minimum of 15 people. I'm... pretty sure that means <i>somebody</i> thinks it's supposed to apply to NPCs at least a chunk of the time.<br /> <br /> Edited a couple of times: If granting purely narrative benefits doesn't feel sufficiently useful to you, I mean, I'm sympathetic to that, but it's hardly the only Charm in that category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-29-2015, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T17:59:05-07:00","id":740350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739965#post739965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* I didn't write the Charm. For a non-Supernal character, it works on a minimum of 15 people. I'm... pretty sure that means <i>somebody</i> thinks it's supposed to apply to NPCs at least a chunk of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're non-supernal, the charm helps out 3 others at full effect and 15 more at reduced effect when you learn it. I doubt many circles are big enough for that to matter, but if you have, idk, 7 people then this still covers them. My read is that it's meant to work well for more typical circles even with an Essence 1 user. If it's meant for NPCs it needs errata since they don't have xp or anything to spend it on. The fact that NPCs aren't rolling off screen in any rules I can find (Bureaucracy, leadership, etc) leads me to believe that the charm isn't directed at them though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=739965#post739965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edited a couple of times: If granting purely narrative benefits doesn't feel sufficiently useful to you, I mean, I'm sympathetic to that, but it's hardly the only Charm in that category.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a black and white thing. Improvements to the non-rated skills of your off-screen helpers would be <i>purely</i> narrative, and just as easily obtained by declaring that you spend some free time working with your dudes on their stuff. I mean, spending xp to boost your circle is one thing, but who is throwing xp down a well that doesn't even exist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T18:09:50-07:00","id":740374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=740350#post740350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're non-supernal, the charm helps out 3 others at full effect and 15 more at reduced effect when you learn it. I doubt many circles are big enough for that to matter, but if you have, idk, 7 people then this still covers them. My read is that it's meant to work well for more typical circles even with an Essence 1 user. If it's meant for NPCs it needs errata since they don't have xp or anything to spend it on. The fact that NPCs aren't rolling off screen in any rules I can find (Bureaucracy, leadership, etc) leads me to believe that the charm isn't directed at them though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars do get Bureaucracy Charms that give die bonuses to their NPC minions for offscreen tasks. I think that might happen in Integrity, too.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's worth the Charm purchase, just that there doesn't seem to be any good reason to make it scale up to 25 if it isn't meant for that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not a black and white thing. Improvements to the non-rated skills of your off-screen helpers would be <i>purely</i> narrative, and just as easily obtained by declaring that you spend some free time working with your dudes on their stuff. I mean, spending xp to boost your circle is one thing, but who is throwing xp down a well that doesn't even exist? </div> </div> </div>This is, basically, my original critique of the Charm. If we differ as to whether we believe the writers thought someone would want to do that, that's probably the source of our argument.<br /> <br /> (I would want to do it, though, if it wasn't for the XP costs. &quot;Gonna train up a city of philosopher-kings&quot; was an ambition of a past character of mine. That this doesn't really make sense to do with the Charm as written is... yeah, basically my issue with it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T18:10:26-07:00","id":740375,"title":"","content":"<u>Medicine</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 23<br /> By Ability requirement: 2/0/4/3/14<br /> By Essence requirement: 5/6/6/4/2<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Reduce Excellency to 1m/2 dice, free full Excellency<br /> <br /> Themes: Heal any injury, sickness, or poison, probably on the cheap, potentially rapidly, and <i>certainly</i> with as many successes as you\u2019ll ever need.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Grant target bonuses to resist disease.</li> <li>Cure disease immediately.</li> <li>Restore health levels immediately.</li> <li>Convert target\u2019s aggravated damage to lethal.</li> <li>Perfectly diagnose an illness.</li> <li>Gain bonuses to treat illness, permanently.</li> <li>Perform an hour of treatment in seconds.</li> <li>Remove a magical crippling injury mid-combat.</li> <li>Negate the target\u2019s wound penalties, though target cannot be active.</li> <li>Grant temporary -0 health levels.</li> <li>Cause a poison to disperse after its next interval.</li> <li>Convert aggravated damage, or cure bashing/lethal, instantly.</li> <li>As #7, but the patient also recovers on their feet in seconds.</li> <li>Restore missing limbs, regrow eyes, or treat madness.</li> <li>Regenerate motes and willpower, and continue to do while making Medicine rolls.</li> <li>Spend health levels for motes for Medicine Charms.</li> <li>Remove target\u2019s wound penalties; if target is active, doctor takes -1 penalties.</li> <li>Medicine Excellency is permanently 1m/2 dice.</li> <li>Use a Medicine Charm without paying its cost.</li> <li>1/scene free full Excellency.</li> <li>Reroll non-successes in Medicine.</li> <li>1/day, double Medicine successes.</li> <li>1/story, double-7s on a Medicine roll.</li> </ol>What is the intended use case of Touch of Blissful Release (#9)? It feels like most typical PC behavior would immediately negate its effects \u2013 who is it for?<br /> <br /> Hm. I think I would have assumed that Instant Treatment Methodology (#7) put the target back on their feet immediately\u2026 if Body-Sculpting Essence Method (#13) hadn\u2019t included a call-out saying that that\u2019s what <i>it</i> does. Am I missing something here?<br /> <br /> Wholeness-Restoring Meditation is <i>nice</i>. Broadly powerful, wide range of uses \u2013 feels very worth a Charm purchase.<br /> <br /> Not a lot to say this time! Medicine is\u2026 pretty medicinal. There\u2019s not a lot of dead wood here \u2013 though by the last few Charms, it\u2019s mostly just ALL THE MEDICINE SUCCESSES. There does seem to be an assumption that doctors are going to be rolling a <i>lot</i> of Medicine rolls in quick succession, such that \u201cShoot, I\u2019m out of motes for medicinal purposes!\u201d is a big concern. That\u2019s interesting \u2013 it feels like in practice, most of the GMs I\u2019ve had would call it after a roll or two, or make one big roll representing a day of work, so I\u2019m curious how they\u2019re picturing that.<br /> <br /> Everything here is very much personal-scale, in any event; there\u2019s no group treatment, nothing like 2e\u2019s A Hood on Death. (Which was kind of a weird Charm, so that\u2019s a good call.) I\u2019m a little bit sad at that decision \u2013 I\u2019d prefer Medicine scale up the way many of the other Abilities do \u2013 but I can understand the decision to keep it on an individual level.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Wholenes-Restoring Meditation.<br /> <i>No:</i> \u201cConvalescence,\u201d a recovery period which appears only in the Charm removing it.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Life-Exchanging Prana (#16). You have to be pretty desperate for motes to spend health levels at 3m a pop \u2013 is this an expected phenomenon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-29-2015, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T18:27:04-07:00","id":740429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=740375#post740375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Life-Exchanging Prana (#16). You have to be pretty desperate for motes to spend health levels at 3m a pop \u2013 is this an expected phenomenon?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little desperate, sure, but with enough Stamina and Ox-Bodies...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T18:45:40-07:00","id":740503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=740374#post740374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars do get Bureaucracy Charms that give die bonuses to their NPC minions for offscreen tasks. I think that might happen in Integrity, too.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's worth the Charm purchase, just that there doesn't seem to be any good reason to make it scale up to 25 if it isn't meant for that kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I forgot about Order-Conferring Action, although the charm does note that the user and other Solars can benefit from it, which seems more likely in practice. I agree that the scaling is odd, which is why I think it's aimed at making the low Essence uses more valuable than at interacting with systems that are either gone or never existed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=740374#post740374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, basically, my original critique of the Charm. If we differ as to whether we believe the writers thought someone would want to do that, that's probably the source of our argument.<br /> <br /> (I would want to do it, though, if it wasn't for the XP costs. &quot;Gonna train up a city of philosopher-kings&quot; was an ambition of a past character of mine. That this doesn't really make sense to do with the Charm as written is... yeah, basically my issue with it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it doesn't seem like it would do that. I don't think the writers want anyone to use a charm for such an important goal. I mean, you could say you're using charms to support the goal, but not to just <i>do </i>it. That seems like it would be a series of leadership projects that you could interact with in a variety of ways (recruiting, training, rooting out spies or dissenters, etc.) rather than something you'd relegate to repeated charm use this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T18:47:25-07:00","id":740507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=740429#post740429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little desperate, sure, but with enough Stamina and Ox-Bodies...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I can get that, but still. The only edge case where this really feels worthwhile is for last-minute rescues of a party member, and then you're probably better off just saving the motes for Had I Known How To Save A Life Prana (and, y'know, buying another Charm) - heck, Instant Treatment Methodology doesn't even cost motes, mid-fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-29-2015, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T19:02:19-07:00","id":740553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=740375#post740375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I think I would have assumed that Instant Treatment Methodology (#7) put the target back on their feet immediately\u2026 if Body-Sculpting Essence Method (#13) hadn\u2019t included a call-out saying that that\u2019s what <i>it</i> does. Am I missing something here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Instant Treatment Methodology lets stitch someone's gaping sword wound up in seconds, but the patient still needs to do their post-surgery bed rest. Body-Sculpting Essence Method lets you stitch the wounds up and have the patient immediately cured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T19:31:56-07:00","id":740615,"title":"","content":"On the risk of lighting the fire again, it seems that unless you have other, more specific plans for an ongoing project, the two &quot;optimised&quot; prophecies for &quot;Prophet of Seventeen Cycles&quot; are simply &quot;The project will continue on unopposed&quot;, giving it a bonus for just continuing and bashing everyone trying to stop it with a penalty, or &quot;The project will be abandoned due to vast opposition&quot;, giving everyone opposing it bonuses and giving the one attempting the project a penalties for not abandoning it.<br /> <br /> I really think this charm needs more rules. Or <i>at least</i> a &quot;Danger: Flying Books&quot; disclaimer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T20:25:26-07:00","id":740731,"title":"","content":"<u>Melee</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 38<br /> By Ability requirement: 2/2/6/7/21<br /> By Essence requirement: 11/13/11/1/2<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Enemy rolls -1 damage for each 1 rolled, bonus dice and successes for rolling a straight, attacker loses one success for each 1 or 2 rolled, free full Excellency<br /> <br /> Themes: Hit anything, and don\u2019t get hit. Kill creatures of darkness \u2013 whatever those are \u2013 pretty dead.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Gain a success and recurring 1s.</li> <li>Add post-soak damage or transfer extra attack successes to a Decisive damage roll.</li> <li>After reducing an enemy from Initiative above yours to Init below yours, make a Reflexive attack.</li> <li>Spend your anima to make an extra attack.</li> <li>Ignore Defense penalties; gain 1i for parrying.</li> <li>Ignore Defense penalties for one turn; opponent does reduced damage.</li> <li>Defend another reflexively.</li> <li>When Defending Other, grant extra Initiative to your charge with a Distract Gambit.</li> <li>Counterattack before damage is rolled against you.</li> <li>Call your weapon to hand with a successful roll.</li> <li>Store a weapon in Elsewhere.</li> <li>Add bonus successes if you roll a straight.</li> <li>Treat your Initiative as being three higher for the purposes of #3.</li> <li>Make a big magical flurry. Can chain off of #4.</li> <li>Ignore \u201ccertain\u201d penalties to Defense.</li> <li>Parry the unparryable.</li> <li>Attacker loses 1 success for each 1 or 2 rolled.</li> <li>Gain 1i when parrying as part of a Defend Other.</li> <li>Attacks may not be applied to the character you\u2019re defending.</li> <li>Counterattack every attack for the next round.</li> <li>Summon a magical glowing sword.</li> <li>Make a Melee attack at Medium range.</li> <li>Make a Decisive attack at Short range, ignoring hardness and cover.</li> <li>Roll Decisive damage dice against Creatures of Darkness on a hit, even if that hit was Withering(!).</li> <li>Gain 1m for every 10 rolled when using #12.</li> <li>Do extra damage to a Crashed opponent.</li> <li>Gain extra attacks with #14.</li> <li>Free full Excellency.</li> <li>Make a Withering counterattack, turning any stolen damage into Decisive dice.</li> <li>Reflexively Clash with an attack.</li> <li>Combine #29 and #30.</li> <li>Extra damage on all attacks for the rest of the scene.</li> <li>Raise defense against creatures of darkness; burn them if they touch you.</li> <li>Gain extra damage against creatures of darkness; treat people you hate as creatures of darkness.</li> <li>Shoot a bolt of energy at an enemy; works better against creatures of darkness.</li> <li>Decisively strike all opponents at close range.</li> <li>If you kill anyone with #36, make a withering strike against all opponents at close range. If you Crash anyone, you can pop #36 again.</li> <li>When you use #16, accumulate extra Initiative for later uses of #16.</li> </ol><br /> A lot of familiar faces here \u2013 many Charm names and general effects repeated from 2e. (I played a lot more Melee characters than I did most other Abilities, so this may be a general truth.)<br /> <br /> Solar Counterattack (#9) raises again the question, \u201cWhat happens if you kill someone with your counterattack \u2013 do they roll damage against you, or not?\u201d<br /> <br /> Call the Blade (#10) is scaled waaaaaaay back, presumably so Disarming doesn\u2019t feel like a chump move.<br /> <br /> Rising Sun Slash (#12) is about my least favorite dice trick so far. Just\u2026 no, game. \u201cCheck for a straight\u201d is too much complexity for something that\u2019s probably almost identical to some double-Xs effect.<br /> <br /> Agile Dragonfly Blade (#13) is one of the most\u2026 limited\u2026 powers I\u2019ve seen so far. I guess more opportunities to use OWTB is always good, but that\u2019s an awfully narrow band of usefulness.<br /> <br /> So, Fivefold Bulwark Stance (#15) does one thing very right, and one thing very wrong. The thing it does <i>right</i> is give you a reason to be glad you still have Dipping Swallow: it makes that Charm into a more efficient Excellency + Initiative generator, even with 5BS running. What it does <i>wrong</i> is\u2026 well\u2026 see, the Charm itself only says it removes \u201ccertain\u201d penalties. So, what\u2019s a \u201ccertain\u201d penalty? For <i>that</i>, we have to consult the sidebar on the next page, which informs us that it means wound, grappling, onslaught, and some crippling, but not blindness, stunning, or poison. Why on earth is the effect of the Charm in the sidebar, and not in the actual Charm? It\u2019s not like the sidebar is applicable to anything else <i>other</i> than the Charm.<br /> <br /> Heavenly Guardian Defense (#16) is back! And isn\u2019t actually a parry, weirdly \u2013 it\u2019s more like a soak effect than anything else. It\u2019s a bit confusingly worded, but the Charm seems to have three modes: spend Initiative to negate damage, spend motes to make the unblockable blockable, and block infinite damage.<br /> <br /> (The art for the past few pages has been much more dynamic and active than the rather stilted, posed art I complained about earlier. It\u2019s also pretty anime, which is probably not unrelated to the first point.)<br /> <br /> Hail-Shattering Practice (#17) is <i>potent</i>. Dodge may get the most out of not being hit, but Melee has a better defensive suite \u2013 late-step success-stealing (or adding) is about as good as it gets, and Melee has that in spades. Expect to roll about 40% successes fewer than normal against a good Meleeist.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that a meleeist Defending Other on a brawler would be all kinds of terrifying.<br /> <br /> Ready in Eight Directions Stance (#20) is an odd one \u2013 since it\u2019s Simple, it consumes your turn just standing there and looking threatening. It combos well with War Lion\u2019s Stance (#7), as has been pointed out to me, but by itself it\u2019s a little lackluster.<br /> <br /> Ah ha ha, Glorious Solar Saber (#21) can do the \u201cmelt through a blast door\u201d thing from Episode 1. I really like the ability to give your summoned weapons evocations, though I\u2019m not sure that makes up for having to waste a Simple action summoning them. (Remember, your soul sword thing is just a logical extension of your skill at swording, and not something to be mistaken for a distinct magical technique.)<br /> <br /> Edge of Morning Sunlight (#24) seems to make a pretty fundamental rule of the game \u2013 that you know you\u2019re safe against a Withering attack. It doesn\u2019t feel implausible that you could, by E3 or so, Wither someone half to death with just this Charm. Of course, it only works on CoDs\u2026 until you grab Sharp Light of Judgment Stance (#34), which makes it work on anyone you hate (like, say, the villain of your campaign).<br /> <br /> Actually, speaking of SLOJS, it references the minimum damage increase from Corona of Radiance (#33)\u2026 which, er, doesn\u2019t actually seem to be a thing; CoR doesn\u2019t do anything to your minimum damage.<br /> <br /> I really love the idea of the cycle of repeatedly triggering Heaven Sword Flash (#36) into Bright Reaving Circle (#37) and back again, but I\u2019m suspicious that it won\u2019t actually get to cycle very often in play \u2013 how many separate people are going to be mobbing you at close range, and also likely to be Crashed/killed?<br /> <br /> Melee is, overall, a very strong tree. Not as much pure lethality as some others, but you <i>will</i> hit, and you\u2019re pretty likely to avoid being hit in return. Very solid; lots of fun effects.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Almost everything. One Weapon Two Blows is great as a finally useful double-attack.<br /> <i>No</i>: Agile Dragonfly Blade. The 5BS sidebar.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> There are a <i>lot</i> of multiattacks here. Like, a <i>lot</i>. Wasn\u2019t that something we were getting rid of, for the most part?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T20:34:03-07:00","id":740741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=740731#post740731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, speaking of SLOJS, it references the minimum damage increase from Corona of Radiance (#33)\u2026 which, er, doesn\u2019t actually seem to be a thing; CoR doesn\u2019t do anything to your minimum damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one took me a while to find; it's near the beginning of Sharp Light of Judgement Stance. Knowing SLoJS boosts your minimum damage by your essence against creatures of darkness while Corona of Radiance is active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T05:32:31-07:00","id":741428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=740741#post740741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That one took me a while to find; it's near the beginning of Sharp Light of Judgement Stance. Knowing SLoJS boosts your minimum damage by your essence against creatures of darkness while Corona of Radiance is active.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhhh, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T06:07:52-07:00","id":741498,"title":"","content":"Really enjoying these, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T07:47:24-07:00","id":741743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=741498#post741498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really enjoying these, thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>My pleasure, thanks for the feedback!<br /> <br /> Up next: Occult! Occult is the 14th Ability in the list, if I'm counting right, which means we're over the halfway point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:41:06-07:00","id":741940,"title":"","content":"<u>Occult</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 36<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/3/6/4/22<br /> By Essence requirement: 13/9/8/3/3<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Free full Excellency<br /> <br /> Themes: Battle spirits; bind spirits; perform exorcisms; have a bunch of spirit minions; spirits spirits spirits spirits spirits.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>See spirits.</li> <li>A mental alarm goes off when there\u2019s a spirit nearby.</li> <li>Permanent bonus dice on attempts to investigate or follow spirits.</li> <li>Strike a spirit.</li> <li>Do extra damage to spirits for the scene.</li> <li>Do aggravated damage to spirits, and steal motes from them. Permanently destroy spirits and, uh, imordials-Pray. (Shhh, don\u2019t mention them by name!)</li> <li>An immaterial enemy becomes material when you strike him.</li> <li>Scenelong bonus dice to attacks vs. spirits. Very cheap Infinite Occult Mastery.</li> <li>An attack that would kill you doesn\u2019t. You need to heal before using this again, though.</li> <li>Allow a spirit ally to materialize for 1m.</li> <li>Speak Old Realm and other spirit language. Bonus successes to shaping actions for the scene(!).</li> <li>Free full Occult Excellency.</li> <li>Detect shaping actions, sorcery, Evocations, and spirit sanctums for one instant.</li> <li>Temporarily absorb the powers of a spirit killed via #6.</li> <li>Force a spirit or spiritual disease(?) from its host.</li> <li>Steal motes equal to damage done to a spirit.</li> <li>Spirits at short range must materialize or retreat.</li> <li>Immaterial beings must pay Willpower to attack you.</li> <li>Trap and materialize a spirit for a few rounds.</li> <li>Materialize several spirit allies.</li> <li>Learn several thaumaturgical rituals. Er, what\u2019s a thaumaturgical ritual?</li> <li>Notice disguises and shapeshifting with #13.</li> <li>Spiritually enter another\u2019s body to do battle with possessing forces (or to inflict possessing forces on the target).</li> <li>#18 works on unshaped fair folk and similar beings.</li> <li>Fuel your Charms and spells with motes stolen from a spirit trapped via #19.</li> <li>Gain social influence bonuses against a spirit trapped via #19.</li> <li>Spirits to an enormous distance are forced to materialize and remain material.</li> <li>Commit motes to learn spirit Charms.</li> <li>When at full anima, #13 automatically activates.</li> <li>When using #23, detect signs of past spiritual predation; come to subject\u2019s aid if such predation recurs.</li> <li>Reduce Essence of a target trapped via #19.</li> <li>Spend your anima to gather motes to spend on thinky-actions.</li> <li>Create a spirit.</li> <li>Terrestrial Circle Sorcery.</li> <li>Celestial Circle Sorcery.</li> <li>Solar Circle Sorcery.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Spirit-Draining Stance (#5) would be a great Charm if it was Reflexive. It feels a little harder to justify spending a Simple action on 1W damage for the rest of the scene \u2013 you could probably land a Withering attack with your action and do more damage than this will give you.<br /> <br /> Ghost Eating Technique (#6) used to be an \u201cevery attack\u201d kind of thing. Now, I\u2019m not sure if you even want it on every Decisive \u2013 until you hit the -4 health levels, it\u2019s a net negative, and Aggravated damage doesn\u2019t matter most if you\u2019re planning to kill the spirit.<br /> <br /> Man, Ancient Tongue understanding (#11) buries the lead. The \u201ctalk to spirits\u201d thing is cool , but this is a pretty substantial Reflexive scenelong buff to sorcery \u2013 that seems like the bigger deal.<br /> <br /> All-Encompassing Sorcerer\u2019s Sight (#13) has two enormous, substantial nerfs applied: (1) It\u2019s Instant duration, and (2) it can\u2019t see Exalted Charms. I somewhat understand (2) \u2013 that always took some of the guesswork out of fighting a new character \u2013 but I\u2019m not sure I follow the motivation for (1).<br /> <br /> Material Exegesis Prana (#20) gives you <i>all</i> your demons if you roll 666. Thaaaat\u2019s a little too cute for me.<br /> <br /> Soul Projection Method (#23) starts off strong, with a clear roll\u2026 which immediately switches to a dramatic action whose effects are Storyteller dependent and completely devoid of examples. I\u2019m less worried about encountering this one as a player than I am as a Storyteller!<br /> <br /> Spirit-Drawing Oculus (#32) pretty clearly should be a Charm with a \u201c3a\u201d in its cost. Instead, the anima cost is described in the text of the Charm. It\u2019s otherwise pretty cool \u2013 if nothing else, it\u2019s a <i>big</i> extra source of motes for shaping sorcery. (Which\u2026 we don\u2019t actually know how that works yet.) Again, though, this makes that one \u201cSpend motes to purge your anima\u201d charm look pretty thin \u2013 and the Medicine \u201cspend HLs for motes\u201d effect, for that matter.<br /> <br /> There is something wrong with the torso of the young lady climbing out of the pool in this picture, I think? It looks\u2026 oddly thick, to me. Like, she\u2019s not particularly heavyset \u2013 her torso just looks disproportionately thick, front-to-back. I am definitely not an anatomy guy, though, so maybe that\u2019s just me.<br /> <br /> The Mandala-binding Charms are just a little odd, to me. Like, I don\u2019t know that they\u2019re bad \u2013 I\u2019m just not sure what you\u2019re supposed to do with them. Hold a spirit down, while the rest of the party beats on it, I guess? The \u201cuse them as mote batteries\u201d effects are a little bit peculiar, given the difficulty in actually pulling this off. These aren\u2019t bad effects, to be clear \u2013 there are just a <i>lot</i> of Charms living in this conceptual space, and I don\u2019t have an immediate vision of what to do with it.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is <i>cool</i>, though. So, sorcery is the first thing so far that <i>isn\u2019t</i> subject to Supernal advantages \u2013 that is, you have to actually be E5 to throw Solar-circle spells. I think I can follow that motivation. On the other hand, sorcery is a pretty good buy now. Buying TCS gets you a free spell and a \u201cshaping ritual,\u201d whatever that is \u2013 further, that one spell you get becomes your \u201ccontrol spell,\u201d which is presumably a good thing (apparently some Charms, though none actually in Occult, may reference it).<br /> <br /> Overall, Occult looks quite good. I don\u2019t know what everything here is <i>for</i>, as I say above, but about the worst you can say of anything is, \u201cEh, don\u2019t think I\u2019d take that.\u201d I suspect an Occult 3 sorcery dip is going to be very common, this edition.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Sorcery looks very hopeful so far. We\u2019ll see!<br /> <i>No:</i> Having a Charm whose effect is purely Storyteller determined, with no guidelines for what that should look like.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird: </i>Uncanny Shroud Defense (#8). It\u2019s a perfect defense\u2026 of sorts? Occult is an odd place for it, and the flavor doesn\u2019t quite hold up (if I\u2019m \u201cstepping between worlds,\u201d shouldn\u2019t Spirit-Cutting Attack still kill me?) \u2013 but I do approve of adding more panic buttons and ways to stop your non-combat character from unexpectedly dying.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T09:01:31-07:00","id":741979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=741743#post741743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Up next: Occult! Occult is the 14th Ability in the list, if I'm counting right, which means we're over the halfway point.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then you have like 10 MA styles :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:02:25-07:00","id":742268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=741979#post741979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then you have like 10 MA styles :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Then Sorcery!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:04:34-07:00","id":742430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=742268#post742268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then Sorcery!</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the Evocations!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:15:30-07:00","id":742465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=742430#post742430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the Evocations!</div> </div> </div> </div>True! All the Evocations together are like, one Charm tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:29:27-07:00","id":742489,"title":"","content":"... Thank you. That is all <i>so very encouraging</i>.<br /> <br /> A bit of a reflection, as we are a little more than halfway through, here: I really, really wish these Charms were in a simpler, cleaner format. Like... I am inevitably Crunch Guy, in my groups. That is my schtick. I love some good, meaty rules.<br /> <br /> And yet these Charms are a <i>slog</i>. That's not a sensation I got in 2e - probably in part because, if this was 2e, I'd be done with Charms by now. (Which had its own problems, obviously.) I don't know if the Charm fluff just isn't quite doing it for me, or if it's the way fluff and crunch intermingle and blend over a couple of paragraphs, or what. I <i>do</i> know that the vagueness in some of the rules isn't helping here - nor is the fact that some (though not as many as I had thought!) of the Charms are pure dice pool/success manipulators.<br /> <br /> I can grant that there seems to be some role for that in 3e - but I really wish that such effects were <i>short</i>. And a clean, clear mechanical terminology would really help with that process. As-is, there's a lot of, &quot;Wait, what did that actually say? Which part of that was actually the rules?&quot; that really shouldn't be necessary.<br /> <br /> That's probably not a universal reaction, but <i>man</i>. I want to have - as I think Holden once said - the &quot;kid in the candy store&quot; reaction to these Charms. And there's some really great candy here - but it's spaced out between things that feel more like vegetables. In general - and this applies at the system level as much as it does the Charm level - this is a very maximalist approach, with a very &quot;Why use one widget when two will do?&quot; feel to it, and that's just not quite working for me. (Combat is an easy example - it seems like land and naval combat should use similar rules, with perhaps some slightly different widgets, such as a boat's maneuverability or speed. Instead, we have two different resolution engines for the two subsystems.) That's a lot of conceptual overhead, and it's a little wearying.<br /> <br /> So there are a lot of things that would help with this. Compressing that same - what, five lines? That same five line header at the start of each Charm down a bit would help - prereq Charms and Abilities don't really need to be separate entries. Reducing, or italicizing, or somehow distinguishing fluff from rules would help. Ditching the &quot;Here's what the Charm actually does&quot; sidebar or two would help. Better keywording, and better technical language in general, would help. Reducing redundant verbiage that boils down to &quot;This has a cost of 3a&quot; or &quot;Supernal works as normal&quot; would help. And, well - one of the things I had hoped, when I heard they were going to have to find some pages to cut, was that some of the dead wood in the Charms would get pruned out. It sounds like that didn't happen - and there are <i>definitely</i> some effects that seem like they should be upgrades, or fused effects, or <i>something</i>.<br /> <br /> Again, personal taste, etc. - but two hundred pages is too much for this chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:38:35-07:00","id":742502,"title":"","content":"If it makes you feel any better, Sorcery, Martial Arts, and Evocations <i>feel</i> more compact to me than the Charm trees. Partially this is because they're meant to supplement Abilities and such, but it does help keep them conceptually distinct and concise. It feels like a Greatest Hits album whereas some of the Charm trees feel like &quot;I bought this for Glorious Solar Saber and they sold me Agile Dragonfly Blade in the meantime because it's all or nothing.&quot; But yeah. The Charms chapter is oh my <i>god</i>.<br /> <br /> That said, your reaction to Glorious Solar Saber (&quot;This is an outward manifestation at your skill at swording and <i>most definitely not</i> a distinct magical technique&quot;) is possibly one of my favorite quotes so far from this readthrough. Of all the ones on the forums, this is one I think I'd re-read for educational <i>and</i> entertainment value both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:49:05-07:00","id":742525,"title":"","content":"I have to agree there is some charm bloat. While I actually think there are some really neat charms, but some just need to be mashed together or cut. Especially in crafts which is probably the most boring charms. I actually<b> like the craft rules</b> &amp; most of the charms are pretty efficient; there is just so many of them! I want to play a crafts person but just getting the bare minimum seems like I won't have enough exp for of the other charm tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","user":"Snakesandsuns","date":". 10-30-2015, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:51:34-07:00","id":742531,"title":"","content":"If it helps, I find my reaction to the amount of Charms to be similar to yours. It's a slog and unfun to read through them all, especially when many of them are uninspiring dice tricks (useful and potent dice tricks, but dice tricks none the less). I appreciate what you're doing, and agree with many of your own assessment. Plus it's just enjoyable to read through another person's thoughts on a similar subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:52:30-07:00","id":742542,"title":"","content":"I agree with pretty much 100% of that. I really wish there were just <i>fewer charms</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:55:03-07:00","id":742581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=742502#post742502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it makes you feel any better, Sorcery, Martial Arts, and Evocations <i>feel</i> more compact to me than the Charm trees. Partially this is because they're meant to supplement Abilities and such, but it does help keep them conceptually distinct and concise. It feels like a Greatest Hits album whereas some of the Charm trees feel like &quot;I bought this for Glorious Solar Saber and they sold me Agile Dragonfly Blade in the meantime because it's all or nothing.&quot; But yeah. The Charms chapter is oh my <i>god</i>.<br /> <br /> That said, your reaction to Glorious Solar Saber (&quot;This is an outward manifestation at your skill at swording and <i>most definitely not</i> a distinct magical technique&quot;) is possibly one of my favorite quotes so far from this readthrough. Of all the ones on the forums, this is one I think I'd re-read for educational <i>and</i> entertainment value both.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have found more cool Charms I like from reading Irked's summaries than I have from the PDF itself. This is an excellent thread, hope Irked can sustain this quality all the way through Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:56:31-07:00","id":742600,"title":"","content":"The impression I have gotten from various commentary is that Solars will have the most bloat because Solars can specialize. They can approach problems with a variety of very specific tools, which gives sometimes too many options but with some practice can make a wide variety of fun character options.<br /> <br /> I've been led to believe that other splats will have fewer options in some respects not necessarily out of a power differential, but out of a different approach. I forsee Sids having fewer charms with more broad applicability in each. This will likely translate to longer charm descriptions too, but time will tell. I forsee DBs having a similar setup to Solars but with just fewer options. If Solars had 500 charms, DBs might have 300 or 350 maybe. That's not insider knowledge, that's an educated guess from various sources. <br /> <br /> tl;dr is I think Solars will have the worst of the charm bloat but for narrative reasons, and others will have less of an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T13:00:45-07:00","id":742624,"title":"","content":"The Charms chapter is rife with M\u00f8rkery, yes. Luckily, there's none of that in the MAs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T13:20:48-07:00","id":742659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=742581#post742581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have found more cool Charms I like from reading Irked's summaries than I have from the PDF itself. This is an excellent thread, hope Irked can sustain this quality all the way through Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad it helps! I want to stress that <i>this is a good game</i>. It is fun to play, in a great world, with some very creative systems. The places it falls down are places a lot of RPGs fall down - but some of those <i>could still be addressed</i>, and even if it was too late for this book, there's a whole line coming after.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Charms chapter is rife with M\u00f8rkery, yes. Luckily, there's none of that in the MAs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to hear. John can be a very evocative writer - I remember one of his big ambitions right after he came onboard was to make Solar Charms less &quot;vanilla,&quot; and I really enjoy a lot of what he wrote in, say, Glories of the Most High. When it works, it works well. When it doesn't quite hit, there is a tendency to sesquipedalian loquaciousness at the expense of brief clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T13:21:26-07:00","id":742662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=742600#post742600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impression I have gotten from various commentary is that Solars will have the most bloat because Solars can specialize. They can approach problems with a variety of very specific tools, which gives sometimes too many options but with some practice can make a wide variety of fun character options.<br /> <br /> I've been led to believe that other splats will have fewer options in some respects not necessarily out of a power differential, but out of a different approach. I forsee Sids having fewer charms with more broad applicability in each. This will likely translate to longer charm descriptions too, but time will tell. I forsee DBs having a similar setup to Solars but with just fewer options. If Solars had 500 charms, DBs might have 300 or 350 maybe. That's not insider knowledge, that's an educated guess from various sources.<br /> <br /> tl;dr is I think Solars will have the worst of the charm bloat but for narrative reasons, and others will have less of an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>During the Kickstarter they teased greatly expanding the Dragon-Blooded Charm trees so that every Ability featured all five elements.If anything I would expect MORE Charms in the DB book, not less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T13:21:32-07:00","id":742663,"title":"","content":"What is the definition of &quot;M\u00f8rkery&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T13:24:32-07:00","id":742670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=742662#post742662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> During the Kickstarter they teased greatly expanding the Dragon-Blooded Charm trees so that every Ability featured all five elements.If anything I would expect MORE Charms in the DB book, not less.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've had confirmation that the DB charm chapter is shorter than the Solar one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T13:29:29-07:00","id":742681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=742663#post742663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the definition of &quot;M\u00f8rkery&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this particular instance, it means &quot;the negative aspects of John M\u00f8rke's writing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T15:59:25-07:00","id":743137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720877#post720877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's true. It can represent having JUST enough money that it all goes into your day-to-day survival and lifestyle with bupkus left over. Basically, you no longer have to factor in your concept when picking a Resources level; it's all about how much excess disposable income you want your character to have. It's a fucking genius design decision and I applaud the developers for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, where is this written? I looked at the character creation, looked at merits, looked at equipment...I think it's a great change, but I'd like to see the actual word of it.<br /> <br /> Also, where's this Firefly reference?? I'm enjoying this read through a lot, but I wish Irked would be more specific about where he sees things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2774-khal-matt","name":"Khal Matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:07:41-07:00","id":743261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khal Matt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=743137#post743137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, where's this Firefly reference?? I'm enjoying this read through a lot, but I wish Irked would be more specific about where he sees things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry! I try to get more specific in the Charms chapter, but I'll bear that in mind.<br /> <br /> Um, there's an offhand reference to hiring away the mercenary who has come to kill you, which sounded familiar to me - that was the possible reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:17:33-07:00","id":743280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=743261#post743261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, sorry! I try to get more specific in the Charms chapter, but I'll bear that in mind.<br /> <br /> Um, there's an offhand reference to hiring away the mercenary who has come to kill you, which sounded familiar to me - that was the possible reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Rad! <br /> <br /> And thank you! Much appreciated. We'll be starting a game with people who have never played exalted before, and I plan on sharing this thread so people can get a feel for the various charm trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2774-khal-matt","name":"Khal Matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T18:45:37-07:00","id":743446,"title":"","content":"<u>Performance</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 37<br /> By Ability requirement: 0/1/6/12/18<br /> By Essence requirement: 15/10/8/2/2<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Free full Excellency<br /> <br /> Themes: Boost the actions of others, make other social influence easier, stir emotions, mimic others.<br /> <br /> Performance is, somewhat unusually, broken down into subtrees by type \u2013 that is, the Charms you use to dance don\u2019t apply to singing.<br /> <br /> Omni-Applicable:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Bonus success + recurring 1s.</li> <li>Inflict emotion on a group; all those affected reconsider a past decision in that emotional context.</li> <li>Recover motes when you influence a group.</li> <li>Gain motes for rolling 10s or attempting performance, but only with scenelong Charms up.</li> <li>Non-supplemental Performance Charms can be used with other performance types.</li> <li>Spend ~25% of your Willpower to make an influence roll more successful and harder to resist.</li> <li>1/scene, free full muted Excellency.</li> <li>1/day, for the next performance, your Performance Charms cost no motes.</li> <li>Reset #7 and #8.</li> </ol>Penultimate Unity of Form (#5) is weird to me \u2013 is the conceptual separation of Performance important, or not? The Ability itself says no \u2013 there\u2019s no Craft-style division. The Charms say yes \u2013 totally separate trees with redundant effects. Penultimate Unity says <i>no</i>, because most of your effects re-fuse, but only post-Essence 3. What gives?<br /> <br /> Utility (not Omni-Applicable?):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>People must pay WP to leave or interrupt your performance.</li> <li>Create illustrative illusions.</li> <li>A group accepts a false memory. Announcing \u201cLelouch vi Britannia commands you!\u201d optional.</li> <li>Vaporize creatures of darkness to long range with an extremely potent Decisive.</li> </ol>So Memory-Reweaving Discipline (#3) specifies that people act in accord with their new memories. That seems like it bypasses an awful lot of the social system \u2013 like, if you land this hit, what can you <i>not</i> do? \u201cHey, remember when so-and-so tried to kill you and I saved your life?\u201d may take penalties for implausibility, but if it lands, that\u2019s pretty compelling motivation for\u2026 well, just about anything.<br /> <br /> Demon-Wracking Shout has prerequisite Charms of \u201c???.\u201d This doesn\u2019t appear to be a mistake \u2013 it looks like the intent is you can only learn this Charm if the Storyteller decides it would be thematically appropriate. Which could be kind of cool, but is also pretty inconsistent with how the rest of the set works \u2013 I get what they\u2019re going for, but I think I\u2019d rather it just be a <i>Charm</i>.<br /> <br /> Oratory:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Double-9s, on oratory.</li> <li>Incite a mob to action.</li> <li>On inspiring a crowd, grant bonus dice to those affected.</li> <li>Convince another character to attempt social influence <i>now</i>, forgoing all other purposes.</li> </ol>Typically, Charms that grant bonus dice to mortals seem to have a \u201cnon-Charm\u201d rider \u2013 I presume because the die cap for a mortal is <i>0</i>. If that\u2019s accurate \u2013 and it\u2019s not clear that it is, as this is more inference than actual rules text \u2013 Dogmatic Contagion Discipline (#3) is missing the rider.<br /> <br /> Infectious Zealotry Approach (#4) is kind of a mixed bag. The whole \u201cforgoes all other concerns\u201d thing suggests some interesting uses, but the trigger condition \u2013 \u201cI\u2019m thinking about making some social influence, buuuuuuut maybe not <i>now</i>\u201d \u2013 seems like a pretty isolated circumstance.<br /> <br /> We come to a half-page art showing exactly what you can do with just a few posed figured copied and pasted fifty times. (Answer: we get a crowd who are all inspired to strike <i>the exact same celebratory pose</i>.)<br /> <br /> Music and Singing:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Double-9s, on music. Hang on, that seems familiar\u2026</li> <li>Grant or remove dice to attempts to create social influence, depending on whether it fits with the mood of your music.</li> <li>Grant bonus dice to battle groups.</li> <li>Grant bonus dice to a social influence.</li> <li>Appeal to an emotionally-charged Intimacy, creating Storyteller-defined action.</li> <li>Allies regenerate extra motes while listening to your music.</li> <li>Either the Solar and an ally are immune to fear, or a larger group (or battle group) gain courage bonuses.</li> </ol>Okay, I really want to build a character with Mood-Inducing Music (#2), now \u2013 just sit in the corner, strumming a sanxian, periodically playing entirely-anachronistic music to mess with what\u2019s going on.<br /> <br /> The primary advantage Plectral Harbinger\u2019s Approach (#4) offers over Mood-Inducing Music seems to be that it offers non-Charm dice rather than Charm dice \u2013 is that accurate? (\u201cPlectral?\u201d)<br /> <br /> Heart-Compelling Method (#5) makes it almost the entire Charm before it mentions that it can be used for anything other than melancholy music \u2013 and even then, the only mechanical description is for sad tunes. It seems like this could be constructed a little more generally. And for that matter\u2026 okay, so the Charm plays off an Intimacy and generates emotion. Isn\u2019t this pretty close to the basic effect of an Instill or Inspire action? What is this doing that you can\u2019t do with a musical stunt? (That\u2019s a legit question \u2013 is there a major mechanical effect here I\u2019m overlooking, beyond a vague \u201cThe storyteller decides what he does,\u201d i.e., same thing as an Instill action?)<br /> <br /> In general, the music and singing section takes a lot of pages from the D&amp;D bard \u2013 lots of \u201cinspire others\u201d-type effects that give a few extra dice to different actions. (\u201cRegen, regen, regenerate the motes!\u201d)<br /> <br /> Soul-Stirring Cantata (#6) says the Wyld Hunt knows what this song sounds like. How the heck does <i>that</i> work?<br /> <br /> Dance:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>\u2026 gain double-9s while dancing. Um.</li> <li>Add (Performance/2) to your Defense.</li> <li>Your dance inspires people to talk about their Ties.</li> <li>Reduce target\u2019s Resolve or Guile by 2 vs. your next social influence.</li> <li>Inspire characters to lust after or admire you.</li> </ol>Battle-Dancer Method (#2) is probably the most efficient Defense booster so far \u2013 1m for a +2 Defense bonus, applicable any time you can stunt your moves as a dance. Compare that to the Charms in Awareness that are a 2m discount to a much more selective roll, under much rarer circumstances. Why does this Charm even bother to say \u201chalf Performance, round down\u201d is added? You need Performance 4 just to buy it, and your Performance can\u2019t go over 5. It\u2019s +2! It\u2019s always +2! <i>Just say +2</i>.<br /> <br /> Shining Expression Style (#3) is just kind of ridiculous. It only works if you overcome Resolve \u2013 sure, okay, fine. It causes your targets to <i>recall a Tie</i> related to the emotion you\u2019re inspiring \u2013 which means you\u2019d better have a pretty good idea of what their Ties <i>are</i>, or you\u2019re fishing blindly. Your targets then reveal their Ties to others \u2013 but, according to the Charm, not necessarily to <i>you</i>. So by beating their Resolve, you get <i>someone</i> (you don\u2019t get to pick who) to find out that the target has a particular Tie (you don\u2019t get to pick what). This is a Charm? Why is this a Charm? (\u201cNot even All-Encompassing Sorcerer\u2019s Sight can reveal the power of this Charm\u201d \u2013 well, yeah, because AESS doesn\u2019t reveal <i>any</i> Exalted Charms.)<br /> <br /> Winding Sinuous Motion (#5) is a Charm, which must overcome Resolve, whose effect is that your next influence can more easily overcome Resolve. I assume the idea is that your second influence runs counter to Intimacies and would otherwise be harder than the initial roll?<br /> <br /> Husband-Seducing Demon Dance is a better name than Monk-Seducing Demon Dance (#5). I\u2019m just saying.<br /> <br /> Acting:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Gain +1 Guile as long as you stay in character. Characters who fail to pierce your Guile read Intimacies for the character you\u2019re playing.</li> <li>\u2026 Wait, that\u2019s it? That\u2019s the acting tree?</li> </ol>On the one hand, Master Thespian Style (#Guess) is pretty great. On the other hand\u2026 so, uh, how \u2018bout that acting tree?<br /> <br /> Voice:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Ventriloquism.</li> <li>Mimic a voice perfectly. For ten seconds, after an hour of warming up.</li> <li>Mimic a voice perfectly for a scene.</li> <li>Mimic an animal.</li> </ol>Cunning Mimicry Technique (#2) is fun, in <i>very selective circumstances</i>. You can\u2019t have a conversation with it; you can\u2019t have an exchange of orders. You can give a short speech, or walk in and say something and walk out, or cast someone\u2019s voice across the room (if you know an hour in advance that you\u2019re going to need to mimic that one person). After you finish that one sentence, hope you\u2019ve got an hour to practice before you need to reply.<br /> <br /> Splendid Magpie Approach (#4) is noted to \u201cdelight and amaze audiences.\u201d Well! <i>That\u2019s</i> certainly worth a Charm purchase \u2013 I don\u2019t know <i>how</i> I\u2019d manage that otherwise. Again, this feels rather like something I should be able to do with just Performance 5.<br /> <br /> Sex:<br /> (Oh, good. White Wolf and sex generally ends well.)<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>+1 Appearance. Seduce without appealing to an Intimacy. Roll influence once; apply as different influence to all present.</li> <li>Defining Tie of Lust. (Essence) auto-successes. \u201cWorld-shaking climax.\u201d \u2026 Stay classy, Exalted.</li> </ol>Thousand Courtesan Ways (#1) is one of the most potent Charms in the Performance set. It would be nice if it was useful in some context other than sexing people up.<br /> <br /> Celestial Bliss Trick (#2), issues of good taste entirely aside, is not a supplemental Charm. Which means, post-Penultimate Unity of Form, you can reroute it through your dance or speeches or etc. And that\u2019s about as far as I\u2019m going with that.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> Not as impressed by this tree as the last few. Lots of effects that feel a half-step removed from stunts; lots of vague, hand-wavey \u201cMaybe people will feel sad!\u201d stuff. The few powers that stand out pack tremendous amounts of raw power \u2013 Memory-Reweaving Discipline, most notably.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes: </i>I\u2026 don\u2019t know. MRD feels <i>too</i> good. Thousandfold Courtesan Ways feels the closest to the power level where Charms feel worthwhile but not overwhelming.<br /> <i>No:</i> THREE DIFFERENT CHARMS to grant double-9s. <i>Three different Charms</i>.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Acting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-30-2015, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T19:32:12-07:00","id":743537,"title":"","content":"Follow-up: I described the previous post to my wife. &quot;Three Charms for double-9s!&quot; I said.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think I'd just buy one and deliver all my speeches while dancing,&quot; she replied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:08:30-07:00","id":743583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=743446#post743446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon-Wracking Shout has prerequisite Charms of \u201c???.\u201d This doesn\u2019t appear to be a mistake \u2013 it looks like the intent is you can only learn this Charm if the Storyteller decides it would be thematically appropriate. Which could be kind of cool, but is also pretty inconsistent with how the rest of the set works \u2013 I get what they\u2019re going for, but I think I\u2019d rather it just be a <i>Charm</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the Demon-Wracking Shout that thing that'ss based on Adorjans memory of how Adri\u00e1ns fetich was killed? I think I remember that each (celestial?) Exalted could learn it, so I guess the prerequisite is not other charms but knowing about this event. Eh ... I guess it would fit much better as really weird story-based merit than as charm.<br /> <br /> Btw, thanks for the thread, Irked. It's awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","user":"Taliesin","date":".  praises for OP 10-30-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:13:38-07:00","id":743588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=743583#post743583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't the Demon-Wracking Shout that thing that'ss based on Adorjans memory of how Adri\u00e1ns fetich was killed? I think I remember that each (celestial?) Exalted could learn it, so I guess the prerequisite is not other charms but knowing about this event. Eh ... I guess it would fit much better as really weird story-based merit than as charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any celestial who hears the charm's effects of Demon Wracking Shout can learn it in 2e.<br /> <br /> Except Infernals who learn it from the Adorjan charm-set.<br /> <br /> This is why the 2e scroll of exalts write-up for Ketchup has DWS listed as an Adorjan charm. He wass not an Akuma, just had a long life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:49:28-07:00","id":743690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=742624#post742624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Charms chapter is rife with M\u00f8rkery, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I was trying to nail down what it was about this Charms chapter that felt irritatingly familiar.<br /> <br /> Then I realized it felt like trying to absorb all of the Ink Monkeys and the 2.5 errata. All at once. This is the first time that, upon getting a new <i>Exalted</i> book, I've looked at the list of Awesome Superpowers and thought, &quot;holy GOD that's a lot of words. TL;DR. I'll get around to that later. In much, much smaller pieces.&quot;<br /> <br /> I still haven't given MA a thorough going-over, because whenever I look at the Solar Charms my brain cells cower in terror. And I'm the guy who congratulated 2e on passing the 3,000 Charm mark. Because I'd been <i>counting</i>.<br /> <br /> The Big \u00d8 is great, but he ain't perfect, and I feel like for this chapter he needed someone to rein him in harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:51:30-07:00","id":743693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=743537#post743537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Follow-up: I described the previous post to my wife. &quot;Three Charms for double-9s!&quot; I said.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think I'd just buy one and deliver all my speeches while dancing,&quot; she replied.</div> </div> </div> </div>No kidding! Though I think for Penultimate Unity of Form, I would've add a stacking condition for those charms; perhaps let the Double 9s stack to become Double 8s or even Double 7s. That'd at least give you an incentive to buy in. But in general, Performance leaves me questioning how they've went with Charm writing in general, when their work in 2e was so much cleaner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/650-dtemplar5","name":"DTemplar5","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar650_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T21:12:14-07:00","id":743754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DTemplar5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=743693#post743693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No kidding! Though I think for Penultimate Unity of Form, I would've add a stacking condition for those charms; perhaps let the Double 9s stack to become Double 8s or even Double 7s. That'd at least give you an incentive to buy in. But in general, Performance leaves me questioning how they've went with Charm writing in general, when their work in 2e was so much cleaner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth noting that 2e, for all its flaws, had an established framework of vocabulary and timing effects? I don't necessarily love everything Borgstromantic, but Dr. Moran did her graduate work in computation - that's a lot of background with systems that need to handle discrete packets in an unambiguous way with built-in conflict resolution.<br /> <br /> Some of the assumptions the rules made in 2e were far more ambiguous, mind - I don't want to act like everything was clarity, all the time, because we still had whatever the heck &quot;Duration: Instant (Story)&quot; was supposed to mean, and the weird corner-cases in the definition of &quot;attack,&quot; and so on. But I wonder whether Ink Monkeys etc. was clearer because it was playing within this strict timing/vocabulary framework, instead of 3e's wide open spaces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 10-31-2015, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T04:20:02-07:00","id":744200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackson MacKenzie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=743690#post743690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Big \u00d8 is great, but he ain't perfect, and I feel like for this chapter he needed someone to rein him in harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a writer and someone with an education in technical writing, you pretty much nailed it. The entire charms chapter reads like somebody who didn't have an editor with the power to tell them &quot;no,&quot; which is a critical aspect of the creation process. I want to love all the charms, but I mentally trip over the language. I have to reread sentences several times to tease out the meaning. Sometimes, I'm not even sure why a charm exists.<br /> <br /> Anything I write more important than a post on this forum always sees a third party before it goes out. <br /> <br /> Irked, this thread is superbly helpful. Please keep it going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T04:58:17-07:00","id":744252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackson MacKenzie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=743690#post743690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I was trying to nail down what it was about this Charms chapter that felt irritatingly familiar.<br /> <br /> Then I realized it felt like trying to absorb all of the Ink Monkeys and the 2.5 errata. All at once. This is the first time that, upon getting a new <i>Exalted</i> book, I've looked at the list of Awesome Superpowers and thought, &quot;holy GOD that's a lot of words. TL;DR. I'll get around to that later. In much, much smaller pieces.&quot;<br /> <br /> I still haven't given MA a thorough going-over, because whenever I look at the Solar Charms my brain cells cower in terror. And I'm the guy who congratulated 2e on passing the 3,000 Charm mark. Because I'd been <i>counting</i>.<br /> <br /> The Big \u00d8 is great, but he ain't perfect, and I feel like for this chapter he needed someone to rein him in harder.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd point out that MA largely had a different writer (Vance).\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T05:13:16-07:00","id":744263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=744252#post744252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> I'd point out that MA largely had a different writer (Vance).\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I should start with Sorcery and work backwards through the book when I examine things with a fine-toothed comb, then. Because seriously that Charms chapter makes my brain lock up whenever I try to read more than one tree at a sitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T05:23:00-07:00","id":744265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackson MacKenzie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=744263#post744263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I should start with Sorcery and work backwards through the book when I examine things with a fine-toothed comb, then. Because seriously that Charms chapter makes my brain lock up whenever I try to read more than one tree at a sitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>MA is dense, but the wording and construction feels tighter to me, personally.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is the crown jewel of this game. You might jump to it directly, or savor the wait as you work through the rest.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, one tree at a time is how I read through the book. Smaller, more focused trees (Medicine) are easier to get through. I split Melee up a fair bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T05:26:33-07:00","id":744268,"title":"","content":"Yeah, regardless of the writing those charm trees are extremely long.<br /> I've probably read all of them, but I certainly don't remember what all the charms actually do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T07:12:32-07:00","id":744379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=742465#post742465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True! All the Evocations together are like, one Charm tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is extraordinarily disappointing in its own way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T08:43:38-07:00","id":744535,"title":"","content":"<u>Presence</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 24<br /> By Ability requirement: 0/1/2/3/18<br /> By Essence requirement: 4/6/11/3/0<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Free full Excellency, about ten different situation bonus dice things.<br /> <br /> Themes: More social dice. Fearless minions. Minions who stand in your place. Supporting allies with extra dice. Terrifying anyone who sees you.<br /> <br /> And back down to a 24-Charmer. So far, 20-30 feels like about the right number \u2013 the trees that go larger than that are the ones that tend to feel bloated or unimpressive. (Or else they\u2019re Awareness.)<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Gain bonuses to Instill or Persuade \u2013 bigger bonuses, if the target boosts his Resolve.</li> <li>Gain bonus dice to social rolls for a scene; social Charms are 1m cheaper.</li> <li>Anyone with Defining Ties to you will perform inconvenient tasks without a roll.</li> <li>Permanent bonus to Presence and intimidate. With #7, auto-intimidate anyone who tries to ambush you.</li> <li>Gain bonuses to persuasion in line with your Intimacies.</li> <li>Grant an ally +1 to one Attribute and one Ability.</li> <li>Enemies must pay 1wp the first time they speak or act against you.</li> <li>Anyone with Intimacies for the Solar also has Intimacies for the target; the target can act with the Solar\u2019s authority.</li> <li>Turn your high-Appearance bonus dice into bonus successes.</li> <li>Increase your Appearance by 1; lower the target\u2019s Resolve if this is seduction.</li> <li>A Decisive attack on creatures of darkness does agg, or a social influence attempt lowers their resolve. Treat people you hate as CoDs, for this one attack.</li> <li>Increase the cost of a Decision Point (i.e., reject successful Persuade) by 1wp.</li> <li>Allies to Medium range are immune to fear penalties. Have we seen fear penalties, so far?</li> <li>Threaten everyone out to Long range. Also, inflict a fear penalty on battle groups \u2013 well, that answers that.</li> <li>Bonus dice to threaten, persuade, or instill.</li> <li>Target forgets one piece of social influence he was about to carry out.</li> <li>Program the target with a series of short commands. Really wishing I hadn\u2019t made a <i>Code Geass</i> joke already.</li> <li>On succeeding at a major task, your enemies must grovel before you for the next few days.</li> <li>Grant a follower motes and a Resolve bonus to act as your prophet.</li> <li>Grant three bonus successes to a follower.</li> <li>Double-9s on seduction. Seduce even people who can\u2019t be seduced.</li> <li>1/scene, free Presence, Performance, or Socialize Excellency.</li> <li>As per #6, but stacking with that bonus and of Indefinite duration.</li> <li>Burn your anima for extra Intimidation dice. Enemies who don\u2019t attack you lose 1i/turn.</li> </ol><br /> Harmonious Presence Meditation (#2) is by far the best pseudo-Infinite Mastery so far; it\u2019s cheap, applies to any social Ability, and \u2013 above all \u2013 <i>Reflexive</i>. Which makes the 7m version a little weird: why would I pay extra motes for a version that\u2019s Indefinite, if I can commit the 5m version instantly whenever I want? This would make better sense if it, say, cost a WP, but for just a mote cost that feels pretty strictly inferior.<br /> <br /> Excellent Friend Approach (#3) makes it so that people who will literally die for you will also agree to do inconvenient things without a roll. I mean, yes, I\u2019m sure they will, but in most cases shouldn\u2019t that fall under the rules for trivial actions? The target\u2019s Resolve is no higher than 6, minus three for a Defining Intimacy \u2013 nine dice would be enough to do that without a roll <i>anyway</i>, and we know the Solar has Presence 5\u2026 Again, this feels like a waste of a Charm.<br /> <br /> Empowering Shout (#6) notes that it can grant +1 to one Att and one Ability, or +1 Defense \u2013 but the +1 Defense has a limitation when used on Defenses over 7. Why not just add +1 to Dex/Melee, or whatever? That\u2019d grant +1 Defense, as well, with no caveat. Also, how does this Charm interact with Excellencies? It says a +1 bonus <i>to the stats</i>, not to rolls based on the stats. (The same question could be asked of Increasing Strength Exercise \u2013 or, for that matter, Awakened Carnal Demiurge (#10).) This would feel a lot more potent if it wasn\u2019t a one-turn bonus \u2013 if a Solar is going to give up his entire turn, a single +2 bonus is pretty limited.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if it\u2019s coming through in the Charm summaries, but as of #9, there are a <i>lot</i> of powers here that are just \u201cMOAR DICE\u201d - #1, 2, 4, 5, and 9 all fit that description. That\u2019s a shame, because this is probably the least interesting thing a Solar Charm can do \u2013 well. Other than maybe imitate animal sounds (great fun at parties!). Unfortunately, it may also be one of the most <i>potent</i> things, as 2e demonstrated amply \u2013 but I don\u2019t <i>want</i> five different variations on \u201cSave some motes on your Excellency.\u201d<br /> <br /> Enemy-Castigating Solar Judgment (#11) is so very much worse than Sharp-Light of Judgment Stance \u2013 3m, 1wp for one attack? There\u2019s also a system limitation here \u2013 there\u2019s no way to express \u201cDecisive-only <i>or</i> social influence\u201d in keywords, and yet that\u2019s what we have.<br /> <br /> My impression is that Presence has a lot of Reflexive Charms that would be Simple in most other Abilities. That\u2019s not a complaint, but it makes the Presence effects considerably more useful in a number of cases. (It also violates the original description of Reflexive, of course - +X dice neither enhances an unrolled action nor creates a reflexive one.)<br /> <br /> Mind-Wiping Gaze (#16) has again the problem of catching people <i>just before</i> they inflict some kind of influence. It feels like there should be an \u201cinfluence radar\u201d Charm, in the same sense that there\u2019s, say, \u201cLarceny Radar\u201d \u2013 otherwise, these effects seem like they\u2019re going to lead to some awkward question exchanges (\u201cHey, is he <i>just about</i> to try to say something?\u201d \u201cUm, you don\u2019t know, dude.\u201d). This is not as bad as \u201cHe <i>was</i> going to say something, but he\u2019s decided to put it off a little,\u201d though \u2013 but I\u2019d like the Charm much more if it was a broader \u201cI was just about to do something\u2026\u201d That feels both a little easier to predict, and a little higher utility \u2013 \u201cSomeone has to tell the king about this!\u201d says the guard; \u201cLovely weather we\u2019re having,\u201d says the Solar.<br /> <br /> Hypnotic Tongue Technique (#17) is just nasty. I especially like the clause that rejecting the influence causes the target to <i>forget</i> the influence \u2013 this was a major limitation in 2e\u2019s version of the power.<br /> <br /> Worshipful Lackey Acquisition (#18) is kind of fun, but I\u2019m not really sure what it\u2019s <i>for</i> \u2013 I initially read it as actually turning minor enemies into allies, which is a fun twist on some narrative tropes, but it looks like that\u2019s more of an edge case.<br /> <br /> <br /> Favor-Conferring Prana (#23) has the duration I wanted Empowering Shout to have \u2013 but can\u2019t raise things over 5. I mean, that\u2019s a sensible result, but it deep-sixes what seems like the most frequent use case (i.e., combat). Possibly this is for enabling otherwise unspecced people to be secondary combatants/socialites/etc.?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m really not feeling either social ability so far \u2013 too many \u201ccheaper Excellency\u201d effects, or things that feel like they should just happen for free (\u201cSure, Beloved Solar, I\u2019ll take out your trash for you.\u201d). Between them, there\u2019s a good spread of powers here, but it doesn\u2019t feel like enough good stuff to support either Ability on its own \u2013 there\u2019s just less <i>interesting</i> stuff to do that isn\u2019t \u201cdicewhomp hard, all day.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Hypnotic Tongue Technique looks very useful. I had a player get a lot of use out of the free Excellency.<br /> <i>No:</i> The lack of any description of how Charm-based bonuses to stats, as opposed to bonuses to <i>stat rolls</i>, interacts with Excellencies.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird: </i>The prophet Charms \u2013 Prophet-Uplifting Evocation (#19) and Shedding Infinite Radiance (#20) \u2013 are baffling. In what circumstances am I going to want to first buy Charms, and then spend further XP or motes sustaining Charms, to grant a small (and potentially temporary) bonus to a mortal follower? What concept is this supporting that has \u2013 to steal a line from Root \u2013 more than purely narrative benefit? (Who\u2019s going to go off and roll a bunch of dice for my three uplifted mortal followers, anyway?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T10:30:37-07:00","id":744688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=744535#post744535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m really not feeling either social ability so far \u2013 too many \u201ccheaper Excellency\u201d effects, or things that feel like they should just happen for free (\u201cSure, Beloved Solar, I\u2019ll take out your trash for you.\u201d). Between them, there\u2019s a good spread of powers here, but it doesn\u2019t feel like enough good stuff to support either Ability on its own \u2013 there\u2019s just less <i>interesting</i> stuff to do that isn\u2019t \u201cdicewhomp hard, all day.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the impression I had as well. When I first read 3e I went straight to the social abilities, as my longest-running 2e character is an Eclipse negotiator/diplomat, and I wanted to see how they were supporting that archetype in 3e. I was pretty disappointed - I'll be interested to see what you think of Socialize. It's a pity because I do like the underlying social system, but overall I'm glad my Eclipse's campaign has no prospects of converting to 3e anytime soon (since it includes a Lunar, a Sidereal and two Dragon-Bloods, as well as another Solar). The 3e characters I have enthusiasm for playing are Lore/Occult-based with sorcery and martial arts, and after your read-through I'm also developing some excitement for the combat abilities, but the social Charmset doesn't excite me. Too many dice-adders/dice-tricks - which probably *are* pretty effective at enabling big dicepools that blow through others' defenses - and not much in the way of Charms enabling genuinely novel, interesting and potent abilities, except within a couple of fairly narrow areas of concept-space (e.g. &quot;I terrify people!&quot;). Where the latter Charms do exist, they tend to be gated behind long series of &quot;MOAR DICE&quot; Charms.<br /> <br /> Seconding all the others who say this reread is supremely useful: I had lost steam pretty fast when trying to tackle the combat abilities on my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8842-eris","name":"Eris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T11:19:43-07:00","id":744748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=744535#post744535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harmonious Presence Meditation (#2) is by far the best pseudo-Infinite Mastery so far; it\u2019s cheap, applies to any social Ability, and \u2013 above all \u2013 <i>Reflexive</i>. Which makes the 7m version a little weird: why would I pay extra motes for a version that\u2019s Indefinite, if I can commit the 5m version instantly whenever I want? This would make better sense if it, say, cost a WP, but for just a mote cost that feels pretty strictly inferior.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can commit the 7m version with peripheral essence without triggering your anima.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T12:52:33-07:00","id":744916,"title":"","content":"It seems like there are lot of charms that just do dice shenanigans. Is there a mechanical reason they do this? What's wrong with the good old add dice/success plus occasional reroll failures or double succeses? If I were more cynical I'd suspect that they were just trying to obfuscate the probabilities, and hence were severely underestimating RPG players' math abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1970-yeangst","name":"yeangst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T13:00:52-07:00","id":744926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yeangst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=744916#post744916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like there are lot of charms that just do dice shenanigans. Is there a mechanical reason they do this? What's wrong with the good old add dice/success plus occasional reroll failures or double succeses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably for variety of effect, and the moment of &quot;oh, cool,&quot; when you discover a killer combination of Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T13:17:07-07:00","id":744936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yeangst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=744916#post744916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like there are lot of charms that just do dice shenanigans. Is there a mechanical reason they do this? What's wrong with the good old add dice/success plus occasional reroll failures or double succeses? If I were more cynical I'd suspect that they were just trying to obfuscate the probabilities, and hence were severely underestimating RPG players' math abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The explanation Holden gave was basically that in 2e, if you wanted to be, say, a strong guy, you bought a couple of charms, and boom, you were the strongest guy in the world. The theory is that in 3e, now you want to be a strong guy, you buy a couple charms and now you've got an excellency plus Double 9s, and you can do some pretty cool strong guy stuff. But if you want to be the strongest guy in the world, now you buy a bunch of charms and you've got an excellency, Double 7s, and reroll 6s, and now you can do some super duper crazy strong guy stuff. Basically, they keep the dice pools the same, but still improve the granularity between &quot;normal guy&quot; and &quot;strongest guy in the world.&quot; Which is a cool theory, I like the idea, but I feel like some charm trees have accomplished it better than others, and that we probably could have improved readability and saved a lot of space by turning the Double 9s, Double 8s, reroll 6s, etc. charms into charms with universal rules, like excellencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T13:50:00-07:00","id":745019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WhirlwindMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=744936#post744936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The explanation Holden gave was basically that in 2e, if you wanted to be, say, a strong guy, you bought a couple of charms, and boom, you were the strongest guy in the world. The theory is that in 3e, now you want to be a strong guy, you buy a couple charms and now you've got an excellency plus Double 9s, and you can do some pretty cool strong guy stuff. But if you want to be the strongest guy in the world, now you buy a bunch of charms and you've got an excellency, Double 7s, and reroll 6s, and now you can do some super duper crazy strong guy stuff. Basically, they keep the dice pools the same, but still improve the granularity between &quot;normal guy&quot; and &quot;strongest guy in the world.&quot; Which is a cool theory, I like the idea, but I feel like some charm trees have accomplished it better than others, and that we probably could have improved readability and saved a lot of space by turning the Double 9s, Double 8s, reroll 6s, etc. charms into charms with universal rules, like excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>4e will create a codified series of charms for all abilities. The Magnificent (Ability) charms. First Magnificent (Ability) lets you reroll 1s. Second Magnificent (Ability) gives you double nines. Third Magnificent (Ability) lets you gain non-charm dice if you roll at least one set of 3 matching successes or a run of 4 successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8907,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","user":"ScarecrowJ","date":". 10-31-2015, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T23:36:10-07:00","id":745952,"title":"","content":"Irked, I'm finding your summary a really good read - it's breaking down some of the harder-to-digest pieces and fitting together some things that just weren't coming together for me. Thank you very much for writing this! I'm looking forward to your next installment, since I have a soft spot for Resistance...<br /> <br /> Also I pointed my players to this thread as an Ex 3 Companion Reader. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/921-malovich","name":"Malovich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar921_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T03:40:39-08:00","id":746292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yeangst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=744916#post744916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like there are lot of charms that just do dice shenanigans. Is there a mechanical reason they do this? What's wrong with the good old add dice/success plus occasional reroll failures or double succeses? If I were more cynical I'd suspect that they were just trying to obfuscate the probabilities, and hence were severely underestimating RPG players' math abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it has to do with probability curves. Let's say, for example, that instead of a D10 we had a D2. With 1 being worth nothing and 2 being worth 10 successes. Extreme example I know, but in that case rolling 3d10 lets you spike up to 30 successes in theory, without making it impossible to botch. That's basically what's going on for rolls like double 7s. They enable your cap to rise way higher, and make your average roll much better, but unlike adding 20 dice, or worse 10 successes, you have the exact same chance to roll nothing, or pretty low, as you did without that charm.<br /> <br /> Doing it the other way makes it almost impossible to do badly when you use a charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T05:24:43-08:00","id":746451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=746292#post746292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it has to do with probability curves. Let's say, for example, that instead of a D10 we had a D2. With 1 being worth nothing and 2 being worth 10 successes. Extreme example I know, but in that case rolling 3d10 lets you spike up to 30 successes in theory, without making it impossible to botch. That's basically what's going on for rolls like double 7s. They enable your cap to rise way higher, and make your average roll much better, but unlike adding 20 dice, or worse 10 successes, you have the exact same chance to roll nothing, or pretty low, as you did without that charm.<br /> <br /> Doing it the other way makes it almost impossible to do badly when you use a charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ta for this DrLoveMonkey, I've been trying to explain this to people for a bit but it's kind of hard to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/698-chalicier","name":"chalicier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T06:30:47-08:00","id":746504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=744748#post744748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can commit the 7m version with peripheral essence without triggering your anima.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, that makes sense. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T07:33:42-08:00","id":746577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=746292#post746292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it has to do with probability curves. Let's say, for example, that instead of a D10 we had a D2. With 1 being worth nothing and 2 being worth 10 successes. Extreme example I know, but in that case rolling 3d10 lets you spike up to 30 successes in theory, without making it impossible to botch. That's basically what's going on for rolls like double 7s. They enable your cap to rise way higher, and make your average roll much better, but unlike adding 20 dice, or worse 10 successes, you have the exact same chance to roll nothing, or pretty low, as you did without that charm.<br /> <br /> Doing it the other way makes it almost impossible to do badly when you use a charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, though it still seems unnecessarily complicated, especially for online dice rollers. I<br /> At the very least they should made them into new excellencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1970-yeangst","name":"yeangst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T07:54:14-08:00","id":746603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yeangst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=746577#post746577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes sense, though it still seems unnecessarily complicated, especially for online dice rollers. I<br /> At the very least they should made them into new excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that there is a strong notion that generalized charms like you describe, is boring design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:13:49-08:00","id":746753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=746603#post746603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that there is a strong notion that generalized charms like you describe, is boring design.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, Excellencies. There's a weird mix of philosophies here (not on your part, I mean - just in the design of the book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:23:07-08:00","id":746780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it has to do with probability curves. Let's say, for example, that instead of a D10 we had a D2. With 1 being worth nothing and 2 being worth 10 successes. Extreme example I know, but in that case rolling 3d10 lets you spike up to 30 successes in theory, without making it impossible to botch. That's basically what's going on for rolls like double 7s. They enable your cap to rise way higher, and make your average roll much better, but unlike adding 20 dice, or worse 10 successes, you have the exact same chance to roll nothing, or pretty low, as you did without that charm.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see some similar things with regards to interactions with 1s and the like myself. It's like, if you've got an effect that helps you when you roll more 1s, then that benefits you more when you <i>do</i> have higher dice pools, so it's a thing that can synergize well with the Excellency, and can give these situational moments in which your stronger exertion yields even greater power. On the other hand, when you've got a Charm that <i>punishes</i> an opponent's 1s, that's something that actually hurts them more for having a larger dice pool, because that increases the probability that they'll roll numbers that end up obviating their successes. It's like, if you've got a Fair Folk Cataphract with an attack pool of sixteen, he might have good odds of rolling five successes, but he's also got better odds of rolling an equal number of ones than he would with a dice pool of ten that brought up five successes, and there are Solar Charms that allow that to mean the raksha warrior's mighty dice pool does absolutely dick. So this is a way for Solars to compete against things that can logically have much larger pools than them such as Fair Folk, mighty demons, God forbid even actual Yozis, without it turning into a game of who has the higher dice pool. And not only are double-numbers a way to increase success without lowering the odds of failure, they also allow <i>you</i> to be less vulnerable to effects such as these. I gather some people dislike the 'dice tricks', but the mechanical and characterisation implications of them may actually be the thing I love the most in this new Charm set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:25:05-08:00","id":746794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=746753#post746753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, Excellencies. There's a weird mix of philosophies here (not on your part, I mean - just in the design of the book).</div> </div> </div> </div>Philosophically, is it more interesting to have 5 mechanically identical charms applying to different situations with differing flavor text, or have one charm with minimal flavor that has a fill in the blank section to apply to 5 different situations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1970-yeangst","name":"yeangst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:26:11-08:00","id":746797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=746753#post746753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, Excellencies. There's a weird mix of philosophies here (not on your part, I mean - just in the design of the book).</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. You get free Excellencies so you're not spending XP on meat-and-potatoes dice-adders, but then you have <i>slightly different</i> dice adders / manipulators gatekeeping the interesting effects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:37:43-08:00","id":746831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yeangst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=746794#post746794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Philosophically, is it more interesting to have 5 mechanically identical charms applying to different situations with differing flavor text, or have one charm with minimal flavor that has a fill in the blank section to apply to 5 different situations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I find those about equally interesting - in which case, I favor the one with the smaller wordcount and conceptual overhead. Something like a Supreme Perfection of (Ability Specialty) would cover a lot of ground. Even easier, I think, would be a &quot;1/scene, free full Excellency.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, there is some reason for not having a &quot;standard double-9s&quot; Charm, say. Double-Xs attached to a particular effect gives a way to say &quot;When the Solar attempts this special power, he probably succeeds - and while double-Xs is common in noncombat trees at a low mote cost, it'd be a pretty huge swing in most combat trees. I can get that motivation - though it still feels like you could get by with two versions of the same (or, well, one version that works differently in combat time). But the free Excellency feels pretty justifiable almost everywhere, and the double-9s in Performance just feel ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:44:01-08:00","id":746866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=746603#post746603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that there is a strong notion that generalized charms like you describe, is boring design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue isn't boringness so much as imbalance. Getting double 7s on a bargain roll is really really strong, but it won't mess up the basic numbers behind the system. Getting double 7s on an attack roll absolutely will. You saw this same issue in 2e with its generic charms - I(A)M is infamously powerful when applied to combat abilities, but who ever cared about, say, Infinite Craft Mastery? Not every ability is equal, and creating generic effects for them as though they were is going to end in bad things happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T10:30:55-08:00","id":747013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=745019#post745019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4e will create a codified series of charms for all abilities. The Magnificent (Ability) charms. First Magnificent (Ability) lets you reroll 1s. Second Magnificent (Ability) gives you double nines. Third Magnificent (Ability) lets you gain non-charm dice if you roll at least one set of 3 matching successes or a run of 4 successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And 5e will give you those for free for caste/favored abilities with a dot, or non-caste/favored abilities with a charm purchase. And then add even wonkier tricks.<br /> <br /> Sigh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T13:30:02-08:00","id":747364,"title":"","content":"<u>Resistance</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 26<br /> By Ability requirement: 2/3/6/5/10<br /> By Essence requirement: 10/8/7/1<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Enemy takes -1i for each 1 rolled on attack roll. Enemy rerolls <i>successful</i> damage dice.<br /> <br /> Themes: Have all the health levels. Recover health levels, or be rewarded for having them. Resist poison and disease. Absorb damage without harm; possibly gain rewards for doing so. Use armor more easily. Bring down the red haze and kill all that moves.<br /> <br /> A surprisingly small number of Ability 5 Charms, here! It really feels like you can invest in Resistance at a number of different levels \u2013 which is nice, for the only universally-applicable defensive Ability. Note that, unlike 2e, Resistance Charms have to be declared <i>before</i> the attack roll (unless they say otherwise) \u2013 being able to mount a cheap soak-based defense is likely to be a big deal, given that it may never go off.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>4 Hardness, -2 damage to all attacks for one tick.</li> <li>Post-hit soak booster. Upgrades to remove damage successes.</li> <li>Soak unsoakable withering damage; against a Decisive attack, create extra health levels.</li> <li>Extra health levels.</li> <li>Heal fast. (Recommended with lots of #4.)</li> <li>Gain [~.25*your health levels]i.</li> <li>Put on armor in a handful of turns. Er, how long does it take normally?</li> <li>Once your armor is on, its Mobility penalty is 0.</li> <li>Scenelong bonus dice vs. poison.</li> <li>When struck by a Withering attack, pay 1i to recover (damage dice/2)m.</li> <li>Become immune to minor scenery damage, from brambles(?) to bonfires. Gain soak or hardness. <i>Can\u2019t be used in armor</i>.</li> <li>Halve (or more) post-soak damage of a Withering attack.</li> <li>Apply soak to a Decisive attack(!). Perfect soak vs. uncountable damage.</li> <li>1/fight, heal when you recover from Crash.</li> <li>Store your armor in Elsewhere.</li> <li>Bonus successes vs. illness.</li> <li>1/fight, when struck by a Decisive, pay 2i to gain 1wp.</li> <li>Go into a berserk rage. Gain +1 die to combat pools; reduce wound penalties by 1.</li> <li>Heal your -0 health levels gradually, but in combat time.</li> <li>Reduce the penalty and duration of a crippling attack. (What\u2019s a crippling attack?)</li> <li>1/scene, force attacker to reroll <i>successful</i> damage dice.</li> <li>Summon magical glowing sun-armor. (Still not a technique!)</li> <li>Gain immunity to any poison or disease you\u2019ve encountered before, and resistance to the rest.</li> <li>When struck by a Decisive attack, gain (half the non-successful damage dice)i.</li> <li>While under #18, go into a more-berserk (berserker?) rage. Gain +3 dice to combat pools; ignore wound penalties; recover 1m/turn.</li> <li>Gain 20 Hardness, bonus soak, and post-soak damage negation, but only as long as you make big attacks every turn.</li> </ol>The ticklong duration of Durability of Oak Meditation (#1) is a big deal \u2013 that makes it a mote-efficient reply to some of the big magical flurries. This feels like a good dip for anyone expecting to run into a bunch of Iron Whirlwinds; 3m for one chance at -2 damage doesn\u2019t feel great, but 3m for <i>six</i> chances feels quite a bit better.<br /> <br /> The upgrade to Spirit Strengthens the Skin (#2) is worded confusingly. Is it correct that this effect has a <i>base</i> cost of 1wp, 2i, and then costs +2m for each damage success bought off? The actual wording says the cost is one thing, and then immediately states the cost is something else. Also, is there any limit to the upgraded use, or can I buy off as much damage as I have motes to spend?<br /> <br /> Iron Skin Concentration (#3) has a pleasantly anime feel, where you take the enemy\u2019s big hit and are barely scratched. Not sure I love how completely different the Withering/Decisive effects are, but that\u2019s a minor complaint. This Charm protects against unsoakable damage; the only Charm granting such is in Black Lotus, so far, as well as\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026 ahaha, the description of cauterizing a wound mentions it\u2019s unsoakable damage. Given that it\u2019s actual damage, I bet so.<br /> <br /> Ox-Body Technique (#4) scales with Stamina and doesn\u2019t have trap options now. I approve!<br /> <br /> At Essence 5, Body-Mending Meditation (#5) + Fate-Shifting Solar Arete can let you recover a -0 bashing level every thirty seconds. I\u2019m just sayin\u2019. ([3600 seconds in an hour] / [19 successes * Essence 5], for the record.) Note that Ox-Body alone won\u2019t raise your healing speed; absent BMM, you can get stuck in your -2s for a looooong time.<br /> <br /> Are Armored Scout\u2019s Invigoration (#8) and Whirlwind Armor-Donning Prana (#7) meant to stack? As written, it doesn\u2019t appear that they do \u2013 ASI doesn\u2019t kick in until the armor is worn. (Why is armor such a pain to put on? I mean, multiple Simple actions with a Charm? Most of the fights I\u2019ve seen so far are <i>over</i> in that much time.)<br /> <br /> Adamant Skin Technique (#13) is a great one-turn panic button \u2013 soaking Decisive attacks is huge. Here\u2019s the weird thing, though: if you use AST, <i>make sure the attack hits</i>. Like, don\u2019t pump the Excellency, do whatever you can to lower your Defense. Let it be 0, if you can \u2013 it\u2019s not like that will (generally) add extra damage. Because, look: you\u2019ve got to activate this Charm before the attack gets rolled, right? So if they hit, you\u2019ve spent 8m to consume almost all of their Initiative, taking little or no damage. If they <i>miss</i>, you just spent 8m to drain them of the 2i they lose for missing. It\u2019s unfortunate that AST requires Diamond Body Technique (#11), since there are a lot of builds (i.e., <i>anything that wears armor</i>) for which the latter Charm is useless. (It\u2019s also kind of weird that 10 damage bounces from AST, 100 damage kills you through it, but infinity damage\u2026 again bounces off. What?)<br /> <br /> Illness-Resisting Meditation (#16) is weirdly less useful than Poison-Resisting Meditation (#9). They\u2019re both cheaper Excellencies, but mid-combat poisoning feels seems common \u2013 mid-combat disease doesn\u2019t, and if you\u2019re not getting sick in combat, who cares how expensive the Excellency is?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a persistent theme here of Stamina <i>mattering</i> for Resistance \u2013 Charms are faster or cheaper or more efficacious with high Stamina. I like this.<br /> <br /> Immunity to Everything Technique (#23) suggests some kind of funny behavior patterns \u2013 poisoning yourself <i>now</i> to gain resistance later. (It also makes the old 2e-ism of \u201csame stats as Arrow Frog Venom, but<i> not</i> Arrow Frog Venom,\u201d a lot more dangerous.)<br /> <br /> <br /> A couple of rough spots aside, Resistance looks solid. I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d want everything in it, but there\u2019s a solid core of powers to take here. (Might not be a great choice for Supernal, though \u2013 <i>one</i> Charm over Essence 3.)<br /> <br /> <i>Yes: </i>Aegis of Invulnerable Might (#20) does a lot to create shifted combat priorities \u2013 it makes what would normally be bad moves into interesting decisions. Kudos!<br /> <i>No:</i> Whirlwind Armor-Donning Prana. Just take Glorious Solar Plate, if you don\u2019t want to wear armor. Or, well, you could, if it wasn\u2019t a prereq.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird: </i>Battle-Fury Focus (#18) and Bloodthirsty Sword-Dancer Spirit (#25) are both powerful Charms \u2013 they\u2019re about the only source of persistent penalty-negation and combat bonus dice. They <i>also</i> eat up two full actions, in addition to their other costs. Again, isn\u2019t the fight likely going to be largely over by then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-01-2015, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T13:56:20-08:00","id":747417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here\u2019s the weird thing, though: if you use AST, make sure the attack hits.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wonder if that gamble might be part of the balance consideration of the Charm... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immunity to Everything Technique (#23) suggests some kind of funny behavior patterns \u2013 poisoning yourself now to gain resistance later.</div> </div> </div> </div> Did you ever see The Princess Bride? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T14:42:53-08:00","id":747482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=747417#post747417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wonder if that gamble might be part of the balance consideration of the Charm...</div> </div> </div> </div>It might well be! Still kind of counter-intuitive - &quot;Okay, to be safe, make sure you step <i>into</i> the next swing, because if you dodge it you'll be in trouble.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did you ever see The Princess Bride? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Ayup. It's not necessarily a bad dynamic, just an odd one. &quot;I hear they have plague in the next city over - field trip!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T14:43:26-08:00","id":747483,"title":"","content":"<u>Ride</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 36<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/2/7/6/20<br /> By Essence requirement: 8/14/14/0/0<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Enemy loses 1 damage per 1 or 2 rolled. Gain 1m for Ride Charms for each 10 the enemy rolls.<br /> <br /> Themes: Have the highest mobility of anyone on the battlefield, especially when running away. Never lose your mount, to circumstance or damage or unhorsing. Your mount is a combatant in his own right.<br /> <br /> A lot of Ride Charms here, given that none of them are over Essence 3.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Gain a number of minor mount-enhancing Abilities \u2013 prevent fatigue, call it to you, etc.</li> <li>Mount resists fatigue, gains a movement success, and can use Graceful Crane Stance/Monkey Leap Technique.</li> <li>Reflexively Disengage while you are mounted.</li> <li>Your mount moves at greater speeds while outside combat. (How fast does it normally move, outside combat?)</li> <li>Mount can rise from prone for 1m.</li> <li>Your mount gains its own move and attack actions, as well as its own Initiative track.</li> <li>Your mount can reflexively Defend Other on you.</li> <li>Spend your health levels on behalf of your mount, at a reduced rate.</li> <li>Tack and bard a mount in 1-4 rounds.</li> <li>Automatically succeed at a Disengage as long as only one enemy is at close range.</li> <li>Convert mount\u2019s speed bonus to successes.</li> <li>Double mount\u2019s speed for the scene.</li> <li>#11 can be used to enhance a Join Battle roll.</li> <li>Your mount ignores wound penalties.</li> <li>Recurring 1s on a mounted movement roll; leave a trail of bonfire flames in your wake.</li> <li>Recover instantly from an unhorse Gambit.</li> <li>Unhorse someone and steal his mount.</li> <li>Transfer half your Initiative to your mount, or vice-versa.</li> <li>Over a scene of treatment, absorb and reduce your mount\u2019s wounds.</li> <li>While using #6 and #7, your mount may Decisively counterattack for attacks on you.</li> <li>Your mount (barely) avoids Crash or death, as long as it had at least 2i or 2 HLs to begin with.</li> <li>An attack on your mount loses 1 damage per 1 or 2 rolled.</li> <li>Summon an Essence-horse. But it\u2019s an expression of skill, and no one would try to label this a\u2026 yeah, you get the joke.</li> <li>Ride off into the sunset. Recover motes and Willpower, and remove a point of Limit.</li> <li>If someone approaches you after a Disengage, retreat two range bands.</li> <li>For each 10 the enemy rolls, gain 1m for use on Ride Charms next turn.</li> <li>Substitute Ride for Awareness in Join Battle.</li> <li>Move three range bands a turn at extreme range from all enemies, or two bands/turn at closer ranges.</li> <li>Your mount runs on water or air for one turn.</li> <li>Rush an enemy in the air.</li> <li>Summon your mount\u2019s tack, barding, and weapons from Elsewhere.</li> <li>Mount armor has no Mobility penalty.</li> <li>Activate \u201cattack-evasive Dodge Charms\u201d on behalf of your mount.</li> <li>Your mount gains 1i/turn, plus bonuses when you outrace an enemy.</li> <li>While using #6 and #7, your mount may (reflexively?) Decisively Clash with attacks aimed at you.</li> <li>Your mount gains bonus soak for the scene.</li> </ol>Elusive Mount Technique (#3) \u2013 i.e., \u201cDisengage reflexively\u201d \u2013 is a pretty big deal for some archetypes. If you\u2019re an archer, being on a horse is a big boost with just a couple of Charms.<br /> <br /> Am I reading it right that Seasoned Beast-Rider\u2019s Approach (#6) makes your mount a potential weak spot? If it has an Initiative track, you can aim Withering attacks at it \u2013 and to this point in the tree, it\u2019s likely to have a lower Defense than the Solar is, which means enemies can use it to juice up to attack the Solar.<br /> <br /> Worthy Mount Technique (#7) is fueled by the mount\u2019s Initiative. What happens if the mount doesn\u2019t have an Initiative track?<br /> <br /> Does Untouchable Horseman\u2019s Attitude (#10) <i>replace</i> the cost to Disengage, or <i>supplement</i> it? The latter, I assume.<br /> <br /> A number of these effects <i>appear to</i> sidestep the normal Charm-die penalties \u2013 boosting Speed, as per Supernal Lash Discipline (#12), seems to be uncapped. So how does this interact with Speed Fury Focus (#13), which adds (Speed) successes to Join Battle?<br /> <br /> Immortal Rider\u2019s Advantage (#18) specifies that it only lets you transfer half your Initiative, rounded up. But, um, the Charm is Reflexive \u2013 so transfer half, and then transfer half again, and then\u2026 Also, I think the cost for this Charm should be \u201c-\u201c \u2013 typically, quantities <i>transferred</i> are not counted as costs. (Cf. Essence-Lending Method.)<br /> <br /> Ariana, what exactly is holding you onto the back of that horse?<br /> <br /> Mounted archer is <i>nasty</i> here. Move while aiming; Disengage farther than normal; reflexively recover from being dismounted. So, say you\u2019re a close-range warrior on foot \u2013 do you have any way to combat this, other than going indoors and never coming out?<br /> <br /> Fierce Charger\u2019s Pulse (#26) adds a Ride-Charms-only mote pool. Been a while since we\u2019ve gotten another of those, but I can\u2019t say I\u2019ve missed them.<br /> <br /> A heavily-invested Solar rider is going to be mean: mobile, generating extra Initiative off the mount, making an extra attack, and so on, and \u2013 critically \u2013 defended by the Solar\u2019s own Dodge Charms. This is an archetype that appears to heavily favor the ranged attacker, though; Melee-based combatants aren\u2019t going to be able to defend their mounts, won\u2019t care about the Disengage bonuses, and may find the mount is more liability than help once enemies begin swinging at it. The primary benefit of being on a mount in such circumstances appears to be countering other mounted combatants, and given that the Disengage benefits outpace the Rush advantages, that\u2019s unlikely to be enough.<br /> <br /> Does anything clarify whether the mount bonuses apply to sapient mounts? I haven\u2019t seen anything saying <i>no</i>, which suggests that you and your Tyrant Lizard Lunar companion are going to be a pretty brutal combination.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Untouchable Solar Speed (#33) is absolutely necessary to make an Initiative-equipped mount a safe investment rather than a liability.<br /> <i>No: </i>Harmonious Tacking Technique (#9). Even with this Charm, it could take you <i>four rounds</i> to get a mount ready to go. Completely outclassed by Whirlwind Horse-Armoring Prana (#28), which does the job instantly.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Hero Rides Away (#24) is exactly as weird as it was\u2026 what, five years ago?... when it meant that John Wayne gets to dispel limit for riding off at the end of the movie, but Kwai Chang Caine doesn\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T15:57:30-08:00","id":747670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=747483#post747483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Hero Rides Away (#24) is exactly as weird as it was\u2026 what, five years ago?... when it meant that John Wayne gets to dispel limit for riding off at the end of the movie, but Kwai Chang Caine doesn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>A custom Integrity Charm of similar effect seems to be in order...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:06:08-08:00","id":747682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=747670#post747670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A custom Integrity Charm of similar effect seems to be in order...</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I dunno, doesn't really fit with the new Integrity theme. It plays into a very specific thing in Ride, I'm not sure it's a good idea to just broadly apply it to other Abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:38:08-08:00","id":747779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hear they have plague in the next city over - field trip!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Pulp hero vaccination; you don't weaken the disease, you're just stronger. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:04:18-08:00","id":747897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=747682#post747682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I dunno, doesn't really fit with the new Integrity theme. It plays into a very specific thing in Ride, I'm not sure it's a good idea to just broadly apply it to other Abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>On one hand, I feel it is good that Integrity good more tightly focused, it was too thematically broad before, to the point I'd be hard-pressed to say what that theme was, exactly. That said, the new tree serves well a quite specific archetype that won't fit every character that could be heavily devoted to Integrity. I think expanding the trees into different archetypes, taking into account the understanding that having every fricking Charm in a given Ability to be good at it is no longer an expectation, is a good place for custom charms.<br /> <br /> And I can imagine some form of &quot;incorruptible folk hero&quot; group of Charms being an archetype within Integrity, and having a Charm somewhat similar to that ride Charm in effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:14:03-08:00","id":747903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=747897#post747897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I can imagine some form of &quot;incorruptible folk hero&quot; group of Charms being an archetype within Integrity</div> </div> </div> </div>Why Integrity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:36:01-08:00","id":747984,"title":"","content":"<u>Sail</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 39<br /> By Ability requirement: 0/0/5/4/30<br /> By Essence requirement: 13/15/11/0/0<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Treat enemy 1s as 10s. Reroll nonsuccesses. Free full Excellency.<br /> <br /> Themes: You\u2019re on a boat! Get bonuses to your speed, your maneuvers, and your ship\u2019s durability \u2013 they can\u2019t stop you, because you\u2019re on a boat. Crush other people\u2019s ships beneath you \u2013 this ain\u2019t Sea World, this is real as it gets. Gain various personal \u201csalty old sailor\u201d bonuses \u2013 you\u2019re on a boat, and don\u2019t you ever forget.<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026 Sorry.<br /> <br /> This will be a nice juxtaposition. In 2e, it was often argued that Sail and Ride were, effectively, one Ability; I\u2019m curious to see how 3e distinguishes them.<br /> <br /> At a glance, this may be one of the most lopsided trees so far. Over 75% of the Charms are at Ability 5; <i>none</i> have Ability requirements less than 3. The Essence requirements are uneven in the other direction \u2013 nothing <i>over</i> a requirement of 3. So to get much mileage out of this, you want to be all in on Sail \u2013 but not <i>all</i>-all in, because it might not be the best choice for Supernal. It doesn\u2019t come through in the description so far, but this is also one of the most compact trees I\u2019ve seen; very few Charms run more than a paragraph or so of text.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Permanent benefits: recurring 6s on Sail; add Sail/2 to Resolve vs. supernatural fear; recover instantly from a fall; find your way to anywhere you\u2019ve been before.</li> <li>Permanently +2 Stamina for resisting deprivation (food, oxygen, etc.).</li> <li>Permanent bonus: if you wake up on a ship, you can ignore the WP cost to resist one social influence that day.</li> <li>+2 dice to avoid hazards, or +2 successes if you\u2019ve avoided these specific hazards before.</li> <li>Anyone on your ship without permission takes -1 die. You can pull 5m from the ship.</li> <li>Ship\u2019s Speed +1.</li> <li>Creatures of darkness in your crew don\u2019t count as such for the purpose of social magic, your anima, or your area-of-effect attacks.</li> <li>Double-9s or recurring 1s on a Sail roll, after the roll is made (!).</li> <li>Double ship\u2019s Maneuverability and add 1 to its Speed for one maneuver.</li> <li>+Speed to a Conceal maneuver.</li> <li>+Essence dice and +Essence non-Charm successes to a Broadside maneuver.</li> <li>+1 level of damage when ramming the enemy; cancel the enemy\u2019s Broadside maneuver.</li> <li>In a Positioning maneuver, treat enemy 1s as your 10s. Cancel the enemy\u2019s Ram maneuver.</li> <li>Permanently gain X dice to your ship-defending actions, where -X is your ship\u2019s hull penalty.</li> <li>Predict the weather for the next day or so.</li> <li>Ship\u2019s Speed +1 for one day. Incompatible with #17.</li> <li>Double ship\u2019s Speed bonus for sails, but reduce any rower bonus to +1. No bonus for being dragged by sea monsters. Incompatible with #16.</li> <li>Negate all damage to the ship for one turn.</li> <li>Spend 3HL to heal one level of damage to your ship.</li> <li>Negate your ship\u2019s hull penalty.</li> <li>Reroll all nonsuccesses on a Sail action.</li> <li>1/scene, free full Sail Excellency.</li> <li>Reduce wind-based penalties (are those a thing, prior to now?) by 3.</li> <li>-2 Momentum to the cost of all maneuvers for the rest of the scene.</li> <li>On a successful ram, also shock and board.</li> <li>+3 non-Charm dice to Join Battle on a boat.</li> <li>Double Momentum gained via a Positioning maneuver.</li> <li>Sense danger (Essence) minutes early, apparently whether on a boat or not. Bonus successes to Awareness on a boat.</li> <li>Render the ship and crew immune to the Wyld.</li> <li>Gain extra health levels equal to the ship\u2019s current hull.</li> <li>Commit motes to keep your ship from falling apart at 0 health.</li> <li>Expend your anima to make SWEET BURNING SUN-SAILS that terrify creatures of darkness.</li> <li>+(Essence) auto-successes to fighting a storm for the next hour.</li> <li>Give bonus dice to your fleet, when maneuvering.</li> <li>Permanently enhance your sailors\u2019 stats.</li> <li>On incapacitating another ship with a maneuver, you keep all your existing Momentum (and gain more!) instead of losing it.</li> <li>On incapacitating another ship with a maneuver, gain motes and Willpower.</li> <li>Add your ship\u2019s Speed to your personal movement, and its Maneuverability to your Defense. Speak an ancient ocean language. Become immune to drowning.</li> </ol>Salty Dog Method (#1) is a permanent Charm with more broad utility than many of the Simple effects in other sets. This does not prevent \u201cshe immediately falls up\u201d from being a ridiculous turn of phrase.<br /> <br /> This is three Permanent effects in a row. Sail would be a great dip, if it didn\u2019t have a five-dot Ability prereq for some of these. SDM is probably <i>still</i> worth the dip.<br /> <br /> The base effect of Perfect Reckoning Technique (#4) doesn\u2019t even break even mote-wise until you\u2019ve used it twice in the same scene. The earlier naval combat examples seem to suggest you\u2019ll be rolling enough to make that worthwhile \u2013 five times for a storm, ten times for Bluehaven. Not sure I love that, though \u2013 the multiplication of rolls feels too much like make-work so an Exalt can\u2019t blow through the problem with one Excellency use.<br /> <br /> Is the effect of Ship-Claiming Stance (#5) permanent? The duration listed is \u201cInstant,\u201d which isn\u2019t much help. Can I claim any number of ships?<br /> <br /> Ship-Sleeking Technique (#6) adds 2mph to your ship\u2019s speed, with a Charm purchase and committed motes. Woo? Edit: It looks like I was unimpressed too early; Tide Cutting Essence Infusion (#16), at Essence 2, is a more expensive and shorter duration version of the exact same effect.<br /> <br /> Okay, Orichalcum Letters of Marque (#7) is actually really cool, if kind of character-specific. Hi, Moray Darktide!<br /> <br /> That is\u2026 a picture of a really enormous ram at the front of a ship. I rather like this picture \u2013 it\u2019s got a swashbuckly \u201cFull speed ahead!\u201d sort of feel.<br /> <br /> Immortal Mariner\u2019s Advantage (#8) is by far the best double-9s or reroll 1s effect so far, because you can <i>wait</i> to activate it.<br /> <br /> Deck-Sweeping Fusillade (#11) says to \u201c[treat] the result as if it was (Essence) successes higher than it really is.\u201d Don\u2019t do this, game; either tell me to add [Ess] successes, or to add [Ess] non-Charm successes, but keep with the established notation!<br /> <br /> Hull-Preserving Technique (#18), i.e., \u201ca perfect defense for your ship,\u201d is pretty cool. I can see some fun uses here, where your vessel just <i>refuses to go down</i> while the enemy hurls sorcery at it \u2013 this is something a good Solar captain might go \u201cHeck yeah\u201d at. Hull-Taming Transfusion (#19), which will kill you long before it fixes your ship, is <i>not</i>.<br /> <br /> So, uh, how does Ship-Leavening Method (#20) interact with Ship-Imperiled Vigor (#14)? Do you have no penalty while SLM is up, or are you just ignoring it?<br /> <br /> Burning Anima Sails (#32) again has an implicit cost of 3a that is communicated only via text.<br /> <br /> Storm-Weathering Essence Infusion (#33) is just a strange Charm. It\u2019s another limited Infinite Ability Mastery \u2013 this one applying only to storms. But we were told that fighting off a storm all night might require five rolls, and this Charm only lasts for an hour \u2013 so you\u2019re going to pay another 6m, 1wp for each of those rolls, right?<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Salty Dog Method is clear and powerful. Burning Anima Sails is going to be a great in-play visual, with several plausible uses \u2013 repairing sails, countering attacks on your mast, and roaring into battle against Skullstone or the Lintha.<br /> <i>No:</i> Ship-Breaker Method (#12) and Superior Positioning Technique (#13). Look, game, commit to your design principles. If combat is transparent, then let it be transparent; don\u2019t tell me in <i>exactly two Charms</i> to write down what I\u2019m doing secretly and reveal it post-roll. Just make the maneuvers chosen secret in general, if this is design space you want.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> What the <i>heck</i> is up with Ocean-Conquering Avater (#22)? \u201cDuration: one turn?\u201d Applies \u201cto her next Sail roll?\u201d That\u2019s not the templating used for any of the other free-full-Excellency boosters. Shouldn\u2019t this be like Supremacy of War Meditation or Supernal Control Method, which are Reflexive, Instant? Or Awakening Eye, which is\u2026 er, Supplemental, Instant? Or Eclectic Verbiage of Law or Life-Sculpting Hands Technique, which are\u2026 Permanent\u2026? Or\u2026 uh\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026 Since we <i>are</i> in Sail, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/p1rIiGk41Zw?t=1m5s\" target=\"_blank\">WHO HIRED THESE CHARMS?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-01-2015, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T18:19:09-08:00","id":748101,"title":"","content":"Going to go back in thread history a bit here.<br /> <br /> Flowing Mind Prana, in Lore, annoyed me on reading too. Unbalanced XP not being a fun thing, after all.<br /> <br /> On reading your summary, I managed to re-read it, and noticed something:<br /> <br /> &quot;To activate this Charm, the Solar commits a number of experience points from her own unspent experience total.&quot;<br /> <br /> Emphasis commits, as in commits essence. And then regains via roll that can only be made at the end of each story. I'm wondering if the use of the term 'commits' was intentional - the Solar is deferring his own development for others, not bypassing his development entirely. In other words, if you don't get all the experience back this story, you can roll again, on the same pool, next story.<br /> <br /> That makes the 'spend 1xp to get a chance to get *more* xp back' charm make more sense too.<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> As an asides, great thread. I find myself disagreeing with a lot of your interpretations as overly harsh, with the meaning reasonably clear, but do agree that much of this could stand being tightened up. I just didn't want to comment on all of my counter-interpretations and necro half the thread. In other parts, some areas, like the repeat double-9s in Performance or the obvious lack of rewriting once the glossary and keywords were updated, really annoy me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9061-tyranny12","name":"tyranny12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T18:31:16-08:00","id":748116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tyranny12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=748101#post748101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going to go back in thread history a bit here.<br /> <br /> Flowing Mind Prana, in Lore, annoyed me on reading too. Unbalanced XP not being a fun thing, after all.<br /> <br /> On reading your summary, I managed to re-read it, and noticed something:<br /> <br /> &quot;To activate this Charm, the Solar commits a number of experience points from her own unspent experience total.&quot;<br /> <br /> Emphasis commits, as in commits essence. And then regains via roll that can only be made at the end of each story. I'm wondering if the use of the term 'commits' was intentional - the Solar is deferring his own development for others, not bypassing his development entirely. In other words, if you don't get all the experience back this story, you can roll again, on the same pool, next story.<br /> <br /> That makes the 'spend 1xp to get a chance to get *more* xp back' charm make more sense too.<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> As an asides, great thread. I find myself disagreeing with a lot of your interpretations as overly harsh, with the meaning reasonably clear, but do agree that much of this could stand being tightened up. I just didn't want to comment on all of my counter-interpretations and necro half the thread. In other parts, some areas, like the repeat double-9s in Performance or the obvious lack of rewriting once the glossary and keywords were updated, really annoy me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as others have noted, there are definitely places where a reread clarifies matters somewhat - price of doing a stream-of-consciousness read-through, I guess. I think there are also some places where intent is... sussable?... but where the actual wording doesn't seem to support it, which may be some of what you're saying, as well.<br /> <br /> Case in point: let's say that you <i>are</i> intended to eventually get back all the XP you spend on FMP. The Charm says &quot;At the end of each story, the Solar may roll a number of dice equal to experience points spent on this Charm, regaining a number of experience equal to her successes, but not beyond the total amount of experience she expended in training.&quot; I was reading &quot;experience points spent on this Charm&quot; as &quot;experience points spent on this Charm <i>this story</i>.&quot; If it's not that, we could parse it as &quot;experience points spent on the Charm, <i>period</i>,&quot; but that's a terrifying thought - once we pick up Tireless Learner Method, we have an uncapped XP-generating engine that gives us back 75% of all of the XP we've spent on the Charm since the start of the game at the end of every story, no matter how much we've recovered already.<br /> <br /> The sane version of that translation, then - and the one I think you're suggesting, if I read you right? - is that it means something like &quot;experience spent on the Charm <i>and not refunded yet</i>, no matter how far back it was spent.&quot; But that's troubling as well - most centrally, because nothing in the Charm's text says anything like the proposed rider. And that's bad for a host of reasons! (It also makes Tireless Learner Method pretty ugly - we're now spending XP in hope that a biiiiiig pool that averages 75% successes will actually earn 100%+.)<br /> <br /> All that said, I think there's a reasonable chance that you're right that this is the intent - but I don't look forward to trying to have that argument with someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-01-2015, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T00:24:44-08:00","id":748612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=747903#post747903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why Integrity?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Somehow, the denotation and connotation of the word &quot;Integrity&quot; are more closely associated with &quot;incorruptible&quot; than the denotation and connotation of &quot;Ride.&quot; How strange...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T02:39:20-08:00","id":748797,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm very leery of those Lore teaching charms.<br /> <br /> I'm looking at a built which has the teaching charms up to Power-Awarding Prana. For around 6 to 12 xp cost (12 if you want the entire circle at once with Legendary Scholar\u2019s Curriculum) you teach lore 5. For another 6 to 12 xp cost, you teach everyone up to Flowing Mind Prana. You can of course also use Power-Awarding Prana (you can just about manage committing 3 uses).<br /> <br /> If you thought the Charms you can of course use Power-Awarding Prana to give the current teacher Tireless Learner Method. From essence 2 on you can teach the group Tireless Learner Method and use Power-Awarding Prana to give Legendary Scholar\u2019s Curriculum and things just break down:<br /> <br /> Everybody in the group can teach two or all the other members abilities &amp; attributes at 25-50% of the xp cost for 1 person. You can of course use Power-Awarding Prana to also give Selfsame Master Instructor and all the Charms currently known by the group can also be shared at 25-50% of the cost.<br /> <br /> This, euhm, seems broken...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T03:15:25-08:00","id":748832,"title":"","content":"Yes, this kind of direct manipulation of XP is a thing that should be categorically outside the purview of charms. XP is an OOC resource.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T03:21:53-08:00","id":748834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=748116#post748116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, as others have noted, there are definitely places where a reread clarifies matters somewhat - price of doing a stream-of-consciousness read-through, I guess. I think there are also some places where intent is... sussable?... but where the actual wording doesn't seem to support it, which may be some of what you're saying, as well.<br /> <br /> Case in point: let's say that you <i>are</i> intended to eventually get back all the XP you spend on FMP. The Charm says &quot;At the end of each story, the Solar may roll a number of dice equal to experience points spent on this Charm, regaining a number of experience equal to her successes, but not beyond the total amount of experience she expended in training.&quot; I was reading &quot;experience points spent on this Charm&quot; as &quot;experience points spent on this Charm <i>this story</i>.&quot; If it's not that, we could parse it as &quot;experience points spent on the Charm, <i>period</i>,&quot; but that's a terrifying thought - once we pick up Tireless Learner Method, we have an uncapped XP-generating engine that gives us back 75% of all of the XP we've spent on the Charm since the start of the game at the end of every story, no matter how much we've recovered already.<br /> <br /> The sane version of that translation, then - and the one I think you're suggesting, if I read you right? - is that it means something like &quot;experience spent on the Charm <i>and not refunded yet</i>, no matter how far back it was spent.&quot; But that's troubling as well - most centrally, because nothing in the Charm's text says anything like the proposed rider. And that's bad for a host of reasons! (It also makes Tireless Learner Method pretty ugly - we're now spending XP in hope that a biiiiiig pool that averages 75% successes will actually earn 100%+.)<br /> <br /> All that said, I think there's a reasonable chance that you're right that this is the intent - but I don't look forward to trying to have that argument with someone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had originally read it as XP roulette. You are likely to just plain lose XP, but might gain more. This struck me as a bit silly.<br /> <br /> I had not considered that the roll could be cumulative (roll ALL the XP invested, instead of just for this story), nor did I consider that you would get more than one chance to roll the pool.<br /> <br /> I read it simply as &quot;You get to roll the XP you spent this story. Every success gets you one back. The others are lost, period.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, what, do we think, is the intent of this charm, as in what purpose does it server for players in an average game? Is it supposed to be a XP engine to feed other effects that cost XP (such as WST), or does it simply allow someone to play the &quot;support&quot; role within Exalted and transfer their XP to someone who might get more use out of it ( like the tank)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T04:51:49-08:00","id":748925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=748797#post748797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm very leery of those Lore teaching charms.<br /> <br /> I'm looking at a built which has the teaching charms up to Power-Awarding Prana. For around 6 to 12 xp cost (12 if you want the entire circle at once with Legendary Scholar\u2019s Curriculum) you teach lore 5. For another 6 to 12 xp cost, you teach everyone up to Flowing Mind Prana. You can of course also use Power-Awarding Prana (you can just about manage committing 3 uses).<br /> <br /> If you thought the Charms you can of course use Power-Awarding Prana to give the current teacher Tireless Learner Method. From essence 2 on you can teach the group Tireless Learner Method and use Power-Awarding Prana to give Legendary Scholar\u2019s Curriculum and things just break down:<br /> <br /> Everybody in the group can teach two or all the other members abilities &amp; attributes at 25-50% of the xp cost for 1 person. You can of course use Power-Awarding Prana to also give Selfsame Master Instructor and all the Charms currently known by the group can also be shared at 25-50% of the cost.<br /> <br /> This, euhm, seems broken...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the numbers above are generated, but do agree that the concept of recurring solar circle training is potentially scary, particularly/specifically in regards to Legendary Scholar's Curriculum. I also don't think any sane ST would let it progress to the above level, but that is not what we are here to discuss.<br /> <br /> How did you get those numbers? I did a bit of math, and Lore 5 + Flowing Mind Prana would require the commitance of 53 xp and 17 weeks of dedicated training time by my calculation. That's without Legendary Scholar, Tireless Learner, or Power Awarding Prana. One read of Legendary Scholar, one that I would support if anyone tried to pull the above, is that each person trained requires the individual training time.<br /> <br /> Hmm... so I commit 53 XP to training one person up if I have 17 weeks of downtime. Even with Tireless Learner, how many stories before I get that XP back in full?<br /> <br /> Also, I get to rewrite their intimacies... at 53 XP, that's 17 new intimacy levels that the teacher gets to assign.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Realised you roll a number of dice equal to XP committed, not an attribute roll. That makes this easier to do and the primary limiter is time.<br /> <br /> Having read the above, I'm thinking that this is a mechanic that is open to abuse, but not wide open. Assuming my numbers are right and I'm not missing some 'discount' charm somewhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9061,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9061-tyranny12","user":"tyranny12","date":". 11-02-2015, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9061-tyranny12","name":"tyranny12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T04:57:59-08:00","id":748928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=748834#post748834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I had originally read it as XP roulette. You are likely to just plain lose XP, but might gain more. This struck me as a bit silly.<br /> <br /> I had not considered that the roll could be cumulative (roll ALL the XP invested, instead of just for this story), nor did I consider that you would get more than one chance to roll the pool.<br /> <br /> I read it simply as &quot;You get to roll the XP you spent this story. Every success gets you one back. The others are lost, period.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this is how it works, and this is how I first read it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, what, do we think, is the intent of this charm, as in what purpose does it server for players in an average game? Is it supposed to be a XP engine to feed other effects that cost XP (such as WST), or does it simply allow someone to play the &quot;support&quot; role within Exalted and transfer their XP to someone who might get more use out of it ( like the tank)? </div> </div> </div>The (IMO, half-baked) idea here is &quot;oh see you can teach people stuff! but training folks is too valuable, so we make it cost your own XP. but no one's going to just give away the XP, so we'll let get half back. and if they invest more in the concept of being this teacher then they can get even more back (see because investing XP to get more XP is a great system). and if your players would exploit this then they're bad roleplayers and rule zero and so on so we don't have to worry about it&quot;.<br /> <br /> If this doesn't make sense to you, good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T05:12:07-08:00","id":748941,"title":"","content":"For the numbers generated I assumed a end cost of 25% of the original cost.<br /> <br /> So, for an non-favored ability 1-5 that would be: 3+2+4+6+8 = 23 xp committed (for teaching essence # students) and around 6 xp 'real' cost after the story. And then, probably in the next story because 53 xp in one go seems unlikely, 30 xp committed for teaching the three Charms (real cost at 25% is 7 or 8 xp).<br /> <br /> Now, xp cost and time-investment will most likely be lower, as there will probably/hopefully be someone else with some dots in lore.<br /> <br /> Sure, the idea of first teaching a couple of circle mates to teach as well starts slow, but by the time the circle hits essence 2, considering the discounts involved, well worth the investment.<br /> <br /> And by the way, I assume Legendary Scholar let's you teach them together as a class, and not one student after another. Otherwise, considering the possible number of students involved, the time committed by the teacher gets rather ridiculous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1550,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","user":"Angwe","date":". 11-02-2015, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T05:30:32-08:00","id":748976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=748941#post748941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the numbers generated I assumed a end cost of 25% of the original cost.<br /> <br /> So, for an non-favored ability 1-5 that would be: 3+2+4+6+8 = 23 xp committed (for teaching essence # students) and around 6 xp 'real' cost after the story.<br /> <br /> And by the way, I assume Legendary Scholar let's you teach them together as a class, and not one student after another. Otherwise, considering the possible number of students involved, the time committed by the teacher gets rather ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Sure, the idea of first teaching a couple of circle mates to teach as well (preferably those who already have dots in lore to get there quicker) starts slow, but in the end, considering the discounts involved, well worth the investment of training time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I was doing pre-roll committed costs as I was looking at story impacts. Not having 53 XP is a serious drawback over a 17 week period. Note that 53, as 23 for the abilities and 30 for the three charms needed to get to Flowing Mind Prana.<br /> <br /> I would prefer to handle Legendary Scholar as synchronous training - but not if it allows a mass circle exploit.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Used the word asynchronous when I meant synchronous.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9061,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9061-tyranny12","user":"tyranny12","date":". 11-02-2015, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9061-tyranny12","name":"tyranny12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T05:33:36-08:00","id":748978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=748834#post748834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I had originally read it as XP roulette. You are likely to just plain lose XP, but might gain more. This struck me as a bit silly.<br /> <br /> I had not considered that the roll could be cumulative (roll ALL the XP invested, instead of just for this story), nor did I consider that you would get more than one chance to roll the pool.<br /> <br /> I read it simply as &quot;You get to roll the XP you spent this story. Every success gets you one back. The others are lost, period.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, what, do we think, is the intent of this charm, as in what purpose does it server for players in an average game? Is it supposed to be a XP engine to feed other effects that cost XP (such as WST), or does it simply allow someone to play the &quot;support&quot; role within Exalted and transfer their XP to someone who might get more use out of it ( like the tank)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my original read as well, but I can see the plausibility of the other interpretation. I think &quot;one roll, for this Story&quot; makes the best sense with what's actually written - it's just an ugly gameplay result.<br /> <br /> The really bizarre thing, to me, is that these aren't the only training Charms in the game. Sail has one. War has one. Neither of those cost the player's XP to train purely mundane stats for NPCs - why does this? As noted upthread, it'd be easy enough to write a version that was &quot;free&quot; when used on NPCs, but still required other PCs to pay for stats gained - in fact, that's pretty much the 2e version. So this isn't a &quot;didn't think about it&quot; thing; it's a deliberate choice, and I'm baffled as to <i>why</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T06:14:48-08:00","id":749015,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the added bonus that Spirit-Stoking Elevation up in Craft lets you spend White XP in place of XP for Flowing Mind Prana. The rules are also unclear whether you get wxp back, regular xp back, or nothing at all. Yeah, it's 5wxp per 1xp, but as has been discussed to death, there is a valid interpretation of the craft rules that makes generating wxp almost trivial, so if that's your storyteller's interpretation, have fun hypercharging your circle's training with spoons!<br /> <br /> Edit: And you can do it at chargen! Woohoo!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T00:47:19-08:00","id":750884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WhirlwindMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=749015#post749015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the added bonus that Spirit-Stoking Elevation up in Craft lets you spend White XP in place of XP for Flowing Mind Prana. The rules are also unclear whether you get wxp back, regular xp back, or nothing at all. Yeah, it's 5wxp per 1xp, but as has been discussed to death, there is a valid interpretation of the craft rules that makes generating wxp almost trivial, so if that's your storyteller's interpretation, have fun hypercharging your circle's training with spoons!<br /> <br /> Edit: And you can do it at chargen! Woohoo!</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilights are no longer the mote-engine. They're the XP engine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:41:02-08:00","id":751513,"title":"","content":"<u>Socialize</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 50<br /> By Ability requirement: 0/0/4/4/42<br /> By Essence requirement: 10/12/20/5/3<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Enemy 1s are negative successes. Whatever that\u2026 thing\u2026 #25 does is. Recurring 5s and 6s.<br /> <br /> Themes: Be unreadable; hurt people who try to read you. Help your allies resist influence. Know what everyone is thinking. Develop artificial personalities, and equip them with their own Charm trees.<br /> <br /> Hoo boy. 50 Charms, 42 of them requiring Ability 5 \u2013 that\u2019s ~84%. This is a chunky tree \u2013 let\u2019s see what it does.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>You are incapable of faux pas. People with Ties to the local culture have Minor Ties to you.</li> <li>Read intentions with double-9s.</li> <li>Sense any application of Resolve or Guile in the next turn.</li> <li>Know the intensity of all Intimacies you\u2019ve Instilled yourself in the target.</li> <li>After Reading Intentions of the target while he was talking to someone else, he takes -2 Guile when you Read Intentions while he\u2019s talking to you.</li> <li>1m for +1 Guile, or 2m for +2 Guile.</li> <li>Ignore all penalties to Guile, except wound penalties and the penalty for thinking you\u2019re alone.</li> <li>Detect when an NPC Reads Intentions on someone else nearby.</li> <li>On observing a ritual, discern its significance. Bonus successes if you have to perform the rite.</li> <li>Recurring 1s any time #1 would apply. (Always?)</li> <li>Intimacies towards you will not drop as a result of any Persuade attempt you make, unless characters pay 1wp.</li> <li>Retry a Read Intentions action on the same target.</li> <li>Gain 2m when you succeed at a Socialize action, to a max of the Socialize motes you\u2019ve spent this scene.</li> <li>Read Intentions on everyone in the scene.</li> <li>Boost an ally\u2019s Guile. By glaring daggers at him. Awesome.</li> <li>Bonus dice when Reading Intentions on someone who failed to do the same to you.</li> <li>Infinite Socialize Mastery; only applies to boosting Guile.</li> <li>Perfectly conceal an Intimacy.</li> <li>If an Intimacy would be detected, you can change it to something else to fool the person looking. If you Limit Break, though, your pretend Intimacy might become real!</li> <li>Witnessing a social action, you may guess at the Intimacy behind it. If correct, you discern an Intimacy without having to roll Read Intentions.</li> <li>Preempt a target about to perform social influence; that influence is treated as if it had already been tried and failed.</li> <li>1/scene, intervene after social influence to boost the target\u2019s Resolve with a counterargument.</li> <li>Advise another to grant bonus successes for use on future social actions. Target gains an Intimacy for you.</li> <li>Anyone you defeat socially becomes obsessed with you, taking die penalties and coming to love or hate you.</li> <li>Got a pencil handy? Okay, take your 1s and 2s, and give them to someone else nearby. He rolls; find his lowest success number, and for each 2 you have, cancel one of those. Find his next success number (i.e., 8 if the first one was 7), and for each 1 you have, cancel one of those. You gain successes equal to those canceled for him; if he doesn\u2019t roll well enough, he looks ridiculous.</li> <li>If a target tries to turn a third party against you, the aspersions fall back on the target instead.</li> <li>Bonus dice to Join Battle and Awareness if you sense hostility in the room.</li> <li>When you block another\u2019s Read Intentions, you may reply with one of your own.</li> <li>Compel another to Read Intentions on you.</li> <li>If a target fails to Read Intentions on you, he believes he can use you to accomplish some aim.</li> <li>Hypnotize a character who fails to read your Guile.</li> <li>Know what it would take to persuade someone to take a particular action.</li> <li>Sense the Ties, mannerisms, and behavior of everyone involved in court, including those currently absent.</li> <li>1/scene, free full Socialize Excellency. This Charm references \u201cventing a point of Limit\u201d by achieving a legendary social goal \u2013 is that a thing mentioned anywhere else?</li> <li>Over the course of a few hours, shift into a different persona with its own Intimacies.</li> <li>Your personas have some of your Ability dots + \u00bd your total XP to spend on more.</li> <li>Your personas may learn Charms.</li> <li>Someone who loves someone who loves you also has a Minor Tie for you.</li> <li>Curse someone to be hated by a social group.</li> <li>1/scene, double-8s on a Socialize roll.</li> <li>1/story, add your Guile to your Resolve or vice-versa. Ignore effect of Intimacies on Resolve.</li> <li>One persona has 75% of your total XP, plus 2/3 of any future XP. (What?)</li> <li>Craft a custom persona to meet someone\u2019s needs.</li> <li>Access a persona\u2019s Abilities and Charms for one tick. On Limit Break, shuffle your Intimacies with the persona\u2019s Intimacies.</li> <li>On death, you regenerate into a persona as per <i>Doctor Who</i>. Like, blatantly as per Doctor Who.</li> </ol>Mastery of Small Manners (#1) is one of those rare Charms that actually inspires me to change the way I play \u2013 inventing new cultural norms for players to suss out (or supernaturally bypass). It\u2019s a fun idea!<br /> <br /> The upgraded version of Motive-Discerning Technique (#2) says it lets you speculate on the existence of Intimacies and be told if you\u2019re right. But that\u2019s already part of the base Read Intentions action, isn\u2019t it? What is this adding? (Is it that you get both \u201cmotives in this scene\u201d and \u201can Intimacy, maybe\u201d with one roll?)<br /> <br /> Umbral Eyes Focus (#4) <i>implies</i> that you don\u2019t normally get the intensity of an Intimacy when you Read Intentions. Do you not? The rules for Read Intentions just say that the ST \u201creveals\u201d an Intimacy \u2013 I would have thought that included strength.<br /> <br /> Shadow Over Day (#6) is a <i>one mote discount</i>. Edit: At Essence 2, Deep-Eyed Soul Gazing (#16) is a <i>situational</i> one-mote discount.<br /> <br /> Intent-Tracing Stare (#8) switches back to feet as a unit of intra-character distance \u2013 I\u2019m not sure any other Charms measure that way.<br /> <br /> Eh heh. \u201cIndecent Proposal Method\u201d (#11) is pretty aptly named. Again, you have to be a particular kind of character to want this, but it supports that archetype pretty well.<br /> <br /> Dauntless Assayer Method (#12) says it lets you \u201creset [your] attempt\u201d on a Read Intentions action. I had to go back to the social actions section to make sense of this \u2013 it notes that once you fail a RI action, you can\u2019t try again on the same character this scene. That\u2019s probably a good rule, but it took me a bit to get that this Charm wasn\u2019t just a reroll.<br /> <br /> Preeminent Gala Knife (#13) asks me to keep track of how many motes I have spent on Socialize Charms this scene. Um, pass.<br /> <br /> Wise-Eyed Courtier Method (#14) is great stuff. Walk into a room, and instantly know everything about everyone. Fabulous. (This charm is half the reason I\u2019m sad that the <i>Second Apocalypse</i> books don\u2019t make the recommended reading list \u2013 in the first two books, Kellhus lives and breathes Solar Socialize, and there\u2019s at least one scene that\u2019s a beautiful illustration of WECM. The books in general parse very well as the story of a newborn Solar \u2013 and given that the first trilogy is <i>The Prince of Nothing</i> and the second is <i>The Aspect-Emperor</i>, well.)<br /> <br /> Okay, there are some really great powers here in the teens through early 20s (edit: or 30s!). This is your bread-and-butter stuff to dominate the social scene \u2013 forget Presence and Performance, this is hands-down my favorite social Ability so far. I can see some players pulling really fun stunts with some of these, as well.<br /> <br /> Effective Counterargument (#22) is great, but we <i>really</i> need a concrete answer to the question, \u201cHow do die caps interact with mortals?\u201d Can this Charm be used on a mortal <i>at all</i>?<br /> <br /> There appears to be no way to counteract Endless Obsession Feint (#24), right? Edit: Or Selfsame Master Procurer (#30), or, gosh, Soul-Void Kata (#31)? (What is up with the \u201cSelfsame Master\u201d Charms?)<br /> <br /> So, Fete-Watcher Stance (#27) grants bonuses to allies as long as you warn them \u201cat least one round before any hostile action occurs.\u201d So, it grants bonuses as long as you warn people one round before Join Battle. But, um, if no one has Joined Battle, time isn\u2019t measured in rounds \u2013 there are explicitly no social rounds. So when do you have to warn them?<br /> <br /> Know the Soul\u2019s Price (#32) is still fabulous. Instant story material, highly useful power. Feels like this should interact with Bargain somehow, though.<br /> <br /> Good gosh, Venemous Rumors Technique (#39) is vicious \u2013 you can\u2019t even resist the effect yourself.<br /> <br /> Oh, Socialize. We were doing so well, and then we hit the Persona tree. I don\u2019t have any problem with the idea that the Solar socialite can flip around all his Intimacies into a whole other self \u2013 that makes a fair amount of sense. But with Draw the Curtain (#42), it\u2019s quite possible your persona has <i>more XP than you do</i> \u2013 and you can have five of these characters. Bookkeeping entirely aside, why does Social Guy get to field six Solar character sheets simultaneously, any one of which could plausibly have more XP than any other member of the party? (Also, why does Draw the Curtain grant <i>past</i> XP and <i>future</i> XP at different rates?) And the ability to buy whatever Charms you want handily sidesteps the dot restrictions \u2013 sure, maybe I need to buy Melee 5 so my Persona can have Melee 5, but that persona can have those dots and <i>also</i> all the Melee Charms it can afford, while I\u2019m sinking mine into, y\u2019know, Socialize. (My other personas can specialize similarly \u2013 heck, I can have one specialized in each caste, if I want!) That just seems\u2026 a little unbalanced, y\u2019know?<br /> <br /> Okay, so Socialize has a <i>lot</i> of stuff I really like in it, and a handful of stuff I really don\u2019t. My suspicion is that you could prune out personas and some of the other weird stuff, and be left with a really solid tree of ~35 Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Winner: Wise-Eyed Courtier Method. Runner up: Discretionary Gesture (#15). You can kick your ally under the table to raise his Guile \u2013 that\u2019s both useful and hi<i>lar</i>ious.<br /> <i>No:</i> Aspersions Cast Aside (#25). I must odd, for I cannot even.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> There\u2019s a lot of powers here that have no good way to stop them from wrecking you, other than maybe \u201cnever fail a Read Intentions roll.\u201d Several of these feel like there should be some Solar way to throw them off, without necessarily going the full-on Integrity \u201copposed Willpower rolls\u201d route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-03-2015, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T09:16:15-08:00","id":751564,"title":"","content":"I was interested to see what you'd make of this one. It has some stuff I really like - gated behind a bunch of situational improve-X-for-slightly-cheaper-than-an-Excellency Charms I find incredibly boring. When I tried pruning it down (without taking out all the Persona stuff) I ended up with 34 Charms iirc, which agrees pretty well with your estimate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8842-eris","name":"Eris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T09:38:42-08:00","id":751588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=751564#post751564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was interested to see what you'd make of this one. It has some stuff I really like - gated behind a bunch of situational improve-X-for-slightly-cheaper-than-an-Excellency Charms I find incredibly boring. When I tried pruning it down (without taking out all the Persona stuff) I ended up with 34 Charms iirc, which agrees pretty well with your estimate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I come strongly to suspect that the sweet spot for tree size is something in the 25-35 range; the trees bigger than that (Brawl, Craft, Socialize) would feel tighter if they were pruned back, and the ones smaller than that (i.e., Awareness) could stand some beefing up with powerful, interesting effects. 30 Charms is enough that you'll be most of the way to E5 before you could take all of them, even theoretically, but not so broad that you can't grab full subtrees without abandoning other concepts.<br /> <br /> And that still leaves you 750 Solar Charms, which feels like plenty to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:42:53-08:00","id":751700,"title":"","content":"The Persona tree is extremely high on my list of charms I would never want to see in an actual game I'm part of. Actually, possibly at the top of that list. It has stiff competition with the Lore-nuke, the Lore XP engine, and the Craft XP engine, but I think wins out for the sheer bookkeeping cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:13:21-08:00","id":751768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=747364#post747364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that, unlike 2e, Resistance Charms have to be declared <i>before</i> the attack roll (unless they say otherwise) \u2013 being able to mount a cheap soak-based defense is likely to be a big deal, given that it may never go off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you direct me to the page where Resistance Charm activation timing is stated? Because as far as I ever knew, during the playtest and now while reading the completed book, Reflexive Charm activation timing is pretty much &quot;whenever.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:16:31-08:00","id":751772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=751768#post751768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you direct me to the page where Resistance Charm activation timing is stated? Because as far as I ever knew, during the playtest and now while reading the completed book, Reflexive Charm activation timing is pretty much &quot;whenever.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 251, second paragraph under Using Charms and Charm Limitations. Unless otherwise specified, all charms must be activated before the attack roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:21:07-08:00","id":751782,"title":"","content":"...huh. I didn't read that line the same way <i>at all</i>.<br /> <br /> I read it as saying that you have to activate a Charm before benefiting from the effects of the Charm--that is to say, that the &quot;dice&quot; being rolled in the case of a Reflexive Resistance Charm are damage dice, so the Charm must be activated before damage is rolled. Has the interpretation you described been confirmed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:29:57-08:00","id":751849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=751782#post751782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...huh. I didn't read that line the same way <i>at all</i>.<br /> <br /> I read it as saying that you have to activate a Charm before benefiting from the effects of the Charm--that is to say, that the &quot;dice&quot; being rolled in the case of a Reflexive Resistance Charm are damage dice, so the Charm must be activated before damage is rolled. Has the interpretation you described been confirmed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I specifically asked Holden on RPGnet, and he confirmed timing. I'll try to dig up the exchange.<br /> <br /> Edit: it's actually on this forum, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715417-ex3-general-mechanics-discussion?p=718649#post718649\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-03-2015, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:45:43-08:00","id":751914,"title":"","content":"I'm willing to take your word for it, but thanks for offering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:50:27-08:00","id":751921,"title":"","content":"<u>Stealth</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 23<br /> By Ability requirement: 0/1/4/5/13<br /> By Essence requirement: 6/7/7/3<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Reroll all dice other than 10s on a Stealth action. Enemies take -1 Awareness success for each 1 or 2 rolled. Enemies take -2 successes for each 1 rolled. Stuff happens if attacker rolls six 1s and 2s and the Solar rolls at least one 10.<br /> <br /> Themes: Go unnoticed, unseen, and unsensed. Appear from the shadows, murder someone, and disappear, reappearing only to kill again. Vanish even from people\u2019s memories.<br /> <br /> A much smaller tree this time \u2013 less than half the Charms in Socialize! - though many of the individual Charms are quite large. Stealth is fourth from the end \u2013 let\u2019s get to it!<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Reroll all dice other than 10s on a Stealth action.</li> <li>Perfect immunity to sight-based detection as long as you don\u2019t move.</li> <li>Blend perfectly in the crowd. Checkpoints or magic actively opposing your cause may still detect you.</li> <li>Join Battle using Stealth; if you act first, you\u2019re also hidden.</li> <li>Ignore the -3 penalty to moving in stealth. Gain Initiative while you remain hidden.</li> <li>Hide someone else.</li> <li>Infinite Stealth Mastery. You can hide in plain sight, but moving range bands automatically reveals you.</li> <li>Roll Stealth against target\u2019s Resolve; if you succeed, you\u2019re imperceptible to him until you Join Battle or try to steal something the target cares about.</li> <li>Reroll Join Battle mid-fight and add the Initiative to your pool.</li> <li>Reset #9 after incapacitating an enemy.</li> <li>Enter stealth reflexively after incapacitating an enemy.</li> <li>Defend Other from concealment.</li> <li>Concealment counts as cover.</li> <li>Commit motes to temporarily hide anima levels.</li> <li>Hide so well that everyone forgets about you.</li> <li>Render yourself proof against detection from one sense (except sight).</li> <li>Attempts to detect you by hearing alone take -1 success for each 1 or 2 rolled.</li> <li>On using #9, everyone forgets you were there for (Essence) rounds.</li> <li>Hide in a target\u2019s shadow, controlling his body.</li> <li>Move one range band in stealth without penalty; incompatible with #7.</li> <li>Enemies <i>permanently</i> take -2 successes for each 1 rolled on Awareness rolls.</li> <li>Still got that pencil? So the attacker rolls and hits you Decisively, and then he rolls damage. Between the two, he rolls six 1s and 2s. You roll Stealth against his Awareness; if you succeed, he misses, and if you roll a 10, you enter stealth.</li> <li>Teleport back to a chosen hiding place.</li> </ol>Essence 1 frontloads us with a lot of power here \u2013 Easily-Overlooked Presence Method (#3) is Assassin\u2019s Creed in one easy package, and Invisible Statue Spirit (#2) is one of the few really uncontestable effects in the game.<br /> <br /> Guardian Fog Approach (#6) helps with a basic problem specialists often have \u2013 the rest of the party can\u2019t keep up with them. Nice!<br /> <br /> Blurred Form Style (#7) is confusingly worded. The fluff claims the Solar blends \u201cperfectly\u201d \u2013 that could be rules text in E-OPM, but here it\u2019s immediately supplanted by \u201c(Essence) auto-successes,\u201d so it can\u2019t be the actual effect. If you plan to switch range bands, though, this Charm seems to automatically reveal your location \u2013 so if you plan on moving around, this is more liability than help.<br /> <br /> Mental Invisibility Technique (#8) is just kind of hilarious \u2013 you can be dancing around making faces at the guy, and you\u2019re still invisible until you kick his cat. The caveats on this Charm are a really good idea, and I\u2019m glad they\u2019re included. So far, Stealth seems to be something of a Swiss army knife power \u2013 roll Stealth for Join Battle! Roll it for mental influence! ALWAYS BE STEALTHING.<br /> <br /> Shew, Shadow Victor\u2019s Repose and Flash-Eyed Killer\u2019s Insight (#9 and 10) are just <i>mean</i>. That\u2019s a big pile of Initiative every time you drop a guy (rolled with Stealth, if you like!). Picture your favorite \u201cWait, weren\u2019t there four of you a minute ago?\u201d scene \u2013 this is that. If there\u2019s no sufficiently Awareness-heavy ally, you\u2019re in for a world of hurt vs. a Solar assassin. \u2026 And then Hidden Snake Recoil (#11) just makes it worse, letting you vanish reflexively. Not sure this is as great if you\u2019re part of a party \u2013 you basically leave your allies to take the hits while you play Predator - but for a solo combatant, this is vicious.<br /> <br /> Can you use Sun-Swallowing Practice (#14) to walk around with three levels of anima ready to go at all times?<br /> <br /> Okay, I was onboard with the Murderghost paradigm, but Mind Shroud Meditation (#18) is too far for me. If you incapacitate someone, everyone else forgets about you, with no opportunity for resistance \u2013 that moves from being Batman to being a Benny Hill sketch.<br /> <br /> Fivefold Shadow Burial (#21) is <i>nuts</i> \u2013 that\u2019s a permanent change in opposing Awareness rolls to something like .3 sux/die average. I\u2019m a little bit uncomfortable with that \u2013 this pushes us out of \u201creally scary\u201d and into \u201ccan\u2019t realistically be opposed without a dedicated Awareness build.\u201d (Sure, recurring 1s shuts it down, but how many characters are going to have that?)<br /> <br /> On balance, I really like Stealth \u2013 the raw power here in a relative handful of Charms is <i>huge</i>. If you aren\u2019t thinking about Stealth in combat, specifically \u2013 if you just want to sneak around and Do Crimes \u2013 even the E1 stuff is probably sufficient for you. That\u2019s a little disappointing, honestly \u2013 it seems like all the high-level stuff is for being a Deathninja specifically. Still\u2026 you can definitely play Arkham City with this, and what more could one really ask? My biggest concern right now is that it\u2019s all <i>too</i> good \u2013 that Fivefold Shadow Burial especially is strong enough to shut out any opposition that isn\u2019t built specifically to counter stealth.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Easily Overlooked Presence Method; Shadow Victor's Repose.<br /> <i>No:</i> False Image Feint (#22). You track how many 1s and 2s someone has gotten on every attack roll, right? And you keep track of that information once they\u2019ve gone on to damage, just in case this is the time that comes up six? (At least six? Exactly six? How does this Charm interact with effects that say you <i>don\u2019t</i> return to base Initiative until such-and-such time, like a magical flurry?)<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Shadow Replacement Technique (#19) feels bizarrely out of step with Solar power themes. I can see an Infernal pulling \u201cI mind control you from within your shadow,\u201d but that\u2019s a pretty far cry from excellence and angelic miracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-03-2015, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T12:32:46-08:00","id":752009,"title":"","content":"The persona-charm tree is not bad in idea, but the execution is extremely bad. Our 2.5 Lunar uses a number of homebrew charms which are basically a mix of these persona-charms + Relentless Lunar Fury (and its counterparts in the other fields), but with much tighter limitations on what you can do with them and how effectively you can spread and multiply your XP / powers.<br /> <br /> But the solar persona-charms as written ... nope, never in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T13:00:42-08:00","id":752099,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Stealth tree was one I didn't immediately read that much into even though my main PC is a Night.<br /> <br /> Then I actually <i>read</i> it and was like &quot;holy shit, I need these&quot;. You think it's nasty in isolation. Add in the Ebon Shadow Style from MA and it gets <i>worse. </i>My initial thought was that Ebon Shadow was underpowered on its own, until I saw the ability it was meant to synergize with.<br /> <br /> Shadow Replacement Technique seems like it's following the Assassin's Creed vibe out into Dishonored's mindshare space, but I agree it feels odd for something that's explicitly <i>an expression of your super skill at being stealthy</i>, and not an explicit magical technique. I'd almost tie it to some voodoo doll style thing and put it in Occult instead. It's a cool idea, but I'm not sure why it's in Stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T13:31:55-08:00","id":752160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=751914#post751914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm willing to take your word for it, but thanks for offering.</div> </div> </div> </div>That being said, they have put a lot of conditional activations in charms.<br /> <br /> For example, it differentiates Reed in the Wind (declare before attack) and Serpentine Evasion (conditional after-attack boost).<br /> <br /> In Resistance, only two soak charms are so specified - Durability of Oak Meditation and Adamant Skin Technique. The rest of the reflexives have activation order riders, or are out of the attack flow, such as the Poison, Illness, Everything branch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9061-tyranny12","name":"tyranny12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T14:21:24-08:00","id":752238,"title":"","content":"<u>Survival</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 24<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/1/4/4/14<br /> By Essence requirement: 3/11/10/0/0<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Recurring 5s and 6s; enemy 1s count as your 10s. Recurring successes. Recurring 1s.<br /> <br /> Themes: Resist the elements. Raise a cute, cuddly puppy and FEED HIM ON THE PAIN OF YOUR ENEMIES.<br /> <br /> Huh. This is one of the very few trees with almost nothing in the E1 range. It also has nothing over E3, though \u2013 all the Charms are crammed into that awkward E3 range. So that\u2019s a little tough for a starting character, but any Supernal benefit dissipates a relatively short distance in.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Gather enough food for one or more people in any environment.</li> <li>Remove penalties and minor troubles for rough environment. Does not resist environmental damage.</li> <li>Wild animals are friendly, or at least won\u2019t attack.</li> <li>Lead a small group safely through the wilderness at 20 miles/day. (How fast is normal?)</li> <li>When tracking another, you have recurring 5s and 6s and his 1s count as 10s for you.</li> <li>Your familiar is unshakably loyal and produces motes and willpower. You can see through its senses.</li> <li>Train a new familiar, or train an existing familiar to use its latent, magical, or blatantly supernatural powers.</li> <li>Call your familiar to attack alongside you.</li> <li>Recurring 1s on a training roll. Grant a familiar bonus stats with an XP investment.</li> <li>Permanent soak/hardness boost for your familiar.</li> <li>Extra health levels for your familiar.</li> <li>Command your familiar, granting it bonus dice on its attacks.</li> <li>Your familiar can see dematerialized spirits.</li> <li>Your familiar gets to use your Join Battle roll, with bonus successes. Bonus dice granted to this action by #12 gain recurring successes.</li> <li>Ignore drowning and toxic gas; reduce all environmental damage by your Resistance.</li> <li>Bonuses to your attempts to leave no tracks with a small group. Mundane tracking automatically fails.</li> <li>Perfectly conceal yourself or your stash against mundane senses.</li> <li>1/scene, your Familiar\u2019s Decisive attacks roll over extra successes into damage.</li> <li>Use your Stealth Charms while possessing your familiar.</li> <li>Your familiar grows, gains stat boosts, and develops beneficial mutations. (Wings!)</li> <li>Your familiar grapples spirits, making them vulnerable to you. Cheaper in conjunction with #12.</li> <li>Your familiar permanently generates 1i/turn, except when #24 is active.</li> <li>When you land a Withering attack, your familiar gains half as much Initiative as you do.</li> <li>Your familiar becomes huge and intimidating. It can attempt huge feats of strength and gains major bonuses to movement actions. Its attacks <i>will</i> hit. Its Initiative <i>does not reset</i>. It <i>CANNOT DIE, </i>or even be wounded by Decisive attacks. If it Crashes, the Charm ends.</li> </ol><br /> Okay, I have no idea what Food-Gathering Exercise (#1) is saying. \u201cIn addition, for every hour the Solar continues to use this Charm, the Solar works toward a climactic encounter with the rawest expression of survivalist skill possible\u2026 This encounter will happen regardless of Storyteller decree, but is still contingent on a difficulty 6 roll in the worst case scenario.\u201d I\u2019m having trouble parsing that \u2013 is it just saying, \u201cIf you use this Charm for a day, you\u2019re guaranteed to also find a larger food source at some point, unless there\u2019s <i>literally nothing</i>?\u201d<br /> <br /> Those first three up there \u2013 that\u2019s what you can get out of Survival at E1. It\u2019s not nothing, but it is a little disappointing; at E1, Stealth lets me be Altair!<br /> <br /> Beast-Mastering Behavior (#7) includes rules for training a familiar under normal circumstances, followed by how the Charm modifies those. Wouldn\u2019t these rules be better included\u2026 well, anywhere other than tucked into one Charm? On the plus side, this Charm will absolutely let you turn a mundane squirrel into Pikachu.<br /> <br /> Why do several of these Charms have dedicated sidebars with one sentence of information? Shouldn\u2019t this information just go in the Charm? That seems both more compact and more useful.<br /> <br /> Sidebar notes that, should your familiar die, you get all the XP invested in it back. That\u2019s a nice gesture, and it makes a lot of these Charms feel like less of a gamble.<br /> <br /> Ambush Predator Style (#14) is going to grant some <i>big</i> Join Battle rolls \u2013 at E5, with a maxed-out pool and support from Familiar-Honing Instruction (#12), you\u2019re looking at something like 14.5 successes for 7m. That\u2019s not bad \u2013 and it\u2019s even better if you use those Ride Charms to share Initiative. (Ride + Survival in general seems like it should be a pretty nice combination \u2013 although, how does that work? Ride assumes your mount has no Initiative or independent actions without a Charm, but this seems to assume your familiar <i>does</i> have Initiative and its own actions. So what happens when you ride your familiar?)<br /> <br /> Element-Resisting Prana (#15) is the first Charm in about the last eleven to <i>not</i> be about enhancing your familiar. Which, the familiar tree is pretty cool so far, but it\u2019s nice to see some more breadth \u2013 though we have to get to E3 to see it! Note that, at Resistance 5, you can ignore any damage below the level of lava \u2013 but a volcano <i>will</i> still kill you over time.<br /> <br /> I really want to see some guy\u2019s dog grapple a dematerialized Octavian to the ground with Phantom-Rending Fangs (#21). Like\u2026 that\u2019s just a fabulous mental image. \u201cSic \u2018em, Rex.\u201d<br /> <br /> The thing I\u2019m curious on, with all this familiar-enhancement, is how well your familiar can actually <i>hit</i> things \u2013 in an Excellency-heavy world, it\u2019s awfully easy to throw down a few motes and ignore that critter you just spent ten Charms on. Familiar-Honing Instruction does a lot to help with this once it\u2019s Reflexive, I think, but prior to that, it looks like rough going.<br /> <br /> \u2026And Deadly Predator Method (#24) resolves <i>that</i> concern. That\u2019s a hefty mote commitment to get things going, but while they go\u2026 good heavens. A Solar\u2019s pet <i>will end you</i>.<br /> <br /> \u2026 so what happens when you run DPM, and your familiar is Defending Other on you? Are you both just functionally immune to Decisives until it Crashes?<br /> <br /> I love the familiar tree, even if it doesn\u2019t quite cash in until the very end. Survival as a whole feels like it could use some more toys \u2013 everything <i>not</i> familiar-buffing feels almost like an afterthought \u2013 but those Charms it does have tend to be pretty potent and useful. This is a solid and extremely powerful tree.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Deadly Predator Method. Good sweet heavens.<br /> <i>No:</i> Probably Hardship-Surviving Mendicant Spirit (#2). \u201cYou are immune to bugbites and nettles\u201d just doesn\u2019t stack up to some of the other things in this list.<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> The undefined interactions of riding your familiar. This is, like, the first thing people are going to want to do, right? So how <i>does</i> that work? Does the familiar render a bunch of Ride Charms superfluous, or does it become drastically less competent when you jump on its back?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T15:03:43-08:00","id":752270,"title":"","content":"Have you been sending all this stuff you consider unclear to RichT? The process is mostly for typo finding, but I think Vance suggested this sort of uncertainties should also be sent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T15:43:16-08:00","id":752293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752270#post752270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you been sending all this stuff you consider unclear to RichT? The process is mostly for typo finding, but I think Vance suggested this sort of uncertainties should also be sent</div> </div> </div> </div>The things that seem unambiguously wrong, yes. The things where I'm just unclear, no - I could pile all these up once I'm done, but right now, just compiling them is work enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T15:44:21-08:00","id":752294,"title":"","content":"The way I've read riding your familiar: normally, your mount does not roll initiative, even if it is a familiar. You two, together, have one initiative attack, and withering attacks against either of you go against it and your mounts attacks use your actions. You can attack the mount decisively and kill it out from under the rider, but you're encouraged to use the dehorse gambit instead. If you check the respective rolling into battle charms in Ride and Survival, Seasoned Beast-Rider's approach allows you to roll your mount in and give it its own Initiative track and actions, while Ambush Predator Style enhances that roll, so no incompatibilities there.<br /> <br /> So yes, your familiar is less competent if you leap onto it. It's part of the penalty for riding <i>anything </i>being a very significant advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T15:44:37-08:00","id":752296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752293#post752293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The things that seem unambiguously wrong, yes. The things where I'm just unclear, no - I could pile all these up once I'm done, but right now, just compiling them is work enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's unclear, it's worth sending in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:25:22-08:00","id":752366,"title":"","content":"<u>Thrown</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 24<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/1/3/5/15<br /> By Essence requirement: 7/9/8/1/0<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Reroll one nonsuccess for each 10. Reroll 6s equal to the 7s you rolled. Gain Initiative equal to the 9s and 10s on your last roll.<br /> <br /> Themes: Strike a large number of targets. Attack without breaking stealth. Render your target unable to defend against you. Make a lightning-fast alpha strike.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Calculate Accuracy on a Withering attack as if you were at Close range. At Close range, subtract 1 from target\u2019s Defense.</li> <li>Cheap Excellency on your first attack if you roll the highest Join Battle. At E3, doesn\u2019t reset your Initiative.</li> <li>Take your first turn earlier, even though you don\u2019t gain extra Initiative. Works cross-Ability.</li> <li>If your Decisive deals 3HL, the target takes -3 to all die pools for the scene.</li> <li>Negate the target\u2019s cover.</li> <li>Make Thrown attacks from Long range.</li> <li>1/scene, make an undodgeable attack with a full Excellency that also strikes all targets nearby.</li> <li>Reroll one nonsuccess for each 10 on a Join Battle. If you roll highest, attack (Dexterity) opponents.</li> <li>Target struck by a Decisive attack can make no sound for several rounds.</li> <li>A thrown attack appears to come from a different direction. At E3, make thrown attacks from stealth without revealing yourself.</li> <li>\u201cReroll 6s equal to your 7s\u201d on a Distract or Disarm gambit, + bonus successes.</li> <li>1/scene, keep your Initiative after disarming the target.</li> <li>Knock a dropped weapon one range band.</li> <li>Bonus Initiative when you Aim to make a Decisive from cover or stealth.</li> <li>Your Withering attack strikes all enemies within short range of the target.</li> <li>When you use #8 to strike a target Decisively, you may retain extra Initiative equal to the 9s and 10s rolled.</li> <li>When you fool an opponent with #10, you can make a Decisive ambush attack</li> <li>Automatically hit with a Distract attack.</li> <li>Roll a Decisive attack or Disarm gambit twice, taking the better result.</li> <li>When you hit with #18, you also Disarm the target.</li> <li>When someone tries to recover a weapon you\u2019ve Disarmed from him, you get a free <i>unblockable, undodgeable</i> Withering attack on him.</li> <li>Double damage on an ambush attack.</li> <li>Throw an accurate, extra-damaging Kamehameha.</li> <li>Throw an attack that strikes multiple enemies with Withering blows before reaching a final enemy with a Decisive.</li> </ol><br /> I\u2019m not hugely impressed by Steel Storm Descending (#2), but once it auto-upgrades, a free Decisive is pretty nice. Given that you won Join Battle, you\u2019re probably throwing quite a bit of damage when you fire that Decisive off.<br /> <br /> Joint-Wounding Attack (#4) doesn\u2019t seem that great at low levels, when 3HL is a big chunk of your totals \u2013 but as the health levels for both you and your enemies rise, this is a way to put an opponent in a bad way while doing a pittance of damage.<br /> <br /> We get a sidebar on \u201celected targets\u201d in battle groups \u2013 which, again, feels like it would go better back in the core rules for battle groups.<br /> <br /> Cascade of Cutting Terror (#7) is kind of a big deal \u2013 just being a reflexive attack would be big, but the free Excellency and the undodgeability make it a pretty great once-per-fight pop. Against, say, an enemy archer, this is going to be devastating.<br /> <br /> Why is Swarm-Culling Instinct\u2019s (#8) \u201creroll one nonsuccess for each 10\u201d not just recurring 10s? In almost all rolls, there\u2019s no statistical difference. The power itself is probably the cheapest multiattack Charm in the set \u2013 <i>if</i> it lets you roll high enough. Thrown in general looks like it has a great opening game, and a much weaker followup.<br /> <br /> Shower of Deadly Blades (#15) is again a very strong one-use move. Oddly, it seems to assume you\u2019re using the \u201cammo save\u201d rules \u2013 but even those rules presented \u201ctrack ammo\u201d as an alternate solution. Why assume that this one is in use? More generally, Thrown is the <i>only</i> place in the rules where ammo consumption seems to be a concern. Thrown is also odd in that it seems to have no option to <i>make</i> weapons \u2013 2e had \u201cSpirit Weapons,\u201d but that\u2019s conspicuously absent here.<br /> <br /> Crimson Razor Wind (#17) drops a bombshell with almost no fanfare: one distracting roll, and you get a free ambush attack \u2013 that is, a strike at Defense 0. That\u2019s a big deal for a reusable Decisive attack. Edit: Falling Icicle Strike (#22) makes it an even bigger deal \u2013 your basically-guaranteed-to-hit attack now doubles its damage as well. That\u2019s a pretty solid one-hit-kill combo; very little short of a perfect defense is going to get you out of it.<br /> <br /> Shadow Wind Slash (#19) is similarly a big deal \u2013 2m for a Decisive attack with a reroll. That\u2019s effectively a big boost to average accuracy. Why is the Disarming version of this effect so expensive? \u201cReroll your Disarm\u201d is more expensive than making both a normal attack <i>and</i> a Disarm. (Also, this Charm seems to assume that gambits are not Decisives, which, again, is not unambiguous.)<br /> <br /> Fiery Solar Chakram (#23) describes doing extra damage for creatures of darkness, but oddly avoids the actual term.<br /> <br /> In general, Thrown looks like lots of big single-use attacks, as noted above. There\u2019s not a lot to add to your accuracy, but if you want to attack from stealth or win the fight before anyone else even knows it\u2019s started, this is your go-to. The potential for big \u2013 and <i>lethal</i> \u2013 ambushes just makes it nastier. If you can live through that opening volley, though, there\u2019s not a lot of meat-and-potatoes here; a Thrown combatant might want to either have a backup attack or a plan to run away quick.<br /> <br /> Overall, strong tree with no obvious dead Charms. Curious to see how the balance does in play.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Lots of good choices, but probably Cascade of Cutting Terror.<br /> <i>No:</i> Some of the bizarre die options \u2013 \u201cReroll 6s equal to 7s?\u201d<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird: </i>The absence of weapon-summoning and weapon creation stands out particularly \u2013 I assume this was a balance concern? Also, what <i>are</i> the rules on using Thrown weapons \u2013 do you have to ready another one when the old one gets tossed away?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:33:12-08:00","id":752372,"title":"","content":"How do you think Thrown compares to Archery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:38:24-08:00","id":752377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752366#post752366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what <i>are</i> the rules on using Thrown weapons \u2013 do you have to ready another one when the old one gets tossed away?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the examples in the draw/ready weapon action is preparing a brace of knives for throwing, which indicates that you don't need to ready each individual thrown weapon. You'd need a ready weapon to switch from knives to shurikens, but as long as you keep throwing knives it's not an action to draw another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:52:58-08:00","id":752414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752372#post752372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you think Thrown compares to Archery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Archery feels more sustainable, and definitely <i>safer</i> - you can be an archer from range just fine. Archery has a lot of big reusable attacks, which Thrown is low on, and it can put a lot of sustained pressure on via magical flurries. It's also easier to guarantee you're never unarmed, if you're an archer - either by a summoned bow or by one you're keeping in Elsewhere - while Thrown seems almost designed to run out of ammo fast.<br /> <br /> Thrown feels light on sustained pressure. But Thrown is faster, and alpha-strikes <i>hard</i>; it can cripple you for the whole fight, or hit you at Defense 0 for double damage, or fire attacks without ever breaking stealth. I would probably want Archery for a sustained combat, but if I need guerrilla warfare, I'm going to go Thrown. I suspect a Thrown-based enemy could be a real pain in the neck to hunt down and pulverize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:56:02-08:00","id":752421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752377#post752377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the examples in the draw/ready weapon action is preparing a brace of knives for throwing, which indicates that you don't need to ready each individual thrown weapon. You'd need a ready weapon to switch from knives to shurikens, but as long as you keep throwing knives it's not an action to draw another.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* But is this a brace as in a pair? Two attacks to the reload is still a lot of wasted actions over the course of the fight. Or is this more figurative - a brace as in &quot;as many as you're going to use?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:58:57-08:00","id":752425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752421#post752421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*nods* But is this a brace as in a pair? Two attacks to the reload is still a lot of wasted actions over the course of the fight. Or is this more figurative - a brace as in &quot;as many as you're going to use?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My read of it was &quot;unless you're a simulationist, you only need to ready a different weapon if you're changing types, and ammunition is not a concern&quot;<br /> <br /> For the realists, there's even an Artifact belt that basically has shuriken that disappear and teleport back to the belt once they've hit their target or missed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T17:05:59-08:00","id":752456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752421#post752421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*nods* But is this a brace as in a pair? Two attacks to the reload is still a lot of wasted actions over the course of the fight. Or is this more figurative - a brace as in &quot;as many as you're going to use?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to say. I would go with the more charitable interpretation that doesn't screw over thrown users, but it's something that could do with a clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T17:17:13-08:00","id":752486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752366#post752366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More generally, Thrown is the <i>only</i> place in the rules where ammo consumption seems to be a concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, the existence of Phantom Arrow Technique implies that ammo consumption is a concern for archers too, but for some strange reason none of the archery flurries has this weird drawback from Shower of Deadly Blades.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T17:34:08-08:00","id":752542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752294#post752294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I've read riding your familiar: normally, your mount does not roll initiative, even if it is a familiar. You two, together, have one initiative attack, and withering attacks against either of you go against it and your mounts attacks use your actions. You can attack the mount decisively and kill it out from under the rider, but you're encouraged to use the dehorse gambit instead. If you check the respective rolling into battle charms in Ride and Survival, Seasoned Beast-Rider's approach allows you to roll your mount in and give it its own Initiative track and actions, while Ambush Predator Style enhances that roll, so no incompatibilities there.<br /> <br /> So yes, your familiar is less competent if you leap onto it. It's part of the penalty for riding <i>anything </i>being a very significant advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>From Seasoned Beast-Rider:<br /> <br /> &quot;With this Charm, activated when the player rolls<br /> Join Battle, the Exalt\u2019s mount gains an Initiative track<br /> with a starting value equal to her own, and may make<br /> attacks on its own turn.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which means Ambush Predator Style can't be used (since your mount never rolls join battle) and Force Building Predator Style doesn't work since it requires your familiar to have been rolled into battle with Ambush Predator Style.<br /> <br /> OTOH it means you get double the payoff from using an awareness excellency for join battle since its generating your own and your familiars initiative.<br /> <br /> Beast Rider tree and survival have great synergy in general, but some of the better ride charms require essence 2-3.<br /> <br /> Once you get there though Wrathful Mount Invigoration (1 initiative per turn plus [your Essence] initiative for every successful movement action) + Crimson Talon Vigor (half the initiative from your withering attacks) lets your mount-familiar generate pretty decent amounts of initiative without even making its own withering attacks, which means with Deadly Predator Method it can just keep decisive attacking for ever larger amounts of damage unless people manage to do withering damage to it through its 30+ soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 11-03-2015, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T18:04:19-08:00","id":752641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752425#post752425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My read of it was &quot;unless you're a simulationist, you only need to ready a different weapon if you're changing types, and ammunition is not a concern&quot;<br /> <br /> For the realists, there's even an Artifact belt that basically has shuriken that disappear and teleport back to the belt once they've hit their target or missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's an unreasonable read, but simulationism entirely aside, I'd like to know cleanly that I can keep hurling thrown weapons as long as I like, rather than leave it vaguely implicit. I'd prefer the ruling you give as well, but Thrown is pretty ammo-focused!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T18:28:14-08:00","id":752696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752641#post752641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's an unreasonable read, but simulationism entirely aside, I'd like to know cleanly that I can keep hurling thrown weapons as long as I like, rather than leave it vaguely implicit. I'd prefer the ruling you give as well, but Thrown is pretty ammo-focused!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I admit part of the read is just me going &quot;do I want to keep track of how many knives I've thrown out? Hell no.&quot; If part of the balance of Thrown is reliant on the fact you have to actually keep these things in hand, then it's important for it to be concrete. Otherwise, I'd almost just assume most Thrown Charms had Glorious Solar Throwing Knives integrated somehow. It'd fit the urge on keeping the combat fast paced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T18:36:58-08:00","id":752700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752414#post752414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archery feels more sustainable, and definitely <i>safer</i> - you can be an archer from range just fine. Archery has a lot of big reusable attacks, which Thrown is low on, and it can put a lot of sustained pressure on via magical flurries. It's also easier to guarantee you're never unarmed, if you're an archer - either by a summoned bow or by one you're keeping in Elsewhere - while Thrown seems almost designed to run out of ammo fast.<br /> <br /> Thrown feels light on sustained pressure. But Thrown is faster, and alpha-strikes <i>hard</i>; it can cripple you for the whole fight, or hit you at Defense 0 for double damage, or fire attacks without ever breaking stealth. I would probably want Archery for a sustained combat, but if I need guerrilla warfare, I'm going to go Thrown. I suspect a Thrown-based enemy could be a real pain in the neck to hunt down and pulverize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice analysis. Trying to decide on a secondary ranged combat ability for a Supernal MA Dawn who is a shinmaic monk and I reallllllllly can't choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T18:42:11-08:00","id":752732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752700#post752700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice analysis. Trying to decide on a secondary ranged combat ability for a Supernal MA Dawn who is a shinmaic monk and I reallllllllly can't choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>For secondary combat, I might go Thrown - open with that, switch to fisticuffs where possible, and occasionally liven it up with another unexpected throw. But yeah, it's a hard call!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T18:46:30-08:00","id":752736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752700#post752700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice analysis. Trying to decide on a secondary ranged combat ability for a Supernal MA Dawn who is a shinmaic monk and I reallllllllly can't choose.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, offhand, I'd think Archery, just for the associations with zen archery in real life as part of that sort of thing, but it depends on your mechanics-vs-story balance ratio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T19:21:32-08:00","id":752822,"title":"","content":"<u>War</u><br /> <br /> Number of Charms: 17<br /> By Ability requirement: 1/3/3/5/5<br /> By Essence requirement: 6/6/5/0/0<br /> Nonstandard dice tricks: Recurring 6s.<br /> <br /> Themes: Train your troops to the peak of humanity. Outmaneuver your enemy. Protect your army. Produce lots of successes on a War roll.<br /> <br /> One final tree! And if it\u2019s not the smallest yet, it\u2019s darn close. Let\u2019s take a look at War.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Your army has +1 Size and ignores the penalty for poor drill troops.</li> <li>Train a crew to reroll nonsuccesses on an artillery weapon.</li> <li>Your troops are immune to mundane demoralization (as per the maneuver), as well as penalties for weather, food, etc.</li> <li>Make a reflexive rally action with bonus successes.</li> <li>When rolling for a stratagem, ignore penalties for unfamiliarity with the enemy general or army.</li> <li>Double-9s or double-8s on an Order.</li> <li>Grant your unit improved stats and drill; spend XP to grant them bonuses against select enemies or perfect morale.</li> <li>Recover points of Magnitude equal to the 1s and 2s on an enemy rally for numbers roll.</li> <li>Finish a strategic maneuver with one less success.</li> <li>Excellency discount on a Strategic Maneuver; with sufficient successes, pull several maneuvers at once.</li> <li>Enact an uncounterable Strategic Maneuver with double-7s.</li> <li>When your army empties the Magnitude of another army, you can roll Join Battle.</li> <li>1/scene, make an automatically successful rally action.</li> <li>Make a reflexive rally for numbers action, recruiting animals or nature itself to your side.</li> <li>Permanently, recurring 6s on a War roll.</li> <li>When activating #12, you can perform a maneuver with successes no higher than half the Initiative gained.</li> <li>Choose two maneuvers; if the enemy chooses one of them, you automatically win the maneuver roll and can enact a stratagem of equal or fewer successes.</li> </ol><br /> The image of the lady in white burning through a pile of enemies with, presumably, the final Thrown Charm is pretty sweet.<br /> <br /> Several of these War Charms \u2013 League of Iron Preparation (#3), Holistic Battle Understanding (#5) \u2013 are really stressing that Ex3 <i>really expects</i> you to regularly apply penalties to rolls.<br /> <br /> Tiger-Warrior Training (#7) has gotten a <i>major</i> buff from 2e \u2013 a week and a month will get your soldiers up to about maximum human capacity, rather than having to track them dot by dot. I like it! (I also wish Lore\u2019s training effects were a little more like this.)<br /> <br /> General of the All-Seeing Sun (#10) starts out pretty weak, but I do like the ability to pop several maneuvers \u2013 that\u2019s potentially a big effect. Does the discount from Redoubt-Raising Gesture (#9) apply to each of the several?<br /> <br /> Immortal Warlord\u2019s Tactic (#11) has an Initiative cost. Do you have Initiative at the step that you\u2019re rolling Strategic Maneuvers, though? The Ambush Maneuver implies that you aren\u2019t rolling Join Battle until <i>afterwards</i> \u2013 so where is this Initiative coming from? Hm - and Transcendent Warlord\u2019s Genius (#16) implies you can pull maneuvers mid-fight. So how <i>does</i> this work?<br /> <br /> On balance, most of the War Charms look solid. Even the dice-trick-y ones are potent dice tricks \u2013 recurring 6s isn\u2019t much on its own, but as a permanent upgrade it\u2019s pretty nice. But it feels like the whole thing runs out of steam a little too early, compared to all the other Abilities \u2013 I\u2019d like to see a little more at the upper end.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes:</i> Tiger Warrior Training Technique!<br /> <i>No:</i> Nothing here <i>quite</i> gives me that Solar Admiral Thrawn feel. This is a good start, but gimme moar!<br /> <i>Just Plain Weird:</i> Immortal Commander\u2019s Presence (#2) is very artillery-centric. Does the book present artillery rules ore weapons at some later point? As of where I am, I\u2019d be purely in houserules territory for how useful this is.<br /> <br /> And that is, at long last, Charms. Up next\u2026 *sigh*\u2026 \u201cMartial Arts and Sorcery.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2026 more Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T19:44:05-08:00","id":752852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752822#post752822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is, at long last, Charms. Up next\u2026 *sigh*\u2026 \u201cMartial Arts and Sorcery.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, for what it's worth? The Martial Arts and Sorcery Systems are <i>much</i> more streamlined and more clearly-written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:13:09-08:00","id":752868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752852#post752852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, for what it's worth? The Martial Arts and Sorcery Systems are <i>much</i> more streamlined and more clearly-written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're actually pretty fun to read and think of possible characters for them. Especially Sorcerous Workings, which are pretty much the crown jewel of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T23:40:35-08:00","id":753121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752868#post752868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, they're actually pretty fun to read and think of possible characters for them. <b>Especially Sorcerous Workings, which are pretty much the crown jewel of the book.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Because a simple like wouldn't be enough, QFT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T23:47:53-08:00","id":753125,"title":"","content":"If you're anything like me, though, you're gonna be so sad when you see all the initiations, and realize you have no idea how to make and balance your own.<br /> <br /> ((I like everything else about sorcery, but the simple reality that I cannot even start trying to replicate the Five Trials as an alternative to the written initiations makes me very sad. Hopefully the Paths of Brigid will give a lot more detail on writing new ones.))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T03:37:37-08:00","id":753617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=752542#post752542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From Seasoned Beast-Rider:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;With this Charm, activated when the player rolls<br /> Join Battle, the Exalt\u2019s mount gains an Initiative track<br /> with a starting value equal to her own, and may make<br /> attacks on its own turn.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Which means Ambush Predator Style can't be used (since your mount never rolls join battle) and Force Building Predator Style doesn't work since it requires your familiar to have been rolled into battle with Ambush Predator Style.<br /> <br /> OTOH it means you get double the payoff from using an awareness excellency for join battle since its generating your own and your familiars initiative.<br /> <br /> Beast Rider tree and survival have great synergy in general, but some of the better ride charms require essence 2-3.<br /> <br /> Once you get there though Wrathful Mount Invigoration (1 initiative per turn plus [your Essence] initiative for every successful movement action) + Crimson Talon Vigor (half the initiative from your withering attacks) lets your mount-familiar generate pretty decent amounts of initiative without even making its own withering attacks, which means with Deadly Predator Method it can just keep decisive attacking for ever larger amounts of damage unless people manage to do withering damage to it through its 30+ soak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Derp. I even read these charms again before posting.<br /> <br /> I hate not being able to read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T03:55:32-08:00","id":753626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=753125#post753125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're anything like me, though, you're gonna be so sad when you see all the initiations, and realize you have no idea how to make and balance your own.<br /> <br /> ((I like everything else about sorcery, but the simple reality that I cannot even start trying to replicate the Five Trials as an alternative to the written initiations makes me very sad. Hopefully the Paths of Brigid will give a lot more detail on writing new ones.))</div> </div> </div> </div>Just give some ability that gives access to about 1-5 sorcerous motes per scene, done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T06:19:47-08:00","id":753835,"title":"","content":"Okay: \u201cChapter Seven: Martial Arts and Sorcery.\u201d<br /> <br /> We get an opening fiction with Shen, and gosh is it verbose. The first half-page or so boils down to \u201cShen sells drugs as a cover for his actual work\u201d; the latter half is him actually doing things (summoning, infecting, and promptly banishing a demon, in this case). The art of the same on the following page isn\u2019t really a standout in either direction \u2013 it does its job, and that\u2019s that.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re told that martial arts \u201care not compatible with\u201d Charms of other Abilities \u2013 but what does this mean, precisely? I get that I can\u2019t activate both Brawl and Martial Arts Charms on the same instant, but what about long-duration Charms? What about permanent ones? I assume using a martial art for offense and something else for defense (or vice-versa) is kosher, but all of this could stand a little more explicit delineation.<br /> <br /> Styles may have \u201clost\u201d Charms known only to ancient masters, or newly uncovered through rare and remarkable circumstances. That\u2019s kind of a nice touch.<br /> <br /> Form Charms are still a thing, but switching Forms only requires you to pay the difference between them. That\u2019s a nice touch.<br /> <br /> Okay, so Solars, Dragon-Blooded, and everybody else all use the same Charms now. <i>But</i>, if you\u2019re a Solar-tier Exalt, you get the \u201cMastery\u201d keyword for bonus effect; if you\u2019re a Dragon-Blooded, you get the \u201cTerrestrial\u201d keyword for reduced effect (unless you\u2019re an Immaculate monk!). That\u2019s a nice solution to the old problem of \u201cThere are, like, two guys who practice Snake Style, tops,\u201d and it also lets a Solar train in a Dragon-Blooded dojo and then do the whole \u201cNow I\u2019ve surpassed my master\u201d thing. (One presumes Sidereals get access to Mastery, as well?)<br /> <br /> The whole \u201cbuy a whole Ability from scratch\u201d thing rankles a little, with Martial Arts. They are, of course, combat stuff you can buy with Solar XP \u2013 but at 19 XP for the Ability, plus, what, 80+ XP for the actual tree? That\u2019s a minimum of 25 sessions to buy one full tree \u2013 by that time, you\u2019ll be Essence 3, and you haven\u2019t bought any sorcery/Evocations/<i>any other stats</i>. The latter has felt most critical in my games so far; no one\u2019s been interested in much in the way of XP dumps, but raising stats has gotten a lot of attention.<br /> <br /> <u>Snake Style</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 3<br /> Armor: Light or none.<br /> Weapons: Unarmed, seven-section staves, hook swords.<br /> Shtick: Have a higher Initiative than your opponent, and then cripple your opponent with penalties and poison. Backstop your offense with bonuses to soak and limited damage-negation.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>+1 Evasion; can be activated after attack if you have higher Initiative.</li> <li>Bonus damage against slower enemies. Extra bonus damage if they\u2019re crashed.</li> <li>Form: attacks on you take -1 die, or -3 if your Initiative is higher. Bonus soak.</li> <li>Ignore armor soak or some hardness.</li> <li>Perform gambits to blind or paralyze your enemy.</li> <li>Upgrade #3 to give extra soak and Withering damage (and Decisive damage, with Mastery).</li> <li>Drag an enemy from Medium to Close range.</li> <li>Reflexively Clash with an enemy.</li> <li>Use your Initiative to cancel damage from a Decisive attack.</li> <li>Poison your enemy with Aggravated damage-dealing venom.</li> </ol>Serpentine Evasion (#1) is a less good Drifting Leaf Elusion, even with the Mastery discount. And the two don\u2019t stack, which is uninspiring.<br /> <br /> Snake Form (#3), on the other hand, is kind of a big deal. -3 dice to all attack rolls is a major shift in the probabilities. Even better, these rules adopt something introduced at the very tail (har) of the Monkeys era: a way to reflexively shift into a Form, if you don\u2019t have a turn to spend activating a Simple Charm. Snake Form has a nice, easy shift condition that\u2019s almost certainly going to come up if you push for it \u2013 nice! If you\u2019re in light armor, it wouldn\u2019t be unpleasant to sit in Snake even if you don\u2019t use the rest of the style \u2013 pretty wasteful of XP, sure, but\u2026<br /> <br /> Ignoring armor on a Withering Strike, as Armor-Penetrating Fang Strike (#4) does, is nice \u2013 but shew, also expensive. I don\u2019t have a good sense of how powerful this is for the cost.<br /> <br /> Crippling Pressure Point Strike (#5), by contrast, is cheap and potent. You could paralyze both of your opponent\u2019s arms with a couple of hits \u2013 but then, you could also deal him 8L instead\u2026 Shouldn\u2019t this have the Crippling keyword, like Joint-Wounding Attack?<br /> <br /> \u2026 Wait, hang on. Joint-Wounding Attack definitely has the Crippling keyword. You know who <i>doesn\u2019t</i> have the Crippling keyword? <i>The Keyword list</i>.<br /> <br /> Uncoiling Serpent Prana (#7) is just cool. This is the first \u201cGet over here!\u201d power I\u2019ve seen, and it\u2019s a great counter to kiting builds without dumping scads of XP in Athletics. Take <i>that</i>, horse archers.<br /> <br /> Snake Strikes the Heel (#8) implies gambits <i>are</i> Decisive attacks, because your Decisive clash has to be a gambit, contrary to earlier Charms that implied they <i>weren\u2019t</i>. So which is it? The Terrestrial note implies this Charm does not normally consume your attack for the turn; does that need to be explicitly stated?<br /> <br /> Heck yeah, Tiger Style illustration. That is a picture of a dude whose expression fully commits to the fact that he is about to be murdered by a magical kung fu lady (who is also sort of a tiger). Looking forward to that one.<br /> <br /> This is a tight, satisfying tree \u2013 as was foretold! It\u2019s got most of your bases covered: Clashes, nasty offense, range, soak, late-step Defense buffs, Decisive attack negation, and so on. There\u2019s no Onslaught negation, but that\u2019s the only major hole that stands out to me. In general, the powers here are less good than dedicated Solar Charms \u2013 Countless Coils Evasion (#9), say, is similar to but less good than Heavenly Guardian Defense. On the other hand, they\u2019re all in one short tree\u2026<br /> <br /> This is a tree that really, really wants you to be faster than your enemy; if you can\u2019t regularly sustain that, you\u2019re probably in for a bad time. A lot of its powers are more effective if the enemy is Crashed, though, so if you <i>can</i> get that upper hand, you\u2019re going to be piling on a lot of hurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-04-2015, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T06:34:55-08:00","id":753854,"title":"","content":"I can forgive the martial arts sub-abilities honestly. Grabbing the martial artist merit effectively gives you a sub-exaltation that you can spend solar xp on the charms for.<br /> <br /> If it weren't for the sub-abilities, martial arts would effectively double the amount of charms a character can earn in a campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T06:40:16-08:00","id":753877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=720809#post720809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what people think of the overall contents of the new Resources merit, since I (arguably over)wrote it this time. The currency numbers per dot are, I believe, the same as they ever were, but I spent a lot of time working out what they (were always apparently meant to) mean.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll be honest for two editions I banged my head trying to figure how much far enough would legitimately get you, the write up was extremely helpful as essentially class brackets...and really impresses you how stupidly rich some people are. It was also nice that you could slide by with resources zero and feel like you werent actively f'ing yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/811-santino","name":"Santino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar811_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T06:50:47-08:00","id":753897,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, combining charm effects is referring to supplemental charms - you can't supplement a Brawl attack with a Martial Arts charm, or vice versa (much like brawl and melee combining), but you should be able to increase evasion and soak and stuff with both native charms and martial arts.<br /> <br /> This could be more clear, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T07:20:51-08:00","id":753954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=753854#post753854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can forgive the martial arts sub-abilities honestly. Grabbing the martial artist merit effectively gives you a sub-exaltation that you can spend solar xp on the charms for.<br /> <br /> If it weren't for the sub-abilities, martial arts would effectively double the amount of charms a character can earn in a campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but you can already effectively do that with sorcery or evocations, right? And if your MA Charms are specifically incompatible with anything else...<br /> <br /> I dunno, I can kind of understand it, but it still seems sort of excessive. We're talking about maaaaaybe two trees by the time you hit Essence 5, as is - and that's if you sink your entire crop of Solar XP into it. For that same cost, your buddy has bought ten Abilities from 0 to 5, or five Attributes from 1 to 5, or 37 spells, or 20 Evocations, or...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=753897#post753897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, combining charm effects is referring to supplemental charms - you can't supplement a Brawl attack with a Martial Arts charm, or vice versa (much like brawl and melee combining), but you should be able to increase evasion and soak and stuff with both native charms and martial arts.<br /> <br /> This could be more clear, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, that wasn't my read at all - the example is that you can't combine a Snake Charm with a Brawl Charm, so I assumed that meant &quot;no combination of cross-Ability Charms where one is from MA.&quot; You could certainly be right, but yeah, this is not an unambiguous passage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:01:43-08:00","id":754036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=753954#post753954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, that wasn't my read at all - the example is that you can't combine a Snake Charm with a Brawl Charm, so I assumed that meant &amp;quot;no combination of cross-Ability Charms where one is from MA.&amp;quot; You could certainly be right, but yeah, this is not an unambiguous passage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance clarified it in another thread. I'll try to find a quote. <br /> <br /> The gist is &quot;long duration stack, but you can't stack instants.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:07:11-08:00","id":754050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=753835#post753835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (One presumes Sidereals get access to Mastery, as well?)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently they need to engage in some kind of esoteric techniques to get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:24:11-08:00","id":754073,"title":"","content":"<u>Tiger Style</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 3<br /> Armor: Light or none.<br /> Weapons: Unarmed, tiger claws<br /> <br /> Shtick: Close with your enemy. Punish him for trying to run away. Leap at him from the shadows, knock him to the ground, and savage him in a grapple.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Steal 1i from an enemy when you successfully Rush him. Extra Rush successes grant bonus dice to your next attack on that enemy, as long as it\u2019s within the next round.</li> <li>On a Withering attack, some of your extra attack successes become post-soak damage. This is increased if your target tried to run, or if you\u2019re a Solar.</li> <li>Form. Some extra attack successes count double on a Withering roll. Fight prone without penalties. Bonus dice to Rush or counter Disengages; gain Initiative when the enemy Disengages.</li> <li>Gain soak and Hardness; drop this Charm to subtract Hardness from an incoming Decisive.</li> <li>Bonus rounds of control on a grapple.</li> <li>Deal extra damage, and reset to higher Initiative, when you savage a grappled enemy.</li> <li>Knock an enemy prone with any attack; steal Initiative if he tries to stand up. If Mastery, your attack on a prone enemy is undodgeable and does even more damage.</li> <li>On a successful Decisive, trade damage for preventing your enemy from moving.</li> <li>For the scene, enemies at short or medium range must Disengage to move away from you and take -1 Defense vs. surprise attacks.</li> <li>Limited double-9s, double-8s, or double-7s on an <i>attack </i>roll.</li> <li>Upgrade #3. Some extra attack successes transfer to damage on Decisives. <i>Rush reflexively</i>. You can\u2019t Disengage.</li> </ol>Can I just say how nice it is that these Charms are about 2/3 crunch, with a sentence or two of fluff at the start? It\u2019s a very clear divide to when the Charm starts talking about actual mechanical things. I also like that so many of these powers reward you for raising your other physical Attributes (in this case, Strength).<br /> <br /> The Mastery clause of Striking Fury Claws (#2) is kind of awkwardly worded \u2013 it looks like the word \u201cdice\u201d might have been in this sentence once upon a time, to contrast with \u201csuccesses.\u201d<br /> <br /> Again, the form Charm (#3) is a broad, useful power that almost no close-combat build is going to be sorry to have around. Like Snake, Tiger has a solution to the problem of mobile enemies, and the solution is to run up to them and murder them to death, laughing at them when they try to run away. Not a lot of finesse, there, but hard to argue with the results! Looks like the reflexive activation is part of the standard form-Charm package now \u2013 good!<br /> <br /> Celestial Tiger Hide (#4) is not a great defense \u2013 given that you aren\u2019t in much armor, we\u2019re talking about something like -2-5i, costing a Willpower, usable once per scene, and removing the soak bonus afterwards. I\u2019d much rather have Snake\u2019s defense vs. Decisives \u2013 but Snake seems like a much more defensive tree in general.<br /> <br /> Okay, wow. Stalking Cat Movement Meditation (#9) is <i>huge</i> battlefield control \u2013 that\u2019s a big shift in how well people can move you, even two range bands away. I was not expecting that in a scenelong power.<br /> <br /> Leap from Cloaking Shadows (#10) is one of the <i>very</i> few powers that grant double-Xs (even limited double-Xs) on an <i>attack</i> roll. It\u2019s expensive, but if you can get the surprise attack, you\u2019re going to have a pretty painful Decisive to throw around. Snake felt like it stood mostly alone; Tiger feels like it really wants some Athletics or Stealth to really bring on the pain. The Batman stealth combo would go really well with this Charm.<br /> <br /> Angry Predator Frenzy (#11) is very strong overall \u2013 rushing reflexively for the rest of the scene is great! \u2013 but it\u2019s the Mastery effect that really sells me on this: your anima turns into a tiger and eats the other guy\u2019s anima. That\u2019s amazing.<br /> <br /> On balance, this is a very offense-heavy package. It has amazing mobility, good accuracy, and a lot of ways to boost your Decisives \u2013 but it\u2019s not going to care a lot about Withering attacks, and you\u2019re just about on your own if you get hit. It feels like it would play very differently from the last style, which is nice. This feels like a very Night style \u2013 Dodge (or Melee), Stealth, and Athletics are all going to play well with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Single Point Shining Into the Void</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 3<br /> Armor: Light, medium, or none.<br /> Weapons: Slashing swords, reaper daiklaves.<br /> <br /> Shtick: Let your sword speak (and attack) for you. If you are faster than your enemy, cut him. If he exposes a momentary weakness, which you could exploit at great personal risk, cut him. If he has the temerity to attack you, cut the attack. If he hurls impossible twisting magic at you, cut that, too. And if he lets you build up long enough, launch an attack that cannot be countered and will end with you taking his head.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>When you parry an attack, give the Onslaught penalty to your attacker instead of taking it yourself.</li> <li>Add extra damage to a Decisive \u2013 more, if it\u2019s a <i>big</i> Decisive \u2013 but risk losing more if your attack fails.</li> <li>Form. Your sword Joins Battle and makes its own attacks each turn.</li> <li>Gain extra damage on a Decisive if your Initiative is higher than your enemy\u2019s, but lose extra Initiative if the attack fails.</li> <li>Scenelong extra damage to Withering attacks; you can end the Charm for a big hit with a Decisive (or two big hits, if your sword helps).</li> <li>Strike an enemy out to medium range, adding accuracy and damage the further out he is. Slice all opponents between you and him.</li> <li>Clash reflexively, albeit expensively. Deal extra damage on this Decisive.</li> <li>Clash with shaping magic. Cut a path through the Wyld with your irresistible sword spirit.</li> <li>Make a gambit with no need for an attack roll. If it succeeds, make an undodgeable, unblockable Decisive attack.</li> </ol>Shining Point is definitely the <i>weirdest</i> of the three styles so far, once we hit the form. (Does delaying your sword\u2019s action cost it Initiative? One presumes so.) There\u2019s some extra bookkeeping here, but the power of a free attack each turn is pretty huge. Unlike other options so far, you\u2019re either going to get Shining Point up at the start of the fight, or you\u2019re not going to activate it without a Simple action \u2013 there\u2019s no chance of a mid-fight buff. This is not a great form for Terrestrials \u2013 1wp/turn for a second attack is pretty rough \u2013 but a Solar is going to get free attacks every turn with basically no downside.<br /> <br /> This illustration of a Shining Point stylist is pretty great. I can\u2019t quite follow what\u2019s happening here, though somebody seems to be getting chopped up, but the stylist himself looks rad. I would play that guy.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a real all-or-nothing theme so far \u2013 attacks that are murderous if they land (add the difference between your Initiative and the other guy\u2019s to damage? <i>Ouch</i>.) but will mess you up pretty badly if they don\u2019t. Keeping a good defense handy against a SP stylist looks like a good call.<br /> <br /> Void-Slicing Wind (#6) again calls for you to know who is in a line between you and your enemy. The game needs battle maps, book! Commit to that fact!<br /> <br /> \u2026 Whoa. Six-Demon Scabbard Binding is probably the best response to no-defense twisting magic so far. It\u2019s certainly a step up from Integrity\u2019s \u201cGive up a bunch of Willpower, hope for the best.\u201d<br /> <br /> Blinding Nova Flare is absolutely terrifying. If this is not the first un/un attack so far, it\u2019s pretty darn close \u2013 and this is an attack with <i>no cost</i>. There doesn\u2019t seem to be any clear response to this power that isn\u2019t a perfect defense \u2013 you can\u2019t avoid the gambit, and as long as that goes off successfully, you\u2019re going to eat the second attack. That almost feels out of step with the game as presented to this point \u2013 if your attacker gets to this point, you\u2019re dead; just accept it.<br /> <br /> Some balance concerns aside, great style. Risky, but ready to murder the enemy if it succeeds. Your only defense seems to be some (quite expensive) Clashes, though the \u201creturn their Onslaught\u201d effect is fun. Both the descriptions and the actual powers capture the high speed iaijutsu anime feel really well \u2013 this is not a style with a lot of options, but the options it has are amazing. I\u2019m a little surprised there\u2019s no Join Battle enhancer, given the focus on this being a <i>fast</i> style.<br /> <br /> My one critique is that this is also a <i>wordy</i> style - it lacks the short, clear statements of Snake and Tiger. Some of these Charms take a half-page or more to describe their effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:46:56-08:00","id":754088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=753954#post753954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but you can already effectively do that with sorcery or evocations, right? And if your MA Charms are specifically incompatible with anything else...<br /> <br /> I dunno, I can kind of understand it, but it still seems sort of excessive. We're talking about maaaaaybe two trees by the time you hit Essence 5, as is - and that's if you sink your entire crop of Solar XP into it. For that same cost, your buddy has bought ten Abilities from 0 to 5, or five Attributes from 1 to 5, or 37 spells, or 20 Evocations, or...<br /> <br /> <br /> Hm, that wasn't my read at all - the example is that you can't combine a Snake Charm with a Brawl Charm, so I assumed that meant &quot;no combination of cross-Ability Charms where one is from MA.&quot; You could certainly be right, but yeah, this is not an unambiguous passage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Martial arts can be supernal, evocations and spells cannot.<br /> <br /> Only real advantage that MA has over them, and I doubt it overcomes the flaw.<br /> <br /> Edit: Evocations also cap at 5 per artifact without solar charms boosting the numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:55:27-08:00","id":754096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=753954#post753954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but you can already effectively do that with sorcery or evocations, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcery spells are much more horizontal than vertical development, and pure sorcerer is a fairly limited combat role. Evocations cost merit dots per tree and generally can't substitute for a set of combat ability charms.<br /> <br /> I do feel like the cost is a teensy bit higher than necessary. I'd actually rather that they'd just made MA charms only purchasable with regular XP, then the merit and the separate abilities wouldn't be needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:27:56-08:00","id":754208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=753954#post753954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, that wasn't my read at all - the example is that you can't combine a Snake Charm with a Brawl Charm, so I assumed that meant &quot;no combination of cross-Ability Charms where one is from MA.&quot; You could certainly be right, but yeah, this is not an unambiguous passage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pg. 191 defines combat abilities as Brawl, Thrown, Melee, Archery. It's pretty clear to my group that Dodge, Athletics, Resistance are allowed. There is no clear definition I found of whether Reflexive vs. Supplemental matter, but as every Reflexive charm I've read follows a theme of 'separate activity or reactive activity' it still fits together pretty well - Supplemental is a definitely no-no and reflexive is likely up to table interpretation.<br /> <br /> But yes, to avoid speedbumps I'd let Drifting Lead Elusion and Serpentine Evasion combo. <br /> <br /> It's funny how I keep getting into discussions about concepts and combos that I have no intention of trying on my first character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9061-tyranny12","name":"tyranny12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:34:10-08:00","id":754216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=753835#post753835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Snake Strikes the Heel (#8) implies gambits <i>are</i> Decisive attacks, because your Decisive clash has to be a gambit, contrary to earlier Charms that implied they <i>weren\u2019t</i>. So which is it? The Terrestrial note implies this Charm does not normally consume your attack for the turn; does that need to be explicitly stated?<br /> ------<br /> This is a tree that really, really wants you to be faster than your enemy; if you can\u2019t regularly sustain that, you\u2019re probably in for a bad time. A lot of its powers are more effective if the enemy is Crashed, though, so if you <i>can</i> get that upper hand, you\u2019re going to be piling on a lot of hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saw you note the Gambit thing a few times. Gambits are Decisive, flat out, but do not reset like Decisive attacks. Which charms are unclear?<br /> <br /> As for the attack use, in many places in the book they require you to notice the use of a word such as 'reflexive' in the main body, or 'use this after an attack', to state charm order or whether it consumes a combat action. It requires close reading, which many people may not immediately realise. <br /> <br /> Snake Style goes well with Dodge and other initiative increasing abilities, methinks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9061-tyranny12","name":"tyranny12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:44:58-08:00","id":754254,"title":"","content":"For the cost of re-buying an entire Ability, you could initiate into Sorcery, grab ISoB as your control (giving you permanent, free, stacking soak), and then buy Wood Dragon's Claw, which allows you to burn a shaping ritual and have a light Artifact weapon with no committed essence. Or, reverse the order if you want to do some Evocations.<br /> <br /> And then nothing stops you from buying Celestial Sorcery at E3, and getting another free spell that will help you a great deal in combat.<br /> <br /> The above isn't superfun kill-tricks like MA, but it's a lot of benefit for a small investment. So yeah, I agree it's over-costed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:51:10-08:00","id":754289,"title":"","content":"Vance confirmed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/737402-please-help-me-understand-3e-martial-arts?p=750752#post750752\">here</a> that it's only archery/brawl/melee/thrown that you can't combine with martial arts charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:02:31-08:00","id":754326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=753835#post753835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring armor on a Withering Strike, as Armor-Penetrating Fang Strike (#4) does, is nice \u2013 but shew, also expensive. I don\u2019t have a good sense of how powerful this is for the cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can confirm this with actual gameplay. My Night combined this with one of the Ebon Shadow charms to basically crash an armored Behemoth on turn 1, and jumped from 6 Initiative to 26 in the same hit with a few Excellency dice added in. Completely ignoring soak on a Withering hit opens the door to exploiting a lot of stuff that turns threshold successes into bonus dice for your damage roll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:36:23-08:00","id":754416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754088#post754088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Evocations also cap at 5 per artifact without solar charms boosting the numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my biggest gripe. Were the previewed trees and the amount of Evocations in the leak long and/or excessive? Long, sure. Excessive...well, trimming was probably in order. Trimming from 20 to 5, I would also call excessive. <br /> <br /> Evocations just don't feel impressive to me when you get 1-2 at E1, 1-2 at E2 and then 1 each at E3 and E4. That's not the &quot;deep investment&quot; I was looking forward to (which we were also promised and which was massively hyped up) and it pretty much ruined the concept of &quot;Exalt who focuses more on his relationship with a weapon than his own native spiritual growth.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 11-04-2015, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:50:54-08:00","id":754436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754088#post754088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Evocations also cap at 5 per artifact without solar charms boosting the numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where exactly is this rule? I didn't find it anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:58:14-08:00","id":754816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754326#post754326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can confirm this with actual gameplay. My Night combined this with one of the Ebon Shadow charms to basically crash an armored Behemoth on turn 1, and jumped from 6 Initiative to 26 in the same hit with a few Excellency dice added in. Completely ignoring soak on a Withering hit opens the door to exploiting a lot of stuff that turns threshold successes into bonus dice for your damage roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not <i>completely</i> ignoring soak, right? Just armor soak. Your natural soak and Resistance Charms still work fine.<br /> <br /> Still, that's good to hear!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-04-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T13:07:34-08:00","id":754832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tyranny12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754216#post754216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm saw you note the Gambit thing a few times. Gambits are Decisive, flat out, but do not reset like Decisive attacks. Which charms are unclear?<br /> <br /> As for the attack use, in many places in the book they require you to notice the use of a word such as 'reflexive' in the main body, or 'use this after an attack', to state charm order or whether it consumes a combat action. It requires close reading, which many people may not immediately realise.<br /> <br /> Snake Style goes well with Dodge and other initiative increasing abilities, methinks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Wind Slash says you can use it on a Decisive for 2m, <i>or</i> on a Disarm gambit for 1m 1wp, which suggests (to me) that the 2m version can't be used on gambits. If gambits are just a kind of Decisive...<br /> <br /> The book actually vacillates on this somewhat. P. 183 says a gambit is <i>similar to</i> a Decisive, while p. 199 says it's <i>a special sort of</i> Decisive. That makes a big difference!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T13:07:39-08:00","id":754833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754816#post754816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, not <i>completely</i> ignoring soak, right? Just armor soak. Your natural soak and Resistance Charms still work fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Charm in question is &quot;Subtracts your Stealth from the enemy's armored soak. Unexpected attacks double the amount of soak ignored.&quot; The Mastery rider is that if it reduces their armored soak to zero, any remaining points of soak are turned into post-soak damage dice.<br /> <br /> Armor Piercing Fangs basically completely negated the soak to start with, and doubled Stealth (5x2 = 10) turned into 10 dice of post-soak withering damage. Some of it was being a really good roll, but that's 10 dice on top of whatever you get normally. Essentially, it doesn't <i>ignore </i>your personal soak, but it allows you to slip a lot of damage past it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T13:08:10-08:00","id":754835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754416#post754416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my biggest gripe. Were the previewed trees and the amount of Evocations in the leak long and/or excessive? Long, sure. Excessive...well, trimming was probably in order. Trimming from 20 to 5, I would also call excessive.<br /> <br /> Evocations just don't feel impressive to me when you get 1-2 at E1, 1-2 at E2 and then 1 each at E3 and E4. That's not the &quot;deep investment&quot; I was looking forward to (which we were also promised and which was massively hyped up) and it pretty much ruined the concept of &quot;Exalt who focuses more on his relationship with a weapon than his own native spiritual growth.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing stopping you from writing huge Evocation trees if your ST is up for it and you want your character to really be focused on his weapon. It's not like they made a rule limiting the amount of Charms, they just gave examples with low Charm numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T13:10:22-08:00","id":754836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754833#post754833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the Charm in question is &quot;Subtracts your Stealth from the enemy's armored soak. Unexpected attacks double the amount of soak ignored.&quot; The Mastery rider is that if it reduces their armored soak to zero, any remaining points of soak are turned into post-soak damage dice.<br /> <br /> Armor Piercing Fangs basically completely negated the soak to start with, and doubled Stealth (5x2 = 10) turned into 10 dice of post-soak withering damage. Some of it was being a really good roll, but that's 10 dice on top of whatever you get normally. Essentially, it doesn't <i>ignore </i>your personal soak, but it allows you to slip a lot of damage past it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>GM here. OpMegs here was reduced to Minimum after the natural soak (and ignoring the Armored soak). And then yes, gained the full 10 <i>post</i> soak dice.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that Vance would say that this is working more-or-less as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T13:17:06-08:00","id":754842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754833#post754833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the Charm in question is &quot;Subtracts your Stealth from the enemy's armored soak. Unexpected attacks double the amount of soak ignored.&quot; The Mastery rider is that if it reduces their armored soak to zero, any remaining points of soak are turned into post-soak damage dice.<br /> <br /> Armor Piercing Fangs basically completely negated the soak to start with, and doubled Stealth (5x2 = 10) turned into 10 dice of post-soak withering damage. Some of it was being a really good roll, but that's 10 dice on top of whatever you get normally. Essentially, it doesn't <i>ignore </i>your personal soak, but it allows you to slip a lot of damage past it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh, okay, I forgot that you said there was an Ebon Shadow Charm in there. That makes sense, then - and wow, that does sound vicious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T13:20:24-08:00","id":754848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754436#post754436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where exactly is this rule? I didn't find it anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is because it is not a rule that exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T13:30:32-08:00","id":754860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754842#post754842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahhh, okay, I forgot that you said there was an Ebon Shadow Charm in there. That makes sense, then - and wow, that does sound vicious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, my Night started out with just Ebon Shadow, and it was okay, mostly because I hadn't grasped the Stealth Charms yet. But combining styles is a <i>crazy</i> thing. Buying up styles repeatedly seems like an XP sink until you read through and notice there are exactly <i>two</i> styles that can't be used bare-handed (Single Point and Steel Devil)... meaning all the others are cross-compatible-combinable with each other.<br /> <br /> Edit: Correction, <i>three</i> styles. Because I forgot Righteous Devil exists. And, y'know, no barehanding firewand stuff. I think. Unless you were a Fire DB, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1817,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","user":"OpMegs","date":". 11-04-2015, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T14:44:17-08:00","id":754977,"title":"","content":"<u>White Reaper Style</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 3<br /> Armor: Any.<br /> Weapons: Scythes, spears, staves, unarmed attacks.<br /> <br /> Shtick: Kill battle groups dead. Charge up from defeating one enemy to face another; expend that charge for temporary bonuses. Layer defensive buffs based on the \u201chalos\u201d you\u2019ve gained from clobbering battle groups.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Add bonus damage based on Strength to a Withering or Decisive attack.</li> <li>Your Onslaught penalties turn into bonuses vs. one attack.</li> <li>Form. Double-10s on Decisive damage. -1 Defense to all battle groups. Move through battle groups. Collect halos that grant +1 Resolve each for crashing or killing notable enemies, or for damaging battle groups.</li> <li>Limited double-9s (or double-8s, vs. battle groups) on an attack roll. Expend halos for +1 die each.</li> <li>Extra Withering or Decisive damage. Vs. a battle group, ignore soak from Size or add extra damage for high Initiative. Burn halos for post-soak Withering damage.</li> <li>Make two Decisive attacks, or two Withering attacks on a battle group. Burn halos for +1 attack each.</li> <li>Add (halos) to Parry, or burn them for double that bonus.</li> <li>Add (2 * [halos + 1]) to soak for the scene, or more if you aren\u2019t wearing armor. Battle groups don\u2019t add Size to damage.</li> <li>Burn halos to heal damage. For the scene, reduce wound penalties by (halos), increase difficulty of rout checks (I bet!), and expend halos for Initiative.</li> </ol><br /> Revolving Crescent Defense (#2) is pretty great \u2013 especially with the Mastery rider that makes it turnlong. The Initiative cost stings a little, but in some fairly reasonable circumstances, that\u2019s about as cheap a full Excellency as you\u2019re ever going to get \u2013 woe betide the guy who mega-flurries you.<br /> <br /> White Reaper Form (#3) is just always -1 to the BG\u2019s Defense, right? Like, it has this calculation based on their current Drill, but practically, it\u2019s just always -1 Defense.<br /> <br /> Bleeding Crescent Strike (#4) is at least the second MA Charm to say something like \u201cdouble-9s (but only to a maximum of Stat dice).\u201d I wonder if that\u2019s a standard thing for non-Solar Exalts.<br /> <br /> How <i>do</i> \u201cautomatic successes\u201d on damage interact with soak, anyway?<br /> <br /> That is a White Reaper Lunar just absolutely murdering a bunch of dudes. Every martial art so far has gotten its own illustration, which I appreciate.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s kind of odd that so many White Reaper Charms <i>require</i> burning halos \u2013 it seems like that makes it hard to use the style at all while amassing halos. Enemies Like Grass (#6) is probably the exception: burn five halos to make seven Withering attacks on a battle group, and immediately recover all halos. Also, y\u2019know, probably kill the battle group. (This is an expensive power, but it\u2019s also about the only one I\u2019ve seen that allows you to flurry Withering attacks \u2013 almost all big Solar multiattacks are Decisive-only.)<br /> <br /> Oof, Flickering Corona Barrier (#7) is <i>potent</i>. 2m for, potentially, a full defensive Excellency, not consuming your halos, that a Solar can activate after the attack is rolled. That\u2019s just nasty \u2013 if you can use it at all, of course; absent a handy BG, you\u2019re going to have a much harder time building it up.<br /> <br /> The styles seem to favor these permanent form-enhancers, which I absolutely approve of \u2013 it\u2019s cool to have your existing Charms become more awesome over time.<br /> <br /> Standing by my initial impressions, here. When four Dragon-Blooded jump you, this style isn\u2019t going to add much; you\u2019ll only infrequently Crash or kill anyone, and so you\u2019re rarely going to have more than one or two halos to burn \u2013 that\u2019s a ho-hum bonus at a not-insignificant cost. Against a battle group, though, you could easily pull a halo every round \u2013 or more, with Enemies Like Grass. That\u2019s a big buff \u2013 and anyone who doesn\u2019t want Flickering Corona Barrier in a setup like that is crazy. In its niche, this is a pretty horribly lethal style. (Probably still wasn\u2019t Lilith\u2019s best choice against one Sidereal and one god, but apparently that worked out for her.)<br /> <br /> This is probably the most defensive style I\u2019ve seen so far. No general-use mobility buffs or anti-kiting, but we\u2019ve got Charms to help with Onslaught, soak, late-step Defense boosting, healing, and debuffing battle groups. On offense, the style is lighter on solid powers\u2026 unless you\u2019re a battle group, of course.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Ebon Shadow Style</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 3<br /> Armor: Unarmored only.<br /> Weapons: Sais, tiger claws, knives, unarmed attacks.<br /> <br /> Shtick: Kill from the shadows. Make surprise attacks every chance you get, bypassing armor or hitting harder than your enemy expects; your stealth helps mitigate your foe's counterstrike.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Penalize attempts to see you in combat. Fake your own death to escape battle.</li> <li>Subtract (Stealth), or (2*Stealth) in a surprise attack, from enemy\u2019s armored soak.</li> <li>Form. Anyone who fails their check when you enter stealth loses 1i. Bonus Initiative when you reset after an unexpected Decisive. +1 Defense.</li> <li>Enemy rolls a Decisive twice, taking the lower result.</li> <li>Subtract (Essence + Stealth) from a Decisive aimed at you.</li> <li>Move in shadows more easily; do extra damage if you use this movement to reach Close range on an enemy.</li> <li>Extra successes on a Decisive attack roll convert damage dice to successes \u2013 without limit, on a surprise attack.</li> <li>Strangle an enemy with his own shadow, doing extra damage.</li> </ol><br /> Nothing But Shadows (#1) says it can be used to go to ground by pretending to be dead. I believe that works once\u2026 but after your enemy knows the trick, surely this should stop being so effective.<br /> <br /> I assume this is the Ebon Shadow illustration, with the lady choking in the air? No idea what\u2019s happening here. Edit: Ah, it\u2019s the pinnacle Charm in action.<br /> <br /> Ebon Shadow has probably the easiest reflexive form activation: successfully hide. There\u2019s a fun flavor there: you ambush the stylist, he vanishes and reflexively enters the style, and now the shoe is on the other foot.<br /> <br /> So, here\u2019s fun: combine Elusive Flicker Evasion (#4) with an enemy using Thrown\u2019s Shadow Wind Slash. Does he roll four times? If so, does he take the lower of the higher of each pair, or the higher of the lower of each pair?<br /> <br /> Shadow-Body Dissolution (#5) is a weaker, more expensive Adamant Skin Technique \u2013 that lets you reflexively enter Stealth, if it works well enough. I\u2019m cool with that trade, for a general-use power.<br /> <br /> I like the flavor that several of these Charms leave no bodies \u2013 yours or the enemy\u2019s. That makes for some nice \u201cCan\u2019t prove anything happened\u201d moments. (Although, shouldn\u2019t this help Nothing But Shadows? Faking your death would be a lot more persuasive, and harder to stop, if you were also fading into a shadowy mist.)<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a little bit \u201ceh\u201d on Ebon Shadow overall, but maybe that\u2019s the thematics rather than the actual powers. The style definitely rewards a high investment in Stealth, and it plays well with the stuff Solar Stealth already does rather than just being redundant \u2013 but I\u2019m not sure it adds enough oomph that I\u2019d want this for my main offense. Maybe I\u2019m undervaluing it \u2013 the defensive component is quite solid, and there are a couple of nasty offensive tricks in here, if nothing with the sheer killing power of Single Point or Tiger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T15:11:46-08:00","id":755006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=754977#post754977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bleeding Crescent Strike (#4) is at least the second MA Charm to say something like \u201cdouble-9s (but only to a maximum of Stat dice).\u201d I wonder if that\u2019s a standard thing for non-Solar Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only place in the antagonists chapter I see a similar mechanic is in the quick-and-dirty version of Earth Dragon Style: Force of the Mountain, p. 543. Could be that this is particularly a Martial Arts thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T15:48:44-08:00","id":755124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackson MacKenzie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=755006#post755006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only place in the antagonists chapter I see a similar mechanic is in the quick-and-dirty version of Earth Dragon Style: Force of the Mountain, p. 543. Could be that this is particularly a Martial Arts thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe so! That seems like it would also make sense. I don't think it's a big statistical difference, either way, but it probably cuts down the swing somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-04-2015, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T16:53:02-08:00","id":755246,"title":"","content":"<u>Crane</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 4(!)<br /> Armor: None<br /> Weapons: War fan, hook sword, unarmed. Lacks the normal \u201cunarmed can do lethal\u201d rider.<br /> <br /> Shtick: Defend all your allies, and reply with enhanced counterattacks to anything that comes their way.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A Withering attack is more accurate and damaging against someone who has attacked you (or a Ward you were Defend Othering).</li> <li>+2 Parry when Defending Other.</li> <li>Form. +1 Parry. Cost for Full Defense reduced by 1i. Respond to any attack on you or your ward with a counterattack.</li> <li>Make a roll; bank successes for later use in raising Parry or making counterattacks.</li> <li>Counterattack out to the range of the attack made on you.</li> <li>Fly for 1-2 actions, reducing falling damage at the end if still airborne. Double-10s on Decisive damage rolls.</li> <li>Add stunt dice to Decisive damage rolls. If you do enough damage, create Ties in the target.</li> <li>Double-10s on Decisive damage. Enemy\u2019s Defense is penalized by his Intimacies as per Resolve.</li> <li>Your counterattack throws an enemy two range bands, or disarms at a discount, or returns an attack to the attacker.</li> <li>When you Decisively counterattack your enemy\u2019s Decisive attack, add his Initiative to your own.</li> </ol>Empowering Justice Meditation (#1) is pretty uninspiring in its default mode. Compare 4m on an Excellency to 3m on this; the Excellency will hit at times that this misses, and if they do both hit, the Excellency does just as much Withering damage unless soaked to minimum. The math is considerably better in the secondary \u201cif-they-hit-you\u201d mode, or if you\u2019re a Solar.<br /> <br /> Same thing with Fluttering Cry of Warning (#2), actually \u2013 the default mode is only 1m better than what you could do with just an Excellency. Again, the Mastery benefit helps a lot \u2013 a reflexive Defend Other is a big deal \u2013 but so far, the default Celestial-level effect of this style fails to impress. (Actually, the mastery benefit is <i>really</i> good \u2013 I\u2019d probably take that over War Lion Stance.)<br /> <br /> Crane Form (#3) seems to assume that there are default rules for when a counterattack is made. Which, it makes perfect sense that there <i>would</i> be such rules, but I don\u2019t think there actually are. Reflexive activation is hard here \u2013 you have to <i>defend</i> in a way that drops the attacker\u2019s Initiative below your own.<br /> <br /> Actually\u2026 ha. Actually, are there any rules saying you can\u2019t activate multiple counterattack effects in response to a single attack? Can I respond to an attack with Solar Counterattack <i>and</i> Solar Cross-Counter <i>and</i> Crane Form <i>and</i> Crossed-Wings Denial (#4)? I don\u2019t see anything detailing general counterattack rules <i>at all</i>.<br /> <br /> Kindly Sifu\u2019s Quill (#8) is <i>vicious</i> with the Mastery tag: double-7s on a Decisive damage roll, against which your opponent has something like -4 Defense, if you can exploit a Defining Intimacy. That\u2019s a fight-ender for 5m.<br /> <br /> *snerk* The image of what I assume is Mournful Crane\u2019s Cry (#9) is just ridiculous \u2013 ragdoll bodies and a pale, shrieking central character. Not a fan. Edit: Wait, no, this has to be from Silver-Voiced Nightingale. No Cranepic?<br /> <br /> Okay, what is \u201cher enemy\u2019s Initiative\u201d for the purposes of Wisdom of the Celestial Crane (#1)? Is it the enemy\u2019s pre-attack Initiative, or if they hit, is this their reset-to-base 3i? The latter seems like the natural reading, but that\u2019s a pretty expensive Charm.<br /> <br /> The major thing here seems to be the reflexive Counterattacks \u2013 which is a big deal! \u2013 and the various counterattack-enhancing Charms\u2026 but that just drives the lack of any real counterattack rules home, and absent that, power is hard to evaluate. Otherwise, the Celestial-level defense here is lackluster, though some of the Mastery upgrades are quite nice. I\u2019m afraid I\u2019ll always have some affection for Neph\u2019s mad original vision, here, with its combo-free Charms and its 0m perfect defense and its instant-training effect. This comes close, when it gets into Intimacy manipulation and other nifty tricks, but it just doesn\u2019t have that same wow-factor.<br /> <br /> My suspicion is that, for a group who stay in relatively close proximity, this is going to be a fairly lethal add-on: whenever anyone gets attacked, the Crane stylist Defends Other on them and then replies with a counterattack. My suspicion is <i>also</i> that this is going to be a pretty glass-cannon strategy; the Parry buffs are limited, there\u2019s no Onslaught negation, and there\u2019s nothing to help with soak or mitigating Decisive attacks in a build that can't wear armor. Forget the sidebar telling you to favor social stuff, you need <i>Resistance -</i> one good hit and you\u2019re going to be minus one Crane.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 3<br /> Armor: Light or none<br /> Weapons: Your enhanced kiai.<br /> <br /> Shtick: Strike down your enemy with your resounding song; Bollywood dance number optional. Buff allies to make big cooperative attacks. Make Performance-based influence rolls in combat.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Your shouts are light ranged weapons, permanently. You can flurry them with Performance rolls at no penalty.</li> <li>Reroll (but not recurring reroll?) all 1s on Join Battle for you and all allies who can hear you.</li> <li>Inspire fear in your enemy, forcing him to move away from you. If you also hit him with your kiai, treat him as if he had Intimacies of fear for you.</li> <li>Form. +1 Evasion. +Performance to your Withering damage. Gain 3i when someone pays WP to resist your influence.</li> <li>+(Performance/2) to Evasion vs. a Decisive. If successful, reflexively Read Intentions with bonus dice.</li> <li>Against one enemy, you take no Evasion penalties, gain double-9s to Rush or Disengage, and gain 1i when he gains Initiative.</li> <li>Make a Performance roll vs. all enemies within earshot; those overcome must pay 1wp or take -3 Defense from despair.</li> <li>All enemies in short range are hit by a sonic environmental attack; all who fail to resist can be hit by an extra-accurate Withering kiai the next turn.</li> <li>An ally\u2019s attacks gain double-10s (Decisive) or double-9s (Withering) on damage. Bonus damage if you then attack the same target with your kiai.</li> <li>You and all allies gain 1 WP each turn, which cannot be banked or spent on Charms. Wow!</li> <li>Make a kiai gambit on the target. Each success delays his turn by 1 tick and adds 1i to the damage of all Decisives made on him until his next turn.</li> </ol>Voice of the Night Bird (#1) is a pretty great dip \u2013 or would be, without the Ability requirement. Never be without a ranged weapon! Social attack via your killing song!<br /> <br /> Terrifying Battle Shriek (#3) plus Tiger Style? Terrify your enemy into running away, then run him down and devour him.<br /> <br /> Why do all these Martial Arts Charms have a semicolon after their Mins? We\u2019re often told that rules text \u201cisn\u2019t programming code\u201d \u2013 is this, in fact, a bit of C++ that\u2019s crept into the book? (Probably not.)<br /> <br /> Hearing the Heart\u2019s Song (#5) is a pretty lousy defensive Charm, but it may not be a bad Read Intentions booster.<br /> <br /> Haunting Heart-Rending Melody (#7) is unlikely to actually stick on anyone \u2013 a -3 penalty to Defense is pretty huge. On the other hand, if five guys all spend WP to resist, that\u2019s a big swing to your Initiative, thanks to the form!<br /> <br /> Ooh, Resounding Songbird\u2019s Cry (#8) is an environmental attack! We haven\u2019t seen that space explored yet. That looks like a pretty potent way of getting around many enemies\u2019 primary defenses \u2013 not a lot of damage, but it sets you up for a big follow-up, and damage is damage.<br /> <br /> Aria of Victory (#9) is really stunning; it might as well read \u201cYou and all allies gain 1 non-Charm success to one action every turn.\u201d That\u2019s a huge bonus. Shattering Discord Cacophony, on the other hand, took me a moment to get. It seems like the best thing to do with this is to drop, say, 10i for +4i to all allies. If you can do that right after your enemy <i>last</i> acted, and so significantly delay when he <i>next</i> acts, that means all your allies (and you!) might get 1-2 chances to make Decisives with +4i. With three allies, that could be something like seven attacks, for +28i (less what you spent on the gambit) \u2013 more, if you can afford to chain on Flashing Blade Harmony. That\u2019s not half bad, but it\u2019s still a pretty expensive power requiring a lot of set-up \u2013 you might get one really good opportunity to use this per fight, and then only if you\u2019ve got a solid group.<br /> <br /> Nightingale feels like it should play well with Crane \u2013 lots of Simple effects here that would eat up your turn buffing allies, while Crane adds an enormous pile of counterattacks; neither of them can abide much armor. Crane wants to parry, though, while this wants to dodge \u2013 hm.<br /> <br /> On balance, this is a style that feels more about being helpful than about achieving big things on your own. There\u2019s some social bonuses, some reliable ranged weapons, and some big party buffs \u2013 but not much in the way of meat-and-potatoes. You could get a lot out of this, if you\u2019re social-heavy, but I wouldn\u2019t want it to be my only line of defense (or offense, for that matter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-04-2015, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T16:55:37-08:00","id":755251,"title":"","content":"You named Crane as White Reaper in your most recent post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T16:58:39-08:00","id":755254,"title":"",