ss=\"message\">Actually\u2026 ha. Actually, are there any rules saying you can\u2019t activate multiple counterattack effects in response to a single attack? Can I respond to an attack with Solar Counterattack <i>and</i> Solar Cross-Counter <i>and</i> Crane Form <i>and</i> Crossed-Wings Denial (#4)? I don\u2019t see anything detailing general counterattack rules <i>at all</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of wish we would just get the 10-step attack resolution table back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T17:26:08-08:00","id":755306,"title":"","content":"I'm just amused that the capstone charm for Nightingale Style is &quot;Sing a note at someone... And if they die when under its effects <i>they dissolve</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T17:27:31-08:00","id":755308,"title":"","content":"I really love the &quot;not only songs, any kind of music if you want!&quot;-sidebar on the Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style. One of my characters plays the guqin and I can just see him sit in the middle of the battlefield, plucking the strings and trolling the enemy with his evasion-charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T17:31:18-08:00","id":755315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=755308#post755308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really love the &quot;not only songs, any kind of music if you want!&quot;-sidebar on the Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style. One of my characters plays the guqin and I can just see him sit in the middle of the battlefield, plucking the strings and trolling the enemy with his evasion-charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>My favorite suggestion is &quot;Freestyle Poet whose words burn themselves into your foe&quot;.<br /> <br /> If I had ANY actual skill in rhyming and the like, I'd so make a MA who schooled his foes via freestyle rap-battle.<br /> <br /> As it stands, alas, I'll just have to use my Chosen of Endings who sings the songs of his foe's demise on his Starmetal-strung violin. (And in a pinch, the violin bow can be used as a light whacky-stick)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T21:22:29-08:00","id":755810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=755315#post755315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had ANY actual skill in rhyming and the like, I'd so make a MA who schooled his foes via freestyle rap-battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Epig Rab Badads of Hisady!<br /> <br /> Swan!<br /> <br /> Versus!<br /> <br /> Ragara Myrrun!<br /> <br /> BEGIN!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T04:24:33-08:00","id":756239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=755810#post755810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Epig Rab Badads of Hisady!<br /> <br /> Swan!<br /> <br /> Versus!<br /> <br /> Ragara Myrrun!<br /> <br /> BEGIN!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Swan:<br /> <br /> Let's start this thing off with the number one<br /> hottest god king standing under the sun.<br /> Think you're a threat?<br /> Dude, ima get you,<br /> and beat your ass for fun!<br /> <br /> Have fun being earth when I walk all over you<br /> you got a martial arts dearth what the fuck you go'n to do<br /> my fist's got girth you're the one it's going through<br /> <br /> I hunt your immaculate ass for sport<br /> now come on, let's hear it, come back, retort<br /> <br /> RM:<br /> What was that I heard? A scream? A grunt?<br /> Motherfucker you're dealing with a one-man Wyld Hunt<br /> I'll hit you twice in the stomach, bruise up your front<br /> then finish it off with a swift kick to the cunt<br /> <br /> Immaculate grandmaster here representing<br /> slaying golden demons so you better start repenting<br /> I've got the styles, so many I fucking lost count<br /> Got patience of the Isle, while I sit on the mount<br /> <br /> You're a king, please, picked by the sun?<br /> How many styles under your belt? One?<br /> That's what I thought, I've got the speed and agility<br /> you must be kidding when you talk about killin' me<br /> <br /> Swan:<br /> <br /> *Swan's caste mark flashes as he dishes out the pain*<br /> Be glad you're flexible now<br /> I'll teach you to bow<br /> get down and kowtow<br /> to the king in the tow-<br /> -er who owns your ass<br /> from the stars to the grass<br /> feels good to go first, now you're coming last<br /> <br /> <br /> RM:<br /> <br /> I'll take the last word like we got in the Usurpation<br /> laid the old kings low and started our own nation<br /> Save your breath, but check that caste mark<br /> you're marked for death, watch your soul disembark<br /> Now take this hit, your arrogant snake, I've got a thirst to slake, a right cross to stake<br /> time to cure all your aches with a Fire Drake BREAK!<br /> <br /> *Ragara Myrunn theoretically starts executing his Fire Drake Break combo*<br /> <br /> EDIT: Whoops I forgot<br /> <br /> WHO WON?<br /> <br /> WHO'S NEXT?<br /> <br /> YOU DECIDE!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 11-05-2015, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":23}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T04:25:22-08:00","id":756241,"title":"","content":"It's pretty crappy but I did it in like 10 mintues so don't be so hard on it. Also I know how crappy it can be to read a rap and not get the flow I was going for, but it's there, trust me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T10:24:37-08:00","id":756735,"title":"","content":"If I may?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=756239#post756239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swan:<br /> <br /> Let's start this thing off with the number one<br /> hottest god king standing under the sun.<br /> Think you're a threat?<br /> Dude, ima get you,<br /> and beat your ass for fun!<br /> <br /> Have fun being earth when I walk all over you<br /> you got a martial arts dearth what the fuck you go'n to do<br /> my fist's got girth you're the one it's going through<br /> <br /> I hunt your immaculate ass for sport<br /> now come on, let's hear it, come back, retort<br /> <br /> RM:<br /> What was that I heard? A scream? A grunt?<br /> Motherfucker you're dealing with a one-man Wyld Hunt<br /> I'll hit you twice in the stomach, bruise up your front<br /> then finish it off with a swift kick to the cunt<br /> <br /> Immaculate grandmaster here representing<br /> slaying golden demons so you better start repenting<br /> I've got the styles, so many I fucking lost count<br /> Got patience of the Isle, while I sit on the mount<br /> <br /> You're a king, please, picked by the sun?<br /> How many styles under your belt? One?<br /> That's what I thought, I've got the speed and agility<br /> you must be kidding when you talk about killin' me<br /> <br /> Swan:<br /> <br /> *Swan's caste mark flashes as he dishes out the pain*<br /> Be glad you're flexible now<br /> I'll teach you to bow<br /> get down and kowtow<br /> to the king in the tow-<br /> -er who owns your ass<br /> from the stars to the grass<br /> feels good to go first, now you're coming last<br /> <br /> <br /> RM:<br /> <br /> I'll take the last word like we got in the Usurpation<br /> laid the old kings low and started our own nation<br /> Save your breath, but check that caste mark<br /> you're marked for death, watch your soul disembark<br /> Now take this hit, your arrogant snake, I've got a thirst to slake, a right cross to stake<br /> time to cure all your aches with a Fire Drake BREAK!<br /> <br /> *Ragara Myrunn theoretically starts executing his Fire Drake Break combo*</div> </div> </div> </div>*He's interrupted as a hooded figure steps between them*<br /> <br /> What do you think you could possibly know?<br /> What do you think you could have to show?<br /> Say your prayers, list your regrets,<br /> <br /> *The figure throws back his hood revealing Chejop Kejak*<br /> <br /> 'Cause you're facing the oldest of the Chosen of Secrets!<br /> <br /> So back up, boys, this is my game.<br /> My kung fu's so good, I made the stars forget my name!<br /> And those Dragon styles that so fill you with glee?<br /> Gotta break it to you, kid, they were invented by me!<br /> <br /> To the punk over there, you think a new dawn has risen?<br /> I'll smack your butt right here and send you right back to prison!<br /> I'm five thousand years old, I've met the Sun and the Moon,<br /> I control the Threads of Fate, so <i>you</i> dance to <i>my </i>tune!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=756239#post756239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WHO WON?<br /> <br /> WHO'S NEXT?<br /> <br /> YOU DECIDE!</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:40:46-08:00","id":756998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=756241#post756241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty crappy but I did it in like 10 mintues so don't be so hard on it. Also I know how crappy it can be to read a rap and not get the flow I was going for, but it's there, trust me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read well to me. Nice job. Also if likes were any indication, it was not crappy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WhirlwindMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=756735#post756735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *He's interrupted as a hooded figure steps between them*<br /> <br /> What do you think you could possibly know?<br /> What do you think you could have to show?<br /> Say your prayers, list your regrets,<br /> <br /> *The figure throws back his hood revealing Chejop Kejak*<br /> <br /> 'Cause you're facing the oldest of the Chosen of Secrets!<br /> <br /> So back up, boys, this is my game.<br /> My kung fu's so good, I made the stars forget my name!<br /> And those Dragon styles that so fill you with glee?<br /> Gotta break it to you, kid, they were invented by me!<br /> <br /> To the punk over there, you think a new dawn has risen?<br /> I'll smack your butt right here and send you right back to prison!<br /> I'm five thousand years old, I've met the Sun and the Moon,<br /> I control the Threads of Fate, so <i>you</i> dance to <i>my </i>tune!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The original was fine on its own, but this was a cool addition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T14:48:53-08:00","id":757296,"title":"","content":"<u>Righteous Devil Style</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 3<br /> Armor: Medium, light, or none.<br /> Weapons: Firewands and other flame-based weapons.<br /> <br /> Shtick: Call out the wicked and let them repent or burn. Armor won\u2019t save them; numbers won\u2019t save them; health levels for darn sure won\u2019t save them.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Double-10s on Decisive damage. Use firewands out to medium range.</li> <li>Your Aim actions also allow you to reload your weapon.</li> <li>Add your Aim dice to a Withering attack\u2019s damage, or one die to a Decisive\u2019s damage.</li> <li>Form. Intimidate all enemies; anyone affected takes a penalty to run or hide. Reflexively Aim at anyone affected. Your firewand is a melee weapon.</li> <li>Remove some or all of the target\u2019s soak, depending on how much cover he has.</li> <li>Everyone at close range is treated as standing in a bonfire.</li> <li>Cheap Withering or Decisive damage booster.</li> <li>Hit up to 6 enemies in a 90-degree arc, doing full Decisive damage to each(!).</li> <li>Target repents of his wicked deeds or takes [Essence]A levels of damage.</li> </ol>I\u2019ve always wanted to build a Righteous Devil character \u2013 but, y\u2019know, Scroll of the Monk. Third time might be the charm, here.<br /> <br /> The first three Charms here are all very Aim-heavy: Blossom of Inevitable Demise (#1) requires an Aim to function at Medium range, and Cloud of Ebon Devils (#2) and Kiss of the Sun Concentration (#3) both require an Aim to do anything. That\u2019s a problem for a short-range weapon, because you wouldn\u2019t normally spend turns Aiming at all \u2013 since Aim can\u2019t be flurries, any turn you spend doing that you don\u2019t actually get to attack. And then we get to the Form (#4), and everything clicks: if you intimidate your targets well enough, you get to Aim for free! That\u2019s a pretty potent effect \u2013 it\u2019s effectively +3 non-Charm dice to all your attacks for the scene, plus whatever other Aim upgrades now become reflexive as well. It also sets tone for the style pretty well \u2013 this is an art for calling the wicked out and putting them down, not for defense.<br /> <br /> (It\u2019s also nice to see the Equilibrium-style \u201cfight with my pistols\u201d thing lifted from 2e's Golden Exhalation Style.)<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t much care for the form activation condition \u2013 if you\u2019re losing a turn to Aim anyway, you might as well just spend that turn activating the form (and then Aim reflexively). The form of the roll here (Cha + Pres + Ess) is almost never repeated in the Charms chapter; there, we\u2019d say \u201c(Cha + Pres) roll, adding (Essence) bonus dice.\u201d I\u2019m very happy with the more compact form, as long as we all understand what it means \u2013 I assume the (Ess) dice count towards your die cap?<br /> <br /> Azure Abacus Meditation (#5) is a vicious little charm \u2013 in most close-range encounters (i.e., your default use case) you\u2019re obviating their soak completely. This is both cheaper and more powerful than Snake\u2019s soak-negation \u2013 plus it works at Short range! I know it isn\u2019t original to this edition, but I do love the anima targeting reticule.<br /> <br /> In general, this style (together with, maybe, Single Point) has some of the strongest visuals \u2013 I can very clearly see the gunslinger standing in the heart of the fire he\u2019s set.<br /> <br /> Dancing Devil Trigger Finger (#8) requires tracking all enemies \u201cin a 90-degree arc\u201d out to Medium range. Maps, game! You need maps! <i>Suggest using maps</i>. This is very close to the most dangerous multiattack so far \u2013 maybe Melee\u2019s \u201chit everyone\u201d powers are better, but those only work at close range. If you can actually set this up on three or four enemies \u2013 and you should be able to! \u2013 with a decent amount of Initiative, you could pretty easily end a fight in one shot. It\u2019s expensive, but looks very much worthwhile \u2013 and of course, you could stack it with Caress of 1000 Hells (#9), Kiss of the Sun Concentration, and Phoenix Flies on Golden Wings (#7) for an extra-accurate attack dealing an extra [Ess] levels and 6 dice of damage to everyone in the area, on top of your full base Initiative damage \u2013 unless they repent, of course, which is <i>also</i> a solution to a persistent Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> (I like Caress\u2019s \u201cREPENT OR BURN\u201d theme in general. Solar Judge Dredd is a totally viable concept, complete with armor.)<br /> <br /> This is probably one of my favorites so far. Don\u2019t ask Righteous Devil for defense \u2013 it\u2019s not there. On the plus side, you <i>can</i> wear armor, and you could pretty easily stack Resistance or Dodge \u2013 or, heck, Melee; don\u2019t tell me you can\u2019t stunt that. But for pure, unfiltered offense, with high-accuracy, high-damage Decisives, this style has you covered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Black Claw Style</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 3<br /> Armor: None.<br /> Weapons: Unarmed only. (Well, and stolen weapons \u2013 see #7.)<br /> <br /> Shtick: You are an innocent, defenseless dove. You were attacked unjustly, and the crowd is turning to your side \u2013 even your enemy is compelled to love you, and his ability to fight you falters. Then you rip out his still-beating heart and burn it to ash.<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If anyone beats you at Join Battle, he is perceived as starting the fight \u2013 both by others and by himself, unless he beats your Guile.</li> <li>When attacked, counterattack socially to create positive Ties to yourself and steal Initiative. With the form active, also affects bystanders.</li> <li>Poison your enemy with a long-lasting Initiative-draining venom. Gain the Initiative it drains.</li> <li>Form. +1 Evasion; disengage more easily and at lower cost. Penalize enemy defenses if they have positive Ties to you.</li> <li>An attack on you loses (Guile + positive Tie strength) dice.</li> <li>Grab and hold an enemy without savaging him. If he is poisoned, turns of grappling don\u2019t count against the poison\u2019s duration.</li> <li>Counterattack with a Disarm gambit, stealing your enemy\u2019s weapon. It is a Black Claw style weapon as long as you carry it.</li> <li>When attacked Decisively, counterattack with social influence against everyone in earshot, subtracting your wound penalties from Resolves. Anyone affected turns on the attacker \u2013 violently, with appropriate Ties to you.</li> <li>Rip out your enemy\u2019s heart. Double damage if he likes you; <i>triple</i> damage if he loves you.</li> </ol>The Mastery effect of Open Palm Caress lets you grapple as an ambush. Well, that\u2019s the fight. (What <i>does</i> happen if you ambush someone who then beats your Join Battle?) I like that this Charm \u2013 and, it looks like, the style in general \u2013 reverses the normal combat incentives: \u201cOh, you spent 10m to win Join Battle? Hope you like being the bad guy!\u201d<br /> <br /> Heck <i>yeah</i>, Righteous Devil lady. I don\u2019t know who you are, but you look awesome.<br /> <br /> This is the second style to have \u201csuccessfully defend against an attack that drops your enemy\u2019s Initiative below your own\u201d as a form trigger. It seems like the <i>only</i> way to make that fire, barring some Dodge Charm shenanigans, is to defend with exactly 1 less Initiative than your attacker \u2013 right? That\u2019s awfully selective of a trigger.<br /> <br /> Okay, let\u2019s see. Practically speaking, a stylist here is going to have Guile 5-6 \u2013 right? So Doe Eyes Defense (#5) is somewhere between 5-10 dice subtracted for 4m1i; if you\u2019re a Solar, at least the 1i is likely refunded, and maybe more. That\u2019s very solid \u2013 it\u2019s better than a non-Charm bonus of the same size would be, for instance. It seems like this could be used to stave off an enemy Decisive <i>really</i> effectively \u2013 the enemy has to substantially outspend you just to have a reasonable chance of hitting. Lesson here seems to be &quot;Crash the Black Claw stylist <i>first</i>, try to actually kill her second.&quot;<br /> <br /> Storm-Calming Embrace (#6) is just great. You can\u2019t hit the enemy, of course, but you can hold on to him while the poison kills him for you. Hm. Although he can swing back now, so this is not nearly as deadly as it would have been in 2e \u2013 okay, now I\u2019m uncertain whether this feels worth the cost. Baseline grappling is already so lethal, you have to give a compelling reason to do something different with it.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m now picturing a Black Claw stylist deliberately picking fights just so she can steal weapons of particular types. \u201cSorry, I need a firewand to be a form weapon!\u201d It doesn\u2019t <i>seem</i> like that should break anything, but it might lead to some kind of odd combinations, given that the stolen weapon appears to be in-form indefinitely at no committed cost.<br /> <br /> Black Claw has one of the tightest themes so far. Everything works together to create the narrative of the fight; all the Charms push you towards the upper-level stuff, where all those Intimacies cash in and reward you for being such a poor, innocent soul. There\u2019s very little direct offense here (until the pinnacle), but the defensive tricks are pretty solid \u2013 and the social counterattacks move the front line somewhere many fighters won\u2019t be well-defended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-05-2015, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T16:00:52-08:00","id":757425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=757296#post757296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(What <i>does</i> happen if you ambush someone who then beats your Join Battle?)</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, If person A is stealthed and person B doesn't know they are there...<br /> --Person A performs an ambush on person B.<br /> --A and B roll Join Battle.<br /> -----If A wins, they Ambush B (0 Defense for B)<br /> -----If person B wins, they get to roll a Perception + Awareness against A's Stealth roll to notice A.<br /> ----------If A beats B, then A's attack becomes a Surprise Attack (-2 Defense to B)<br /> ----------If B beats A, then B is aware he is in combat and A's attack is normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T20:53:50-08:00","id":757863,"title":"","content":"You lose 3 initiative for missing on a decisive attack if you have more than 10 initiative, and certain supplemental/simple charms have initiative costs. Also, Solar Dodge and, to a lesser extent, Solar Melee. There's also a couple of tricks in Martial Arts, notably, Doe Eyes Defense Mastery. That opens up a much larger margin for Black Claw Form and Crane Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1581,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","user":"tonberrian","date":". 11-06-2015, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T05:10:19-08:00","id":758448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=757863#post757863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You lose 3 initiative for missing on a decisive attack if you have more than 10 initiative, and certain supplemental/simple charms have initiative costs. Also, Solar Dodge and, to a lesser extent, Solar Melee. There's also a couple of tricks in Martial Arts, notably, Doe Eyes Defense Mastery. That opens up a much larger margin for Black Claw Form and Crane Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think DED would trigger it? The condition says your enemy has to drop below your Initiative - does it count if most of the change is you going <i>up</i>?<br /> <br /> Yeah, Solar Dodge is the big, obvious source - it's just weird that the tree itself contains so few options to trigger it. If I want to pop, say, Snake, I mostly have to do Snake-ish things - and in general, &quot;reduce someone else's Initiative below yours&quot; is a lot easier than &quot;let them reduce it themselves.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T05:13:19-08:00","id":758452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=757425#post757425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I recall correctly, If person A is stealthed and person B doesn't know they are there...<br /> --Person A performs an ambush on person B.<br /> --A and B roll Join Battle.<br /> -----If A wins, they Ambush B (0 Defense for B)<br /> -----If person B wins, they get to roll a Perception + Awareness against A's Stealth roll to notice A.<br /> ----------If A beats B, then A's attack becomes a Surprise Attack (-2 Defense to B)<br /> ----------If B beats A, then B is aware he is in combat and A's attack is normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a reasonable interpretation of the rules, though it's a little bizarre - how does B winning Join Battle alert him to A's presence, given that he still can't see through A's stealth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T05:53:59-08:00","id":758478,"title":"","content":"I believe it goes like this:<br /> <br /> --<i>Person A performs an ambush on person B.<br /> --A rolls stealth, B rolls awareness.<br /> ----If B wins, no ambush is possible. Battle proceeds without stealth considerations after Join Battle.<br /> ----If A wins, ambush is possible. Proceed to Join Battle.</i><br /> <i>--A and B roll Join Battle.</i><br /> <i>-----If A wins, they Ambush B (0 Defense for B)</i><br /> <i>-----If person B wins, then A's attack becomes a Surprise Attack (-2 Defense to B)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":894,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","user":"Skeptic Tank","date":". 11-06-2015, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:46:34-08:00","id":758784,"title":"","content":"<u>Gazellecarp \u2013 er, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 3<br /> Armor: None.<br /> Weapons: War fans, whips, improvised weapons, unarmed.<br /> <br /> Shtick: High-synergy style. Fight at short range with whatever is lying around your boudoir; your improvised weapons and bathrobe will be as good as real artifact tools, if not better. Mix social influence into your defenses; surprise your enemy with punishing damage, or by turning into an enormous flying deer-giraffe-gazelle-carp thing. Wait, what?<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>+1 Evasion, or +1 success to Disengage. +2 if your Appearance is higher than their Resolve. +1i if you succeed.</li> <li>Add weapon\u2019s accuracy Withering damage, or treat a mundane object as a light weapon.</li> <li>Your clothes are light armor. Spend motes for temporary bonus soak.</li> <li>Form. #2 and #3 grant artifact weapons or armor. Make attacks from Short range.</li> <li>Your weapon tags are more effective than normal.</li> <li>Decisive damage roll gains anywhere from double-10s to double-7s, depending on how many triggers are satisfied. Activated after attack succeeds.</li> <li>Bonus successes to entice your enemy. Steal 1i in combat, if you succeed. Triggers #6.</li> <li>\u2013(Appearance) to attempts to Rush, stop a Disengage, or control a grapple. Triggers #6.</li> <li>Turn into a sort of deer-giraffe-gazelle-carp thing. Yes, really. Fly. Enhance all other Charms of this style in substantial ways. Fade from reality if you take any damage to your -4 level. Yes, this means you\u2019re dead.</li> </ol><br /> *snerks* This picture of the lady zapping the guy in armor does not <i>have</i> compression issues. This picture <i>is</i> a compression issue \u2013 it looks like it was blown up from a thumbnail.<br /> <br /> Again, Demure Carp Feint (#1) is pretty unimpressive in its base form. Actually, I\u2019ll go one better there \u2013 if you\u2019re an Exalt, it seems like there is almost <i>no</i> reason to use the base form, here; it\u2019s 3m for a bonus you could buy for 2m. (I suppose if you think the 1i is worth the extra mote and the Charm pick?) The high Appearance version is better, but I\u2019m not instantly wowed.<br /> <br /> At a glance, the only benefit of the \u201cmake a weapon\u201d function of Elegant Weapon Repertoire (#2) is to gain access to various tags \u2013 your hands, after all, are <i>already</i> mundane light weapons, so you aren\u2019t gaining much there. I can\u2019t tell how useful the tags are, since we haven\u2019t gotten to that part of the book yet. Again, though, not enormously impressed yet.<br /> <br /> Pearlescent Filigree Defense (#3), on the other hand, is <i>so</i> much better than the Solar armor-donning Charms. 1m Reflexive? Yes, please.<br /> <br /> Ahhh, and we get to the form (#4), and some things make sense \u2013 on-tap artifacts for a handful of motes are a much better use of the preceding Charms, and the focus on Disengaging makes better sense for a fighter who can hit from range. Okay, that\u2019s at least a little bit mollifying.<br /> <br /> Flurry of August Leaves (#5) says it \u201cenhances\u201d an attack \u2013 but the Charm is Simple; shouldn\u2019t this be \u201cprovides an attack with enhanced\u2026\u201d? Either way, again, EWR looks better in hindsight \u2013 we have at least some sense of what to do with those tags. And some of them are pretty excellent \u2013 the Shield power, for instance, is basically a turnlong non-Charm +2 Defense. Unraveling Loose Threads is, again, strictly better than Snake\u2019s armor bypass \u2013 cheaper, longer-lasting.<br /> <br /> Vindictive Concubine\u2019s Pillow-Book (#6) is a vicious little Charm; the late-step activation means you can, potentially, double your Decisive damage as a surprise. It\u2019s not cheap, but, y\u2019know, <i>double damage after hitting</i>. There\u2019s a lot of overlap between these Charms, where they play better together than they do apart \u2013 I wasn\u2019t sold immediately, but they\u2019re growing on me.<br /> <br /> All right, having finished the style, I have much more positive reactions than I did at the start. Everything about Dreaming Pearl works together, much like Black Claw \u2013 rather than separate powers, many of these effects are only useful in conjunction with each other. That still makes the first 30 XP or so pretty painful of an investment, but by the end, you\u2019ve got a nasty package put together. Your only real defense is being at Short range, though; you have some tools to hold enemies away, but anyone who can close in despite that (or, for that matter, <i>shoot you</i>) is going to cause problems. The pinnacle effect (#9) makes all of the earlier stuff even better (and, you know, is hilarious \u2013 this is one of Dr. Moran\u2019s, once upon a time, isn\u2019t it?), but with a steep risk \u2013 I wouldn\u2019t even consider going into this form off the \u201call my -2s are full\u201d trigger unless I was sure I was dead anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Steel Devil Style</u><br /> <br /> Essence to Master: 3<br /> Armor: Light, medium, and none.<br /> Weapons: Dual-wielded swords only.<br /> <br /> Shtick: Store Initiative in your second sword, using it to boost damage. Unleash massive area attacks from inside a superior defensive form, chaining into enormous overwhelm-the-target\u2019s-Defense combos.<br /> <br /> Okay, before we get started: Sidebar explains that you keep a stock of Initiative in your offhand sword; this is called your <i>Charge</i>. You can move (2 or Essence)i into your sword whenever you land a Withering hit, to a max of (Dex + Essence).<br /> <br /> Charms:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>+(2 or Essence) successes to a Join Battle roll. You can move Initiative to Charge. +1 Charge if you rolled highest.</li> <li>Make a Withering attack. If you roll enough extra successes to hit the target again, add (Dex + Charge/2) to damage.</li> <li>When using #2, if you roll enough successes to hit the target a third time, increase bonus damage to (Dex + Charge).</li> <li>After using #2 or #3 to deal significant damage, make a reflexive Decisive with bonus successes, spending only the Initiative you collected by using #2 or #3.</li> <li>Form. +2 to your Charge capacity. +1 to your Charge capacity per unique opponent you Crash. No penalties to your off-hand attack. #2 and #4 are cheaper.</li> <li>+1 success on a Rush per point of Charge spent. If Rush succeeds, Charge is refunded.</li> <li>After successfully using #6, if the opponent retreats, make a Decisive that hits all enemies in front out to Medium range, with damage equal to your Charge. Does not expend Charge.</li> <li>Form. +2 Parry. Your Parry cannot drop below 2. If you do not attack on your turn, you may make Decisive counterattacks with a mix of Charge and initiative.</li> <li>Spend Charge after an attack hits to add extra bonuses to your Parry.</li> <li>After using #8 with at least 3 Charge left, reflexively Disarm your enemy. If successful, use #7.</li> <li>As per #4, but spending Charge instead of Initiative.</li> <li>On using #11, +1 Charge, and use #3 reflexively with bonus damage. If Solar, this activation of #3 allows a repeated use of #4 or #11.</li> <li>Fuse #5 and #8.</li> </ol><br /> I was initially going to complain that Double Attack Technique (#2) needs to explain how it works with Onslaught - but then it does! And opens new questions, because the target is apparently suffering from Onslaught penalties before we\u2019ve even finished comparing attack successes to Defense. Does an attack benefit from <i>its own</i> Onslaught penalty? When do these things go into effect? And what if I use, say, Dipping Swallow Defense \u2013 do I need to reactivate it for the \u201csecond\u201d attack, or does one application persist? Can I counterattack them individually?<br /> <br /> I am fairly sure Steel Devil Form (#5) is the second place the rules mention a penalty to your off-hand attack; the only other place is the ambidextrous merit. In other words, the only places the rules acknowledge there <i>is </i>an offhand penalty is when they\u2019re getting rid of it. Why would I even care that there\u2019s such a penalty? 2e\u2019s Rate is gone \u2013 there\u2019s no impetus to attack with anything but my main hand.<br /> <br /> Picture of the Steel Devil stylist looks pretty cool, but I\u2019m more interested in that skull-thing behind him.<br /> <br /> Sonic Slash (#7) is kind of ridiculous \u2013 it hits all enemies out to medium range, as long as they\u2019re in front of you. Okay, first \u2013 in a line, in front of you? In a 180-degree arc? Second \u2013 <i>maps</i>, game. Third \u2013 wow, that\u2019s potentially a <i>very</i> large, reusable Decisive that doesn\u2019t expend your Initiative; as far as I can tell, it also doesn\u2019t expend your Charge. True, your enemy has to retreat to trigger it, but if he does\u2026 good grief. Combine with those Athletics \u201cmultiple follow-up moves\u201d Rush enhancers for extra pain \u2013 but honestly, a multi-target no-reset Decisive seems like it\u2019s plenty of pain already.<br /> <br /> Oh! Or we could use Iron Lotus Unfurling to (1) make it so we never have to pay for Excellencies, and (2) reflexively pop Sonic Slash with bonus dice at reduced cost. This is starting to feel a little bit ridiculous. The early Charms of this tree didn\u2019t impress me; how often do you roll 3x your enemy\u2019s Defense on a meaningful foe? But these later effects\u2026 late-step, practically-unlimited Parry boosting is <i>huge</i>; I really wish the rules were clearer on how this interacts with, say, Fivefold Bulwark Stance. This is a substantially better defensive power than Drifting Leaf Elusion, which caps at, effectively, +1 Evasion. That you can follow that up by Decisively striking every enemy out to Medium range at no Initiative cost just starts to get absurd. This style has both offense <i>and</i> defense comparable to the most offensive and defensive styles so far; Sonic Slash looks like it\u2019s in the same playing field as Righteous Devil, and Iron Lotus Unfurling compares well with Crane or Snake.<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s still going! Steel Devil <i>also</i> gives two different Form Charms, which can then be fused into a single Form Charm that is, yes, strong offensively (more Charge) and <i>really</i> strong defensively (+2 Parry is a better Defense buff than literally any other style gets).<br /> <br /> This just feels too good to me. Just\u2026 way, way too good. The pre-form stuff is not great in meaningful fights, but it\u2019s cheap and can pile on Onslaught penalties; the later stuff is just kind of ridiculous. Steel Devil seems like it is far and away the strongest style in the game, <i>especially</i> against more than one opponent. Single Point had a really strong two-attacks thing going, but at least you could defend against the base form of that to shut it down. This\u2026 ugh. This thing has an infinite-as-long-as-you-have-motes combo that you can chain from inside your +2 Defense Form, backstopped by a late-step Parry booster that, hey look, also combos into a 3m Decisive against everyone out to Medium range at no Initiative cost. That seems completely out of line for the rest of these styles.<br /> <br /> Okay, martial arts. Sorry to end on a down note there, but\u2026 good grief. Next time: sorcery!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T10:00:53-08:00","id":758928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=758784#post758784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would I even care that there\u2019s such a penalty? 2e\u2019s Rate is gone \u2013 there\u2019s no impetus to attack with anything but my main hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, weapon tags. E.g., you have a sword in your main hand for normal withering and decisive attacks, and a sai in your off-hand for disarming people. Or maybe a lethal weapon in one hand and a bashing in the other, so you can kill everyone you don't need, but more easily keep the guy you want to interrogate alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T11:08:47-08:00","id":759073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=758452#post758452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like a reasonable interpretation of the rules, though it's a little bizarre - how does B winning Join Battle alert him to A's presence, given that he still can't see through A's stealth?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering the same thing, but my best guess is that it's supposed to represent the target sensing the assassin's &quot;killing intent&quot;, like you see in a lot of anime. If that's the case, I think I can live with that, both mechanically and thematically. Just means that any sneak attack character you create should probably invest in some JB boosters, because otherwise they'll really risk not getting the full drop on supernatural opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:07:34-08:00","id":759124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=758452#post758452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like a reasonable interpretation of the rules, though it's a little bizarre - how does B winning Join Battle alert him to A's presence, given that he still can't see through A's stealth?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it as like this: Join Battle rolls represent how quick the two characters spring into action and make their initial attack. If B wins, then A started making his attack, breaking stealth, but B reacts quick enough to defend normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:27:34-08:00","id":759141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=758784#post758784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is one of Dr. Moran\u2019s, once upon a time, isn\u2019t it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless she did some uncredited work on the 1e Player's Guide, doesn't look like it. Though I agree it does seem like something she might have done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:34:35-08:00","id":759181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WhirlwindMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=758928#post758928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably, weapon tags. E.g., you have a sword in your main hand for normal withering and decisive attacks, and a sai in your off-hand for disarming people. Or maybe a lethal weapon in one hand and a bashing in the other, so you can kill everyone you don't need, but more easily keep the guy you want to interrogate alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's rules in the weapon section, I believe, for dual wielding. If the weapons are different, you can choose which to attack with, for access to different weapon tags. If the weapons are the same (such as, for example, the weapons of Steel Devil) you gain like a +2 bonus to clash attacks. So there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:36:09-08:00","id":759185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759124#post759124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see it as like this: Join Battle rolls represent how quick the two characters spring into action and make their initial attack. If B wins, then A started making his attack, breaking stealth, but B reacts quick enough to defend normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually makes it work for me - thank you! I still wish it was a little clearer, but that does make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackson MacKenzie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759141#post759141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless she did some uncredited work on the 1e Player's Guide, doesn't look like it. Though I agree it does seem like something she might have done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, misremembered. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:45:05-08:00","id":759198,"title":"","content":"The question then is, if B won the Join Battle against Stealthed A, can B attack A? Or are they stuck wondering which way to look for a turn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:36:59-08:00","id":759359,"title":"","content":"Sorcery time!<br /> <br /> I always wanted to like sorcery, and I never quite could \u2013 it was just too obviously a deathtrap, in 2e. Stand there with no Charms for 5-15 seconds? <i>Pass</i>. Plus there was the whole opening costs thing: buy a Charm that does nothing but enable you to buy more Charms \u2013 that\u2019s just off-putting.<br /> <br /> (Oh, hi, Martial Arts, fancy meeting <i>you</i> here.)<br /> <br /> Anyway. But the sorcery write-up back in Occult looked really promising \u2013 it obviated a lot of the costs and made sorcery look like a good buy. So let\u2019s see whether spells are actually worth taking.<br /> <br /> Looks like Circles work more or less as they did before. There\u2019s no mention of the Five Trials, just a more general \u201cSorcery is hard and will change your outlook\u201d-type statement. I\u2019m okay with that.<br /> <br /> Hm \u2013 so spells don\u2019t come out of your own motes anymore. Well, <i>that\u2019s</i> easier. And there\u2019s no fixed casting time \u2013 they take however long it takes you to come up with enough successes on an extended (Int + Occult) roll. Which can be backed by Charms \u2013 huzzah, Occult Excellencies are no longer useless! Successful casting also refunds the Willpower; combined, presumably this means a Terrestrial Circle Sorcerer can throw spells literally all day long. Finally, you get one spell as a <i>control spell</i>, which works better for you than anyone else.<br /> <br /> Okay, I love that last idea. This seems to fit in the same category as supernals: it means that even two characters with similar traits (both Dawns, or both sorcerers) will have at least some tricks that are wildly different for them \u2013 and indeed, that the other one may be literally unable to emulate. That\u2019s a nice degree of personalization, without a lot of overhead. Very very cool. In general, sorcery is winning the \u201cmost improved\u201d award so far.<br /> <br /> Countermagic is an automatic power for sorcerers! And\u2026 really inefficient; you\u2019re only slowing your target by about half. Hm. But you can also try to <i>distort</i> a freestanding spell. That\u2019s kind of cool; 2e had the problem that if a Lunar bumped into a freestanding Solar spell, there was just nothing he could ever do about it. Now, he has some chance to at least <i>modify</i> the spell, without just effortlessly destroying it. (Huh, or a spell can be negated altogether by a Working, whatever those are. So, okay, no more \u201cSome Solar trapped this city in mists eternally, and that\u2019s that.\u201d)<br /> <br /> Every sorcerer has one or more <i>shaping rituals</i> \u2013 again, a little bit of personalization for how you collect your sorcerous motes. Apparently Solars can get up to 3 through Charms, but can vaguely get others via roleplaying. That seems like something to prioritize pretty hard, if you\u2019re a sorcerer, which is perhaps by design.<br /> <br /> Mara\u2019s shaping rituals! Mara is a \u201cdeer-footed creature of shadows,\u201d yeah, and a <i>Third-Circle Demon</i>, (Edit: by which I clearly mean a <i>Second</i> Circle Demon), unless that\u2019s been changed. This section is labeled \u201cShaping Rituals,\u201d so I assume the three paragraphs for Mara are three <i>different</i> shaping rituals, and that you get <i>one</i> of them \u2013 but that\u2019s not at all unambiguous. Some kind of subheading would be really useful here. Mara is about love and darkness: motes if people love you futilely, motes if you devour someone\u2019s soul during sex, motes if you start the scene in heavy shadow. Mara-shaping apparently also unlocks some custom merits, which is a nice touch. Sorcerers get a lot of toys, man.<br /> <br /> \u2026 I mean, actually, a <i>lot</i> of toys. Occult 3, Essence 1, and one Charm pick gets you: a spell (with a turbocharger attached!), countermagic, distortion, Workings (whatever those are), a shaping ritual, the potential to learn any number of other shaping rituals, and access to custom merits (some of which seem to be free). Why <i>wouldn\u2019t</i> you take that?<br /> <br /> Lots of other options for shaping rituals:<ul><li>You can make pact with a fire lord, draining motes from fire (okay, sorcerer-slash-Righteous Devil, anyone?), motes from burnt offerings, or motes from passion. This can also let you, say, resist fire or spit flames.</li> <li>You might have seen something terrible in the Wyld \u2013 one of my players is using a refluff of this. You can gain motes instead of willpower for sleeping, motes for holding to a strange taboo, or motes for devouring emotion. You might be immune to the Wyld, or shape better in the Wyld.</li> <li>You might brew a magical elixir, drawing power from potions or asceticism.</li> <li>You might construct a wondrous artifact, drawing motes when you incorporate it into your casting, or storing motes in it long-term.</li> </ul>\u2026 This section is really badly edited; I found several mistakes per page on a casual read-through of the preceding. That\u2019s well below the quality of the last couple of chapters.<br /> <br /> Okay, the Heptagram gets at least a <i>mention</i> as a shaping ritual, which is nice. I assume the DB book might expand on this more, but it\u2019s good that scholar-sorcerer has some support.<br /> <br /> And finally we reach the spells! In the Terrestrial Circle:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Cirrus Skiff is a pet flying cloud \u2013 if you\u2019re making DBZ comparisons, yes, basically exactly like that. It\u2019s slow, and it only carries you and a plus-one, but it\u2019s still safe transport and a counter to flying enemies. As a control spell, you never have to recast it \u2013 your cloud follows you and comes when you call.</li> <li>Corrupted Words makes the target unable to speak about a particular target, which has all kinds of utility. If it\u2019s your control spell, you can even cast it with almost no visible sign, for instant suppression.</li> <li>Death of Obsidian Butterflies attacks all enemies in a straight line out to medium range with a swarm of deadly glass butterflies. It deals (Essence + extra successes) damage to any enemy it hits \u2013 which is not all that great at Essence 1, honestly; 2+ rounds of charging probably only gets you 2-3 Decisive damage. Against battle groups, it\u2019s more accurate and effective. As a control spell, it\u2019s slightly more accurate. And\u2026 well, this is interesting. The spell also permanently changes you; your shadow grows little butterflies, and your fingernails might turn to black glass in a rage.</li> <li>Demon of the First Circle lets you summon a demon (derp). Unlike other spells, this one can only be cast over a period of hours; it also appears to have no control effect. So if you pick this first, is your control slot wasted? A sidebar assures us that bound demons will obey \u201cthe letter and spirit\u201d of your instructions, but might still misbehave due to being alien creatures. Eh? Didn\u2019t an earlier chapter say they would try to tempt the sorcerer to wickedness?</li> <li>Flight of the Brilliant Raptor consumes your Initiative for a long-range decisive attack, potentially starting a bonfire in the target range band. As a control spell, it stretches to extreme range.</li> <li>Infallible Messenger lets you quickly contact anyone in the same realm of existence \u2013 one-way only, unfortunately. As a control spell, you can see through the Messenger\u2019s eyes as it flies, which seems <i>very</i> potent if what you really need is to locate your missing husband (or find out <i>why</i> he\u2019s missing) \u2013 but this also causes little cherubs to pop into existence around you randomly.</li> <li>Invulnerable Skin of Bronze is daylong no-commitment bonus soak and Hardness. Score! I can\u2019t tell whether this prevents you from wearing normal armor or not \u2013 it\u2019s a natural soak bonus, which says no, but it also says you\u2019re \u201cconsidered wearing medium armor.\u201d Can you put on armor if you\u2019re already wearing armor? Actually, wait, is there any rule that says you can\u2019t stack multiple sources of armor? P. 194 is silent on this issue. \u2026 Anyway, the armor also gives you a handful of basically-free Charms, which is pretty great. As a control spell, the armor adds (+Essence) bonus soak, <i>whether or not you\u2019re in armor</i>, at the cost of having kind of bronze-y looking skin. Woe is me, my permanent tan now also turns aside arrows.</li> <li>The Mists of Eventide are a three-round cloud of Initiative-draining poison. If a Crashed character fails to make 6 successes on his Resistance roll, he is immediately knocked out. That, uh, that seems kind of nuts. If it\u2019s your control spell, you can force the sleepers to sleepwalk through a dream of your choice. You can also fire the spell reflexively \u2013 okay, no. No Charm should give \u201cReflexive action, no cost: Target Crashed character must roll a diff 6 (Stamina + Resistance check), or he is instantly knocked out\u201d \u2013 much less \u201cor you take control of him.\u201d</li> <li>Silent Words of Dreams and Nightmares lets you try to instill Intimacies in someone while they sleep. You need a lock of their hair or similar for the attempt, unless it\u2019s your control spell.</li> <li>Stormwind Rider will create a <i>very fast</i> magical tornado to carry you and the rest of the party around. As a control spell, you jump good, but your moods cause windstorms. On balance, this looks a lot better than Cirrus Skiff, but I guess it\u2019s also quite a bit more obvious.</li> <li>Summon Elemental does not, in fact, summon elementals \u2013 instead, it creates them from scratch. Hm. This seems to avoid the old 2e problem where a Terrestrial Circle spell could, in principle, bind a Greater Elemental Dragon to your service (or at least allow it to fast-travel to you).</li> <li>With Wood Dragon\u2019s Claws, your hands are indefinitely light artifact weapons, at no commitment cost. I mean, sure, I\u2019ll take that. They can also add bonus damage to a grapple or gain any weapon tag you like. As your control spell, you can learn Evocations for them, which just sounds awesome. I like this more than Glorious Solar Saber on about every count.</li> </ol>Sorceress lady, maybe if you put some pants on, you would not have an arrow sticking out of you now.<br /> <br /> Distortion is just vicious, on a couple of these effects. Invulnerable Skin of Bronze is great, but getting stuck with a -4 Mobility penalty (that you can\u2019t turn off until the end of the day) is a lot less so.<br /> <br /> Hey, how <i>do</i> you turn off Wood Dragon\u2019s Claws? P. 466 implies that you, uh, can\u2019t. Is there anything I\u2019m overlooking that allows your own spells to be deactivated? (Edit: By dismissing it, as has been pointed out to me. Unfortunately, this raises new questions - is that Simple? Reflexive? Can it be flurried? Can any other spells be dismissed?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-06-2015, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:58:36-08:00","id":759382,"title":"","content":"Wood Dragon's Claws have a duration of &quot;until dismissed&quot;. As far as I know, there's no action listed for dismissing a spell, but at least you should be able to do so whenever you want (I'd probably rule it as a reflexive action), unless the spell is distorted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:59:40-08:00","id":759383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Invulnerable Skin of Bronze is daylong no-commitment bonus soak and Hardness. Score! I can\u2019t tell whether this prevents you from wearing normal armor or not \u2013 it\u2019s a natural soak bonus, which says no, but it also says you\u2019re \u201cconsidered wearing medium armor.\u201d Can you put on armor if you\u2019re already wearing armor? Actually, wait, is there any rule that says you can\u2019t stack multiple sources of armor? P. 194 is silent on this issue. \u2026 Anyway, the armor also gives you a handful of basically-free Charms, which is pretty great. As a control spell, the armor adds (+Essence) bonus soak, <i>whether or not you\u2019re in armor</i>, at the cost of having kind of bronze-y looking skin. Woe is me, my permanent tan now also turns aside arrows. </div> </div> </div>Vance has said in another thread that yes, it stacks with armor.<br /> <br /> It's SKIN of Bronze, and adds to your natural soak. But if you practice, say, Ebon Shadow Style, which says &quot;May not be practiced in armor&quot;, or in Snake Style which can only be practiced in no- or light-armor, then you <i>count</i> as having Medium Armor. So no, your Ebon Shadow Ninja can't stack Bronze Skin on themselves and become a stealthy juggernaut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T15:03:49-08:00","id":759403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759382#post759382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wood Dragon's Claws have a duration of &quot;until dismissed&quot;. As far as I know, there's no action listed for dismissing a spell, but at least you should be able to do so whenever you want (I'd probably rule it as a reflexive action), unless the spell is distorted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, derp. Thanks! &quot;Dismissed&quot; seems like something that could stand at least a <i>word</i> of explanation somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T15:05:11-08:00","id":759404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759359#post759359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mara\u2019s shaping rituals! Mara is a \u201cdeer-footed creature of shadows,\u201d yeah, and a <i>Third-Circle Demon</i>, unless that\u2019s been changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mara has always been a Second Circle demon. We have always been at war with Eurasia.<br /> <br /> (Seriously though, she has. She's the defining soul of Erembour.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759359#post759359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Demon of the First Circle lets you summon a demon (derp). Unlike other spells, this one can only be cast over a period of hours; it also appears to have no control effect. So if you pick this first, is your control slot wasted? A sidebar assures us that bound demons will obey \u201ct</span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">he letter and spirit\u201d of your instructions, but might still misbehave due to being alien creatures. Eh? Didn\u2019t an earlier chapter say they would try to tempt the sorcerer to wickedness?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>My reading of this is: bound demons will always do what you tell them to. They behave strangely, because, y'know, demon. The more intelligent ones may act on Defining Ties or Principles other than that of loyalty to the summoner, at times. Probably depends on the demon. But in general, I like the whole &quot;they're dangerous because they're alien, not <i>necessarily</i> because they're evil&quot;. That being said, some demons are very much of the &quot;try to tempt the sorcerer to wickedness&quot; type. See also the aforementioned Mara.<br /> <br /> As to the control spell issue, I'd allow someone who only knew Demon of the First Circle to take the second spell they learn as their control spell. But that's me, not RAW. I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759359#post759359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorceress lady, maybe if you put some pants on, you would not have an arrow sticking out of you now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit, Irked, you made me laugh so hard I now have curry on my keyboard. And, because I can't be bothered to stop nerding for petty distractions like a korma-tainted keyboard, on my fingers as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759359#post759359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, how <i>do</i> you turn off Wood Dragon\u2019s Claws? P. 466 implies that you, uh, can\u2019t. Is there anything I\u2019m overlooking that allows your own spells to be deactivated?</div> </div> </div> </div>You turn it off by... wanting to? Its duration is listed as &quot;until dismissed&quot; on p. 476, implying that it can <i>be</i> dismissed. I think this is peculiar to Wood Dragon's Claws, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":4277,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","user":"Jackson MacKenzie","date":".  formatting derp 11-06-2015, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T15:14:21-08:00","id":759412,"title":"","content":"There was a post that one of the devs made in another forum, basically boiling down to &quot;Demons that you successfully bind are loyal, but still demons&quot;, ending with the memorable line of &quot;Sure, they'll keep your son safe, and they'll kill anything that threatens him, but at the end of the day Blood Apes make for shitty babysitters&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think that it's more what Jackson says, yes. Demons will be loyal during their binding, yes. But they'll still suggest plans.<br /> <br /> If you bind Mara, she'll be genuinely helpful... But when you note that someone's bothering you, she can offer to help. And she WILL help! By appearing to your rival in the night, seducing them, stealing their soul, and maybe giving some of it to you to empower you. Because she's helping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T15:21:53-08:00","id":759430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackson MacKenzie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759404#post759404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mara has always been a Second Circle demon. We have always been at war with Eurasia.<br /> <br /> (Seriously though, she has. She's the defining soul of Erembour.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Should I look this up before posting it?&quot; I thought. &quot;Nah, she's gotta be Third Circle. She defines sorcery! I mean, I have, at worst, like a 50-50 chance - she can't be First Circle. Gotta be Third.&quot;<br /> <br /> *research fail'd*<br /> <br /> (Thanks!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to the control spell issue, I'd allow someone who only knew Demon of the First Circle to take the second spell they learn as their control spell. But that's me, not RAW. I think. </div> </div> </div>Likewise, but it seems like an easy edge case to cover explicitly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dammit, Irked, you made me laugh so hard I now have curry on my keyboard. And, because I can't be bothered to stop nerding for petty distractions like a korma-tainted keyboard, on my fingers as well. </div> </div> </div>Just as planned!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T16:11:22-08:00","id":759463,"title":"","content":"Seems to me like a spell with no control effects would be a good choice for a sorceror who wants to avoid developing a tell. Weirding people out in subtle but noticeable ways, and betraying your power to anyone who knows what to look for? Not every sorceror is going to think being able to jump really high is worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T16:12:55-08:00","id":759468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759463#post759463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems to me like a spell with no control effects would be a good choice for a sorceror who wants to avoid developing a tell. Weirding people out in subtle but noticeable ways, and betraying your power to anyone who knows what to look for? Not every sorceror is going to think being able to jump really high is worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also true of a lot of the spells that <i>do</i> have control effects, though - the &quot;tells&quot; seem to be in a minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:55:40-08:00","id":759581,"title":"","content":"Moving right along: The Celestial Circle of Sorcery!<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Cantata of Empty Voices is an immediate jump from anything we saw at the Terrestrial level. It takes a while to charge up \u2013 which is going to make it slow to pull off in combat \u2013 but at the end of that process, you\u2019ve created a mile-radius zone full of the dead. Yeesh. If you <i>do</i> want to go for combat applications, it\u2019s no slower to fire than, say, Death of Obsidian Butterflies. Hm \u2013 the control effect indicates that you normally lose control of the spell during Crash. Is that a standard rule for shape sorcery? I missed it, if so \u2013 you lose the 1wp bonus, but Ctrl-F doesn\u2019t turn up anything else. Ah, the spell\u2019s <i>perilous</i> \u2013 okay, that took a second read.</li> <li>Demon of the Second Circle: second verse, same as the first, a little bit louder and a little bit AGH HELP IT\u2019S EATING MY HEAD.</li> <li>Impenetrable Veil of Night mutes all lights within a mile, as everything is enveloped in inky darkness. This can panic armies, and at a minimum, it makes stealth pretty easy. As a control spell, this is potent, but with major tradeoffs: bonuses to stealth and movement in the dark are countered by matching penalties in the light, and your voice is permanently distorted.</li> <li>Incomparable Body Arsenal grants instant access to any weapon you want, as you turn into a weird techno-golem made of blades \u2013 I picture something a little like the Shrike from the <i>Hyperion</i> books. Your new weapon-body also doubles as heavy artifact armor; if this is a control spell, you also get Evocations! Getting distorted is bad news, though \u2013 you suffer as though from amputation until you recover.</li> <li>Ivory Orchid Pavilion grows you an instant mansion. This costs only 1wp \u2013 which means you can plausibly cast it at the end of every day at no resource outlay, giving the party portable food and shelter. Very fun!</li> <li>MAGMA KRAKEN summons a GIANT OCTOPUS made of SWEET LAVA TENTACLES to DESTROY EVERYTHING. It does not actually permanently force the sorcerer to speak in all caps (instead, it makes fire grow tentacles around you), but heck, why wouldn\u2019t you? If anyone objects: KRAKEN TIME. The kraken can try to attack multiple people at once, but really shouldn\u2019t, since it divides its successes among all of them; on the other hand, if you can assign someone 0 successes, there\u2019s no risk, I guess. On balance, this looks like a much better \u201cwreck stuff\u201d Charm than it is a direct combat effect \u2013 the combat pools aren\u2019t bad, but they aren\u2019t great, either. There\u2019s a basic problem with this spell, though: there\u2019s no actual way to pull Initiative out of it, and yet there\u2019s no way to <i>kill </i>it without making a bunch of big Initiative-consuming Gambits. A sorcerer who (quite sensibly) stands back and lets his kraken do the talking is going to find it nigh-immortal (or else subject to the gamemaster completely fudging the scene\u2019s resolution).</li> <li>Shadows of the Ancient Past lets you peer into visions of local history, as long as you don\u2019t go too far back (~500 years) or too recent (~1 year). Those\u2026 actually seem like really sensible caveats. If you have this as a control spell, you can even save the visions for later replay. Wait, why do I hear \u201cCome and Get Your Love\u201d playing?</li> <li>Travel Without Distance is a personal teleporter, out to some dozens of miles. As a control spell, you can take people with you. This is one of my favorite control effects, though I really like Shadow of the Ancient Past\u2019s effect, too \u2013 it doesn\u2019t just make the spell slightly better, it fundamentally changes how you\u2019re going to use it.</li> </ol>We get a sidebar about summoned demons and sorcerous workings. Okay, game, but <i>what\u2019s a sorcerous working?</i><br /> <br /> The illustration for MAGMA KRAKEN is everything you would want a picture of an undying lava-monster to be.<br /> <br /> And at least, we reach the Solar Circle:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Benediction of Archgenesis lets you make an <i>enormous</i> region fertile. You can\u2019t stack activations too nearby \u2013 I guess to stop That One Guy who wants to Archgenesis the entire south? There are also some interesting hooks about it potentially depleting the soil. This is fun, but I wish there was a system that things like \u201cmassive amounts of food, suddenly\u201d could actually hook into. As a control effect, you can cast the patches closer together; you also get that \u201cplants spring up under your feet\u201d thing, so good luck with the secret identity. And \u2013 and then we literally switch font sizes mid spell, what the heck.</li> <li>Death Ray is\u2026 descriptive, I guess, if a little out-of-genre as a name; the description says \u201cyour conjoined hands [turn] into a channel for violent energy,\u201d but I suppose calling it \u201cKi-Ko-Ho\u201d might have caused a few problems. The spell says it adds your Willpower and extra successes to raw damage \u2013 okay, but what\u2019s the base for the damage? It <i>looks</i> like your Initiative, but earlier spells (i.e., Flight of the Brilliant Raptor) were explicit about that. Hitting anyone with the spell is likely to knock them out of range of it, unfortunately \u2013 but the spell gradually extends its range, until you\u2019re zapping everyone in a line out to six bands away. That\u2019s <i>stupid </i>far; this is a spell that can nuke castles from literally three times as far as they can fire back. As a control spell, you also get motes for killing people with it, just in case you had any concerns about it shutting down early.</li> <li>Demon of the Third Circle is as the name suggests; there\u2019s nothing to actually do with this spell, unless the book actually includes a Third Circle demon. This is probably the poster child for \u201cPCs solve a problem in a fashion worse than the actual problem.\u201d</li> <li>Rain of Doom melts an entire city. As a control spell, it becomes <i>mobile</i>; also, you\u2019re now bad at any social influence that doesn\u2019t involve threatening to melt someone\u2019s city. (Really.) Welp, that\u2019s a thing.</li> </ol>SORCEROUS WORKINGS! Well, it\u2019s nice to know that these actually do exist\u2026<br /> <br /> Sorcerous workings are maybe the coolest thing so far, and definitely my favorite new subsystem. If you\u2019re a sorcerer, you can try to permanently alter the world as a sort of one-off thing that\u2019s not really worth a spell of its own \u2013 turning your hair into snakes, say, or making Howl\u2019s Moving Castle (which is all-but namedropped as the example Working). Doing so requires three steps. First, figure out your <i>Ambition</i>, i.e., roughly how powerful the thing you want to do is (and so how many successes you\u2019ll need on an extended roll). At the low end, an Ambition 1 Terrestrial Working can do some major earthmoving; at the upper end, an Ambition 3 Solar Working is, well, the Salinan Working: universe-wide permanent reality edits.<br /> <br /> Second, figure out how much <i>Finesse</i> you want \u2013 that is, how much fine control over the results. The more control you give up, the easier each individual roll is, but, uh, how much wiggle room are you willing to give your new snake-hair?<br /> <br /> (There are rules here for botching a Working. Game, I\u2019m going to roll every single die I can scrape together, here, plus a Willpower \u2013 I\u2019m not going to botch.)<br /> <br /> Finally, you look at your <i>Means</i> \u2013 the tools to help you accomplish your goal. See, you can\u2019t just declare a Working: you have to actually do stuff in the world to make it happen, <i>which means</i> other people have a chance to do stuff to <i>stop</i> it from happening. Cue instant plot generation to stop the Deathknight for ripping a hole between Yu-Shan and the Mouth of the Void, or whatever. You get a base of 5 rolls to make your Sorcerous Working (representing 5 weeks of effort) before you have to give up on it, but with appropriate Means, you can add more rolls before the deadline. Anything that logically would help, <i>does</i> help: if you have relevant Abilities, or Charms, or spells, or powerful allies, or extra time, or exotic materials\u2026 well, all of that just made your time limit easier. This is gorgeous: it\u2019s a broad, flexible set of guidelines that still provides mechanical support for doing exactly the sort of things that make sense to do, while generating storylines for either the sorcerer or his opponents. This is a great system; I only wish I saw this design applied elsewhere in the game.<br /> <br /> There are some nice follow-up notes: desperate/crazy sorcerers can try to perform almost-uncontrolled workings beyond their normal limit (hi, plots!), and anyone near an ongoing working can feel its presence and general effect (hi again!).<br /> <br /> <i>Why would anyone not be a sorcerer?</i> This is a wonderful sentence to type.<br /> <br /> The section on Howl\u2019s Moving \u2013 I mean, <i>Ivory Eyes\u2019s Mobile Fortress</i> starts three sentences in a row with the word \u201cHowever.\u201d Guys.<br /> <br /> (Are there a lot of font changes through this chapter \u2013 like, the text suddenly getting smaller for a few lines \u2013 or is it just me? Also, really starting to hate those blood-spatters that overlap the bottom line of text in this chapter.)<br /> <br /> If there\u2019s one problem I have here, it\u2019s not actually in the Working rules themselves \u2013 it\u2019s in the probabilities they assume. Say you want a Finesse 5 Solar Ambition 3 Working \u2013 that\u2019s 75 successes, losing the first 4 successes off each roll. Even as a Solar with a maxed-out pool of 21 dice + stunt + Willpower, I\u2019m only averaging ~12.5 successes a roll, netting 8 \u2013 I need to extend my Means to 10 to have better than 50/50 odds of success. That\u2019s a lot of plotting I\u2019m going to need to do.<br /> <br /> \u2026 Unless I activate Fate-Shifting Solar Arete on each of those rolls. Which I <i>can</i>, upping my average results to &gt;21 successes per roll. Now even the base Means 5 is enough for a likely success.<br /> <br /> The above note is not original to me, but I think it\u2019s an important observation: FSSA breaks the game\u2019s expected probability curves<i> everywhere those curves exist</i>. It is <i>the</i> best Craft, Sorcery, or Wyld-Shaping aid in the game.<br /> <br /> We close with a section on Thaumaturgy, which is\u2026 eh. Okay, so in 2e, Thaumaturgy was a sort of magical science practiced by shamans the world over. It\u2019s kind of weird, one-off miracles now, for those weird, one-off miracles that can\u2019t be covered by sorcerous merits or Wyld mutations or Working side-effects or divine parentage or minor Exigence or you get the idea. But these powers are so, so trivial, and they\u2019re so absurdly rare on top of that. Like, there\u2019s a \u201cStart a campfire\u201d power; it hasn\u2019t been seen in ten years. Well, then, <i>who cares</i>? What am I meant to do with that? It\u2019s rare enough to not inform the setting, and it\u2019s not like the Second Coming of Campfire Guy is going to shake up the houses of power. Another power lets you spend 1wp to break one loaf of bread into two. Would you take that power, if it was offered to your character for free? Would you use it, if you did? (Yes, obvious Jesus allusions in this power \u2013 but they didn\u2019t call it the Feeding of the Five.) Exorcism, at least, is mildly useful \u2013 but we\u2019re now two pages into something that feels like a general Occult power, and I\u2019m still not at all sure what Thaumaturgy-as-a-thing is adding to my game.<br /> <br /> So the final verdict on this chapter is mixed. I really like the shorter Charm cascades and tight theming of martial arts, though the power levels there seem to wobble somewhat, and they suffer from the lack of clarity in earlier chapters. The sorcery section needs a good beating with the edit stick, and thaumaturgy seems so far to be a waste of page count (to me!) \u2013 but the sorcery section is beautiful and enticing, and Workings are a system to be proud of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-06-2015, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T23:33:21-08:00","id":759774,"title":"","content":"Irked, you ever think of attaching your short charm descriptions to one of the community made 3rd Edition charm cascades? I think it would be a great resource for new-players and those of us who have a hard time synisizing information in non - chart form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9039-heartwood-jack","name":"Heartwood Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T02:17:22-08:00","id":759836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759581#post759581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We close with a section on Thaumaturgy, which is\u2026 eh. Okay, so in 2e, Thaumaturgy was a sort of magical science practiced by shamans the world over. It\u2019s kind of weird, one-off miracles now, for those weird, one-off miracles that can\u2019t be covered by sorcerous merits or Wyld mutations or Working side-effects or divine parentage or minor Exigence or you get the idea. But these powers are so, so trivial, and they\u2019re so absurdly rare on top of that. Like, there\u2019s a \u201cStart a campfire\u201d power; it hasn\u2019t been seen in ten years. Well, then, <i>who cares</i>? What am I meant to do with that? It\u2019s rare enough to not inform the setting, and it\u2019s not like the Second Coming of Campfire Guy is going to shake up the houses of power. Another power lets you spend 1wp to break one loaf of bread into two. Would you take that power, if it was offered to your character for free? Would you use it, if you did? (Yes, obvious Jesus allusions in this power \u2013 but they didn\u2019t call it the Feeding of the Five.) Exorcism, at least, is mildly useful \u2013 but we\u2019re now two pages into something that feels like a general Occult power, and I\u2019m still not at all sure what Thaumaturgy-as-a-thing is adding to my game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The really peculiar thing is that being a Thaumuturgist is a 4pt merit for mortals, and being a full-out Sorcerer is....5. Gee, let me think about if I want to spend that extra point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T02:22:30-08:00","id":759838,"title":"","content":"2nd Edition Thaumaturgy is, as far as I can tell, folded into sorcery, especially sorcery workings, in 3rd Edition. And why not get both? It's not like mortals get thaumaturgy for free when they get sorcery, like Exalts do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T05:49:24-08:00","id":759928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heartwood Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759774#post759774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irked, you ever think of attaching your short charm descriptions to one of the community made 3rd Edition charm cascades? I think it would be a great resource for new-players and those of us who have a hard time synisizing information in non - chart form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be happy to do so, or for someone else to do so if they want - I probably ought to go back and fill in short descriptions for the first few trees anyway. At the moment, I'm making kind of a mad dash just to get through the book, because (a) only four more days to give feedback, apparently, and (b) running a game tomorrow, and I still don't know how Evocations work now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T08:02:15-08:00","id":759986,"title":"","content":"Chapter Eight: Antagonists<br /> <br /> We get a fiction from Abyssal Wario, i.e., the Physician \u2013 huh, is this the first returning signature character? I guess not \u2013 we had Seven Devil earlier. Anyway. It\u2019s a pretty good piece \u2013 not a lot happening, but it gives a good sense of flavor and has some fun black humor with the banality of evil: \u201cWho would have known that practicing black magic would involve so much cobbler\u2019s twine?\u201d The illustration is competent, but uninspiring. Unfortunately, this chapter continues the trend from those previous: no mortals with speaking parts here. (I don\u2019t believe the last chapter had any, either, though it had some off-camera who were theoretically important.) The fiction is selling me a world where mortals are setting, not actors \u2013 that\u2019s going to be a hard impression to shake.<br /> <br /> Actual chapter text! We have a new quick characters system, which is one of the much-ballyhooed features of the new game. It boils down to assigning Essence, Willpower, and some basic die pools \u2013 no stats, just guidelines for how big to make different pools. For something like a mortal opponent, this is probably plenty; heck, it may be overkill. The actual magical powers involved seem to still be largely a matter of \u201cmake something appropriate up,\u201d supplemented by some specific examples \u2013 which, that doesn\u2019t feel all that much better than just having full sheets. Still, for some folks this will probably be a big help; it\u2019s not really my thing, but it seems to do its job about as well as is possible in a system based around thousands of independent rules exceptions.<br /> <br /> We open with some mortal antagonists. There\u2019s an odd thing here where some antagonists get to be specific examples (the medium infantry example is a lady named Rain Plum), where others are just generic summaries \u2013 it\u2019s a little funny when the text abruptly switches from one to the other. (This is one of those places where a sidebar feels like it would be appropriate, honestly.)<br /> <br /> The mortal stats don\u2019t impress that much \u2013 I mean, mortals, but still. The elite soldier has a Withering pool of 11, which will probably actually hit fairly often, but most of the weaker examples are throwing around seven dice \u2013 that\u2019s not even meaningful opposition for the (brand new!) players I have. I get the sense that these examples are trying to do double-duty as worldbuilding, but still \u2013 four pages of perfectly vanilla mortal antagonists?<br /> <br /> Ahh! Okay, I was not expecting the illustration of the bright yellow snake-lady. I\u2019m not sure what it is that bugs me about this piece \u2013 it\u2019s not just her face, but the merchant guy looks off, too. The next page makes up for this by giving us the fogshark; I am pretty sure my players still don\u2019t know what Sidereals are, but they all know Fogshark. Apparently the fogshark carries an \u201cInterregnum sword\u201d \u2013 ah, this must be one of the places where the text is hidden behind the illustration.<br /> <br /> We see again one of the sample spoiler characters: Kina, the hungry ghost with the misfortune of still being alive. I respect the goal here, but we\u2019re more than a paragraph into this odd exception before we know what the base case looks like \u2013 this is a rough introduction if you\u2019re new to the world.<br /> <br /> There are a <i>lot</i> of ghosts in this section. With a lot of unique powers, which is nice \u2013 I feel like I could hack together a spirit-enemy (or just an NPC) from what I\u2019m seeing.<br /> <br /> Black Breath of the Abyss is one of the first Eclipse-tagged powers I\u2019ve seen, and it\u2019s <i>mean</i>: everyone living out to medium range is struck blind. Solar animas dispel the effect, which is great if you\u2019re a Solar, but for anyone else this is pretty crippling.<br /> <br /> The Nephwrack is pretty sweet \u2013 this is a cool boss for a party at about the E1-2 range, depending on their composition. He\u2019s got a number of really nasty unique powers, but my feel is that he\u2019s going to have a hard time crossing \u201cthe Excellency line\u201d \u2013 that is, unless he\u2019s supplemented by a large number of minions, he\u2019s just going to have trouble actually connecting with an Excellency-equipped party.<br /> <br /> We get some basic rules on spirits \u2013 good! Divine immortality is discussed, as well as a few standard spirit Charms \u2013 that\u2019s a good space-saver. Measure the Wind is mentioned; it detects Exalts (the first power so far to do so) but fails automatically against magical disguises (good).<br /> <br /> Hm. The dogs of unbroken earth are gods now, not elementals. Wonder why. New Eclipse Charm: sense when intruders enter an area claimed by a dog. Hmkay \u2013 that\u2019s a bit less impressive.<br /> <br /> The field god gets us another Eclipse Charm: grow a bunch of wheat instantly, for 10m1wp. Excuse me, <i>two</i> powers: another lets you spend 30m1wp to harvest a field in a day. Okay, we\u2019re not trending in the direction I\u2019d hope, here.<br /> <br /> The storm mother gets us an Eclipse power to generate a storm, which is still kind of ho-hum \u2013 but it also lets us call down lightning. I\u2019m not sure how great that power is in general, but anything that lets a player generate environmental effects on command is worth noticing, at least.<br /> <br /> Here we go: Ahlat. Ahlat is a <i>big</i> god; from what I understand, he\u2019s probably the toughest nut to crack in the book. And justifiably so: he can trigger a second Join Battle roll at any time, which means he\u2019s going to act first; he can drop up to 10 dice on his already-quite-accurate attacks; he can throw 24 dice of accuracy with double-9s on a Decisive that leaves the target bleeding to death (or just straight-out dead). On defense, he can give himself infinite soak and halve Decisive damage, spending Initiative to raise his Parry and cancel further damage, and he heals whenever he recovers from Crash. It\u2019s the offense that\u2019s the real problem here: Ahlat <i>will</i> build up to 20+ Initiative, if he wants to, and most of that is going to dump into someone. There aren\u2019t a lot of tricks to survive a load of that magnitude; Adamant Skin Technique and Heavenly Guardian Defense probably will, but it\u2019s not a long list. If you can actually weather that first big hit, he\u2019s very vulnerable to magical flurries: no Onslaught negation or flurrybreaking unless the GM feels like letting Whispering Warrior Souls give him some appropriate martial art. (Pity the party where he suddenly acquires Steel Devil.)<br /> <br /> (Actually, this is a point where Accuracy for quick characters shows a problem. No one cares if the medium infantry gets a couple more dice on his Decisive, but when Ahlat gets an extra 3 dice beyond a Solar\u2019s maximum, it\u2019s kind of a big deal \u2013 that\u2019s a huge jump in the probability of the attack actually landing. Really, Ahlat seems like exactly the kind of character that the opening of the chapter said <i>shouldn\u2019t</i> be a QC.)<br /> <br /> We move into elementals. The garda bird gives us the Eclipse Charm <i>Immolating Pyre</i>, which\u2026 seems pretty legit, actually: enemy-only bonfire damage out to medium range. That\u2019s pretty nice! There\u2019s some good plot-hooks here; the greenmaw, for instance, might as well have \u201cHit me with sticks to get treasure\u201d written on it, and the tidemare serves a clear purpose as \u201cliving submarine.\u201d (The tidemare\u2019s Eclipse Charms, which lets a Solar make pretty lightshows or move an extra range band underwater, seem a little\u2026 iffy.)<br /> <br /> We also get Fakharu, Censor of the West \u2013 that\u2019s another familiar face, and another <i>big</i> fight. Fakharu isn\u2019t going to throw the raw damage or defense of Ahlat, but he\u2019s built well for facing a large group simultaneously: he has a couple of multi-target attacks, reduces incoming damage, and has a poison breath that\u2026 I don\u2019t quite understand the rules for. First, the poison\u2019s duration is kind of absurd; ten rounds means that basically no one is going to resist it. Second, the poison says that Initiative lost becomes a penalty to resist the poison, but at the point you\u2019d actually lose any Initiative, you\u2019ve already made your resistance check \u2013 what? Fakharu\u2019s always been a good character to have around: he\u2019s sympathetic and somewhat approachable, but he\u2019s also part of the problem of heavenly corruption. Getting him on your side is one of the big neon arrows labeled \u201cStart CLEAN UP HEAVEN project here,\u201d and his Intimacies in 3e look calibrated to make that hard, but not impossible.<br /> <br /> Man, this demon picture is\u2026 not great. Why is the blood ape two stories tall and mostly bald? Why is the neomah, of all things, kind of hideous? I miss 2e\u2019s weird, alien androgynous illustration \u2013 that was a believable demon-courtesan.<br /> <br /> The array of demons here is high-utility, for the most part: agatae for transportation (and driving home just how alien demons are \u2013 they don\u2019t understand your confusion any more than you understand their weird, arbitrary reactions), erymanthoi for footsoldiers, neomah for pleasure or children, Alveua for crafting, Mara for seduction and training, Octavian for face-beating, Sigereth for ill-considered wagers. Neomah give us a Charm that grants a targeted +2 Appearance; that\u2019s pretty nice, for some concepts.<br /> <br /> I like that we get a strong sense of the default for each First Circle, as well as some variations \u2013 the offhand note that some neomah are enthralled by dance or poison suggests some fun unique characters.<br /> <br /> Erymanthoi have one of the broadest Measure the Winds I\u2019ve seen so far \u2013 \u201ctaste someone\u2019s blood\u201d is easy enough to arrange that I can picture a sort of Wyld Hunt TSA backed by Erymanthus tasters. (Not as a general thing, of course, but if they know there\u2019s a Solar in the village <i>somewhere</i>\u2026) I\u2019m glad that MtW fails against magical concealment; it\u2019s a little odd that random First Circles can say \u201cYup, that\u2019s a Solar,\u201d when even, say, All-Encompassing Sorcerer\u2019s Sight can\u2019t.<br /> <br /> We get Alveua\u2019s usual catchphrase, which name-drops both the Ebon Dragon and Erembour, neither of which we otherwise know anything about (though Ebby seems to be in the background of all the pages of this chapter).<br /> <br /> Octavian gives us an illustration, which is beefy and intimidating. None of the other Second Circles get pictures, which is kind of a shame \u2013 there are descriptions, but I miss Alveua\u2019s \u201ctiny lady with a ridonkulously huge hammer.\u201d Octavian is also, yep, a big pile of NOPE \u2013 poison fists, double Decisive damage, Withering attacks that <i>multiply</i> their damage by extra successes, and so on. His defense is similarly piled up, sporting Parry enhancers, reflexive Clashes, Disarming counterattacks, and (while not Crashed) the power to cap how much damage he actually takes from an attack. Late in 2e, I had a player test his build by soloing a beefed-up Octavian, and it was a narrow thing; I\u2019m curious to see how a rematch would go now. Binding him actually doesn\u2019t look that hard \u2013 he can\u2019t in general enhance unrolled values, so his Resolve caps at 6. As with Ahlat, Octavian does <i>not</i> have any kind of Onslaught negator or flurrybreaker; I suspect a circle with, say, Revolving Bow Discipline or a bunch of magical flurries are going to give him a bad time.<br /> <br /> Oddly, the demons are the first ones we\u2019ve seen with Principle of Motion, which makes them both more dangerous and more mobile than their base stats would indicate. (What does happen if you flurry a Rush, anyway?) It\u2019s odd that the gods and elementals <i>don\u2019t</i> have that \u2013 a deliberate design choice, or just happenstance? It\u2019s also worth noting at this point that there\u2019s almost nothing like a general spirit Excellency \u2013 the die adders we see are (1) very limited and situational, like Fakharu\u2019s \u201cadd (current Willpower) dice\u201d or Ahlat\u2019s \u201cAdd (Initiative) dice,\u201d and (2) all seem to have a minimum Essence requirement of 4.<br /> <br /> The demon spread is probably the best so far \u2013 which is good, since they\u2019re going to put in regular appearances in any sorcerer-heavy game. This section is <i>enormous</i>, which I have sort of mixed feelings about, and a GM expecting \u201cquick characters\u201d may be a little surprised when some of their choices take up nearly three pages. Still, they effectively convey a sense of individuality \u2013 that these aren\u2019t just Ancient Red Dragon #37, but they\u2019re particular beings with their own drives. This is a solid (if somewhat bloated-feeling) section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T08:52:31-08:00","id":760010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759986#post759986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. The dogs of unbroken earth are gods now, not elementals. Wonder why. </div> </div> </div> </div>I forget if it changed in 2E, but they were definitely gods in 1E.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759986#post759986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The field god gets us another Eclipse Charm: grow a bunch of wheat instantly, for 10m1wp. Excuse me, <i>two</i> powers: another lets you spend 30m1wp to harvest a field in a day. Okay, we\u2019re not trending in the direction I\u2019d hope, here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, what direction was that? Me, I quite liked the Eclipse charms, they felt situationally useful enough that you might actually buy them, but eclectic enough to not be the auto-include that Principle of Motion was.<br /> <br /> And the rapid-growth Charm isn't restricted to wheat despite the name, you can use it to create areas of rough terrain / cover in combat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T09:15:17-08:00","id":760021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The field god gets us another Eclipse Charm: grow a bunch of wheat instantly, for 10m1wp. Excuse me, <i>two</i> powers: another lets you spend 30m1wp to harvest a field in a day. Okay, we\u2019re not trending in the direction I\u2019d hope, here.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760010#post760010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the rapid-growth Charm isn't restricted to wheat despite the name, you can use it to create areas of rough terrain / cover in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who cares about combat? You have an instant Intimacy builder with any community that depends on the land for its prosperity, which is, uh, approximately most of them. I will take those Charms in a heartbeat, and I will build an empire with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T09:24:30-08:00","id":760027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760021#post760021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who cares about combat? You have an instant Intimacy builder with any community that depends on the land for its prosperity, which is, uh, approximately most of them. I will take those Charms in a heartbeat, and I will build an empire with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>THANK YOU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T10:27:04-08:00","id":760062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760010#post760010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, what direction was that? Me, I quite liked the Eclipse charms, they felt situationally useful enough that you might actually buy them, but eclectic enough to not be the auto-include that Principle of Motion was.<br /> <br /> And the rapid-growth Charm isn't restricted to wheat despite the name, you can use it to create areas of rough terrain / cover in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760021#post760021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who cares about combat? You have an instant Intimacy builder with any community that depends on the land for its prosperity, which is, uh, approximately most of them. I will take those Charms in a heartbeat, and I will build an empire with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely not angling for another Principle of Motion, and I thought a number of the Eclipse Charms were quite good. I see the point about Intimacy-building, but I could take the 8XP I'd sink in this and instead grab Terrestrial sorcery; one working later, I have abundant fields that work <i>all</i> the time rather than just when I'm standing over them. (And I'm also a sorcerer.) Or, if I'm going the Eclipse route, I can persuade the actual harvest god to do his darn job, rather than drop substantial resources on doing it myself.<br /> <br /> I think it's good to have non-combat effects, and I am absolutely fine with the Eclipse thing being &quot;more breadth&quot; rather than &quot;more power&quot; - that feels like the better way to go. If this was something like &quot;Bless a field; it's permanently more productive,&quot; I'd have no objection at all. It's purely the &quot;For my daily Willpower, I can feed no more than 12 people for one day&quot; and &quot;I blew my entire mote pool to harvest <i>one field</i>&quot; aspect that particularly fails to impress. I can see using these to win points with a village, but... I dunno, I don't feel like that's something Solars struggle with to the point where they need to invest Charms in just that. &quot;I am the Grain Emperor&quot; is a really cool idea, and something it feels like Eclipse powers should support; to me, the scale of these effects don't work well for that outcome.<br /> <br /> That said, I did overlook that scale of the rough terrain effect - thanks! That is considerably more useful than I caught on first pass in its secondary mode; I'm just not sold on it in the primary form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-07-2015, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T10:33:02-08:00","id":760065,"title":"","content":"Moving on: Wyld Things! (<i>Dum bum</i>, dundun, <i>dum bum, </i>dundundun.)<br /> <br /> We open with a handful of raksha, who are\u2026 wow, those are healthy little suckers \u2013 something like 15 HL buys even a basic cataphract some time. This is also the highest base attack pools I\u2019ve seen so far \u2013 16 dice is substantially better than even Ahlat or Octavian were throwing around. Presumably that\u2019s because it\u2019s a more accurate weapon \u2013 again, it\u2019s really starting to feel weird with these stronger enemies that there\u2019s not a Decisive/Withering pool split, because that makes them a <i>lot</i> more dangerous.<br /> <br /> Iron is noted as dealing aggravated damage to the fae, but who cares? It\u2019s not like there\u2019s soak to bypass at that point. (Iron <i>does</i> seem to work better against some raksha magic, which is nice.) The raksha gets a power to sub your Resolve for your soak, which, <i>that\u2019s</i> a game changer for 3m \u2013 and then we get this odd stand-in where appropriate Intimacies can pull the job that Valor used to do. This feels awkward \u2013 nothing in the Intimacy rules suggests that my brave hero will get in trouble without an actual Intimacy of bravery (instead of, say, love for the people and places he wants to protect). The big limitation here is that the fae have no standard die-adders \u2013 they\u2019re going to need to significantly outnumber a Solar in order to wear through his defenses.<br /> <br /> Hm, maybe the raksha <i>do</i> still have enormous base pools \u2013 the lorelei has Appearance 7, at least. She also has a power that removes your ability to realize something is dangerous, making possible influence that would otherwise be blocked \u2013 that\u2019s a fun, thematic power.<br /> <br /> Silverwights are probably the weakest creatures to get an effective excellency \u2013 a pack of four wights hunting together gets +3 successes to all of their attacks, which makes them substantially more dangerous than their stat line would show. Except\u2026 can you actually have a pack of four individual silverwights? They\u2019re <i>literally identical</i>, fused into a gestalt hive-mind \u2013 by the rules for battle groups, more than two of them automatically glom together.<br /> <br /> Is this illustration meant to show a buck-ogre? Because it\u2026 kind of looks just like an ogre \u2013 no deer-heads, which is confusing in the context of the <i>other</i> two-headed thing that was just described. It\u2019s also oddly lopsided \u2013 the second head looks like a cartoon doodled onto the shoulder of the original sketch.<br /> <br /> The manticore may be \u201cthat most terrible of creatures,\u201d but it\u2019s unlikely to ever successfully sting something with 8 dice. I think this is my problem in general, here: a lot of these creatures get detailed write-ups taking a page or more of special abilities, but they <i>can\u2019t actually hit</i> a player with a decent starting statline \u2013 not unless a led battlegroup of manticores falls on the party, or something. And that\u2019s before we get to actual Charms \u2013 realistically, even a single Solar with 4s in his stats should be able to hold off two or three of these creatures long enough to Crash one and bisect another just off his Excellencies. So, again, who are these detailed statlines for? What threat are they meant to offer, that justifies how much pagecount they\u2019re eating?<br /> <br /> \u2026 Well, here\u2019s a section where the answer should be obvious: The Exalted. We get Essence calculations: Solars win the mote-pool war, of course, though Sidereals\u2026 okay, what in Sam Hill? Sidereals <i>lose</i> personal motes between E1 and E2? That can\u2019t be right. Lunars actually start out well ahead of Solars in terms of total motes, and then gradually fall behind, which is kind of an odd set-up, but sure.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded lose their old half-cost Excellencies; now they pay the same rate as Solars, to a lower die-cap. But\u2026 huh. They <i>gain</i> the ability to spend 1wp for a late-step reroll. That\u2019s <i>huge</i> \u2013 a DB who misses you by only one success can cash in to close the gap, while one who fell several short can cut his losses. The Dragon-Blooded anima flux is back, but any level of armor blocks damage from it \u2013 sorry, martial artists.<br /> <br /> The first Dragon-Blood example is\u2026 E1, really? That\u2019s kind of sad, but I guess he\u2019s starting character opposition. We get some sample Charms for each of the Exalts here \u2013 homebrewers, ahoy! \u2013 which is good, since this is the first real opportunity to calibrate how Solars stand out. And\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026 and that\u2019s a power costing 6m and your full anima that only grants +1/2 success on a Decisive roll. What? Why would you \u2013 what? I guess it\u2019s more useful on a Withering attack, but that Decisive effect passes \u201csad\u201d straight on into \u201cborderline useless.\u201d There\u2019s a 2m effect right afterwards with <i>the same or better </i>effect on your Decisive pool. This does not seem exceptionally well balanced, so far. Is the balance factor here a late-step activation? That\u2019s not clear, if so.<br /> <br /> Ooh, we get chunks of the Elemental Dragon styles here \u2013 that\u2019s a nice bonus. I wish these DB Charms included a \u201cfor characters of this Essence\u201d note the way the spirit Charms do. Fire Dragon Form looks like the most vicious of these \u2013 slower enemies take -2 to their Parry as an Onslaught penalty. (Fire Dragon Form + Solar Brawl?)<br /> <br /> Critiques aside, it is <i>really nice</i> to have some Charm guidelines here, especially since we\u2019re probably\u2026 what, a year and a half or more out from having any of the old Exalt types other than DBs?<br /> <br /> Huh. Lunar Excellencies are <i>substantially</i> changed; with a stunt, the Lunar die cap now becomes (Attribute + other Attribute). That\u2019s Solar-level, despite a base that\u2019s lower than Dragon-Blooded die-adders. Interesting.<br /> <br /> There is a Lunar dude tearing it up, here. Interestingly, he only has a very small, crescent-shaped tattoo pattern on his chest \u2013 is he casteless (probably not; it\u2019s a crescent moon tattoo), or are the tattoos no longer full-body affairs, or\u2026?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s hard to get the flavor of most of these Lunar Charms, but there is one that lets the Lunar rush better against a wounded enemy. That\u2019s a nice touch. There\u2019s also a promise of at least temporary form-theft without murder, which, yes, please and thank you. (If you don\u2019t already <i>know</i> about the \u201cmust eat people\u201d thing, I suspect it\u2019s easy to mistake \u201ctake the heart\u2019s blood\u201d for something more poetic than it actually is.<br /> <br /> Why is \u201cTHE SIDEREAL EXALTED\u201d in a smaller, less obvious font than the sub-heading \u201cESSENCE\u201d a few lines down?<br /> <br /> The Sidereal Excellency is\u2026 okay, so, let\u2019s talk probability. In 2e, the Sids had a die cap of (Essence), which they could (like all Celestials) render free by using an Infinite Mastery. They could <i>also</i> buy down their TNs from 7 to 4, which meant each of those few dice was more efficient \u2013 but there was no discount on the buy-down, unless I\u2019m misremembering. So at Essence 4, a 2e Solar could drop 23 dice, averaging 11.5 successes, for free; a 2e Sidereal could only muster 17 dice, for 8.5 successes, for free, but could do 13.6 dice if he dropped 3m on it. Since 3m was also the cost of a perfect, not such a big deal.<br /> <br /> So, here we are. <i>Nobody</i> gets Infinite Masteries anymore. At E4, a Solar drops 21 dice, for 11.5 successes, but it costs him 10m to do so. At E4, a Sidereal drops 15 dice, for 12 successes, but it only costs him 3m. At equivalent mote costs, with identical base pools, the Sidereal <i>substantially </i>beats the Solar for raw output at any Essence rating; from E4 onward, he also caps out higher. (If we\u2019re looking at, say, Withering pools, this happens a lot earlier.) That\u2019s kind of bothersome.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously, we only have a tiny piece of the picture right now, but one way or another, this power is a <i>much bigger deal</i> than it was in 2e \u2013 currently, it makes the Sidereals king of the dicewhompers, in terms of sustainability at an absolute minimum. An E4 Sidereal who wants to hit you with his Decisive <i>will do so</i> a majority of the time, and he\u2019ll pay less than half what it takes you just to cut his odds back <i>that</i> far.<br /> <br /> It bears watching, I guess is what I\u2019m saying.<br /> <br /> Abyssal Charms still look like they have a number of Solar mirrors \u2013 I see Dipping Swallow and Ready in Eight Directions, at a glance. Which I\u2019m cool with. The sample Abyssal in general is pretty low-accuracy; I think I\u2019d rather fight him than the sample Sid.<br /> <br /> Oh, man, this Abyssal picture. Okay, first, it\u2019s really well done: a mournful-looking deathknight standing atop a pile of corpses, his enormous daiklave buried a foot deep in one of them; around him, his army of the dead shuffles through the ruins of a city. In his hand, he holds a single, perfect red rose, which he contemplates mournfully.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s darkly gorgeous, and I really wish this was the Abyssal pic used in the chargen chapter instead of that ugly brown one they actually have. It really seems to capture that mood of \u201cthe romanticism of the dead,\u201d or whatever, that the earlier chapter referenced. The Abyssal <i>also</i> has this expression that suggests he hangs out in a lot of coffeeshops in between mass murders, talking about how tragic pop culture is and asking if he can read you his poetry, and I want to slap him more than I want to engage in awesome kung-fu duels with him. So, mixed emotions.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re still not going to admit that Abyssals are corrupted Solar Exaltations? Hokay.<br /> <br /> Liminals! The Frankenstein themes are strong here, but I feel like most of these powers could be easily refluffed for Abyssals instead \u2013 I\u2019m not catching the divide strongly. There\u2019s a Charm here that explicitly ruins one of your arms to use, which is a fun mechanic.<br /> <br /> Sidebars are still misplaced \u2013 this Liminal sidebar is solidly into the section on Exigents. Speaking of, we do get one Exigent: the chosen of Wu Jian, whose powers are city themed (though that\u2019s surprisingly broad \u2013 stealth in crowds, sex appeal like a prostitution district, the power to open any door in a city, the ability to analyze a building to learn what\u2019s happening inside.) And\u2026 that\u2019s actually it. One Abyssal, one Liminal, one Exigent. I kinda wish some of the earlier stuff was cut to make more room here.<br /> <br /> And finally, we have\u2026 animals? Guess I would have expected these to come earlier, back with the mortals. Animals have some innate powers, some latent powers that can be unlocked by training, and some magical gifts that Exalts can awaken \u2013 that\u2019s a nice tiering. It\u2019s a little funny that humans are the only thing in-setting not to get <i>any</i> edges\u2026 anyway. We get a nice spread of default powers \u2013 including, good grief, what\u2019s basically Adamant Skin Technique. My familiar can get AST?<br /> <br /> Animals are, in general, big threats to mortals \u2013 a bear, as many have noted, will mess you up if it gets its paws on you. It\u2019s the \u201cIf\u201d that\u2019s the key, there \u2013 again, Excellencies make for a big swing. My suspicion is, again, that most of these animals are going to rapidly become non-threats except in numbers that would ordinarily suggest battle-groups. (As an easy example, the death moa gets <i>huge</i> damage bonuses against low-Initiative or Crashed enemies, can gain bonus successes, and so on. But it\u2019s biggest attack pool is, again, eight dice \u2013 what\u2019s it supposed to do with that?)<br /> <br /> This observation isn\u2019t original to me, but: it\u2019s kind of a problem that we don\u2019t have actual Attribute/Ability stats for animals, given how the training Charms interact with that.<br /> <br /> Ah ha ha, raptors \u2013 er, <i>claw striders</i> have a power that might as well be called \u201cClever Girl\u201d \u2013 that get bonuses to distract on behalf of a raptor in stealth. Fabulous.<br /> <br /> Okay, this list is enormous \u2013 I\u2019ve seen close to 20 creatures, and I\u2019m only up to the Gs. Presumably this is for the sake of Lunar players? This almost feels like it might go better in their book \u2013 again, I\u2019m not sure these are going to be meaningful antagonists to use in any other context.<br /> <br /> Yep, the quoll-lion is a drop bear. Don\u2019t think I\u2019d have caught that one.<br /> <br /> I had never realized until this edition that raitons are something like an archaeopteryx, not just ravens. That is immensely cooler.<br /> <br /> I feel like about half the creatures in this list are real megafauna, and unfortunately, I just don\u2019t recognize most of them \u2013 the raptor, t-rex, stegosaur, ankylosaur, and triceratops aside. (Childhood dinosaur obsession, don\u2019t fail me now.) The dinosaur art, though, is just not doing it for me; first, I\u2019d rather have fewer crittters with more pictures, and second, the pictures that do exist are mostly wooden affairs, where the creatures themselves don\u2019t quite seem to fit with their environment.<br /> <br /> Hooray, yeddim stats! We finally find out their size: Legendary. And aw, no simhata?<br /> <br /> And oof, that\u2019s the end of chapter eight. The Exalt and demon stats are the best of the bunch, probably followed by the other spirits and the fair folk. There\u2019s waaaaaay too much overkill here for my tastes, and too many lovingly-described enemies with unique powers\u2026 that are totally useless against anything that can generate a Defense over 5. Still, if you want a wide range of choices for your familiar or animal form, or if your players are sporting combat pools of about 7, there\u2019s a lot here to choose from \u2013 it\u2019s not <i>bad</i> so much as it is just not especially <i>useful</i>. The editing continues to have some gaps in it, though not as badly as the sorcery chapter. In the particularly good sections \u2013 especially the selection of demons \u2013 the book really shines, and its presented boss-monsters look like they fill the job very nicely.<br /> <br /> One more chapter to go: Chapter 10, The Grand Panoply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-07-2015, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T10:53:08-08:00","id":760076,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of animals are pretty useful as familiars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T10:55:09-08:00","id":760078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760062#post760062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's good to have non-combat effects, and I am absolutely fine with the Eclipse thing being &quot;more breadth&quot; rather than &quot;more power&quot; - that feels like the better way to go. If this was something like &quot;Bless a field; it's permanently more productive,&quot; I'd have no objection at all. It's purely the &quot;For my daily Willpower, I can feed no more than 12 people for one day&quot; and &quot;I blew my entire mote pool to harvest <i>one field</i>&quot; aspect that particularly fails to impress. I can see using these to win points with a village, but... I dunno, I don't feel like that's something Solars struggle with to the point where they need to invest Charms in just that. &quot;I am the Grain Emperor&quot; is a really cool idea, and something it feels like Eclipse powers should support; to me, the scale of these effects don't work well for that outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, yeah. I was thinking it'd come out something like &quot;spend a week or a month in a village, and then they can make their harvest for the year&quot;. Now it sounds more like ... I dunno, &quot;generate emergency rations so the village doesn't outright starve, while you're doing something else to actually fix their problems&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T11:00:17-08:00","id":760081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760076#post760076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of animals are pretty useful as familiars.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* As noted - if you want a <i>lot</i> of options for familiar, this list has your back. But the dratted thing also stretches on for twenty pages, and I suspect you could get a lot of the utility out of a couple of pages of mix-and-match starting powers, latent powers, and magical powers. Which the opening of this section has, to its credit - the actual stat-blocks just started to drag by the end.<br /> <br /> I mean, practically speaking, we know why the benthic knifetooth or ox-dragon are here: somebody requested them as a backer critter. I don't begrudge the folks who shelled out for that the chance to have their favorite megafauna in the book, but I also don't think their existence adds a whole lot to the tome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T11:03:19-08:00","id":760082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760078#post760078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, yeah. I was thinking it'd come out something like &quot;spend a week or a month in a village, and then they can make their harvest for the year&quot;. Now it sounds more like ... I dunno, &quot;generate emergency rations so the village doesn't outright starve, while you're doing something else to actually fix their problems&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay - yeah, I could get behind that as an Eclipse power!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T11:51:14-08:00","id":760121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=759986#post759986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s an odd thing here where some antagonists get to be specific examples (the medium infantry example is a lady named Rain Plum), where others are just generic summaries \u2013 it\u2019s a little funny when the text abruptly switches from one to the other. (This is one of those places where a sidebar feels like it would be appropriate, honestly.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There were more specific examples, but they were cut for space. <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2015/10/27/exalted-3e-individual-antagonist-writeups/\" target=\"_blank\">Eric Minton posted the cut descriptions on his blog</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T13:56:04-08:00","id":760193,"title":"","content":"All right. One last push.<br /> <br /> Chapter Ten: The Grand Panoply.<br /> <br /> The size of this chapter is a bit deceiving; rather than the eightysome pages we have left, it only stretches for about another sixty (\u201conly\u201d) \u2013 the last 20 or so are backer names.<br /> <br /> New fiction starring Chejop, and\u2026 ugh. Okay, this one fails to hold my interest from the very first paragraph. \u201cHe often wondered if he hadn\u2019t lost himself somewhere along the way.\u201d The writing doesn\u2019t get any better, either \u2013 the whole page is just Chejjy Kejjy contemplating to himself. That worked with the Physician, both because it stood out from the other pieces so far, and because it was a piece with some amusing humor, but here it falls completely flat. It's also a little too fond of the passive voice: \u201cThe east was where he let his eye rest.\u201d Also, those <i>freaking period-commas</i>.<br /> <br /> (No mortals! Not even any mention of mortals doing things, I think.)<br /> <br /> Then we get to the infamously stolen art \u2013 which ain\u2019t the authors\u2019 fault, obviously, and kudos to them for taking steps to fix it.<br /> <br /> But, um. Entirely aside from that.<br /> <br /> \u2026 is Chejop Kejak secretly Rich Thomas? Like, compare this illustration with his Kickstarter picture.<br /> <br /> Two interesting notes here: first, a discussion on characters being habitually in debt, which is a nice touch, and second, a note that you don\u2019t have to have Resources 3 just to start with a suit of armor. That\u2019s an <i>excellent</i> fix; this was a really obnoxious restriction in past editions that typically lasted until about the end of the first fight.<br /> <br /> Detailed resource discussions in Exaled always make me a little bit uncomfortable \u2013 I feel like I\u2019m playing the game wrong (or, well, in an unintended way), because I track \u201cYou have 1-5 dots\u201d and then kind of otherwise ignore the system. When it starts talking about inflation rates and currency exchanges and debased silver\u2026 there\u2019s just nothing in my games that plugs into that, and I don\u2019t really know how to bridge the gap between <i>Spice &amp; Wolf</i>-style \u201cThis coin is part tin!\u201d and the order-of-magnitude pricing of a thing.<br /> <br /> Is this a picture of Swan, with the ghost lady? It has kind of his look \u2013 probably not, I guess, but it\u2019s hard to be sure.<br /> <br /> We get a note that thaumaturgy can create warding talismans. That sounds useful, or at least mortal-level valuable, and I wish we\u2019d seen more of it during the Thaumaturgy section (or am I just being forgetful?).<br /> <br /> Okay, weapons! The weapon system has been simplified <i>drastically</i>, which I very much approve of. Your weapon is either light, medium, or heavy; the distinction corresponds roughly to a 1:1 tradeoff between decreasing Accuracy and increasing damage. That seems not ideal, in this system; a weapon with +4 accuracy also gets +2 average successes, which translates to +2 damage even if we ignore that it\u2019s more likely to hit in the first place. (If we don\u2019t ignore that, its comparative damage does quite a bit better.) Heavy weapons also give a defense penalty, while medium ones give a defense <i>bonus</i>; I\u2019m feeling pretty confident that you should never, ever take a heavy weapon, here.<br /> <br /> Some (very brief) math, here: say you have a base pool of 8 and a medium weapon, vs. an opponent with the same pool and a heavy weapon. You\u2019re going to hit him (with 10 dice at Parry 3) something like 89% of the time, while he hits you (with 8 dice at Parry 5) something closer to 38% of the time. (These are very approximate numbers.) In his <i>absolute best case</i>, and ignoring the fact that you sometimes get extra successes, you\u2019ll get soaked down to 1 die exactly, while he\u2019ll be throwing 3 dice. That means you average ~.45 damage per hit, while he averages ~.57 damage - very very slightly better. If we shift that soak value by 1 in either direction, the medium weapon outperforms the heavy.<br /> <br /> My chosen pools are arbitrary here, rather than optimal \u2013 8 felt like a good combatant without being purely optimized. Try your own comparative pools and see how the numbers stack up, but right now, heavy weapons are feeling like a trap. (And this completely ignores that hitting with a Withering attack always earns you 1i, which makes more frequent hits better, or that even a tap is enough to trigger most Charms that you\u2019d stack onto a Withering attack, which does the same thing.)<br /> <br /> Okay, so if all weapons are in one of three categories, how do we distinguish them? Answer: weapons have <i>tags</i>, which mark special attack options (\u201cI can knock you back a range band\u201d) or persistent bonuses (\u201cMy minimum damage is one higher\u201d). There\u2019s no cap on the number of tags \u2013 this isn\u2019t Wulin-style \u201cnormally 1, or 2 if they\u2019re special\u201d \u2013 so it feels like you mostly want as many as you can have. That\u2019s an odd balance thing, if tags are meant to be a balance consideration at all.<br /> <br /> There follows a long list of tagged mundane weapons. None of the tags are defined until after the list, which is exactly opposite of how keywords have been handled everywhere else in the book. A number of the weapons have illustrations accompanying them, which are fine if not exceptional \u2013 no problem here; I don\u2019t need a Picasso to show me what tiger claws look like. Whips have <i>six</i> tags, which starts to feel excessive. (Edit: so does the fighting chain; the hand crossbow has 7-8.) There are, alas, no bat\u2019leth stats \u2013 er, I mean, there\u2019s no entry for the <i>spread-the-water knife</i>.<br /> <br /> If tags <i>are</i> meant to be balance features, there are some odd inclusions here: the axe/hatchet is a strict superset of the chopping sword, and is also cheaper; the same is true of the fighting chain for the seven-section staff. The slashing sword and straight sword are apparently different weapons, but have exactly the same stats, as do the poleaxe and great axe.<br /> <br /> We reach the initial set of tags. <i>Shield</i>, interestingly, gives no persistent bonuses; you can use a shield to Rush and Full Defend at the same time, at a cost of it doing less damage, but once you\u2019re actually swinging a weapon it\u2019s no help. I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s a bad thing; shields were far too good in 2e, and it looks like <i>actually being able to hit</i> is pretty important here.<br /> <br /> Hm, two-handed weapons get you a +2 Clash bonus (as does dual-wielding identical stuff) \u2013 that\u2019s not bad, but I\u2019m not sure it makes up for not having a shield, not having a free hand, having a hard time in grapples, etc. We get a dual-wielding sidebar, which <i>still</i> doesn\u2019t mention the off-hand penalty. The heck, game.<br /> <br /> Thrown weapons seem to get strictly better as weight goes up, in direct contrast to everything else. Eh? There are no heavy thrown weapons, which is also kind of odd.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a keyword indicating that some Thrown weapons can be used while mounted. Is, um, is there anything saying you normally <i>can\u2019t</i> use Thrown weapons while mounted? (Edit: also applies to Archery, apparently.)<br /> <br /> Okay, so, throwing needles. First, strictly inferior to shurikens. Second, throwing needles are <i>subtle</i> \u2013 which means that they don\u2019t actually inflict damage; they just inflict poison. So how does that work? Do you still roll Initiative, and the poison sticks if you get at least one success?<br /> <br /> Archery weapons have the same \u201cincreasing weight\u201d problem as Thrown. On balance, it looks like Archery weapons are at least as accurate at all ranges except Close \u2013 where Thrown excels, and Archery stinks. Past Medium range, you definitely want an archery weapon, though.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019m definitely not a gun guy, but why does the picture of the firewand include a lever-action, given that the weapon loads like a musket? Am I misunderstanding this? Like, literally all I know about lever-action weapons is that Arnold looks cool flipping one around in Terminator 2, but I\u2019m still pretty sure they don\u2019t fit here.<br /> <br /> Armor! Mundane armor gives no Hardness \u2013 huh, wasn\u2019t expecting that. So mundane armor will <i>not</i> stop a Dragon-Blooded\u2019s anima, then \u2013 this is good reason for no Solar to shirk artifacts, here.<br /> <br /> I like these armor illustrations quite a bit, actually. Simple, but they look cool.<br /> <br /> Artifacts next!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T14:03:47-08:00","id":760196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760081#post760081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*nods* As noted - if you want a <i>lot</i> of options for familiar, this list has your back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless your player takes a 3-dot familiar and wants a god-blooded animal, because we get absolutely no explanation of what that means, nor any examples of what powers they can have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:03:03-08:00","id":760246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760193#post760193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">heavy weapons are feeling like a trap</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in a duel between two combatants, equal in every respect, the medium weapon wins. However, when you and your buddies outnumber your enemy, heavy weapons start to look a little better. Not really sure yet how <i>much</i> better.<br /> <br /> But hey, there's a reason my iconic images of &quot;guy who is awesome in armed melee combat&quot; are almost all wielding medium weapons - the wuxia <i>jian-</i>wielder, the iaijutsu and kenjutsu masters, the hoplites, the staff-twirling monk, the musketeer in an <i>affaire d'honneur.</i><br /> <br /> The issue isn't as bad with artifact weapons, I think, since the Defense margin is smaller (1 point rather than 2) and heavy artifact weapons have an extra point of Overwhelming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:10:23-08:00","id":760251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackson MacKenzie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760246#post760246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, in a duel between two combatants, equal in every respect, the medium weapon wins. However, when you and your buddies outnumber your enemy, heavy weapons start to look a little better. Not really sure yet how <i>much</i> better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I mean, at Defense 0, the edge definitely goes to the Heavy; beyond that, I'm not sold yet - and it seems unlikely that most meaningful fights are going to get down that low on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But hey, there's a reason my iconic images of &quot;guy who is awesome in armed melee combat&quot; are almost all wielding medium weapons - the wuxia <i>jian-</i>wielder, the iaijutsu and kenjutsu masters, the hoplites, the staff-twirling monk, the musketeer in an <i>affaire d'honneur.</i> </div> </div> </div>I don't inherently have a problem with that, but the math here is not obvious; if Medium is intentionally the sweet spot, I wish the game was a little more clear about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue isn't as bad with artifact weapons, I think, since the Defense margin is smaller (1 point rather than 2) and heavy artifact weapons have an extra point of Overwhelming. </div> </div> </div>I actually think artifacts might make it worse, despite the +1 Defense - see following post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:10:54-08:00","id":760252,"title":"","content":"Okay, Artifact weapons. At a glance, you want an artifact weapon because it gives:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>+1 Accuracy over its mundane equivalent.</li> <li>+3 Damage over its mundane equivalent.</li> <li>Better Defense, if it\u2019s heavy.</li> <li>Better minimum damage.</li> </ol>Those are compelling reasons, but heavy seems even more like a trap, here. Again, compare the Medium to the Heavy user: Medium now has (throwing 11 dice vs. Parry 4) something like an 81% chance of hitting, while Heavy has (throwing 9 dice vs. Parry 5) roughly a 47% chance of hitting. That\u2019s similar to the numbers last time \u2013 but now, in Heavy\u2019s ideal soak case, Medium throws 4 damage dice to Heavy\u2019s six. In a case like that, Medium averages 1.62 damage successes per attack, while Heavy averages 1.41 per attack \u2013 advantage Medium, and it\u2019s only going to get worse from there. (Note that, even going up against a higher Defense, the artifact version of a Medium does something like 3-4x more average damage than the mundane Medium.)<br /> <br /> Plus all that was mentioned before; plus the Heavy is going to be two-handed. <i>Don\u2019t use Heavy weapons</i>.<br /> <br /> We do not get tags repeated for artifacts, which makes sense space-wise but makes me wish even more that all the tags were in one place.<br /> <br /> Huh, attunement is almost instant now. That removes an obnoxious part of the \u201cacquire an artifact\u201d process.<br /> <br /> The artifact pictures are not bad \u2013 a little World of Warcraft, maybe, but they look clearly magical-er than the Melee versions. I don\u2019t quite catch the sense of <i>oversized</i> that I would want, though. No mention of hearthstone sockets?<br /> <br /> The only artifact shield described here is\u2026 a wrackstaff? What? That feels kind of like an oversight. (Also, it seems like it makes the wrackstaff a better shield than an artifact shield would be, since it also has the Reach tag.)<br /> <br /> Aw, no non-Slow flame weapons. Well, that\u2019s what Righteous Devil is for \u2013 still, I miss that five-shot alchemical flame piece.<br /> <br /> Huh \u2013 the artifact armor gets +2/+3/+4 damage over its mundane equivalent. That\u2019s interesting. Heavy armor actually gives <i>quite a lot</i> of soak and Hardness \u2013 even at -2 Evasion, that\u2019s pretty tempting.<br /> <br /> Then we get to utility artifacts. Is there no just general gear list? I was expecting at least a table of prices for things. Several of these are familiar \u2013 and okay, good, we <i>do </i>get a mention of hearthstone bracers \u2013 but I like the traveler\u2019s staff; not a showy tool, but free food and shelter isn\u2019t an awful thing to have.<br /> <br /> Illustration: Ken, having left Barbie, has slipped into a poorly fitting Ninja GI Joe outfit and gone out to pick a fight.<br /> <br /> The Belt of Shadow Walking is <i>really</i> good: free dematerialization; free +3 non-Charm dice to Stealth. That\u2019s more than a little nuts. \u2026 Wait, hang on, no; all bonus dice from artifacts count as Charm dice. So, er, my die cap is higher with a high-quality mundane lockpick than it is with the Bracers of Universal Crafting?<br /> <br /> Hearthstones! Not Evocations? Well, whatever. Holden famously <i>hates</i> hearthstones; let\u2019s see what they look like now. We already know there are only two levels of hearthstone. Hearthstone keywords come <i>first</i>, which is right and proper. Apparently only some stones actually depend on the manse staying healthy, which is a big change; others only grow in a wild demesne. Hm \u2013 that\u2019s an odd distinction to require, and I\u2019m curious of the reasons.<br /> <br /> We get four or five stones from each element, as follows.<br /> <br /> Air:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Generate cool, refreshing breezes.</li> <li>Maintain perfect memory.</li> <li>Know one additional Terrestrial spell.</li> <li>Control the direction of the wind.</li> <li>+1 Essence for calculations when supporting a Defining Intimacy.</li> </ol>Earth:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Minimize earthquakes and collapses in a city.</li> <li>Protect all within 100 yards from the Wyld. The fae hate you.</li> <li>Turn raw earth to stone or back again. Doesn\u2019t work on buildings.</li> <li>Disable an enemy\u2019s weapon or armor by cramming the stone into an empty socket.</li> <li>Use your weapon\u2019s next Evocation.</li> </ol>Fire:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Minimize fire in the city.</li> <li>Store 1 Willpower.</li> <li>Know one additional fire-based Terrestrial spell.</li> <li>Make it always summertime in a city.</li> <li>Evocations: bonus damage on unarmed attacks; shoot fire out to short range.</li> </ol>Water:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Water in the city is always safe.</li> <li>A spring appears for the next day.</li> <li>The sea nearby is never stormy. (What happens if magic conflicts with this?)</li> <li>Evocations: bonuses to escape your bonds; successfully get away from a grapple faster; use dodge to contest a grapple Control Roll.</li> </ol>Wood:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Food keeps longer in the city.</li> <li>Negate armor Mobility penalty for jumping and climbing.</li> <li>Fields nearby produce extra.</li> <li>Commit an Intimacy to the stone; sense when someone else has the same Intimacy.</li> </ol>Solar:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>No creature of darkness can enter a home containing a sleeping child.</li> <li>An area out to two miles wide is filled with daylight.</li> <li>+1 success on shape sorcery.</li> <li>Commit 2m; gain one Evocation on an orichalcum weapon. (Is this just worse than Earth #5?)</li> <li>Learn one Charm or Evocation requiring +1 Essence.</li> </ol>Abyssal:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Speak with the dead in the city.</li> <li>Cause a corpse to rise as a zombie.</li> <li>Anyone robbing from those in the city is afflicted by poltergeists. Those apparitions are not for hurting. They are for haunting, and distraction.</li> </ol>Lunar:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>+2 Survival bonus to find food.</li> <li>Make minor appearance changes to blend in.</li> <li>Animals nearby have exceptional offspring.</li> </ol>Sidereal:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Everyone in the city is slightly lucky.</li> <li>See divine sanctums, and be heard by the gods within.</li> <li>Know one additional combat Charm.</li> <li>Hide a small city from those with hostile intent.</li> </ol>Some of these stones only seem to make sense to discover, or to use as fuel; who is the guy who is going to insist on spending chargen resources on having a Stone of Lesser Air Conditioning (Air #1, paraphrased)? Like, some of these are things I would definitely want, in real life \u2013 the Stone of Stability (Earth #1), for instance, makes your city earthquake proof! But they aren\u2019t\u2026 sexy, I guess? They don\u2019t <i>appeal</i>, and even if you did have one, you\u2019re mostly going to leave it somewhere to do its thing undisturbed. That\u2019s not bad, but it\u2019s a pretty big change from the focus of 2e stones \u2013 very few stones have any kind of combat potential. (If you\u2019re playing Make the Ultimate City Guy, though, I suppose you want as many of these as you can grab \u2013 they\u2019re definitely quality-of-life improvements.)<br /> <br /> Wow, they kept the Twice-Striking Lightning Prism (Air #5). And it even looks not-broken: only works in support of Defining Intimacies, doesn\u2019t actually factor into as many essential calculations.<br /> <br /> Okay, the Mountain-Burden Stone (Earth #4) has combat application, but only as long as your enemy has empty hearthstone slots and you don\u2019t mind wasting a Gambit on them.<br /> <br /> Ah, we <i>do</i> get Evocations! Some stones (i.e., Fire #5) apparently have built-in Evocations to learn. That\u2019s interesting. I\u2019m not really sold on the examples, though. The Freedom Stone (Water #4) used to be very nearly essential, if you didn\u2019t want to die to a grapple; now, you need to buy a Greater stone (plus manse?) for 4-5 merit dots, then spend 30 XP on Evocations, and all you gain is the ability to contest the roll with Dodge. I mean, for 30 XP, I could buy Brawl to 5 and get a grappling Charm, y\u2019know?<br /> <br /> Doe bonuses from hearthstones count against your die cap? Several here add bonuses to various pools (the Shape Sorcery bonus could be particularly nice!), but I have no idea how they stack.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s the list. It\u2019s not bad, and it doesn\u2019t look overpowered, but it\u2019s not really inspiring, either \u2013 there\u2019s nothing here where I said, \u201cYES, I want <i>that</i> for my next character.\u201d Why take a hearthstone that grants a Charm, when I could just take another Charm? Why, at chargen, do I want to have a \u201ccity gains some benefit\u201d power? These are by no means useless, and again, I\u2019d want to cultivate them if I was city-building, but they seem more like flavor than really useful tools worth multiple merit dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-07-2015, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:37:12-08:00","id":760276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760252#post760252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus all that was mentioned before; plus the Heavy is going to be two-handed. <i>Don\u2019t use Heavy weapons</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the strictly-optimal case here is dual wielding identical mediums, but you may not be able to do that with artifacts. How big of a factor do you think the +2 to Clash attacks is for dual wielding identical mediums, or wielding a two handed heavy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:47:28-08:00","id":760287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackson MacKenzie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760276#post760276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the strictly-optimal case here is dual wielding identical mediums, but you may not be able to do that with artifacts. How big of a factor do you think the +2 to Clash attacks is for dual wielding identical mediums, or wielding a two handed heavy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably depends heavily on your strategy - some builds are going to depend on Clashes for defense, and if that's your plan, yeah, you want the double-up. At Essence 1, that's an awfully big chunk of your pool to commit, though; if I wasn't going all-in on the Clash, I'd probably prefer to stick to one weapon, plus maybe a mundane buckler of some sort.<br /> <br /> (Actually, at that point, I could also see doing a single Light artifact weapon - the shield covers you for the +1 Defense, and I suspect the accuracy numbers continue to work out all right.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-07-2015, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T16:22:19-08:00","id":760320,"title":"","content":"I would say the weapon choice for optimal stats in a generic whiteroom fight is a Small Daiklave (for having the accuracy of a small weapon with the overwhelming bonus from Balanced) and a shield for +1 parry &amp; shield tag, plus ambidexterity (assuming the off-hand penalty applies to your parry).<br /> <br /> The artifact weapon that looks like it would be the strongest is also the one you get two of for taking the artifact background. Which is kind of funny. Honorable mention to Direlash for being light and having a lot of tags, but Balanced is probably still better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 11-07-2015, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T16:26:09-08:00","id":760322,"title":"","content":"Okay, Evocations, i.e. \u201cSo we heard you like <i>Bleach</i>.\u201d I really like the idea of Evocations, but we\u2019ve gone literally the entire book with no idea what they actually are; let\u2019s fix that.<br /> <br /> So artifacts have Evocations; <i>what</i> Evocations varies with the weapon, its history, and the wielder. That seems complicated, but okay. Stronger artifacts have <i>more</i> or <i>better</i> Evocations \u2013 sure \u2013 with a minimum rating of Art 3 to get any at all.<br /> <br /> Solars apparently do equally well with all magical materials, now, while other Exalts specialize. Interesting; solves the \u201cBut all I kill is Dragon-Blooded, so all I have is jade stuff,\u201d problem.<br /> <br /> We get a brief description of the five magical materials and the sorts of Evocations that resonate with each, which is nice but will probably be pretty tough to homebrew until the artifact book drops.<br /> <br /> Then we get the actual artifacts themselves. Which, wonder of wonders, are described as having a fixed number of hearthstone sockets! So how many do other artifacts have, then?<br /> <br /> Beloved Adorei, Orichalcum Daiklave<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>\u201cAutomatic:\u201d +1 Accuracy, +1 success on Withering damage.</li> <li>A successful Decisive doubles as a Read Intentions roll.</li> <li>+1 non-Charm success on targets you\u2019ve hit with #1, with a rolled 10. -1 dice to any other weapon.</li> <li>Roll bonus Decisive damage based on Intimacies revealed with #1.</li> <li>If you know Intimacies related to your target, you may destroy an undestroyable thing (the deathlord\u2019s unbreakable curse or lock, etc.).</li> <li>Heal; gain bonus Initiative; preserve your own Resolve and learn the Intimacies of those who strike you. At the end of the scene, Adorei dies.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Beloved Adorei offers, basically, +1 Accuracy just for attuning to her, which is one of the <i>very</i> few tools to cap-break in the game. That\u2019s a potent direction to go in, as 2e amply demonstrated. It\u2019s a fun artifact, in any event; I like that the sword has a personality (and, apparently, talks?), and it seems like you could build some fun plots around a player\u2019s relationship with Adorei and, potentially, attempt to revive her.<br /> <br /> Brilliant Sentinel, Orichalcum Heavy Plate<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Automatic: Enemies take -1 to Join Battle rolls (or -1 success if Creatures of Darkness); store anima levels in artifact.</li> <li>Dump 3 levels of anima to blind enemies.</li> <li>Prevent blinded enemies from attacking anyone but you.</li> </ol><br /> Moonlit Huntress, Moonsilver Powerbow<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Automatic: Gain one of various bonuses, depending on your Initiative.</li> <li>Spend 1wp for +15i; gain all bonuses from #1 for the next three turns.</li> </ol><br /> Shining Ice Mirror, Blue Jade Reaper Daiklave<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Automatic: for 2m commitment, +2 Defense on any turn when you Aim.</li> <li>When you crash an enemy, he takes -2 dice and -1 Defense until he recovers.</li> <li>+1 nonCharm bonus to Resolve vs. attempts to cow you; temporarily reduce all passion Intimacies by one step. Learn this for free given a proper trigger.</li> <li>Strike at enemy at range, creating movement penalties as well as damage.</li> <li>Inflict further penalties on anyone suffering from #2 or #4.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Man, these advanced artifact illustrations are just entirely underwhelming. Shining Ice Mirror in particular has some ugly compression lines through it. This feels like a spot for more of that eye-popping super-detailed art; instead we get\u2026 thin, simple line-drawings in a different color palette.<br /> <br /> Shining Ice Mirror is stalked by the ghost of its old Solar owner. That\u2019s awesome. And\u2026 goodness, any turn when you Aim also gives a Full Defense. That\u2019s a +2 non-Charm bonus to your Defense, and I\u2019m immediately trying to figure out how to stack this with Righteous Devil \u2013 ice sword in one hand, firewand in the other? Nah, I don\u2019t think that works \u2013 but there\u2019s got to be <i>something</i>. Maybe something in Solar Archery that applies to Melee Aiming\u2026?<br /> <br /> This is definitely my favorite artifact so far \u2013 the sword has a clear personality of wanting you to be a cold, scheming killer, and that comes through even more so than for Adorei. This does <i>exactly</i> what the Hearthstones didn\u2019t: it instantly fires my imagination and gets me wanting to run chargen, or at least drop a juicy plothook in my players\u2019 paths.<br /> <br /> Spring Razor, green jade daiklave<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>No automatic powers.</li> <li>Poison a target as per Arrow Frog Venom on a successful Decisive.</li> <li>On a successful hit, any poison the target suffers from intensifies and increases in duration.</li> <li>Targets always suffer at least one round of poison from #2.</li> <li>After three rounds of charging, improve the poison inflicted by #2.</li> <li>The target grows flowers that leach poison from him\u2026 and then inflict twice the damage leached.</li> </ol><br /> *whistles* Spring Razor does only one thing, but it does it <i>really well</i>. This is a <i>vicious</i> little blade \u2013 being poisoned is not quite as bad as it sometimes has been in the past, but those penalties will still kill you pretty dead.<br /> <br /> Freedom\u2019s Cadence, starmetal chain shirt<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Automatic: for 3m, doesn\u2019t count as armor for martial arts.</li> <li>Bonus social dice vs. an enemy you Crashed; reversed if he then Crashes you.</li> <li>+1 soak when you Evade an attack.</li> <li>For each Rush you succeed at, +1 success on future Rushes until you fail.</li> <li>+1 soak permanently.</li> <li>+1i to all allies at Short range each round as long as you flurry a dance.</li> </ol><br /> Freedom\u2019s Cadence is basically a \u201cYes, please, this,\u201d for any martial artist concept that would normally ban armor. Beautiful, but feels awfully close to a must-have, even if you never plan to dip into the Evocations \u2013 Dreaming Pearl or Ebon Shadow, say, <i>really</i> want something like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T16:46:28-08:00","id":760339,"title":"","content":"Any artifact Silken Armor works just as well as Freedom's Cadance, costs the same (4 dots), doesn't require you to commit 3 extra motes, and doesn't stop not-counting as armor in crash. So I wouldn't really say must-have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 11-07-2015, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T17:23:44-08:00","id":760357,"title":"","content":"On the Fire Dynast's damage charm. Let's not forget the withering effect converts ALL post soak withering damage.<br /> <br /> Also, I suspect the charm's 'true' text for decisive attacks is to convert [Essence] decisive dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T17:52:02-08:00","id":760370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760339#post760339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any artifact Silken Armor works just as well as Freedom's Cadance, costs the same (4 dots), doesn't require you to commit 3 extra motes, and doesn't stop not-counting as armor in crash. So I wouldn't really say must-have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, true! I missed that - but then again, if it's going to be a 4-dot artifact to make it silken, you might as well grab Freedom's Cadence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760357#post760357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Fire Dynast's damage charm. Let's not forget the withering effect converts ALL post soak withering damage.<br /> <br /> Also, I suspect the charm's 'true' text for decisive attacks is to convert [Essence] decisive dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, it's much better as a Withering effect. And that's a plausible interpretation. It was just kind of a shock to stumble across that - &quot;All this, for <i>one</i> die?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T17:52:37-08:00","id":760371,"title":"","content":"Orichalcum Hunting Hawk, orichalcum powerbow<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Automatic: Ignore visibility penalties.</li> <li>Jump one additional range band with Monkey Leap Technique.</li> <li>Hide in trees using Survival and Archery. Free Evocation once you fight a difficult monster.</li> <li>Hover while shooting enemies below you.</li> <li>Reroll attack dice based on how high up you are.</li> <li>Your anima becomes a hawk and fights alongside you.</li> </ol>Hunting Hawk wants a very specific playstyle \u2013 not just an archer, but a <i>flying</i> archer. I love the idea of having the bow come to life and support you in combat, but I wonder whether the shtick of \u201calways take off at the start of combat\u201d would get a little old.<br /> <br /> Dauntless, orichalcum lamellar<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Automatic: +4m commitment. Bonus strength for feats of strength; reduce or absorb Decisive damage, especially from battle groups.</li> <li>Temporarily reduce soak, but +1 success on close-combat Withering attacks for the scene.</li> <li>On hitting with a close-range attack, negate two points of Onslaught penalty to yourself.</li> <li>1/day, ignore all penalties from wounds or disease vs. a Crashed opponent.</li> <li>Give up soak to negate damage to you.</li> </ol>Dauntless does this interesting thing where the armor becomes less and less valuable over time as it absorbs damage, but you can regenerate that soak by landing attacks. It feels <i>strong:</i> free damage negation + scenelong nonCharm bonus successes adds up.<br /> <br /> *snerks* Black Wind looks ridiculous. \u201cIt\u2019s a big boomerang! With a little gem thingy. And some compression issues.\u201d<br /> <br /> Black Wind, soulsteel skycutter<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Automatic: on dealing Decisive damage, the blood crystallizes into a \u201cblood blade\u201d granting +1 Withering damage.</li> <li>Spawn two blood blades instead of one. Free Evocation after killing someone important in line with a Principle.</li> <li>Bonuses to Awareness and Investigation rolls in pursuit of a killer. Free Evocation after hunting down and killing a criminal.</li> <li>Spend blood blades for bonus Decisive damage. Free Evocation for killing someone important in line with a Principle <i>and</i> a Tie.</li> <li>Spend blood blades to make multiple Withering attacks. Free Evocation after gaining 5 blood blades.</li> <li>Kill a known murderer from miles away, regardless of his protections. Kill 100 other murderers to recharge this power. Free Evocation after investigating and killing a serial killer.</li> </ol>Okay, Black Wind is hardcore. I take back every bad thing I said about it, for fear that it is listening. Note that this is an <i>entirely free Charm tree</i>, as long as you\u2019re playing the right kind of character. (I know a guy who would absolutely eat this stuff up \u2013 it\u2019s a really, well, evocative design.)<br /> <br /> Volcano Cutter, red jade grand daiklave<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Automatic: free access to #2; rarely, gain 1i on a Withering attack.</li> <li>Gather motes every time you attack; spend these motes (and these motes only) on this Charm. Make an unblockable attack out to medium range; target band becomes an <i>eruption point</i>, which gathers power over time and explodes if people re-enter it.</li> <li>Consume an eruption point for bonus damage on a Decisive.</li> <li>Channel an eruption point to leap two range bands and make a Decisive, carrying the eruption point with you.</li> <li>Move all eruption points to attack enemies; create a new point.</li> <li>All eruption points explode; anyone within close range or between two of them takes 25-40L damage automatically. 1/season.</li> </ol>I absolutely love Volcano Cutter\u2019s flavor. Dude got so sick of tricksy \u201cCut it in half, the halves grow back\u201d monsters that he built an enormous volcano-forge to create the Daiklave of Everything Burns. That\u2019s a Solar solution right there. Volcano Cutter \u2013 it\u2019s the only way to be sure. The final effect here is just <i>insane;</i> anything without a perfect defense is going to die, and even those with, say, AST or HGD are going to have a heck of a time mitigating 25L. (Again, a little odd that they\u2019d do just fine if it was infinite damage!)<br /> <br /> And <i>that\u2019s it</i>. That\u2019s the panoply chapter.<br /> <br /> There are only a few pages left. We see again the story of Strawmaiden Janest, Chosen of a single field god. The editing here is atrocious, but the story is everything it ought to be: haunting, stirring, and ending with an awesome <i>heck yeah</i> moment that\u2019s only furthered by the accompanying illustration: Janest standing alone against the horde of the Fae. This is one of the best two or three pieces in the whole book, and it\u2019s the perfect note to end on.<br /> <br /> We close with a character sheet. It\u2019s imperfect \u2013 it features the Attribute \u201cMamipulation,\u201d and it requires your entire complement of health levels to be redrawn every time you gain or lose any levels. But it does recognize the need to mark, say, Withering and Decisive pools; XP and Solar XP totals; derived stats; and different kinds of soak \u2013 and no previous official sheet has. And it has room for Charms \u2013 Charms with a hilariously undersized blank for \u201cEffect,\u201d but room nonetheless.<br /> <br /> And then come pages and pages of lovely backers.<br /> <br /> And we\u2019re done. Page 657 \u2013 still uselessly centered in the middle, edged in lovely cherry blossoms, heavy with the names of the Lords of Creation. There\u2019s a metaphor in there somewhere \u2013 but I\u2019ll leave that for someone else.<br /> <br /> The end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-07-2015, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T18:28:19-08:00","id":760390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760371#post760371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are only a few pages left. We see again the story of Strawmaiden Janest, Chosen of a single field god. The editing here is atrocious, but the story is everything it ought to be: haunting, stirring, and ending with an awesome <i>heck yeah</i> moment that\u2019s only furthered by the accompanying illustration: Janest standing alone against the horde of the Fae. This is one of the best two or three pieces in the whole book, and it\u2019s the perfect note to end on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That illustration, that story, gosh dang, I love it so much.<br /> <br /> &quot;The lords of chaos signaled the advance. Strawmaiden Janest crossed the field to meet them.&quot; Fantastic. I can't help but be reminded of <a href=\"http://www.kiwisbybeat.com/minus37.html\" target=\"_blank\">this comic</a>.<br /> <br /> ...And once again, gosh dang, that illustration. Put that on the cover. Forget generic wuxia person, forget this is the Solars book and Strawmaiden Janest is an exigent, forget all of that. That picture is more evocative of what it is to be one of the exalted than nearly anything else I have seen. Just fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T18:36:01-08:00","id":760394,"title":"","content":"I love the personality that they gave these Artifact Weapons. Like how not only does Spring Razor do the Poisoning thing well, but also that most of its Evocations can only be used by people with Dex 4+, App 4+, and not hideous. Just such a prissy prima-donna, and I kind of love it for that.<br /> <br /> And Black Wind and Volcano Cutter are awesome. And so's Adorei.<br /> <br /> Hell, the personality in these is just something I look forward to building on. I've got ideas for some Artifacts. Like a Soulsteel Direlance that was forged from people who were slain by Terrestrials, to give its Deathknight owners bonuses to fighting Dragon Bloods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T18:40:28-08:00","id":760397,"title":"","content":"Very enjoyable overview! I think that when I start designing my custom artifact evocation trees I will probably make sure each charm has a free purchase condition. It seems like a great way to reinforce the artifact's personal theme and keep evocations from being too large of an xp sink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8807-galatine","name":"Galatine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T18:41:07-08:00","id":760398,"title":"","content":"Black Wind takes the &quot;Soulsteel as Absolute Justice&quot; concept normally reserved for Autochtonia and Alchemicals and brings it to Creation. I love it, and I imagine that in the first age Soulsteel was used for crafting artifacts in that way more often than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T18:58:03-08:00","id":760403,"title":"","content":"The Evocation artifacts are hands-down one of the best parts of the book to read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WhirlwindMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760390#post760390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The lords of chaos signaled the advance. Strawmaiden Janest crossed the field to meet them.&quot; Fantastic. I can't help but be reminded of <a href=\"http://www.kiwisbybeat.com/minus37.html\" target=\"_blank\">this comic</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before mousing over, I bet myself this was going to be the Minus comic with the baseball bat.<br /> <br /> (I win!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T20:05:32-08:00","id":760438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760370#post760370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, true! I missed that - but then again, if it's going to be a 4-dot artifact to make it silken, you might as well grab Freedom's Cadence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would honestly never take Freedom's Cadance on a martial artist. Maybe I'm more of a pessimist but the basic functions of it are that you're rewarded more when you're already winning (bonuses against an opponent you' ve crashed), and punished harder when things aren't going as well (get crashed and now you can't use your martial art, and if you get counter-crashed you also take penalties on your attacks).<br /> <br /> You're going to shine like a diamond untill someone who is a serious challenge has a bit of luck and then you're screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 11-07-2015, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T21:39:21-08:00","id":760486,"title":"","content":"I built a damage calculator for withering attacks. At higher Defense ranges dex still wins out in damage, but for mundane weapons (assuming I've got my calculations right), your 5 Dex, 5 strength, 5 and specialty attack combat brute vs. soak 10 is getting marginally more damage out of a heavy mundane weapon through defense 5, a brief peak of medium weapons being best at defense 6/7, and then light starts winning out. Shifting to artifact weapons decreases these thresholds by 1 (to 4 and 6), increasing soak to 15 pushes them back again. A full excellency seems to push artifact heavy into pure superiority through Defense 10 on anything less than, like, 18 soak. Overwhelming favors light weapons, increasing dice pools tends to make the averages closer together, and heavy weapons <i>really</i> like double xs on attack rolls, though the only effects that grant that in 3e available to solars as-is only do so for light weapons or grapple attack rolls <i>very</i> condititonally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1581,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","user":"tonberrian","date":". 11-08-2015, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T03:40:19-08:00","id":760593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760065#post760065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving on: Wyld Things! (<i>Dum bum</i>, dundun, <i>dum bum, </i>dundundun.)<br /> <br /> We open with a handful of raksha, who are\u2026 wow, those are healthy little suckers \u2013 something like 15 HL buys even a basic cataphract some time. This is also the highest base attack pools I\u2019ve<br /> <br /> <br /> Cut for space!<br /> <br /> <br /> oetry, and I want to slap him more than I want to engage in awesome kung-fu duels with him. So, mixed emotions.<br /> One more chapter to go: Chapter 10, The Grand Panoply.</div> </div> </div> </div>After two sessions I'm kind of having the problem you were worried about. A seriously large number of the antagonist section seems to be dedicated to showing of how far and above everyone else the PCs are, which in some respects I like because the Solar PCs should be beating up a lot of guys pretty easily, but I'm finding that a really big number of antagonists are finding my players to be just untouchable, without them even going into peripheral essence. So far I haven't pitted them up against too much stuff, but everything has been a group of essence 3 spirits or other likewise powerful foes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T08:41:48-08:00","id":760683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760486#post760486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I built a damage calculator for withering attacks. At higher Defense ranges dex still wins out in damage, but for mundane weapons (assuming I've got my calculations right), your 5 Dex, 5 strength, 5 and specialty attack combat brute vs. soak 10 is getting marginally more damage out of a heavy mundane weapon through defense 5, a brief peak of medium weapons being best at defense 6/7, and then light starts winning out. Shifting to artifact weapons decreases these thresholds by 1 (to 4 and 6), increasing soak to 15 pushes them back again. A full excellency seems to push artifact heavy into pure superiority through Defense 10 on anything less than, like, 18 soak. Overwhelming favors light weapons, increasing dice pools tends to make the averages closer together, and heavy weapons <i>really</i> like double xs on attack rolls, though the only effects that grant that in 3e available to solars as-is only do so for light weapons or grapple attack rolls <i>very</i> condititonally.</div> </div> </div> </div>This deserves a thread of its own. Great information.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I didn't realize we just finished the read-through. Well.<br /> <br /> It was great. Useful just for the Charm summaries alone, I say, and there's so much more than that here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":4729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","user":"Childofthesun1","date":". 11-08-2015, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T09:32:13-08:00","id":760709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760683#post760683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This deserves a thread of its own. Great information.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I didn't realize we just finished the read-through. Well.<br /> <br /> It was great. Useful just for the Charm summaries alone, I say, and there's so much more than that here.</div> </div> </div> </div>tonberrian, I'd also be really interested in seeing your calculations in more detail - unfortunately, I run into a &quot;maximum integer size&quot; wall around 24 or 25 dice, so I've had trouble calculating for pools that large.<br /> <br /> (Thanks for the kind words!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:27:29-08:00","id":760785,"title":"","content":"The basic probabilities of Exalted dicepools are relatively easy to figure out recursively. I built a dynamic worksheet that figures out the probability curve for dice pools up to 30 dice, given the double rule and target number. I could easily extend it up to 40 or more, but it doesn't figure out reroll stuff because that needs a different approach. I linked the sheet in a thread here, but I'm on my phone so it's hard to find right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:37:27-08:00","id":760796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760593#post760593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After two sessions I'm kind of having the problem you were worried about. A seriously large number of the antagonist section seems to be dedicated to showing of how far and above everyone else the PCs are, which in some respects I like because the Solar PCs should be beating up a lot of guys pretty easily, but I'm finding that a really big number of antagonists are finding my players to be just untouchable, without them even going into peripheral essence. So far I haven't pitted them up against too much stuff, but everything has been a group of essence 3 spirits or other likewise powerful foes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you been using individuals or battlegroup rules?<br /> <br /> Really that's my biggest gripe with battlegroups - as with, say, Dynasty Warriors, it's visually cool to scythe through a whole regiment of enemies, but it's pretty boring at the same time if they're not actually that threatening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T12:18:27-08:00","id":760834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760796#post760796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you been using individuals or battlegroup rules?<br /> <br /> Really that's my biggest gripe with battlegroups - as with, say, Dynasty Warriors, it's visually cool to scythe through a whole regiment of enemies, but it's pretty boring at the same time if they're not actually that threatening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Individuals always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:21:16-08:00","id":761017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760785#post760785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic probabilities of Exalted dicepools are relatively easy to figure out recursively. I built a dynamic worksheet that figures out the probability curve for dice pools up to 30 dice, given the double rule and target number. I could easily extend it up to 40 or more, but it doesn't figure out reroll stuff because that needs a different approach. I linked the sheet in a thread here, but I'm on my phone so it's hard to find right now.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/759311-withering-damage-calculator\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/759311-withering-damage-calculator\"> Withering Damage Calculator - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/759311-withering-damage-calculator\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/759311-withering-damage-calculator </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I made one (https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1qgOh3-eJFu5YJ6HC642hvanG-dEgossJDjSdm99dwig/edit) in Google Sheets. Tell me if you come across any issues. I'm not adding in rerolls, or double [NUMBER] of 7s etc. That would require reworking the entire thing. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Basically, the probability of x successes on n dice P(x,n) is P(x-2,n-1)*P(2,1) + P(x-1,n-1) * P(1,1) + P(x,n-1) * P(0,1). With standard dice rules, P(2,1) = .1, P(1,1) = .3, and P(0,1) = .6. From here, you can recursively find the probabilities of successes for arbitrary dice pools. The sheet can find P(2,1), P(1,1), and P(0,1) from double rules and target numbers, and can account for those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:30:21-08:00","id":761026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=760065#post760065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sidereal Excellency is\u2026 okay, so, let\u2019s talk probability. In 2e, the Sids had a die cap of (Essence), which they could (like all Celestials) render free by using an Infinite Mastery. They could <i>also</i> buy down their TNs from 7 to 4, which meant each of those few dice was more efficient \u2013 but there was no discount on the buy-down, unless I\u2019m misremembering. So at Essence 4, a 2e Solar could drop 23 dice, averaging 11.5 successes, for free; a 2e Sidereal could only muster 17 dice, for 8.5 successes, for free, but could do 13.6 dice if he dropped 3m on it. Since 3m was also the cost of a perfect, not such a big deal.<br /> <br /> So, here we are. <i>Nobody</i> gets Infinite Masteries anymore. At E4, a Solar drops 21 dice, for 11.5 successes, but it costs him 10m to do so. At E4, a Sidereal drops 15 dice, for 12 successes, but it only costs him 3m. At equivalent mote costs, with identical base pools, the Sidereal <i>substantially </i>beats the Solar for raw output at any Essence rating; from E4 onward, he also caps out higher. (If we\u2019re looking at, say, Withering pools, this happens a lot earlier.) That\u2019s kind of bothersome.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>With withering, it happens instantly, even with Excellent Strike.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Any essence solar vs. essence 2 sidereal dicepool and mote efficiency comparison:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">-Solar: Dex 5 + Melee 5 + Speciality + Small Artifact weapon + Excellency 2m + Excellent Strike 3m gives average ((18*5/9) + 1) = 11 successes for 5 motes spent.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">-Sidereal: Dex 5 + Melee 5 + Speciality + Small Artifact Weapon + Excellency 2m + Target Number 4 gives average (18*8/10) = 14.4 successes for 5 motes spent.</span></span><br /> <br /> Even if solar blows another 6 motes (cap) he only gets to 14.33 successes, parity, for over twice the mote cost.<br /> <br /> That raw power plus the 'weird' powers sidereals are bound to have? 'You see a sidereal, you do what we do: run.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:47:33-08:00","id":761041,"title":"","content":"It's important to note that QC rules aren't mechanical previews for other Exalts, they're just there to let you quickly assemble something that feels like that kind of Exalt. So I wouldn't read too much into the balance of the QC Exalts. When the actual Sidereal book comes out in 2030 they may have completely different excellency rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T17:04:45-08:00","id":761048,"title":"","content":"Having two sets of excellency rules for exalts depending on if they're PCs or NPCs sounds like needlessly confusing design, and IIRC from what the devs have said lunar excellencies will work the same as they do for QCs.<br /> <br /> Also while sidereals having straight up better dicepools than solars is (IMO) not very good design what what with solars supposedly being the shiniest (I'd rather they have 'jump through hoops for the same dicepool' like lunars, or just Ability Rating + Essence) so is giving NPCs better powers than PCs just for being NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 11-08-2015, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T17:20:31-08:00","id":761056,"title":"","content":"It's not supposed to be a case of NPCs using one set of charms and PCs using another, the QC rules are just a stopgap designed to let STs use non-Solar NPCs until the actual book comes out, at which point all NPCs should be made using the actual rules for that splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T17:24:56-08:00","id":761061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761048#post761048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having two sets of excellency rules for exalts depending on if they're PCs or NPCs sounds like needlessly confusing design</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but they haven't actually started much work on the Sidereals from what it sounds like. They had to pick <i>something</i> to use in the interim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T17:47:53-08:00","id":761079,"title":"","content":"But why would they make it so ridiculously strong? It's not hard to see what lowering the target number by one means; you get on average one extra success per 10 dice rolled. With the dicepools exalts tend to throw around on anything they care about, this is two to four times as strong as a regular excellency per mote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T18:26:05-08:00","id":761097,"title":"","content":"Hasn't the ability for Sidereals to lower the TN of a roll been around since at least the 2E Sidereal Handbook? I distinctly remember there being an Excellency to lower the TN and achieve an auspicious success on a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T19:34:20-08:00","id":761144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761079#post761079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why would they make it so ridiculously strong? It's not hard to see what lowering the target number by one means; you get on average one extra success per 10 dice rolled. With the dicepools exalts tend to throw around on anything they care about, this is two to four times as strong as a regular excellency per mote.</div> </div> </div> </div>They just ported the 2E Sidereal excellency without modification. I mean, maybe they should have changed it, but it shouldn't be <i>confusing</i> that it is the way it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T20:31:43-08:00","id":761179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761097#post761097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hasn't the ability for Sidereals to lower the TN of a roll been around since at least the 2E Sidereal Handbook? I distinctly remember there being an Excellency to lower the TN and achieve an auspicious success on a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The big difference is that in, say, 2e, the Sidereal paid 3m to roll 17 dice at TN 4, while the Solar paid 0m to roll 23 dice at TN 7. Sure, the Sidereal had a higher average, but for what it cost him to use it, the Solar could pop a perfect defense.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, the Solar is paying 10m to throw 21 dice, and the Sidereal's paying less to average more - it's a big shift, not because the rules for the Excellencies themselves have changed, but because the world around them has altered.<br /> <br /> (My current houserule is that the cost per TN reduction is more like 3-4m, which makes repeated TN 4 + bonus dice prohibitively expensive. Still interacts weirdly with Withering dice, though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T20:38:59-08:00","id":761183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761179#post761179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. The big difference is that in, say, 2e, the Sidereal paid 3m to roll 17 dice at TN 4</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one half-assed Sidereal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T00:29:51-08:00","id":761288,"title":"","content":"This was problably mentioned earlier, but I could not find it.<br /> <br /> Have you reported things like missing rules for figthing with the offhand and such? It sounds like something that has been cut by accident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T00:37:14-08:00","id":761293,"title":"","content":"It seems like a Sidereal gets more out of bonus dice (accuracy bonuses, specialties, etc) while a Solar gets more out of straight ability + attribute pools. It's up to the player to find an advantage there. I'm not sure this adds up to a problem especially since we haven't seen Sidereal charms and total capabilities. We were told a long time ago that this would not be the edition of straightforward Solar superiority. The opening fiction showed a Solar losing a fight to a Sidereal, so maybe that was more than the authors waxing poetic about a combat that actually has a foregone conclusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T05:53:32-08:00","id":761407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761183#post761183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one half-assed Sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess? I mean, I'm not assuming either of them are carrying mismatched +10 Accuracy/+10 Defense Glorious Solar Sabers, or wearing Perfected Kata Bracers, or what-have-you; I'm just trying to compare Excellencies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761288#post761288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was problably mentioned earlier, but I could not find it.<br /> <br /> Have you reported things like missing rules for figthing with the offhand and such? It sounds like something that has been cut by accident.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them, but not all - I just wanted to finish the darn thing. I'm going to make a pass back through my notes and look for stuff to report.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761293#post761293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like a Sidereal gets more out of bonus dice (accuracy bonuses, specialties, etc) while a Solar gets more out of straight ability + attribute pools. It's up to the player to find an advantage there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely true that we only have a little piece of the picture so far, but that little piece is tilted in a way none of the other QCs are. Like I said: it bears watching; that's about all we know for sure for now.<br /> <br /> (Also, be careful with Sidereal QCs.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-09-2015, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T05:57:19-08:00","id":761408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761407#post761407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess? I mean, I'm not assuming either of them are carrying matched +10 Accuracy/+10 Defense Glorious Solar Sabers, or wearing Perfected Kata Bracers, or what-have-you; I'm just trying to compare Excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Sidereals have native access to costless passive TN reduction. <br /> <br /> Though, your +10/+10 GSS leads me to think that you're talking about 2.0e here. Why would you talk about Sidereal balance <i>at all </i>in the context of 2.0? They basically don't exist, and to the extent that they do it's as a punchline. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:13:05-08:00","id":761416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761408#post761408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but Sidereals have native access to costless passive TN reduction.<br /> <br /> Though, your +10/+10 GSS leads me to think that you're talking about 2.0e here. Why would you talk about Sidereal balance <i>at all </i>in the context of 2.0? They basically don't exist, and to the extent that they do it's as a punchline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's a little bit of my point: that keeping the Excellency numbers the same from 2e to 3e doesn't work, even though they weren't a problem in 2e - 2e had (to put it mildly) a lot else going on.<br /> <br /> 2.5 Sidereals were more functional, but I'm not sure they were actually more balanced - they just tilted the balance in a very different way. (We had a player with the overlapping Sidereal defensive suite who basically could not be attacked without costing the attacker a greater quantity of resources than it did him..)<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm blanking, anyway - are you talking about a 2.0 or 2.5 means of free TN reduction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:21:35-08:00","id":761426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761416#post761416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's a little bit of my point: that keeping the Excellency numbers the same from 2e to 3e doesn't work, even though they weren't a problem in 2e - 2e had (to put it mildly) a lot else going on.<br /> <br /> 2.5 Sidereals were more functional, but I'm not sure they were actually more balanced - they just tilted the balance in a very different way. (We had a player with the overlapping Sidereal defensive suite who basically could not be attacked without costing the attacker a greater quantity of resources than it did him..)<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm blanking, anyway - are you talking about a 2.0 or 2.5 means of free TN reduction?</div> </div> </div> </div>2.5 has World-Shaping Artistic Vision, which lets you trade stunt dice for TN reduction, Elemental Vision for some much-more conditional reduction, and of course Astrology - preferably Simple Astrology, but canon Astrology <i>can </i>be used, it's just a headache and very resource-intensive to buy into. <br /> <br /> WSAV though should be part of any combat-focused Sidereal's basic suite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:29:19-08:00","id":761430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761426#post761426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.5 has World-Shaping Artistic Vision, which lets you trade stunt dice for TN reduction, Elemental Vision for some much-more conditional reduction, and of course Astrology - preferably Simple Astrology, but canon Astrology <i>can </i>be used, it's just a headache and very resource-intensive to buy into.<br /> <br /> WSAV though should be part of any combat-focused Sidereal's basic suite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right, thanks.<br /> <br /> Standing by the above comments, then - I don't think 2.5 Sidereals were particularly well-balanced. What worked in 2e, because the rest of their set was a joke (and because 3m was a huge offensive outlay!) doesn't work in a world where those things aren't true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T07:02:37-08:00","id":761448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761430#post761430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, right, thanks.<br /> <br /> Standing by the above comments, then - I don't think 2.5 Sidereals were particularly well-balanced. What worked in 2e, because the rest of their set was a joke (and because 3m was a huge offensive outlay!) doesn't work in a world where those things aren't true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, too, once thought that sheer number of free successes was the one key to victory in 2.5 and thus my Sidereal was the Greatest Fighter Ever because he averaged more successes on his attack rolls than even a spec'd Dawn.<br /> <br /> Then I tried to actually compare him to a Dawn and all my dreams of supremacy were crushed.<br /> <br /> 2.5 balance is <i>weird</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T07:20:59-08:00","id":761466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761448#post761448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, too, once thought that sheer number of free successes was the one key to victory in 2.5 and thus my Sidereal was the Greatest Fighter Ever because he averaged more successes on his attack rolls than even a spec'd Dawn.<br /> <br /> Then I tried to actually compare him to a Dawn and all my dreams of supremacy were crushed.<br /> <br /> 2.5 balance is <i>weird</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did the same comparison, actually - I mock-battled a nearly-pure-combat 2.5 Dawn against a fairly-high-combat 2.5 Endings, with both characters developed through play up to Essence 5 and controlled by competent players. Not only did the Dawn not win, he failed to even force resource expenditure beyond the stunt replacement rate.<br /> <br /> This is probably not the place to relitigate 2.5, though. <i>If nothing else</i>, in a Quick Character format - where Excellencies are a lot of your total oomph - the Sidereal is a much nastier piece of work than one might realize without running the probabilities; it seems to that those properties would carry over if applied to a character with a fully-developed sheet, but I'll happily agree that that's a lot of speculation, for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-09-2015, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T08:54:59-08:00","id":761535,"title":"","content":"So, some summary thoughts, before I start the (requested) hunt-back-through-for-bugs-to-report cycle.<br /> <br /> Let's start with the good - and there's a lot of good to talk about. This edition has better pieces of art than any that's come before; the opening shot of Wu Jian, or the Realm parade, or Perfected Soul beneath the statue of the Sun, or the closing image of Strawmaiden Janest, for instance, are beautiful and haunting in a way I've never seen equaled in the older books. Some of these are pieces I wouldn't mind having to hang on my wall (though the Sun one might draw some odd looks). But that's window-dressing: it's important, but (for me, at least), what's more important is that the core engine to the game is fun and exciting in some really innovative ways. Sorcery is great; being a sorcerer opens a lot of doors and enables a flexible system of Workings that is both powerful player tool and immediate Storyteller plot hook. That's great! That's exactly what you want systems to do. The core combat engine allows dynamic shifts in combat that we never saw in 2e, and so far, at least, it seems to allow for a meaningful degree of player decision-making and strategic choice. In the game I ran yesterday, one player got stabbed, poisoned, and nearly drowned. By the end of the fight, he was down seven health levels... and he still hadn't gotten entirely serious about the combat. &quot;Thank goodness for Ox-Body,&quot; one of the other players said. That's wonderful! Can you even <i>imagine</i> hearing that sentence in a previous edition of the game?<br /> <br /> Or consider the existence of martial arts that are, at long last, useful without being game-breaking; or the invention of Evocations to actually give you something interesting to set your artifact weapon apart. (Look at the <i>really cool</i> implementations of those ideas, which allow you make things like &quot;the Righteous Devil&quot; or &quot;the wielder of what's basically The Punisher in weapon form&quot; the heart of a character concept.) Consider, in general, the existence of <i>alternative builds</i>, enabled by things like Supernal, of mutually-exclusive choices where any of several options are viable, interesting, and drastically different. Note the care that's been taken to avoid so many of the failure states of 2e: the ridiculous round-by-round movement tracking, the monotonous-but-vital stunting, the endless mote slogs, the kiting archers and 2/7 filters and poisonous bad-touchers and effortless immunities and and and and <i>and</i>.<br /> <br /> In play, it's a game that feels risky without feeling immediately fatal. That's terrific.<br /> <br /> In social situations, it's also strong - though this is perhaps not quite as stand-out of a difference as the combat. Social interaction feels meaningful, now; Intimacies give a shape to discussions that 2e's &quot;KILL YOUR FAMILY&quot; spam never had.<br /> <br /> Charm-wise, it's solved another constant complaint of the last edition: that if you wanted to be an investigator or a masterful dodger or the ultimate thief, well, that would keep you busy for about ten sessions, and then you were done. There's a breadth of options in most Abilities now; I think the smallest tree is still 17 deep, which is more than twice what some 2e options offered.<br /> <br /> There is a lot to praise, here. That may not always have shown through in my comments over the preceding pages; when a Charm was competently executed but not particularly a stand-out in either direction, there was not always a lot to say about it. Let me be explicit, then: there is a lot - a <i>lot</i> - of good stuff in this book. I look forward to using it for years to come.<br /> <br /> There are other decisions that I find... questionable. Craft continues to disappoint; in my game yesterday, the two craft-heavy players found themselves in yet another situation where they wanted to make a series of perfectly-mundane Major projects and, RAW, would have been unable to do so. Systems in general seem to have multiplied needlessly in places; note, for instance, that the rules for commanding an army by land, and the rules for commanding an army by sea (or, presumably, air) are incompatible and spread across two different multi-page systems. The book in general drags its feet, taking paragraphs to say what a couple of clear definitions could express, or spending pages to argue against 2e-style interpretations of some of its setting details. In general, it suffers from a couple of common RPG errors: it presents material out of order (such that earlier chapters reference, without definition, terms that won't be explained for another fifty pages), and it is rife throughout with spelling, punctuation, and spacing errors. That the authors appear to have different notions of whether they were using the Oxford comma is the least of these; the frequent (in some chapters) hy-phen on a word that's no longer at a col-umn break is much more irksome. None of this is helped by a series of bizarre font choices, which in places include a nearly unreadable italic and nigh-identical punctuation marks for commas and periods, or by a choice of backgrounds that often stick bits of colored muck behind the text I'm trying to read.<br /> <br /> But these are gripes. They bug me, and in some cases they seem like obvious oversights - but they are not, at heart, the book's biggest problems. The things that trouble me about 3e - and the concerns that, left unchecked, are going to be a mounting problem as the number of moving packets in the game increases - are the following, in roughly decreasing order of severity:<br /> <br /> 1) <i>The rules fundamentally fail to describe common, basic interactions</i>. These aren't weird, niche, edge-cases - they're your meat-and-potatoes concerns. In what order do you declare Charms, at the start of an attack? What are the rules for counterattacks - when are they made, by default, and can you use multiple counterattack Charms in response to a single provocation? Are gambits Decisive attacks, or are they <i>similar to</i> Decisive attacks? What happens when a magical flurry Clashes with another attack? What happens if you Crash (or die) partway through an action? When do you actually start suffering from Onslaught penalties? What happens if two effects conflict, and neither has explicit conflict-resolution rules?<br /> <br /> 2) <i>The rules that do exist are sloppy and unclear in numerous places</i>. The lack of an explicit sequence of combat steps leads to <i>painfully</i> vague resolutions, in places. Charm types are used inconsistently, with identical effects written with multiple different types - Reflexive/Instant, Reflexive/Turn, Permanent/Permanent, and so on. Numerous Charms don't actually follow the typing rules; there are, for instance, many Reflexive Charms that neither create a reflexive action nor enhance an unrolled action, and yet, by the book, that's <i>all they should do</i>. Worse, this often makes it unclear whether a given Reflexive Charm is actually creating a new action or not. Several Charms introduce notation (&quot;recurring 10s&quot;) that is not picked up on or repeated by any other effect. Some Charms seem not to know that &quot;3a&quot; is a legitimate cost, rather than something that has to be described in text; others seem to think you can spend yourself into negative Initiative as long as a Charm lacks the Perilous keyword (you cannot). Penalties are introduced only in effects that remove them (the Ambidextrous merit, Steel Devil Form), and general system effects (training animals, for instance) are described only inside Charms that modify them. On the other end of the scale, some Charms <i>lack their own rules</i> - Fivefold Bulwark Stance will never tell you what &quot;certain penalties&quot; it removes unless you read its sidebar; the rules for activating multiple Awareness Charms are also tucked away on a different page (rather than, say, Keyworded into the relevant Charms), as are, say, the rules for determining whether you need to Aim with a Charm or not.<br /> <br /> 3) <i>Even where the Charms are not unclear, they are too often overwrought, wordy, and uninteresting to read through.</i> Numerous Lore Charms include special call-outs that say, basically, &quot;Supernal works as it always does for this Charm.&quot; That's both unnecessary and confusing; it causes the reader to wonder, &quot;Is this <i>not</i> true of the Charms that lack this clause?&quot; Literal dozens of Charms provide only 10% die boosts or 1-2m cost reductions, backed by descriptions worthy of the <i>Princes of the Universe</i> lyrics - and virtually none of these effects are standardized, to cut down on the mental overhead. By far the worst thing about reading the 3e Solar set is that it <i>isn't fun</i>, because for every power that made me drop my jaw and exclaim, &quot;Wow!&quot; I was reading a page or more of Charms that tweaked the rules slightly. I'm not saying the latter aren't powerful - they are! - I'm just saying that they're a poor argument for 200+ pages of rules. Exalted has to sell itself, not just to me but to any new player looking to pick up the game, and too many of these Charms do not do that.<br /> <br /> 4) <i>The game doesn't know what it wants to be</i>. Is it a competitive thing, where the Storyteller throws Limit Breaks at you at dramatically terrible time, or is the ST dialing that back carefully? Are we trusting the player to invent facts and use the powerful XP-generating engines he has, or do we need numerous sidebars tut-tutting at players for using mechanics in <i>too</i> effective of a way? Is this a tight, rules-heavy CCG-style engine, or is it a natural language, &quot;do what feels right&quot; system? Are we relying on carefully-specified gamist-style systems, or is this kind of a Fate-ish &quot;Eh, your background gives you different aspects you can tag to know things?&quot; The answer seems to be, in all cases, <i>yes</i>.<br /> <br /> I remain curious to see what the final-final edition of this game looks like - but while I am <i>overall positive </i>on the result, out-of-the-box Exalted appears to require substantial houseruling just to get everyone on the same page. And that's troubling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-09-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":28}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T11:17:32-08:00","id":761619,"title":"","content":"You give voice to all of my concerns, some I didn't know I had. The word that comes to mind is insightful. Nice job Irked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T11:39:37-08:00","id":761636,"title":"","content":"Great job! Especially your summary is spot on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T12:00:48-08:00","id":761647,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Irked. Great thread and great summary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T12:07:52-08:00","id":761651,"title":"","content":"Joining in the chorus here: you've summarized, in each post, both what I loved and hated about this iteration of the game. <br /> <br /> Working mechanics in some of the big problem areas don't excuse the unclear writing and the downright strange layout choices.<br /> <br /> When I can point to something 2E did and say it was better than how 3E described it, something is <i>wrong.</i><br /> <br /> Every bit of this could have been corrected, I think, with even a TINY bit more openness in development. As it is, this game NEEDS to be delayed longer, MUCH longer, to fix this shoddy attempt at at a release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:56:36-08:00","id":761838,"title":"","content":"Excellent summary there, Irked. Thank you for amusing us with commentary and a detailed comb through the book. I've really enjoyed reading through your read through and a lot of your thoughts mirror my own. I really hope feedback like this will be considered before the book is finished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T17:16:27-08:00","id":761850,"title":"","content":"That is an excellent summary, and it's been a good read-through.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761651#post761651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every bit of this could have been corrected, I think, with even a TINY bit more openness in development. As it is, this game NEEDS to be delayed longer, MUCH longer, to fix this shoddy attempt at at a release.</div> </div> </div> </div>From commentary elsewhere, they cut a wide swath of their playtesters after the first leak. (For reference, the first leak happened a little under a year and a half ago.)<br /> <br /> After the second leak, they cut everyone but devs and layout. (For reference, this happened nine months ago.)<br /> <br /> I don't want to say &quot;they have suffered immeasurably from their decision to value secrecy over hands-on-deck&quot; but it's stamped all over the product.<br /> <br /> (Well-intentioned but thoroughly misguided people jumping up and down demanding an open playtest proooobably didn't help any.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T17:44:38-08:00","id":761872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761850#post761850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an excellent summary, and it's been a good read-through.<br /> <br /> From commentary elsewhere, they cut a wide swath of their playtesters after the first leak. (For reference, the first leak happened a little under a year and a half ago.)<br /> <br /> After the second leak, they cut everyone but devs and layout. (For reference, this happened nine months ago.)<br /> <br /> I don't want to say &quot;they have suffered immeasurably from their decision to value secrecy over hands-on-deck&quot; but it's stamped all over the product.<br /> <br /> (Well-intentioned but thoroughly misguided people jumping up and down demanding an open playtest proooobably didn't help any.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well-intentioned entitled people that weren't happy about not playtesting were and are a problem.<br /> <br /> But cutting off everyone was a really, really shortsighted move.<br /> <br /> Well-intentioned, but ultimately misguided, perhaps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Since you don't wanna say it, I will: They've suffered immeasurably from their decision to value secrecy over hands on-deck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","user":"UltraFennec","date":". 11-10-2015, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T18:08:14-08:00","id":761891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761535#post761535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The things that trouble me about 3e - and the concerns that, left unchecked, are going to be a mounting problem as the number of moving packets in the game increases - are the following, in roughly decreasing order of severity:<br /> <br /> 1) <i>The rules fundamentally fail to describe common, basic interactions</i>. These aren't weird, niche, edge-cases - they're your meat-and-potatoes concerns. In what order do you declare Charms, at the start of an attack? What are the rules for counterattacks - when are they made, by default, and can you use multiple counterattack Charms in response to a single provocation? Are gambits Decisive attacks, or are they <i>similar to</i> Decisive attacks? What happens when a magical flurry Clashes with another attack? What happens if you Crash (or die) partway through an action? When do you actually start suffering from Onslaught penalties? What happens if two effects conflict, and neither has explicit conflict-resolution rules?<br /> <br /> 2) <i>The rules that do exist are sloppy and unclear in numerous places</i>. The lack of an explicit sequence of combat steps leads to <i>painfully</i> vague resolutions, in places. Charm types are used inconsistently, with identical effects written with multiple different types - Reflexive/Instant, Reflexive/Turn, Permanent/Permanent, and so on. Numerous Charms don't actually follow the typing rules; there are, for instance, many Reflexive Charms that neither create a reflexive action nor enhance an unrolled action, and yet, by the book, that's <i>all they should do</i>. Worse, this often makes it unclear whether a given Reflexive Charm is actually creating a new action or not. Several Charms introduce notation (&quot;recurring 10s&quot;) that is not picked up on or repeated by any other effect. Some Charms seem not to know that &quot;3a&quot; is a legitimate cost, rather than something that has to be described in text; others seem to think you can spend yourself into negative Initiative as long as a Charm lacks the Perilous keyword (you cannot). Penalties are introduced only in effects that remove them (the Ambidextrous merit, Steel Devil Form), and general system effects (training animals, for instance) are described only inside Charms that modify them. On the other end of the scale, some Charms <i>lack their own rules</i> - Fivefold Bulwark Stance will never tell you what &quot;certain penalties&quot; it removes unless you read its sidebar; the rules for activating multiple Awareness Charms are also tucked away on a different page (rather than, say, Keyworded into the relevant Charms), as are, say, the rules for determining whether you need to Aim with a Charm or not.<br /> <br /> 3) <i>Even where the Charms are not unclear, they are too often overwrought, wordy, and uninteresting to read through.</i> Numerous Lore Charms include special call-outs that say, basically, &quot;Supernal works as it always does for this Charm.&quot; That's both unnecessary and confusing; it causes the reader to wonder, &quot;Is this <i>not</i> true of the Charms that lack this clause?&quot; Literal dozens of Charms provide only 10% die boosts or 1-2m cost reductions, backed by descriptions worthy of the <i>Princes of the Universe</i> lyrics - and virtually none of these effects are standardized, to cut down on the mental overhead. By far the worst thing about reading the 3e Solar set is that it <i>isn't fun</i>, because for every power that made me drop my jaw and exclaim, &quot;Wow!&quot; I was reading a page or more of Charms that tweaked the rules slightly. I'm not saying the latter aren't powerful - they are! - I'm just saying that they're a poor argument for 200+ pages of rules. Exalted has to sell itself, not just to me but to any new player looking to pick up the game, and too many of these Charms do not do that.<br /> <br /> 4) <i>The game doesn't know what it wants to be</i>. Is it a competitive thing, where the Storyteller throws Limit Breaks at you at dramatically terrible time, or is the ST dialing that back carefully? Are we trusting the player to invent facts and use the powerful XP-generating engines he has, or do we need numerous sidebars tut-tutting at players for using mechanics in <i>too</i> effective of a way? Is this a tight, rules-heavy CCG-style engine, or is it a natural language, &quot;do what feels right&quot; system? Are we relying on carefully-specified gamist-style systems, or is this kind of a Fate-ish &quot;Eh, your background gives you different aspects you can tag to know things?&quot; The answer seems to be, in all cases, <i>yes</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, <i>please</i> submit this on the KS. I truly doubt it will make a difference, but at least they will have it and consciously be saying, &quot;no, we don't consider these problems to fix,&quot; if they ignore it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761535#post761535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remain curious to see what the final-final edition of this game looks like</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I doubt very many of the very proven mechanical issues that have been borne out by the past few weeks will actually be changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T18:45:58-08:00","id":761921,"title":"","content":"Especially as the KS comments will be closing on the 11th!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T19:09:41-08:00","id":761936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761921#post761921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially as the KS comments will be closing on the 11th!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I just saw that too.<br /> <br /> Hurry, Irked! You haven't much time!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T20:12:01-08:00","id":761964,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to second (or third, fourth etc) everyone else. This has been *incredibly* helpful, and I think it would actually be really useful for the devs to take a look at this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8842-eris","name":"Eris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T23:48:29-08:00","id":762044,"title":"","content":"The same as everyone else are saying :-)<br /> <br /> If you feel like, you could also link to thread just to point out how many people agree with your comments.<br /> <br /> Some of the things are probably not going to change, like a major rewrite of charms. But explaining the basic rules more clearly seems like not too much work for a lot of gain.<br /> <br /> In regards to paying for secrecy: I would blame the ones that leaked the documents.<br /> <br /> Also. I asked you to submit your comments because you have more insight than I do :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":80,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","user":"TrueMonk","date":". 11-10-2015, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T00:00:11-08:00","id":762050,"title":"","content":"One or two project leaks should not so thoroughly derail a game. Cutting out all the playtesters is a reactionary, emotion-driven action that did more harm than good, from the result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T02:40:44-08:00","id":762131,"title":"","content":"This thread is a brilliant analysis of the PDF, Irked. Thank you for the time you put into it. I also think you should submit that final post directly to the KS comments.<br /> <br /> For me, personally, it's great to see someone else express the same concerns I have, in a format and and tone that isn't the typical forum rant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T04:05:54-08:00","id":762176,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the kind words, folks. I really appreciate it, and it's good to know this has been useful (and not just me going off on a tear).<br /> <br /> I will definitely be submitting what errata I can between now and Wednesday. I'm not sure the summary post is the most effective way of communicating that information, but most of the specific notes it mentions will show up somewhere in the feedback.<br /> <br /> I'll also try to find time to finish up the last few Charm tree summaries, but that's probably going to be a couple of days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T10:18:07-08:00","id":762391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=761872#post761872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well-intentioned entitled people that weren't happy about not playtesting were and are a problem.<br /> <br /> But cutting off everyone was a really, really shortsighted move.<br /> <br /> Well-intentioned, but ultimately misguised, perhaps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Since you don't wanna say it, I will: They've suffered immeasurably from their decision to value secrecy over hands on-deck.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This notion is what brought us the 3E PDF in it's current state, that people who could see this mess coming are <i>entitled. </i>It's uncharitable to those that knew an open-playtest would improve the new edition of Exalted and were willing to volunteer their time and effort.<br /> <br /> Thanks again Irked for all this analysis, it's invaluable for people like me who find the giant morass of Charms intensely boring and want to quickly sort the wheat from the chaff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T10:26:01-08:00","id":762396,"title":"","content":"Am I completely off base, or does it seem like a lot of the more rules-lawyer inclined 2ed devs weren't involved in the 3e development?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1970-yeangst","name":"yeangst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T10:30:57-08:00","id":762399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yeangst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=762396#post762396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I completely off base, or does it seem like a lot of the more rules-lawyer inclined 2ed devs weren't involved in the 3e development?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really think of who. <br /> <br /> Neph is the only one I can think of and his mechanics were pretty hit or miss. Vance was a home brewer for most (all?) of 2e but his mechanics were always solid (and this is borne out in the MA stuff). A number of recurrent writers had great narrative chops but bad mechanics, or flat out were bad at both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 11-10-2015, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T10:56:15-08:00","id":762424,"title":"","content":"I am also putting in my two cents here, Irked. This is a really good summary of what Ex3 is so far and what would be good to fix and I found it immensely helpful as a companion reader to Ex3 itself.<br /> <br /> So thank you very much for putting the time into this! It's a lot of work, I can tell, and it helped me with my reluctance to dive into the corebook. You did us all a solid by writing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/921-malovich","name":"Malovich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar921_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T11:56:35-08:00","id":762474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=762391#post762391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This notion is what brought us the 3E PDF in it's current state, that people who could see this mess coming are <i>entitled. </i>It's uncharitable to those that knew an open-playtest would improve the new edition of Exalted and were willing to volunteer their time and effort.<br /> <br /> Thanks again Irked for all this analysis, it's invaluable for people like me who find the giant morass of Charms intensely boring and want to quickly sort the wheat from the chaff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have no issue with the people who simply wished to help and wanted the best for the game. <br /> <br /> But I definitely believe there were a number of people who espoused a pro-openness stance that were salty about other things and used that as a vector for their discontent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T14:45:07-08:00","id":762613,"title":"","content":"Okay, I think I've compiled all the unclear things mentioned in the thread and submitted them. In under the wire!<br /> <br /> (I have to admit that I'm hoping, first, that everything that needs to be fixed is fixed, and second, that there's some sort of change log of the results - because heck if I want to do <i>this</i> again.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T15:03:28-08:00","id":762627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=762391#post762391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This notion is what brought us the 3E PDF in it's current state, that people who could see this mess coming are <i>entitled. </i>It's uncharitable to those that knew an open-playtest would improve the new edition of Exalted and were willing to volunteer their time and effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and I think that point of view has been vindicated by just how <b>quickly</b> most of the mistakes / vague rules / gamebreakers / lifted art have been spotted here by a relative handful of people looking on it with fresh eyes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T15:21:15-08:00","id":763518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=762613#post762613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I think I've compiled all the unclear things mentioned in the thread and submitted them. In under the wire!<br /> <br /> (I have to admit that I'm hoping, first, that everything that needs to be fixed is fixed, and second, that there's some sort of change log of the results - because heck if I want to do <i>this</i> again.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Brave new world, where tabletop RPGs have patch notes. :lol:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T18:24:32-08:00","id":763642,"title":"","content":"Heh... actually, that reminds me of the Warhammer 8th edition FAQs... which did, indeed, have a change log of updates. Seriously, patch notes are applicable to tabletop games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T08:38:47-08:00","id":770029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=763642#post763642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh... actually, that reminds me of the Warhammer 8th edition FAQs... which did, indeed, have a change log of updates. Seriously, patch notes are applicable to tabletop games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There was a time not long ago that Exalted itself had a rather large errata PDF...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T15:08:51-08:00","id":770323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=770029#post770029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There was a time not long ago that Exalted itself had a rather large errata PDF...</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shudder&gt;<br /> <br /> Actually it's quite easy to compare two pdfs, we could make our own patch notes for E3 prefix and postfix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T17:10:29-08:00","id":771069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=751513#post751513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(This charm is half the reason I\u2019m sad that the <i>Second Apocalypse</i> books don\u2019t make the recommended reading list \u2013 in the first two books, Kellhus lives and breathes Solar Socialize, and there\u2019s at least one scene that\u2019s a beautiful illustration of WECM. The books in general parse very well as the story of a newborn Solar \u2013 and given that the first trilogy is <i>The Prince of Nothing</i> and the second is <i>The Aspect-Emperor</i>, well.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm late to the party on this, but YES. Kellhus is basically the only Exalt in a world of mortals, including mortal sorcerers (at least in the first trilogy). I mean, other Dunyain could do the same things he does, but they don't have the motivation or reason to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T19:14:58-08:00","id":771138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=771069#post771069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm late to the party on this, but YES. Kellhus is basically the only Exalt in a world of mortals, including mortal sorcerers (at least in the first trilogy). I mean, other Dunyain could do the same things he does, but they don't have the motivation or reason to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think those books shape my view of what Creation should be more than anything else, at this point: the technology, the society gradually recovering from an apocalypse, the weird lands where death bleeds through (or where you might grow an eye in the middle of your heart), the nihilistic threat that the gods can't see because it's outside fate... it all just <i>works</i>. I can't say I manage to capture that in a game very well - and I'm not entirely sorry for that, because Earwa is not a fun place to hang out - but in my head, that's more like Creation than anything else I've read.<br /> <br /> The reaction basically everyone has to Kellhus when they've only heard about him (&quot;C'mon, it's just one guy; how bad could he be?&quot;) is <i>exactly</i> the vibe I'd want to have for newborn Solars. For one tiny, almost-invisible window of time, it's <i>almost </i>true - and then oops, he accidentally an entire religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T19:26:59-08:00","id":771145,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the big difference being that Kellhus basically singlehandedly shaped a huge portion of the relevant world after leaving Ishual. In some ways this is bigger than the scope of Creation, because there are really no other active powers on the same &quot;power level&quot; as Kellhus acting in Earwa, and nothing that could effectively counter him. Compare this to creation with hundreds of other Solars and Lunars, and probably 20,000 DBs. Which, I'm not saying that Kellhus didn't achieve huge things, just that it'd be different if there were a couple hundred other Dunyain acting toward their own individual goals in the world.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, Kellhus is more of a plot device than a character, because whenever he struggles, he's set up the narrative of that struggle in advance to produce a desired effect in those who witness the struggle. I don't think that kind of thing really works in Creation; while Solars are badasses, they don't have the same absolute control of the field, simply because there are other big dogs out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T06:01:15-08:00","id":771430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=771145#post771145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the big difference being that Kellhus basically singlehandedly shaped a huge portion of the relevant world after leaving Ishual. In some ways this is bigger than the scope of Creation, because there are really no other active powers on the same &quot;power level&quot; as Kellhus acting in Earwa, and nothing that could effectively counter him. Compare this to creation with hundreds of other Solars and Lunars, and probably 20,000 DBs. Which, I'm not saying that Kellhus didn't achieve huge things, just that it'd be different if there were a couple hundred other Dunyain acting toward their own individual goals in the world.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, Kellhus is more of a plot device than a character, because whenever he struggles, he's set up the narrative of that struggle in advance to produce a desired effect in those who witness the struggle. I don't think that kind of thing really works in Creation; while Solars are badasses, they don't have the same absolute control of the field, simply because there are other big dogs out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, definitely. Solars can pull the same kind of thing off until they bump into someone else's fiefdom - but it's much more a &quot;What if there was exactly one Solar in the world and no other Exalts?&quot; story.<br /> <br /> (Although, <i>The White-Luck Warrior</i> suggests there's at least one Sidereal...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T14:50:17-07:00","id":1309019,"title":"","content":"It seems a bit odd that after so long, I am still not able to find answers to some of the questions raised in this thread (which was so popular back then)<br /> <br /> Here is an example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/715607-irked-reads-ex3?p=755246#post755246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Crane</u><br /> ...<br /> Okay, what is \u201cher enemy\u2019s Initiative\u201d for the purposes of Wisdom of the Celestial Crane (#1)? Is it the enemy\u2019s pre-attack Initiative, or if they hit, is this their reset-to-base 3i? The latter seems like the natural reading, but that\u2019s a pretty expensive Charm.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I can find the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Unofficial Ex3 Dev Rulings Compilation</span></span></span> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1n3ooTmopm3CBxW5jwPp1761xsaIccea-5XIhVM_PQEc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...IhVM_PQEc/edit</a><br /> <br /> Read here <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1069596#post1069596 that</span></span><br /> <br /> &quot;Crane's counterattacks use the same timing as Solar Counterattack (after attack, but before damage is rolled).&quot;<br /> <br /> go to page 317 and read<br /> <br /> &quot;The Exalt draws focus from her foe\u2019s temerity. To strike<br /> her is to invite death. The Exalt may use this Charm in<br /> response to any attack she attempts to parry, creating a<br /> Melee counterattack that occurs after the opponent\u2019s<br /> attack result, but before damage has been rolled. This<br /> attack functions as a regular decisive attack. Solar Counterattack<br /> does not count as the Exalt\u2019s combat action and<br /> cannot be used in response to another counterattack.&quot;<br /> <br /> and then to page 191<br /> <br /> &quot;Step One: Roll (Dexterity + [relevant combat Ability] +<br /> any modifiers) against a difficulty of the target\u2019s Defense.<br /> You do not add your weapon\u2019s accuracy to this roll. If the<br /> roll fails, and your current Initiative is 1-10, your character<br /> loses 2 Initiative. If it\u2019s 11+ and the attack fails, your<br /> character loses 3 Initiative.<br /> <br /> Step Two: If attack is successful, roll your current Initiative<br /> value as a dice pool. The Double 10s rule (p. 183)<br /> does not apply to this roll. If your target has Hardness<br /> (p. 195) equal to or greater than your damage pool in this<br /> step, you inflict no damage but your attack is still considered<br /> a success; proceed to Step Four.<br /> <br /> Step Three: Count up the successes on the Initiative roll.<br /> Apply that many levels of damage to the target\u2019s Health<br /> Track. This damage will be bashing or lethal, as determined<br /> by the weapon used (see p. 195).<br /> <br /> Step Four: If the attack was successful, reset your character\u2019s<br /> Initiative value to 3 (also known as \u201cResetting to<br /> base value.\u201d)&quot;<br /> <br /> And then I am still not really sure. If they hit then it must be their initative as it was when they hit the crane stylist. But if they don't hit, is before or after they loose the 2/3 initiative?<br /> <br /> I mean the last uncertainty is not as bad as the fact that I had to search online to find a fan collection and read an answer in a forum thread and read a specific charm and compare that with the rules to figure out how another totally unrelated charm works.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know if they plan to publish an official errata? (or already have)<br /> <br /> (and yes, I did go away for quite some time in the hope that some of these things would be fixed if I just gave it a couple of years. It just makes me a bit sad to find that it seems they are not)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":80,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","user":"TrueMonk","date":". 04-30-2019, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T17:13:07-07:00","id":1309044,"title":"","content":"There's a thread right up there for asking Robert Vance questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}